002	EXO	012	003	Tell all the Israelites that on the tenth day of this month, every man must choose a lamb for his family, one for each household.
002	EXO	012	004	However, if the household is too small for a whole lamb, then he and his nearest neighbor may choose a lamb according to the total number of people. Divide up the lamb depending on what everybody can eat.
002	EXO	012	005	Your lamb must be a year-old male without any defects, and you can take it either from the sheep or the goats.
002	EXO	012	006	Keep it until the fourteenth day of the month, when all the Israelites will slaughter the animals after sunset and before it gets dark.
002	EXO	012	007	They are to take some of the blood and put it on the sides and tops of the doorframes of the houses where they have the meal.
002	EXO	012	008	They are to roast the meat over a fire and eat it that night, together with unleavened bread and bitter herbs.
002	EXO	012	009	You are not to eat the meat raw or boiled in water. All of it must be roasted over a fire, including the head, legs, and its insides.
002	EXO	012	010	Make sure nothing is left until the morning. If there is anything left over, burn it by morning.
002	EXO	012	011	This is how you are to eat the meal. You should be dressed ready to travel, with your sandals on your feet and your walking stick in your hand. You are to eat quickly—it is the Lord's Passover.
002	EXO	012	012	That very night I will go all through Egypt and kill every firstborn of both people and animals, and I will bring condemnation on all the gods of Egypt. I am the Lord.
002	EXO	012	013	The blood on the houses where you live will mark them out. When I see the blood, I will pass over you. No deathly plague will fall on you to destroy you when I attack Egypt.
002	EXO	012	014	This will be a day to remember for you. You are to celebrate it as a festival to the Lord for generations to come. You will observe this for all time to come.
002	EXO	012	015	For seven days you must eat only bread made without yeast. On the first day you are to get rid of the yeast from your houses. Anyone who eats anything with yeast from the first day to the seventh day must be excluded from the Israelite community.
002	EXO	012	016	On both the first day and on the seventh day you are to have a holy meeting. You must not work on those days, except to prepare food. That is all you are allowed to do.
002	EXO	012	017	You are to keep the Feast of Unleavened Bread because on this very day I led your tribes by their respective divisions out of Egypt. You are to observe this day for all time to come.
002	EXO	012	018	In the first month you are to eat bread without yeast from the evening of the fourteenth day until the evening of the twenty-first day.
002	EXO	012	019	For seven days there must be no yeast in your houses. If anyone eats something with yeast in it, then they must be excluded from the Israelite community, whether they are a foreigner or a native of the land.
002	EXO	012	020	You must not eat anything with yeast in it. Eat only bread without yeast in all your homes.”
002	EXO	012	021	Then Moses called together all the elders of Israel and told them, “Go immediately and choose a lamb for each of your families, and kill the Passover lamb.
002	EXO	012	022	Get a bunch of hyssop, dip it into the blood in the basin, and put some on the top and sides of the doorframe. None of you are to go out through door of the house until morning.
002	EXO	012	023	When the Lord passes through to punish the Egyptians, he will see the blood on the top and sides of the doorframe. He will pass over the door, and he will not allow the destroyer to enter your houses and kill you.
002	EXO	012	024	You and your descendants are to remember to observe these instructions for all time to come.
002	EXO	012	025	When you enter the land that the Lord promised to give you, you are to observe this ceremony.
