002	EXO	020	024	Make me an altar of earth, and sacrifice on it your burnt offerings and peace offerings, your sheep, goats, and cattle. Wherever I decide to be worshiped, I will come to you and bless you.
002	EXO	020	025	Now if you make an altar out of stones for me, you must not build it with cut stones, because if you use a chisel to cut the stone, you make it unholy.
002	EXO	020	026	Also, you must not go up to my altar using steps, so your private parts are not seen.’”
002	EXO	021	001	“These are the regulations you are to present to them:
002	EXO	021	002	If you buy a Hebrew slave, he is to work for you for six years. But in the seventh year, he is to be freed without having to pay anything.
002	EXO	021	003	If he was single when he came, he is to leave single. If he had a wife when he came, she is to leave with him.
002	EXO	021	004	If his master provides him a wife and she has children with him, the woman and her children shall belong to her master, and only the man shall be freed.
002	EXO	021	005	However, if the slave formally states, ‘I love my master and my wife and children; I do not want to be freed,’
002	EXO	021	006	then his master is to take him before the judges. Then he shall have him stand against the door or doorpost and use a metal tool to make a hole in his ear. Then he shall work for his master for life.
002	EXO	021	007	If a man sells his daughter as a slave, she is not to be freed in the same way as male slaves.
002	EXO	021	008	If the man who chose her for himself is not pleased with her, he must let her be bought back. He is not permitted to sell her to foreigners, since he has been unfair to her.
002	EXO	021	009	If he chooses to give her to his son, he must treat her as a daughter.
002	EXO	021	010	If he takes another woman, he must not reduce the food and clothing allowances and marital rights of the first.
002	EXO	021	011	If he doesn't give her these three things, she is free to leave without paying anything.
002	EXO	021	012	Anyone who hits and kills someone else must be executed.
002	EXO	021	013	However, if it wasn't intentional and God let it happen, then I will arrange a place for you where they can run to and be safe.
002	EXO	021	014	But if someone deliberately plans and purposely kills another, you must take them away from my altar and execute them.
002	EXO	021	015	Anyone who hits their father or mother must be executed.
002	EXO	021	016	Anyone who kidnaps someone else must be executed, whether the victim is sold or is still in their possession.
002	EXO	021	017	Anyone who despises their father or mother must be executed.
002	EXO	021	018	If men are fighting and one hits the other with a stone or with his fist, and the injured man doesn't die but has to stay in bed,
002	EXO	021	019	and then gets up and walks around outside with his walking stick, then the one who hit him won't be punished. Even so, he must still compensate the man for the time lost from his work and make sure that he's completely healed.
002	EXO	021	020	Anyone who hits their male or female slave with a rod, and the slave dies as a result, must be punished.
002	EXO	021	021	However, if after a day or two the slave gets better, the owner won't be punished because the slave is their property.
002	EXO	021	022	If men who are fighting happen to hit a pregnant woman so she gives birth prematurely, but no serious injury occurs, he must be fined whatever amount the woman's husband demands and as permitted by the judges.
002	EXO	021	023	But if a serious injury does occur, then you must pay a life for a life,
002	EXO	021	024	an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth, a hand for a hand, a foot for a foot,
002	EXO	021	025	a burn for a burn, a wound for a wound, and a bruise for a bruise.
002	EXO	021	026	Anyone who hits their male or female slave in the eye and blinds them must free the slave as compensation for the eye.
002	EXO	021	027	Anyone who knocks out the tooth of their male or female slave must free the slave as compensation for the tooth.
002	EXO	021	028	If an ox uses its horns to kill a man or woman, the ox must be stoned to death, and its meat must not be eaten. But the owner of the ox won't be punished.
002	EXO	021	029	But if the ox has repeatedly hurt people with its horns, and its owner has been warned but still doesn't keep it under control, and it kills a man or woman, then the ox must be stoned to death and its owner must also be executed.
002	EXO	021	030	But if instead the payment of compensation is required, the owner may buy back his or her life by paying the full amount of compensation demanded.
002	EXO	021	031	If the ox uses its horns and kills a son or a daughter the same rule is applicable.
002	EXO	021	032	If the ox uses its horns and kills a male or female slave, the owner of the ox must pay thirty shekels of silver to the slave's master, and the ox must be stoned to death.
002	EXO	021	033	If someone removes the cover of a cistern or digs one and doesn't cover it, and an ox or a donkey falls into it,
002	EXO	021	034	the owner of the pit must pay compensation to the animal's owner and keep the dead animal.
002	EXO	021	035	If someone's ox injures another's ox and it dies, they must sell the live one and share money received; they must also share the dead animal.
002	EXO	021	036	But if it was known that the ox had repeatedly hurt people with its horns, and its owner had been warned but still didn't keep it under control, full compensation must be paid, ox for ox, but the owner can keep the dead animal.”
002	EXO	022	001	“Anyone who steals an ox or a sheep and kills or sells it must pay back five oxen for one ox and four sheep for one sheep.
002	EXO	022	002	If a thief is discovered breaking into someone's house and is beaten to death, no one shall be guilty of murder.
002	EXO	022	003	But if it happens during daylight, then someone is guilty of murder. A thief must pay everything back that's stolen. If he doesn't have anything, then he must be sold to pay for what was stolen.
002	EXO	022	004	If what was stolen is a live animal he still has, whether it's an ox, donkey, or sheep, he must pay back double.
002	EXO	022	005	If livestock are grazing in a field or vineyard and their owner lets them stray so that they graze in someone else's field, their owner must pay compensation from the best of their own fields or vineyards.
002	EXO	022	006	If a fire is started and it spreads to thorn bushes and then burns stacked or standing grain, or even the whole field, the person who started the fire must pay full compensation.
002	EXO	022	007	If someone gives his neighbor money or possessions to be kept safe and they are stolen from the neighbor's house, if the thief is caught they must pay back double.
002	EXO	022	008	If the thief isn't caught the owner of the house must appear before the judges to find out whether he took his neighbor's property.
002	EXO	022	009	If there's an argument over the ownership of an ox, a donkey, a sheep, a garment, or anything that was lost that someone says, ‘This is mine,’ both parties are to bring their case before the judges. The one whom the judges find in the wrong must pay the other back double.
002	EXO	022	010	If someone asks a neighbor to look after a donkey, an ox, a sheep, or any other animal, but it dies or is injured or is stolen without anybody noticing,
002	EXO	022	011	then an oath must be taken before the Lord to decide if the neighbor has taken the owner's property. The owner must accept the oath and not demand compensation.
002	EXO	022	012	However, if the animal really was stolen from the neighbor, he must compensate the owner.
002	EXO	022	013	If it was killed and torn to pieces by a wild animal, the neighbor shall present the carcass as evidence and does not need to pay compensation.
002	EXO	022	014	If someone borrows a neighbor's animal and it's injured or dies while its owner is not present, they must pay compensation in full.
002	EXO	022	015	If the owner was present, no compensation is to be paid. If the animal was hired, only the hire charge needs to be paid.
002	EXO	022	016	If a man seduces a virgin who is not engaged to be married and sleeps with her, he must pay the full bride-price for her to become his wife.
002	EXO	022	017	If her father adamantly refuses to give her to him, the man still must pay the same amount as the bride-price for a virgin.
002	EXO	022	018	You must not allow a woman who practices witchcraft to live.
002	EXO	022	019	Anyone who has sex with an animal must be executed.
002	EXO	022	020	Anyone who sacrifices to any other god than the Lord must be set apart and executed.
002	EXO	022	021	You must not exploit or mistreat a foreigner. Remember that you yourselves were once foreigners in Egypt.
002	EXO	022	022	You must not take advantage of any widow or orphan.
002	EXO	022	023	If you mistreat them, and they call out to me for help, I will definitely respond to their cry.
002	EXO	022	024	I will become angry, and I will kill you with the sword. Your wives will become widows and your children will be fatherless.
002	EXO	022	025	If you lend money to any of my people because they're poor, you must not behave as a moneylender to them. You must not charge them any interest.
002	EXO	022	026	If you require your neighbor's cloak as security for a loan, you must return it to him by sunset,
002	EXO	022	027	because it's the only clothing he has for his body. What would he sleep in otherwise? If he calls out to me for help, I will listen, for I am considerate.
002	EXO	022	028	You must not despise God or curse your people's leader.
002	EXO	022	029	You must not hold on to the required offerings of your produce, olive oil, and wine. You must give me the firstborn of your sons.
002	EXO	022	030	You must also give me the firstborn of your cattle, sheep, and goats. They can stay with their mothers for their first seven days, but give them to me on the eighth day.
002	EXO	022	031	You are to be holy people to me. You must not eat any animal carcass that you find in the countryside that has been killed by wild animals. Throw it to the dogs to eat.”
002	EXO	023	001	“You must not spread stories that are lies. You must not help bad people by giving evidence that's malicious.
002	EXO	023	002	Don't follow the crowd in doing wrong. When you give evidence in a lawsuit, don't corrupt justice by siding with the majority.
002	EXO	023	003	Don't show favoritism to poor people in their legal cases either.
002	EXO	023	004	If you come across your enemy's ox or donkey that has wandered off, take it back to him.
002	EXO	023	005	If you see the donkey of someone who hates you that has fallen under its load, don't just leave it there. You must stop and help.
002	EXO	023	006	You must not prevent the poor from getting justice in their lawsuits.
002	EXO	023	007	Don't have anything to do with making false accusations. Don't kill the innocent or those who do right, for I won't let the guilty go unpunished.
002	EXO	023	008	Don't accept bribes, for a bribe blinds those who can see, and undermines the evidence of the honest.
002	EXO	023	009	Don't abuse foreigners living among you, since you know very well what it's like to be foreigners, for you were once foreigners in Egypt.
002	EXO	023	010	Six years you are to sow your land and harvest crops,
002	EXO	023	011	but in the seventh year you are to let it rest and leave it uncultivated, so that poor people may eat what grows naturally from the field and the wild animals can finish what's left. Follow the same procedure for your vineyards and olive groves.
002	EXO	023	012	You have six days to do your work, but on the seventh day you must stop working, so that your ox and your donkey can rest, and your slaves' families can catch their breath, as well as the foreigners living among you.
002	EXO	023	013	Make sure to pay attention to everything I've told you. Don't think to call on the names of other gods—you must not even mention them.
002	EXO	023	014	Three times every year you are to celebrate a feast dedicated to me.
002	EXO	023	015	You are to observe the Festival of Unleavened Bread as I instructed you. You are to eat bread without yeast for seven days at the appropriate time in the month of Abib, because that was the month you left Egypt. No one can come before me without bringing an offering.
002	EXO	023	016	You are also to observe the Festival of Harvest when you present the firstfruits of the produce from what you've sown in the fields. Lastly you are to observe the Festival of Gathering-In the Harvest at the end of the year, when you gather in the harvest of the rest of your crops from the field.
002	EXO	023	017	Every Israelite male is to come before the Lord God at these three times every year.
002	EXO	023	018	You must not offer the blood of my sacrifices together with anything that contains yeast, and the fat from the offerings presented at my festival must not be left until morning.
002	EXO	023	019	Bring the best firstfruits of your crops to the house of the Lord your God. Don't cook a young goat in its mother's milk.
