002	EXO	025	011	Cover it with pure gold on the inside and the outside, and make a gold trim to go around it.
002	EXO	025	012	Cast four gold rings and attach them to its four feet, two on one side and two on the other.
002	EXO	025	013	Make poles of acacia wood and cover them with gold.
002	EXO	025	014	Place the poles into the rings on the sides of the Ark, so it can be carried.
002	EXO	025	015	The poles are to stay in the rings of the Ark; don't take them out.
002	EXO	025	016	Place inside the Ark the Testimony which I'm going to give you.
002	EXO	025	017	You are to make an atonement cover of pure gold, two and a half cubits long by a cubit and a half wide.
002	EXO	025	018	Make two cherubim of hammered gold for the ends of the atonement cover,
002	EXO	025	019	and put one cherub on each end. All of this is to be made from one piece of gold.
002	EXO	025	020	The cherubim are to be designed with spread wings pointing upward, covering the atonement cover. The cherubim are to be placed facing each another, looking down towards the atonement cover.
002	EXO	025	021	Place the atonement cover on top of the Ark, and put the Testimony that I'm going to give you inside the Ark.
002	EXO	025	022	I will meet with you there as arranged above the atonement cover, between the two cherubim that stand over the Ark of the Testimony, and I will talk with you about all the commands I will give the Israelites.
002	EXO	025	023	Then you are to make a table of acacia wood two cubits long by a cubit wide by a cubit and a half high.
002	EXO	025	024	Cover it with pure gold and make a gold trim to go around it.
002	EXO	025	025	Make a border around it the width of a hand and put a gold trim on the border.
002	EXO	025	026	Make four gold rings for the table and attach them to the four corners of the table by the legs.
002	EXO	025	027	The rings are to be close to the border to hold the poles used to carry the table.
002	EXO	025	028	Make the poles of acacia wood for carrying the table and cover them with gold.
002	EXO	025	029	Make plates and dishes for the table, as well as pitchers and bowls for pouring out drink offerings. Make all of them out of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	030	Place the Bread of the Presence on the table so it is always in my presence.
002	EXO	025	031	Make a lampstand of pure, hammered gold. The whole of it is to be made of one piece—its base, shaft, cups, buds, and flowers.
002	EXO	025	032	It is to have six branches coming out of the sides of the lampstand, three on each side.
002	EXO	025	033	Have three cups shaped like almond flowers on the first branch, each with buds and petals, three on the next branch. Each of six branches that come out will have three cups shaped like almond flowers, all complete with buds and petals.
002	EXO	025	034	On the main shaft of the lampstand make four cups shaped like almond flowers, complete with buds and petals.
002	EXO	025	035	On the six branches that come out from the lampstand, place a bud under the first pair of branches, a bud under the second pair, and a bud under the third pair.
002	EXO	025	036	The buds and branches are to be made with the lampstand as one piece, hammered out of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	037	Make seven lamps and place them on the lampstand so they can light up the area in front of it.
002	EXO	025	038	The wick tongs and their trays are to be made of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	039	The lampstand and all these utensils will require a talent of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	040	Be sure to make everything according to the design you were shown on the mountain.”
002	EXO	026	001	Make ten curtains for the Tabernacle of finely-spun linen, using blue, purple, and crimson threads. Have them embroidered with cherubim by someone who is skilled.
002	EXO	026	002	Each curtain is to measure twenty-eight cubits long by four cubits wide, and all the curtains are to be the same size.
002	EXO	026	003	Join five of the curtains together, and then do the same to the other five.
002	EXO	026	004	Use blue material to make loops on the edge of the last curtain of both sets.
002	EXO	026	005	Make fifty loops on one curtain and fifty loops on the last curtain of the second set, lining up the loops with each other.
002	EXO	026	006	Then make fifty gold clips and join the curtains together with the clips, so that the Tabernacle will be a single structure.
002	EXO	026	007	Make eleven curtains of goat hair as a tent to cover the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	008	Each of the eleven curtains is to be the same size—thirty cubits long by four cubits wide.
002	EXO	026	009	Join five of the curtains together as one set and the other six as another set. Then fold the sixth curtain in two at the front of the tent.
002	EXO	026	010	Make fifty loops on the edge of the last curtain in the first set, and fifty loops along the edge of the last curtain in the second set.
002	EXO	026	011	Make fifty bronze clips and put them in the loops to join the tent together as a single cover.
002	EXO	026	012	The extra half-curtain of this tent covering will be left to hang over the back of the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	013	The tent curtains will be a cubit longer on every side, and the extra length will hang over the sides of the Tabernacle so it is all covered.
002	EXO	026	014	Make a covering for the goat hair tent from tanned ram skins, and place an extra covering of fine leather over that.
002	EXO	026	015	Make an upright framework of acacia wood for the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	016	Each frame is to be ten cubits long by one and a half cubits wide.
002	EXO	026	017	Each frame will have two pegs so the frames can be connected to each other. Make all the frames of the Tabernacle like this.
002	EXO	026	018	Make twenty frames for the south side of the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	019	Make forty silver stands as supports for the twenty frames using two stands per frame, one under every frame peg.
002	EXO	026	020	Similarly for the north side of the Tabernacle, make twenty frames
002	EXO	026	021	and forty silver stands, two stands per frame.
002	EXO	026	022	Make six frames for the back (west side) of the Tabernacle,
002	EXO	026	023	along with two frames for its two back corners.
002	EXO	026	024	Join these corner frames at the bottom and at the top near to the first ring. This is how you are to make the two corner frames.
002	EXO	026	025	In total there will be eight frames and sixteen silver stands, two under each frame.
002	EXO	026	026	Make five crossbars of acacia wood to hold together the frames on the south side of the Tabernacle,
002	EXO	026	027	five for those on the north, and five for those at the back of the Tabernacle, to the west.
002	EXO	026	028	The central crossbar which is placed halfway up the frames will run from one end to the other.
002	EXO	026	029	Cover the frames with gold, and make gold rings to hold the crossbars in place. Cover the crossbars with gold too.
002	EXO	026	030	Assemble the Tabernacle following the design you were shown on the mountain.
002	EXO	026	031	Make a veil out of blue, purple, and crimson thread, and finely-spun linen, embroidered with cherubim by someone who is skilled.
002	EXO	026	032	Using gold hooks hang it from four posts of acacia wood covered with gold, held up by four silver stands.
002	EXO	026	033	Place the veil under the clips and take the Ark of the Testimony inside behind the veil. The veil will separate the Holy Place from the Most Holy Place.
002	EXO	026	034	Put the atonement cover on the Ark of the Testimony in the Most Holy Place.
002	EXO	026	035	Place the table outside the veil on the north side of the Tabernacle and put the lampstand opposite it on the south side.
002	EXO	026	036	Make a screen for the entrance to the tent using blue, purple, and crimson thread, and finely-spun linen. Have it embroidered.
002	EXO	026	037	Make five posts of acacia wood with gold hooks to hang the screen, and cast five bronze stands to hold them.
002	EXO	027	001	Make an altar of acacia wood. It is to be square and measure five cubits long by five cubits wide by three cubits high.
002	EXO	027	002	Make horns for each of its corners, all one piece with the altar, and cover the whole altar with bronze.
002	EXO	027	003	Make all its utensils of bronze: buckets for removing ashes, shovels, sprinkling bowls, meat forks, and firepans.
002	EXO	027	004	Make a bronze mesh grate for it with a bronze ring on each of its corners.
002	EXO	027	005	Put the grate under the ledge of the altar, so that the mesh comes halfway down the altar.
002	EXO	027	006	Make poles of acacia wood for the altar and cover them with bronze.
002	EXO	027	007	The poles are to be placed in the rings so that the poles are on either side of the altar when it is carried.
002	EXO	027	008	Make the altar hollow, using boards, just as you were shown on the mountain.
002	EXO	027	009	Make a courtyard for the Tabernacle. For the south side of the courtyard make curtains of finely-spun linen, a hundred cubits long on one side,
002	EXO	027	010	with twenty posts and twenty bronze stands, with silver hooks and bands on the posts.
002	EXO	027	011	Similarly there are to be curtains placed on the north side in an identical arrangement.
002	EXO	027	012	The curtains for the west side of the courtyard are to be fifty cubits wide, with ten posts and ten stands.
002	EXO	027	013	The east side of the courtyard that faces the sunrise is to be fifty cubits wide.
002	EXO	027	014	Make the curtains on one side fifteen cubits long, with three posts and three stands,
002	EXO	027	015	and the curtains on the other side just the same.
002	EXO	027	016	The entrance to the courtyard is to be twenty cubits wide, with a curtain embroidered with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and finely-spun linen, held up by four posts and four stands.
002	EXO	027	017	All the posts around the courtyard are to have silver bands, silver hooks, and bronze stands.
002	EXO	027	018	The whole courtyard is to be a hundred cubits long and fifty cubits wide, with curtains made of finely-spun linen five cubits high, and with bronze stands.
002	EXO	027	019	All the rest of the equipment used in the Tabernacle, including its tent pegs and those for the courtyard, are to be made of bronze.
002	EXO	027	020	You are to order the Israelites to bring you pure, hand-pressed olive oil for the lamps so they can go on burning, giving light.
002	EXO	027	021	In the Tent of Meeting, outside the veil in front of the Testimony, Aaron and his sons are to keep the lamps burning in the Lord's presence from evening until morning. This requirement is to be observed by the Israelites for all generations.
002	EXO	028	001	Have your brother Aaron come to you, along with his sons Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar. They of all the Israelites are to serve me as priests.
002	EXO	028	002	You are to have holy clothing made for your brother Aaron to make him look splendid and dignified.
002	EXO	028	003	You are to give instructions to all the skilful workers, to those who have received from me their abilities, as to how to make clothing for Aaron's dedication, so that he can serve me as priest.
002	EXO	028	004	These are the clothes for them to make: a breastpiece, an ephod, a robe, a pleated tunic, a turban, and a sash. These are the holy clothes they shall make for your brother Aaron and his sons so that they can serve me as priests.
002	EXO	028	005	The workers are to use gold thread, together with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and finely-spun linen.
002	EXO	028	006	They are to make the ephod of finely-woven linen embroidered with gold, and with blue, purple, and crimson thread, skillfully worked.
002	EXO	028	007	Two shoulder pieces are to be attached to the front and back pieces.
002	EXO	028	008	The waistband of the ephod is to be one piece made in the same way, using gold thread, with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and with finely-woven linen.
002	EXO	028	009	Engrave on two onyx stones the names of the Israelite tribes,
002	EXO	028	010	six names on one stone and six on the other, in birth order.
002	EXO	028	011	Engrave the names on the two stones the same way a jeweler engraves a personal seal. Then place the stones in ornamental gold settings.
002	EXO	028	012	Attach both stones to the shoulder pieces of the ephod as reminders for the Israelite tribes. Aaron is to wear their names on his two shoulders to remind the Israelites that he represents them when he goes in to the Lord's presence.
002	EXO	028	013	Make ornamental gold settings
002	EXO	028	014	and two braided chains of pure gold, and fasten these chains to the settings.
002	EXO	028	015	You are also to make a breastpiece for decisions in the same skilful way as the ephod, to be used in determining the Lord's will. Make it using gold thread, with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and with finely-woven linen.
002	EXO	028	016	It has to be square when folded, measuring around nine inches in length and width.
002	EXO	028	017	Attach an arrangement of precious stones in four rows as follows. In the first row carnelian, peridot, and emerald.
002	EXO	028	018	In the second row turquoise, lapis lazuli, and sardonyx.
002	EXO	028	019	In the third row jacinth, agate, and amethyst.
002	EXO	028	020	In the fourth row topaz, beryl, and jasper. Place these stones in ornamental gold settings.
002	EXO	028	021	Each of the twelve stones will be engraved like a personal seal with the name of one of the twelve Israelite tribes and will represent them.
002	EXO	028	022	Make cords of braided chains from pure gold to attach the breastpiece.
002	EXO	028	023	Make two gold rings and fasten them to the two top corners of the breastpiece.
002	EXO	028	024	Attach the two gold chains to the two gold rings on the corners of the breastpiece,
002	EXO	028	025	and then fasten the opposite ends of the two chains to the ornamental gold settings on the shoulder pieces of the front side of the ephod.
002	EXO	028	026	Make two more gold rings and attach them to the two lower corners of the breastpiece, on the inside edge next to the ephod.
002	EXO	028	027	Make two more gold rings and attach them to the bottom of the two shoulder pieces of the front side of the ephod, near where it joins its woven waistband.
002	EXO	028	028	Tie the rings of the breastpiece to the rings of the ephod with a cord of blue thread, so that the breastpiece won't come loose from the ephod.
002	EXO	028	029	Like this, whenever Aaron enters the Holy Place, he will wear the names of the Israelite tribes over his heart on the breastpiece, as a constant reminder before the Lord.
002	EXO	028	030	Place the Urim and Thummim in the breastpiece of decision, so that they too will be over Aaron's heart whenever he comes into the Lord's presence. Aaron will continually carry the means of gaining decisions over his heart before the Lord.
002	EXO	028	031	Make the robe that goes with the ephod exclusively from blue cloth,
002	EXO	028	032	with an opening in the middle at the top. Stitch a woven collar around the opening to strengthen it so it won't tear.
002	EXO	028	033	Make pomegranates using blue, purple, and crimson thread and attach them all the way around its hem, with gold bells between them,
002	EXO	028	034	having the gold bells and the pomegranates alternate.
002	EXO	028	035	Aaron is to wear the robe whenever he serves, and the sound it makes will be heard when he enters or leaves the sanctuary as he goes into the Lord's presence, so that he won't die.
002	EXO	028	036	Make a plate of pure gold and engrave on it like a seal, “Holy to the Lord.”
002	EXO	028	037	Attach it to the front of the turban using a blue cord.
002	EXO	028	038	Aaron will wear it on his forehead, so that he may take responsibility for the guilt of the offerings the Israelites make, and this applies to all their holy gifts. It must always remain on his forehead in order that the people are accepted in the Lord's presence.
002	EXO	028	039	Weave the tunic with finely-spun linen and make the turban of the same material, and also make a sash and have it embroidered.
002	EXO	028	040	Make tunics, sashes, and headdresses for Aaron's sons, so that they will look splendid and dignified.
002	EXO	028	041	Put these clothes on your brother Aaron and his sons and then anoint them and ordain them. Dedicate them so that they can serve me as priests.
002	EXO	028	042	Make linen undershorts to cover their bare bodies, reaching from waist to thigh.
002	EXO	028	043	Aaron and his sons are to wear them when they enter the Tent of Meeting or when they approach the altar to serve in the Holy Place, so that they will not bring guilt on themselves and die. This is a law for Aaron and his descendants forever.
002	EXO	029	001	Now this is how you are to proceed to dedicate them to serve me as priests. Take a young bull and two rams with no defects.
002	EXO	029	002	Then using the best wheat flour, make the following without yeast: bread, cakes mixed with olive oil, and wafers sprinkled with olive oil.
002	EXO	029	003	Put them all in a basket, and bring them as an offering, along with the bull and the two rams.
002	EXO	029	004	Then bring Aaron and his sons to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting, and wash them with water.
002	EXO	029	005	Take the clothes and put them on Aaron: the tunic, the robe of the ephod, the ephod itself, and the breastpiece. Tie the ephod on him with its waistband.
002	EXO	029	006	Wrap the turban on his head and attach the holy crown to the turban.
002	EXO	029	007	Then use the anointing oil to anoint him by pouring it over his head.
002	EXO	029	008	Then have his sons come and put the tunics on them.
002	EXO	029	009	Tie the sashes around Aaron and his sons and put headdresses on them. The priesthood belongs to them forever. This is how you are to ordain Aaron and his sons.
002	EXO	029	010	Take the bull to the front of the Tent of Meeting, and Aaron and his sons are to place their hands on its head.
002	EXO	029	011	Then slaughter the bull in the Lord's presence at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
002	EXO	029	012	Take some of the bull's blood and smear it on the horns of the altar with your finger. Then pour out the rest of the blood at the base of the altar.
002	EXO	029	013	Take all the fat that covers the intestines, the best parts of the liver, and the two kidneys with their fat, and burn them on the altar.
002	EXO	029	014	But burn the bull's meat, its hide, and its excrement outside the camp—it is an offering for sin.
002	EXO	029	015	Next have Aaron and his sons place their hands on the head of one of the rams.
002	EXO	029	016	Slaughter the ram, take its blood, and splash it all around the altar.
002	EXO	029	017	Cut the ram in pieces, wash the intestines and legs, and put them with the other pieces and the head.
002	EXO	029	018	Then burn all of the ram on the altar. It is a burnt offering to the Lord to be accepted by him.
002	EXO	029	019	Then have Aaron and his sons place their hands on the head of the other ram.
002	EXO	029	020	Slaughter the ram, and put some of its blood on the right earlobes of Aaron and his sons, and on the thumbs of their right hands, and on the big toes of their right feet. Splash the rest of its blood all around the altar.
002	EXO	029	021	Take some of the blood from the altar and some of the anointing oil and sprinkle it on Aaron and his clothes, and on his sons and their clothes. Then he and his clothes will be made holy, likewise his sons and their clothes.
002	EXO	029	022	Take the fat from the ram, including the fat of its broad tail, the fat covering the intestines, the best parts of the liver, the two kidneys with their fat, as well as the right thigh (because this is a ram for ordination).
002	EXO	029	023	Also take one loaf of bread, one cake of bread made with olive oil, and one wafer from the basket of bread made without yeast that is in the Lord's presence.
002	EXO	029	024	Give all of them to Aaron and his sons to wave before the Lord as a wave offering.
002	EXO	029	025	Then take the different breads back and burn them on the altar on top of the burnt offering to the Lord to be accepted by him.
002	EXO	029	026	Take the breast of the ram of Aaron's ordination and wave it before the Lord as a wave offering. This is the part you can keep.
002	EXO	029	027	Set apart for Aaron and his sons the breast of the wave offering and the thigh of the offering that is lifted up, both taken from the ram of ordination.
002	EXO	029	028	From now on whenever the Israelites lift up peace offerings to the Lord, these parts will belong to Aaron and his sons forever as a regular share from the Israelites.
002	EXO	029	029	The holy garments that Aaron has will be passed down to his descendants, so they can wear them when they're anointed and ordained.
002	EXO	029	030	The descendant who succeeds him as priest and enters the Tent of Meeting to serve in the Holy Place must wear them for the seven days of his ordination.
002	EXO	029	031	Take the ram of ordination and boil its meat in a holy place.
002	EXO	029	032	Aaron and his sons are to eat the ram's meat, and the bread that is in the basket, at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
002	EXO	029	033	They are to eat the meat and the bread that were part of the offerings that symbolized the forgiveness required for their ordination and dedication. No one else may eat them, because they are holy.
002	EXO	029	034	If any of the meat of ordination or any bread remains until the morning, burn what's left. It must not be eaten, because it's holy.
002	EXO	029	035	This is the process you are to follow for Aaron and his sons, observing all the instructions I have given you. It will take seven days to ordain them.
002	EXO	029	036	Every day you are to sacrifice a bull as a sin offering for forgiveness. When you do this the altar needs to be purified. Anoint it to make it holy.
002	EXO	029	037	For seven days you shall purify the altar and consecrate it. Then the altar will become completely holy, and everything that touches the altar will become holy.
002	EXO	029	038	You are to offer two lambs that are a year old on the altar, daily and continually.
002	EXO	029	039	In the morning offer one lamb, and offer the other one in the evening before it gets dark.
002	EXO	029	040	With the first lamb also offer a tenth of an ephah of best quality flour, mixed with a quarter of a hin of olive oil, and a drink offering of a quarter of a hin of wine.
002	EXO	029	041	Then offer the second lamb in the evening, with the same grain and drink offerings as in the morning, a burnt offering to the Lord and accepted by him.
002	EXO	029	042	These burnt offerings will be made continually for all generations at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting in the Lord's presence. I will meet you there to speak with you.
002	EXO	029	043	I will meet with the Israelites there, and that place will be made holy by my glory.
002	EXO	029	044	In this way I will dedicate the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and I will dedicate Aaron and his sons to serve me as priests.
002	EXO	029	045	Then I will live with the Israelites and be their God.
002	EXO	029	046	They will know that I am the Lord their God, who led them out of Egypt, so that I could live with them. I am the Lord their God.
002	EXO	030	001	“Make from acacia wood an altar for burning incense.
002	EXO	030	002	It shall be square, measuring a cubit by a cubit, by two cubits high, with horns on its corners that are all one piece with the altar.
002	EXO	030	003	Cover its top, its side, and its horns with pure gold, and make a gold trim to go all around it.
002	EXO	030	004	On two of the altar's sides make two gold rings and attach them below the trim to hold the poles that carry it.
002	EXO	030	005	Make the poles of acacia wood and cover them with gold.
002	EXO	030	006	Put the altar in front of the veil that hangs before the Ark of the Testimony and the atonement cover that is over the Testimony where I will meet with you.
002	EXO	030	007	Aaron is to burn fragrant incense on the altar every morning when he takes care of the lamps.
002	EXO	030	008	When he lights the lamps in the evening he must burn incense again so that incense will always be burned in the Lord's presence for generations to come.
002	EXO	030	009	Don't offer on this altar any unapproved incense or any burnt offering or grain offering, and do not pour out a drink offering upon it.
002	EXO	030	010	Once a year Aaron must perform the atonement ritual by placing blood on the horns of the altar from the sin offering for atonement. This yearly atonement ritual must be carried out for generations to come. This is the Lord's holy altar.”
002	EXO	030	011	The Lord told Moses,
002	EXO	030	012	“When you take a census of the Israelites, each man must pay the Lord to buy back his life when he's counted. Then they won't suffer from the plague when they're counted.
002	EXO	030	013	Each one who crosses over to those counted must give a half shekel (using the sanctuary shekel standard, which weighs twenty gerahs). This half shekel is an offering to the Lord.
002	EXO	030	014	This offering to the Lord is required from everyone twenty years old and more.
002	EXO	030	015	When you give this offering to buy back your lives the rich are not to give more than a half shekel and the poor are not to give less.
002	EXO	030	016	Take this money paid by the Israelites and use it for the expenses involved in the services of the Tent of Meeting. It will serve as a reminder for the Israelites to buy back your lives in the presence of the Lord.”
002	EXO	030	017	The Lord told Moses,
002	EXO	030	018	“Make a bronze basin with a bronze stand for washing. Place it between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and put water in it.
002	EXO	030	019	Aaron and his sons will use it to wash their hands and feet.
002	EXO	030	020	Whenever they enter the Tent of Meeting, they are to wash with water so that they will not die. When they approach the altar to present burnt offerings to the Lord,
002	EXO	030	021	they must also wash so that they will not die. This requirement is to be observed by them and their descendants for all generations.”
002	EXO	030	022	The Lord told Moses,
002	EXO	030	023	“Take the best quality spices: 500 shekels of liquid myrrh, 250 shekels of sweet-smelling cinnamon, 250 shekels of aromatic reed,
002	EXO	030	024	500 shekels of cassia (weights using the sanctuary shekel standard), and a hin of olive oil.
002	EXO	030	025	Mix these together into holy anointing oil, an aromatic blend like the product of an expert perfumer. Use it as holy anointing oil.
002	EXO	030	026	Use it to anoint the Tent of Meeting, the Ark of the Testimony,
002	EXO	030	027	the table and all its equipment, the lampstand and its equipment, the altar of incense,
002	EXO	030	028	the altar of burnt offering and all its utensils, and the basin plus its stand.
002	EXO	030	029	Dedicate them so that they will be especially holy. Whatever touches them will become holy.
002	EXO	030	030	Anoint Aaron and his sons too and dedicate them to serve as priests for me.
002	EXO	030	031	Tell the Israelites, ‘This is to be my holy anointing oil for all generations to come.
002	EXO	030	032	Don't use it on ordinary people and don't make anything like it using the same formula. It is holy, and you must treat it as being holy.
002	EXO	030	033	Anyone who mixes anointing oil like it, or puts it on someone other than a priest, will be expelled from their people.’”
002	EXO	030	034	The Lord told Moses, “Take equal amounts of these aromatic spices: balsam resin, onycha, galbanum, and pure frankincense.
002	EXO	030	035	Add some salt and make pure and holy incense blended like the product of an expert perfumer.
002	EXO	030	036	Grind some of it into powder and place it in front of the Ark of the Testimony in the Tent of Meeting, where I will meet with you. It shall be especially holy to you.
002	EXO	030	037	Don't make for yourselves any incense like it using the same formula. You are to consider this incense as holy to the Lord.
002	EXO	030	038	Anyone who makes incense like this for themselves to enjoy will be expelled from their people.”
002	EXO	031	001	The Lord told Moses,
002	EXO	031	002	“I have chosen by name Bezalel, son of Uri, son of Hur, from the tribe of Judah.
002	EXO	031	003	I have filled him with the Spirit of God giving him ability, creativity, and expertise in all kinds of craftsmanship.
002	EXO	031	004	He can produce designs in gold, silver, and bronze,
002	EXO	031	005	he can cut gemstones to place in settings, and he can carve wood. He is a master of every craft.
