002	EXO	037	023	He made seven lamps, as well as wick tongs and their trays of pure gold.
002	EXO	037	024	The lampstand and all these utensils required a talent of pure gold.
002	EXO	037	025	He made the altar for burning incense from acacia wood. It was square, measuring a cubit by a cubit, by two cubits high, with horns on its corners that were all one piece with the altar.
002	EXO	037	026	He covered its top, its side, and its horns with pure gold, and made a gold trim to go all around it.
002	EXO	037	027	He made two gold rings for the altar and attached them below the trim, two on either side, to hold the poles to carry it.
002	EXO	037	028	He made the poles of acacia wood and covered them with gold.
002	EXO	037	029	He made the holy anointing oil and the pure, aromatic incense like the product of an expert perfumer.
002	EXO	038	001	Bezalel made the altar of burnt offering from acacia wood. It was square, and measured five cubits long by five cubits wide by three cubits high.
002	EXO	038	002	He made horns for each of its corners, all one piece with the altar, and covered the whole altar with bronze.
002	EXO	038	003	He made all its utensils: buckets for removing ashes, shovels, sprinkling bowls, meat forks, and firepans. He made all its utensils of bronze.
002	EXO	038	004	He made a bronze mesh grate for the altar and placed it under the ledge of the altar, so that the mesh came halfway down the altar.
002	EXO	038	005	He cast four bronze rings for the four corners of the grate as holders for the poles.
002	EXO	038	006	He made poles of acacia wood for the altar and covered them with bronze.
002	EXO	038	007	He put the poles through the rings on either side of the altar so it could be carried. He made the altar hollow, using boards.
002	EXO	038	008	He made the bronze basin with its stand with bronze from the mirrors of the women who served at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
002	EXO	038	009	Then he made a courtyard. For the south side of the courtyard he made curtains of finely-spun linen, a hundred cubits long on one side,
002	EXO	038	010	with twenty posts and twenty bronze stands, with silver hooks and bands on the posts.
002	EXO	038	011	Similarly he made curtains placed on the north side in an identical arrangement.
002	EXO	038	012	He made curtains for the west side of the courtyard fifty cubits wide, with ten posts and ten stands.
002	EXO	038	013	The east side of the courtyard that faces the sunrise was fifty cubits wide.
002	EXO	038	014	He made the curtains on one side fifteen cubits long, with three posts and three stands,
002	EXO	038	015	and the curtains on the other side just the same.
002	EXO	038	016	All the curtains around the courtyard were of finely-woven linen.
002	EXO	038	017	The stands for the posts were bronze, the hooks and bands were silver, and the tops of the posts were covered with silver. All the posts around the courtyard had silver bands.
002	EXO	038	018	The curtain for the entrance to the courtyard was embroidered with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and finely-spun linen. It was twenty cubits long by five cubits high, the same height as the courtyard curtains.
002	EXO	038	019	It was held up by four posts and four stands. The posts had silver hooks, tops, and bands.
002	EXO	038	020	All the tent pegs for the Tabernacle and for the surrounding courtyard were made of bronze.
002	EXO	038	021	The following is what was used for the Tabernacle, the Tabernacle of the Testimony, recorded at Moses' direction by the Levites under the supervision of Ithamar, son of Aaron the priest.
002	EXO	038	022	Bezalel, son of Uri, son of Hur, from the tribe of Judah, made everything that the Lord had ordered Moses to make.
002	EXO	038	023	He was assisted by Oholiab, son of Ahisamach, from the tribe of Dan, an engraver, designer, and embroiderer using blue, purple, and crimson thread and finely-woven linen.
002	EXO	038	024	The total amount of gold from the offering that was used for the work on the sanctuary was 29 talents and 730 shekels (using the sanctuary shekel standard).
002	EXO	038	025	The total amount of silver from those who had been counted in the census was 100 talents and 1,775 shekels (using the sanctuary shekel standard).
002	EXO	038	026	This represents a beka per person, or half a shekel (using the sanctuary shekel standard) from everyone twenty years of age or older who had been censused, a total of 603,550 men.
002	EXO	038	027	The hundred talents of silver were used to cast the sanctuary stands and the curtain stands, 100 bases from the 100 talents, or one talent per base.
002	EXO	038	028	Bezalel used the 1,775 shekels of silver to make the hooks for the posts, cover their tops, and make bands for them.
002	EXO	038	029	The total amount of bronze from the offering was 70 talents and 2,400 shekels.
002	EXO	038	030	Bezalel used it to make the stands for the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, the bronze altar and its bronze grate, all the utensils for the altar,
002	EXO	038	031	the stands for the courtyard and its entrance, and all the tent pegs for the Tabernacle and the courtyard.
002	EXO	039	001	They made woven clothing from blue, purple, and crimson thread for serving in the sanctuary. They also made holy garments for Aaron, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	002	They made the ephod of finely-woven linen embroidered with gold, and with blue, purple, and crimson thread.
002	EXO	039	003	They hammered out thin sheets of gold and cut threads from them to weave in with the blue, purple, and scarlet thread, together with fine linen, all skillfully worked.
002	EXO	039	004	Two shoulder pieces were attached to the front and back pieces.
002	EXO	039	005	The waistband of the ephod was one piece made in the same way, using gold thread, with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and with finely-woven linen, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	006	They placed the onyx stones in ornamental gold settings, engraved with the names of the Israelite tribes in the same way a jeweler engraves a personal seal.
002	EXO	039	007	They attached both stones to the shoulder pieces of the ephod as reminders for the Israelite tribes, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	008	They also made a breastpiece for decisions in the same skilful way as the ephod, to be used in determining the Lord's will. They made it using gold thread, with blue, purple, and crimson thread, and with finely-woven linen.
002	EXO	039	009	It was square when folded, measuring around nine inches in length and width.
002	EXO	039	010	They attached an arrangement of precious stones in four rows as follows. In the first row carnelian, peridot, and emerald.
002	EXO	039	011	In the second row turquoise, lapis lazuli, and sardonyx.
002	EXO	039	012	In the third row jacinth, agate, and amethyst.
002	EXO	039	013	In the fourth row topaz, beryl, and jasper. They were all placed in ornamental gold settings.
002	EXO	039	014	Each of the twelve stones were engraved like a personal seal with the name of one of the twelve Israelites tribes and represented them.
002	EXO	039	015	They made cords of braided chains from pure gold to attach the breastpiece.
002	EXO	039	016	They made two gold settings and two gold rings and fastened the rings to the two top corners of the breastpiece.
002	EXO	039	017	They attached the two gold chains to the two gold rings on the corners of the breastpiece,
002	EXO	039	018	and then fastened the opposite ends of the two chains to the ornamental gold settings on the shoulder pieces of the front side of the ephod.
002	EXO	039	019	They made two more gold rings and attached them to the two lower corners of the breastpiece, on the inside edge next to the ephod.
002	EXO	039	020	They made two more gold rings and attached them to the bottom of the two shoulder pieces of the front side of the ephod, near where it joins its woven waistband.
002	EXO	039	021	They tied the rings of the breastpiece to the rings of the ephod with a cord of blue thread, so that the breastpiece wouldn't come loose from the ephod, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	022	They made the robe that goes with the ephod exclusively from woven blue cloth,
002	EXO	039	023	with an opening in the middle at the top. They stitched a woven collar around the opening to strengthen it so it wouldn't tear.
002	EXO	039	024	They made pomegranates using blue, purple, and crimson thread and finely-woven linen and attached them all the way around its hem.
002	EXO	039	025	They made pure gold bells and attached them between the pomegranates all the way around its hem,
002	EXO	039	026	having the bells and the pomegranates alternate. The robe was to be used for priestly service, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	027	They made tunics with finely-spun linen made by a weaver for Aaron and his sons.
002	EXO	039	028	They also made turbans, headdresses, and headbands of fine linen, and finely-woven linen undershorts,
002	EXO	039	029	as well as sashes of finely-woven linen embroidered with blue, purple, and crimson thread, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	030	They made the plate of the holy crown of pure gold and wrote on it, engraved like a seal, “Holy to the Lord.”
002	EXO	039	031	They tied a blue cord to it to attach it to the front of the turban, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	032	So all the work for the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting, was finished. The Israelites did everything as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	033	Then they presented the Tabernacle to Moses: the tent with all its furniture, its clips, its frames, its crossbars, and its posts and stands;
002	EXO	039	034	the covering of tanned ram skins, the covering of fine leather, and the veil;
002	EXO	039	035	the Ark of the Testimony with its poles and the atonement cover;
002	EXO	039	036	the table with all its equipment and the Bread of the Presence;
002	EXO	039	037	the pure gold lampstand with its lamps placed in a row, and all its equipment, as well as the olive oil for the lamps;
002	EXO	039	038	the gold altar, the anointing oil, the aromatic incense, and the screen for the tent's entrance;
002	EXO	039	039	the bronze altar with its bronze grate, its poles, and all its utensils; the basin plus its stand;
002	EXO	039	040	the curtains of the courtyard and its posts and stands; the curtain for the courtyard entrance, its ropes and tent pegs, and all the equipment for the services of the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting;
002	EXO	039	041	and the woven garments for serving in the sanctuary, the holy clothes for Aaron the priest and for his sons to serve as priests.
002	EXO	039	042	The Israelites did all the work that the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	039	043	Moses inspected all the work and made sure they had done it as the Lord had ordered. Then Moses blessed them.
002	EXO	040	001	The Lord told Moses,
002	EXO	040	002	“Put up the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting, on the first day of the first month of the year.
002	EXO	040	003	Place the Ark of the Testimony inside it. Make sure the Ark is behind the veil.
002	EXO	040	004	Bring in the table and put on it what's necessary. Bring in the lampstand too, and set up its lamps.
002	EXO	040	005	Place the gold altar of incense in front of the Ark of the Testimony, and put up the screen at the entrance to the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	006	Set up the altar of burnt offering opposite the entrance to the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting.
002	EXO	040	007	Place the basin between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and put water in it.
002	EXO	040	008	Set up the courtyard that's around it, and put up the curtain for the courtyard entrance.
002	EXO	040	009	Use the anointing oil to anoint the Tabernacle and everything in it. Dedicate it and all its furniture to make it holy.
002	EXO	040	010	Anoint the altar of burnt offering and all its utensils. Dedicate the altar and it will be especially holy.
002	EXO	040	011	Anoint and dedicate the basin with its stand.
002	EXO	040	012	Take Aaron and his sons to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting and wash them there with water.
002	EXO	040	013	Then you are to put on Aaron the holy clothes, anoint him, and dedicate him, so that he may serve me as a priest.
002	EXO	040	014	Have his sons come forward and dress them with tunics.
002	EXO	040	015	Anoint them in the same way as you anointed their father, so that they can also serve me as priests. Their anointing makes their line priests forever, for generations to come.”
002	EXO	040	016	Moses carried out all the Lord's instructions.
002	EXO	040	017	The Tabernacle was put up on the first day of the first month of the second year.
002	EXO	040	018	When Moses put up the Tabernacle, he placed its stands, attached its frames, connected its crossbars, and erected its posts.
002	EXO	040	019	Then he spread the tent over the Tabernacle and placed the covering over the tent, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	020	Moses took the Testimony and put it in the Ark. He attached the poles to the Ark, and he placed the atonement cover on the top of the Ark.
002	EXO	040	021	Then he carried the Ark into the Tabernacle. He put up the veil, and made sure the Ark of the Testimony was behind it, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	022	Moses placed the table inside the Tent of Meeting on the north side of the Tabernacle, outside the veil.
002	EXO	040	023	He laid out the bread on it in the presence of the Lord, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	024	He placed the lampstand in the Tent of Meeting opposite the table on the south side of the Tabernacle
002	EXO	040	025	and put up the lamps in the presence of the Lord, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	026	Moses set up the gold altar in the Tent of Meeting, in front of the veil,
002	EXO	040	027	and he burned aromatic incense on it, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	028	Then he put up the screen at the entrance to the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	029	He set up the altar of burnt offering near the entrance to the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting, and presented the burnt offering and the grain offering, as the Lord had ordered him to do.
002	EXO	040	030	He placed the basin between the Tent of Meeting and the altar and put water in it for washing.
002	EXO	040	031	Moses, Aaron, and his sons used it to wash their hands and feet
002	EXO	040	032	They washed whenever they went into the Tent of Meeting or approached the altar, as the Lord had ordered Moses to do.
002	EXO	040	033	Moses set up the courtyard around the Tabernacle and the altar, and he put up the curtain for the courtyard entrance. This marked the end of the work done by Moses.
002	EXO	040	034	Then the cloud covered the Tent of Meeting, and the glory of the Lord filled the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	035	Moses could not enter the Tent of Meeting because the cloud remained on it, and the glory of the Lord filled the Tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	036	Whenever the cloud rose from the Tabernacle, the Israelites would set off again on their journey.
002	EXO	040	037	If the cloud did not rise, they wouldn't set out until it did.
002	EXO	040	038	The cloud of the Lord stayed over the Tabernacle by day, and fire burned inside the cloud by night, so that it could be seen by every Israelite wherever they traveled.
#
# BOOK	003	LEV	Leviticus	Leviticus
003	LEV	001	001	The Lord called Moses and spoke to him from the Tent of Meeting, saying,
003	LEV	001	002	“Go and speak to the Israelites and tell them: When you present an offering to the Lord, you may bring as your offering an animal from the herd of cattle or the flock of sheep or goats.
003	LEV	001	003	If your offering is a burnt offering from a herd of cattle, you must offer a male without any defects. Bring it to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting so it can be accepted before the Lord.
003	LEV	001	004	Put your hand on the head of the burnt offering, so it can be accepted on your behalf to make you right.
003	LEV	001	005	You are to kill the bull in the Lord's presence, and Aaron's sons, the priests, are to take the blood and sprinkle it on all sides of the altar at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	001	006	Then you are to skin the burnt offering and cut it into pieces.
003	LEV	001	007	The sons of Aaron the priest shall start a fire on the altar and put wood on it.
003	LEV	001	008	Then the priests shall carefully place the pieces, including the head and the fat, on the wood burning on the altar.
003	LEV	001	009	You shall wash the insides and legs with water, and the priest shall burn all of it on the altar as a burnt offering, a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	001	010	If your offering is a burnt offering from a flock, either sheep or goats, you must offer a male without any defects.
003	LEV	001	011	You are to kill it on the north side of the altar in the Lord's presence, and Aaron's sons, the priests, are to take the blood and sprinkle it on all sides of the altar.
003	LEV	001	012	Then you are to cut it into pieces, and the priest shall carefully place the pieces, including the head and the fat, on the wood burning on the altar.
003	LEV	001	013	You shall wash the insides and legs with water, and the priest shall burn all of it on the altar as a burnt offering, a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	001	014	If your offering to the Lord is a burnt offering of birds, you are to offer a turtledove or a young pigeon.
003	LEV	001	015	The priest shall take it to the altar, twist off its head, and burn it on the altar. Its blood shall be drained out on the side of the altar.
003	LEV	001	016	He must remove the crop and the feathers, and throw them to the east side of the altar into the ash pile.
003	LEV	001	017	He shall tear it open by its wings, but not completely apart. The priest is to burn it on the altar on the burning wood. It is a burnt offering, a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.”
003	LEV	002	001	“When you bring a grain offering to the Lord, your offering must be of the best flour. Pour olive oil on it and put frankincense on it,
003	LEV	002	002	and take it to Aaron's sons the priests. The priest shall take a handful of the flour and olive oil mixture, as well as all the frankincense, and burn this as a ‘reminder part’ on the altar, a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	002	003	The rest of the grain offering is for Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the offerings given to the Lord as food offerings.
003	LEV	002	004	If your offering is of grain baked in an oven, it must be made from fine flour without using yeast. It can be cakes mixed with olive oil or wafers with olive oil spread on them.
003	LEV	002	005	If your offering is a grain offering cooked on a griddle, it must be made of fine flour mixed with olive oil without using yeast.
003	LEV	002	006	Break it up and pour olive oil over it; it is a grain offering.
003	LEV	002	007	If your offering is a grain offering cooked in a pan, it must be made of fine flour with olive oil.
003	LEV	002	008	Bring to the Lord the grain offering in whatever way it has been prepared. Present it to the priest, who will take it to the altar.
003	LEV	002	009	The priest is to take the ‘reminder part’ from the grain offering and burn it on the altar as a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	002	010	The rest of the grain offering is for Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the food offerings given to the Lord.
003	LEV	002	011	No grain offering that you give to the Lord may be made using yeast. Don't burn any yeast or honey as a food offering to the Lord.
003	LEV	002	012	You may give them to the Lord when you present your offerings of firstfruits, but they must not be offered on the altar to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	002	013	All of your grain offerings are to be seasoned with salt. Don't leave the salt of God's agreement out of your grain offering. Add salt to all of your offerings.
003	LEV	002	014	When you bring a grain offering of firstfruits to the Lord, offer crushed heads of new grain roasted on the fire.
003	LEV	002	015	Put olive oil and frankincense on it; it is a grain offering.
003	LEV	002	016	The priest will burn the ‘reminder part’ of the crushed grain and olive oil, as well as all its frankincense, as a food offering to the Lord.”
003	LEV	003	001	“When you want to give a peace offering and you offer an animal from a herd of cattle, whether male or female, you must present one without any defects before the Lord.
003	LEV	003	002	Put your hand on the head of the offering and kill it at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting. Then Aaron's sons the priests will sprinkle the blood on all sides of the altar.
003	LEV	003	003	From the peace offering you are to bring a food offering to the Lord: all the fat that covers the insides,
003	LEV	003	004	both kidneys with the fat on them by the loins, and the best part of the liver, which you are to remove together with the kidneys.
003	LEV	003	005	Aaron's sons are to burn this on the altar on top of the burnt offering that is on the burning wood, as a food offering, to be accepted by the Lord.
003	LEV	003	006	When you want to give a peace offering and you offer an animal from a flock of sheep or goats, either male or female, you must present one without any defects before the Lord.
003	LEV	003	007	If you are giving a lamb as your offering, you must present it before the Lord.
003	LEV	003	008	Put your hand on the head of the offering and kill it in front of the Tent of Meeting. Then Aaron's sons the priests will sprinkle the blood on all sides of the altar.
003	LEV	003	009	From the peace offering you are to bring a food offering to the Lord made up of its fat: the whole fat tail removed from close to the tailbone, all the fat that covers the insides,
003	LEV	003	010	both kidneys with the fat on them by the loins, and the best part of the liver, which you are to remove together with the kidneys.
003	LEV	003	011	Then the priest is to burn this on the altar as a food offering, a food offering to the Lord.
003	LEV	003	012	If your offering is a goat, you are to present it before the Lord.
003	LEV	003	013	Put your hand on its head and kill it in front of the Tent of Meeting. Then Aaron's sons the priests will sprinkle the blood on all sides of the altar.
003	LEV	003	014	From your offering you are to present a food offering to the Lord made up of all the fat that covers the insides,
003	LEV	003	015	both kidneys with the fat on them by the loins, and the best part of the liver, which you are to remove together with the kidneys.
003	LEV	003	016	Then the priest is to burn this on the altar as a food offering, an offering to the Lord using fire. All the fat is for the Lord.
003	LEV	003	017	You must not eat any fat or any blood. This regulation is for all time and for all future generations everywhere you live.”
003	LEV	004	001	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	004	002	“Tell the Israelites that these are the rules to handle cases of those who sin unintentionally against any of the Lord's commandments and do what is not permitted.
003	LEV	004	003	If it is the high priest who sins and brings guilt on everyone, he must present to the Lord a young bull without defects as a sin offering for his sin.
003	LEV	004	004	He must take the bull to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting before the Lord, put his hand on its head and kill it before the Lord.
003	LEV	004	005	Then the high priest shall take some of the bull's blood into the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	004	006	The high priest shall dip his finger in the blood and sprinkle some of it seven times before the Lord in front of the veil of the sanctuary.
003	LEV	004	007	The priest shall put some of the blood on the horns of the altar of aromatic incense that stands before the Lord in the Tent of Meeting. The rest of the bull's blood he is to pour out at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	004	008	Then he shall remove all the fat from the bull of the sin offering: all the fat that covers the insides,
003	LEV	004	009	both kidneys with the fat on them by the loins, and the best part of the liver, which he is to remove together with the kidneys
003	LEV	004	010	in the same way as the fat is removed from the bull of the peace offering. Then the priest shall burn this on the altar of burnt offering.
003	LEV	004	011	But the skin of the bull, all its flesh, head, legs, insides and waste—
003	LEV	004	012	all the rest of it—he has to take outside the camp to a place that is ceremonially clean, where the ashes are dumped, and he must burn it on a wood fire there on the ash heap.
003	LEV	004	013	If the whole Israelite community goes astray unintentionally, and even though they are unaware of doing what is not permitted by any of the Lord's commandments, they are all still guilty.
003	LEV	004	014	When they realize their sin, then they must bring a young bull as a sin offering and present it before the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	004	015	The elders of Israel are to put their hands on its head and kill it before the Lord.
003	LEV	004	016	Then the high priest shall take some of the bull's blood into the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	004	017	He shall dip his finger in the blood and sprinkle it seven times before the Lord in front of the veil.
003	LEV	004	018	He shall put some of the blood on the horns of the altar that stands before the Lord in the Tent of Meeting. Then he is to pour out the rest of the bull's blood at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	004	019	Then he shall remove all the fat from the bull and burn it on the altar.
003	LEV	004	020	He shall offer this bull in the same way he did for the sin offering. This is how the priest will make them right, and they will be forgiven.
003	LEV	004	021	Then he shall take the bull outside the camp and burn it, just as he burned the bull previously mentioned. It is the sin offering for the whole community.
003	LEV	004	022	If a leader sins unintentionally and does what is not permitted by any of the commandments of the Lord his God, he is guilty.
003	LEV	004	023	When he realizes his sin, he must bring a male goat without defects as his offering.
003	LEV	004	024	He must put his hand on the head of the goat and kill it at the place where the burnt offering is killed before the Lord. It is a sin offering.
003	LEV	004	025	Then the priest is to take some of the blood of the sin offering with his finger and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and pour out the rest of the blood at the bottom of the altar.
003	LEV	004	026	He shall burn all its fat on the altar like the fat of the peace offerings. In this way the priest will make the man's sin right, and he will be forgiven.
003	LEV	004	027	If any other Israelite sins unintentionally and does what is not permitted by any of the commandments of the Lord his God, he is guilty.
003	LEV	004	028	When he realizes his sin, he must bring a female goat without defects as his offering for that sin.
003	LEV	004	029	He must put his hand on the head of the sin offering and kill it at the place of the burnt offering.
003	LEV	004	030	Then the priest is to take some of its blood with his finger and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and pour out the rest of the blood at the bottom of the altar.
003	LEV	004	031	He shall remove all its fat like the fat of the peace offerings and burn it on the altar and it will be accepted by the Lord. In this way the priest will make the man's sin right, and he will be forgiven.
003	LEV	004	032	If he brings a lamb as a sin offering, he is to bring a female without defects.
003	LEV	004	033	He must put his hand on the head of the sin offering and kill it as a sin offering at the place where the burnt offering is killed.
003	LEV	004	034	Then the priest is to take some of its blood with his finger and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and pour out the rest of the blood at the bottom of the altar.
003	LEV	004	035	He shall remove all its fat like the fat of the lamb is removed from the peace offerings and burn it on the altar to be accepted by the Lord. In this way the priest will make the man's sin right, and he will be forgiven.”
003	LEV	005	001	“If you sin by not giving the evidence you have about a legal case, whether you saw something yourself or heard about it, you bear responsibility for your guilt.
003	LEV	005	002	If you touch anything unclean such as the dead body of any unclean wild animal or farm animal or vermin, even if you're unaware of it, you become unclean and guilty.
003	LEV	005	003	If you touch something unclean from someone else who is unclean, even if you're unaware of it, you become guilty.
003	LEV	005	004	If you foolishly swear to do something (whether good or bad, and in whatever way people impulsively swear an oath), even if you're unaware of it being wrong, when you eventually realize it, you are guilty.
003	LEV	005	005	If you become guilty in one of these ways, you must confess your sin,
003	LEV	005	006	and you must take your guilt offering of a female lamb or goat to the Lord as a sin offering for your sin. The priest will make your sin right.
