003	LEV	011	001	The Lord told Moses and Aaron,
003	LEV	011	002	“Give these instructions to the Israelites. These are the animals you are allowed to eat:
003	LEV	011	003	any animal that both has a divided hoof and also chews the cud.
003	LEV	011	004	However, if it either chews the cud, or has a divided hoof, then you may not eat it. These include: the camel, which though it chews the cud doesn't have a divided hoof, so it is unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	005	The rock hyrax, which though it chews the cud doesn't have a divided hoof, so it is unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	006	The hare, which though it chews the cud doesn't have a divided hoof, so it is unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	007	The pig, which though it has a divided hoof doesn't chew the cud, so it is unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	008	You are not to eat their meat or touch their dead bodies. They are unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	009	You are allowed to eat any creature with fins and scales that lives in the water, whether in the sea or in fresh water.
003	LEV	011	010	But you are not allowed to eat any of the many creatures that don't have fins and scales that live in the water, whether in the sea or in fresh water.
003	LEV	011	011	They are repulsive. You must not eat their meat, and you must treat their dead bodies as repulsive.
003	LEV	011	012	All such water creatures that don't have fins and scales are to be repulsive to you.
003	LEV	011	013	As for the birds, these must not be eaten because they are repulsive: eagle, griffon vulture, bearded vulture,
003	LEV	011	014	buzzard, kite and similar birds of prey,
003	LEV	011	015	any raven or crow,
003	LEV	011	016	tawny owl, long-eared owl, gulls, any kind of hawk,
003	LEV	011	017	little owl, fish owl, eagle owl,
003	LEV	011	018	barn owl, desert owl, Egyptian vulture,
003	LEV	011	019	storks and any kind of heron, hoopoe, and bats.
003	LEV	011	020	All flying insects that crawl are repulsive to you.
003	LEV	011	021	But you can eat the following kinds of flying insects that crawl: those that have jointed legs they use to jump.
003	LEV	011	022	So in this category you can eat any kind of locust, bald locust, cricket, or grasshopper.
003	LEV	011	023	All other flying insects that crawl are repulsive to you,
003	LEV	011	024	and will make you unclean. If you touch their dead bodies you will be unclean until the evening,
003	LEV	011	025	and if you pick up one of their dead bodies you must wash your clothes, and you will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	011	026	Every animal with hooves that are not divided, or that does not chew the cud, is unclean for you. If you touch any of them you will be unclean.
003	LEV	011	027	Any four-legged animal that walks on its paws are unclean for you. If you touch their dead bodies you will be unclean until the evening,
003	LEV	011	028	and if you pick up one of their dead bodies you must wash your clothes, and you will be unclean until the evening. They are unclean for you.
003	LEV	011	029	The following animals that run along the ground are unclean for you: rats, mice, any kind of large lizards,
003	LEV	011	030	geckos, monitor lizards, wall lizards, skinks, and chameleons.
003	LEV	011	031	These animals that run along the ground are unclean for you. If you touch a dead one of them you will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	011	032	Anything that one of them dies and lands on becomes unclean. Whatever it is—something made of wood, clothing, leather, sackcloth, or any work tool—it must be washed with water and will be unclean until the evening. Then it will become clean.
