003	LEV	011	040	If you eat anything from the dead body you must wash your clothes and you will be unclean until the evening. If you pick up the dead body you must wash your clothes and you will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	011	041	Every animal that crawls along the ground is repulsive—you must not eat it.
003	LEV	011	042	Don't eat any animal that crawls along the ground, whether it moves on its belly or walks on four feet or many feet. All such animals are repulsive.
003	LEV	011	043	Don't defile yourselves by any such crawling animal. Don't make yourselves unclean or defiled by them,
003	LEV	011	044	because I am the Lord your God; so dedicate yourselves and be holy, because I am holy. Don't defile yourselves by any animal that crawls along the ground.
003	LEV	011	045	I am the Lord who led you out of Egypt so that I could be your God. So be holy, because I am holy.
003	LEV	011	046	These are the regulations about animals, birds, everything that lives in the water, and all animals that crawl along the ground.
003	LEV	011	047	You must recognize the difference between unclean and clean, between those animals that can be eaten and those that can't.”
003	LEV	012	001	The Lord told Moses, “Give these instructions to the Israelites.
003	LEV	012	002	Any woman who becomes pregnant and has a boy, she will be unclean for one week, in the same way that she is unclean during her period.
003	LEV	012	003	The boy's foreskin must be circumcised on the eighth day.
003	LEV	012	004	The woman must wait a further thirty-three days for the purification of her bleeding. She is not allowed to touch anything holy, and she is not allowed to enter the sanctuary until her time of purification is finished.
003	LEV	012	005	If a woman has a daughter, she will be unclean for two weeks, in the same way that she is unclean during her menstrual period. The woman must wait a further sixty-six days for the purification of her blood.
003	LEV	012	006	Once the time of purification is finished for either a son or a daughter, the woman must bring a year-old lamb as a burnt offering and a young pigeon or turtledove as a purification offering. She is to bring her offerings to the priest at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	012	007	The priest will then present them to the Lord to purify her so she will be clean from her bleeding. These are the regulations for a woman after she's had a son or a daughter.
003	LEV	012	008	If a woman can't afford to bring a lamb, she is to bring two turtledoves or two young pigeons. One is for the burnt offering and the other for the purification offering. The priest will offer them to purify her, and she will be clean.”
003	LEV	013	001	The Lord told Moses and Aaron,
003	LEV	013	002	“Anyone who has a swelling, a rash, or a spot on the skin that may be an infectious skin disease must be taken to Aaron the priest or to one of his descendants.
003	LEV	013	003	The priest will inspect whatever is on the skin. If the hair there has turned white and if the issue seems to be more than something on the surface, it is a serious skin disease, and the priest who inspects it will declare the person unclean.
003	LEV	013	004	But if the spot is only a white discoloration and doesn't seem to be more than superficial, and if the hair on the spot has not turned white, the priest will place the person in isolation for seven days.
003	LEV	013	005	On the seventh day the priest will conduct another inspection, and if he discovers that the spot hasn't changed and hasn't spread on the skin, the priest must place the person in isolation for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	006	On the seventh day after this the priest will inspect it again. If the spot has faded and has not spread on the skin, the priest will declare the person clean since it was a rash. They must wash their clothes and will be clean.
003	LEV	013	007	However, if the rash does spread after the person has been inspected by the priest and has been declared clean, the person must go back to be inspected again.
003	LEV	013	008	If the priest discovers that the rash has spread, he must declare the person unclean because it is certainly a skin disease.
003	LEV	013	009	Anyone who develops an infectious skin disease must be taken to the priest.
003	LEV	013	010	The priest will inspect them, and if there is a white swelling on the skin and the hair there has turned white, and there is an open wound in the swelling,
003	LEV	013	011	it is a serious skin disease and the priest must declare them unclean. He doesn't need to place the person in isolation because they are unclean.
003	LEV	013	012	However, if the skin disease affects all their skin so that it covers their skin from head to toe, everywhere the priest can see,
003	LEV	013	013	the priest shall inspect them, and if the disease has covered their entire body, he will declare the person clean. As it has all turned white, they are clean.
003	LEV	013	014	But if when someone's inspected an open wound is found, they will be unclean.
003	LEV	013	015	When the priest discovers an open wound, he must declare the person unclean. The open wound is unclean; it is an infectious skin disease.
003	LEV	013	016	But if the open wound heals and becomes white, the person must go back to the priest.
003	LEV	013	017	The priest will inspect them again, and if the wound has turned white, the priest is to declare the person clean; then they are clean.
003	LEV	013	018	When a boil comes up on someone's skin and then it heals,
003	LEV	013	019	and a white swelling or a reddish-white spot appears in its place, they must show themselves to the priest.
003	LEV	013	020	The priest shall inspect it, and if it seems to be more than something on the surface, and if the hair there has turned white, the priest shall declare him unclean. It is a serious skin disease that has infected the boil.
003	LEV	013	021	However, if when the priest inspects it, it doesn't have white hair in it and doesn't seem to be more than superficial, and has faded, the priest is to place the person in isolation for seven days.
003	LEV	013	022	If then the spot has spread further on the skin, the priest will declare them unclean; it is a disease.
003	LEV	013	023	But if the spot stays the same and doesn't spread, it's just the scar from the boil, and the priest will declare them clean.
003	LEV	013	024	If someone has a burn on their skin and the place where it's raw changes into a reddish-white or white spot,
003	LEV	013	025	the priest must inspect it. If the hair in the spot has turned white and the spot seems to be more than something on the surface, it is a serious skin disease that has infected the burn, and the priest who inspects it will declare the person unclean. It is an infectious skin disease.
003	LEV	013	026	However, if when the priest inspects it, it doesn't have white hair in it and doesn't seem to be more than superficial, and has faded, the priest is to place the person in isolation for seven days.
003	LEV	013	027	On the seventh day the priest will inspect the person again. If then the spot has spread further on the skin, the priest will declare them unclean; it is a serious skin disease.
003	LEV	013	028	But if the spot stays the same and hasn't spread on the skin, but has faded, it's the swelling from the burn, and the priest will declare them clean because it's just the scar from the burn.
003	LEV	013	029	If someone, man or woman, has a sore on the head or chin,
003	LEV	013	030	the priest shall inspect it, and if it appears to be more than superficial and the hair in it has become pale and thin, the priest must declare them unclean; it is an infection producing scabs, a serious disease of the head or chin.
003	LEV	013	031	However, if the priest inspects the scabby infection and it doesn't seem to be more than superficial and has no pale hair in it, the priest is to place the person in isolation for seven days.
003	LEV	013	032	On the seventh day the priest will inspect the person again and if the scabby infection has not spread and there is no pale hair in it, and it doesn't seem to be more than superficial,
003	LEV	013	033	then the person must shave themselves except for the scaly area. The priest is to place the person in isolation for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	034	On the seventh day the priest will inspect the scabby infection, and if it has not spread on the skin and doesn't seem to be more than superficial, the priest is to pronounce the person clean. They must wash their clothes and will be clean.
003	LEV	013	035	However, if the scabby infection has spread on the skin after having been declared clean,
003	LEV	013	036	the priest must inspect them, and if the scabby infection has indeed spread on the skin, the priest doesn't need to check for pale hair; the person is unclean.
003	LEV	013	037	But if the priest sees that the scabby infection hasn't changed, and black hair has grown in it, then it has healed. The person is clean, and the priest must declare it.
003	LEV	013	038	If someone, man or woman, has white spots on the skin,
003	LEV	013	039	the priest shall inspect them, and if the spots appear a dull white, it's just a rash that has developed on the skin; the person is clean.
003	LEV	013	040	If a man loses his hair and goes bald, he is still clean.
003	LEV	013	041	If he has a receding hairline and he goes bald on his forehead, he is still clean.
003	LEV	013	042	But if a reddish-white sore appears on his bald head or forehead, it is an infectious disease developing.
003	LEV	013	043	The priest must inspect him, and if the swelling of the sore on his bald head or forehead looks reddish-white like a skin disease,
003	LEV	013	044	then he has an infectious disease; he is unclean. The priest must declare him unclean because of the infection on his head.
003	LEV	013	045	Anyone who has such diseases must wear clothes that are torn and let their hair remain uncombed. They must cover their faces and shout out, ‘Unclean, unclean!’
003	LEV	013	046	They remain unclean as long as the infection lasts. They have to live alone somewhere outside the camp.
003	LEV	013	047	The following regulations relate to any material that becomes affected by mold, such as wool or linen clothing,
003	LEV	013	048	anything woven or knitted made from linen or wool, or anything made of leather:
003	LEV	013	049	If the spot is green or red on the material, whether it's leather, woven, or knitted or some other leather item, then it is infected with mold and must be shown to the priest.
003	LEV	013	050	The priest must inspect the mold and place the item in isolation for seven days.
003	LEV	013	051	On the seventh day the priest shall inspect it again, and if the patch of mold has spread in the material, whether it's leather, woven, or knitted or some other leather item, then it is a harmful mold; the article is unclean, whatever it is being used for.
003	LEV	013	052	The priest is to burn it, whether the affected item is wool or linen or leather. Because the mold is harmful, the article must be burned.
003	LEV	013	053	However, if when the priest inspects it again, the patch of mold has not spread,
003	LEV	013	054	then the priest shall order that the affected item be washed and placed in isolation for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	055	Once it has been washed, the priest is to inspect it again, and if the item with the mold hasn't changed how it looks, it is unclean. Though the mold hasn't spread, you must burn the item, whether the mold damage is on the inside or the outside.
003	LEV	013	056	If the priest inspects it and the patch of mold has faded after it has been washed, he is to cut out the affected part of the material, whether it's leather, woven, or knitted.
003	LEV	013	057	However, if the mold comes back then it is spreading. In that case you must burn the affected item.
003	LEV	013	058	If the mold disappears after washing, then have it washed again, and it will be clean.
003	LEV	013	059	These are the regulations regarding what needs to be done when mold contaminates wool or linen material, whether woven or knitted, or any leather item, as to declaring it clean or unclean.”
003	LEV	014	001	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	014	002	“These are the regulations regarding those who have had a skin disease when having been brought to the priest they are declared clean.
003	LEV	014	003	The priest must go outside the camp and inspect the person. If the skin disease has healed,
003	LEV	014	004	the priest shall have two ceremonially clean birds brought to him, with some cedar wood, crimson thread, and hyssop, on behalf of the person to be made clean.
003	LEV	014	005	The priest will order one of the birds to be killed over a clay pot filled with fresh water.
003	LEV	014	006	He will take the live bird together with the cedar wood, crimson thread, and hyssop, and dip them in the blood of the bird that was killed over the fresh water.
003	LEV	014	007	He will use the blood to sprinkle seven times the person being made clean of the skin disease. Then the priest will declare them clean and let the live bird fly away.
003	LEV	014	008	The one being made clean must wash their clothes, shave off all their hair, and wash themselves with water; then they will be ceremonially clean. After that they can enter the camp, but they must stay outside their tent for seven days.
003	LEV	014	009	On the seventh day they must shave off all their hair: their head, beard, eyebrows, and the rest of their hair. They must wash their clothes and wash themselves with water, and they will be clean.
003	LEV	014	010	On the eighth day they are to bring two male lambs and one female lamb, all a year old and without defects; a grain offering consisting of three-tenths of an ephah of the best flour mixed with olive oil, and one ‘log’ of olive oil.
003	LEV	014	011	The priest who conducts the ceremony will present the person to be made clean to the Lord, along with these offerings, at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	014	012	The priest will take one of the male lambs and present it as a guilt offering, together with the log of olive oil; and he will wave them before the Lord as a wave offering.
003	LEV	014	013	Then he will kill the lamb near the sanctuary where the sin offering and burnt offering are killed. The sin offering and the guilt offering belong to the priest; they are most holy.
003	LEV	014	014	The priest will put some of the blood from the guilt offering on their right earlobe, on their right thumb, and on the big toe of their right foot of the person being made clean.
003	LEV	014	015	The priest will pour some of the log of olive oil into his left palm,
003	LEV	014	016	dip his right index finger in it, and using his finger, sprinkle some of the olive oil seven times before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	017	The priest will then use some of the rest of the olive oil remaining in his palm on the person being made clean, and put it on top of the blood of the guilt offering. This will be on their right earlobe, on their right thumb, and on the big toe of their right foot, on top of the blood of the guilt offering.
003	LEV	014	018	What is left of the olive oil in his palm, the priest will put on the head of the person being made clean and then make them right before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	019	The priest will sacrifice the sin offering to make the person right, so that they are now clean from their uncleanness. After that, the priest will kill the burnt offering
003	LEV	014	020	and offer it on the altar, together with the grain offering, to make them right, and they will be clean.
003	LEV	014	021	But those who are poor and can't afford these offerings must bring one male lamb as a guilt offering to be waved to make them right, as well as a tenth an ephah of the best flour mixed with olive oil for a grain offering, a log of olive oil,
003	LEV	014	022	and two turtledoves or two young pigeons, whichever they can afford. One is to be used as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering.
003	LEV	014	023	On the eighth day they are to take them to the priest at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting before the Lord so they can be made clean.
003	LEV	014	024	The priest will take the lamb for the guilt offering, together with the log of olive oil, and wave them as a wave offering before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	025	After he kills the lamb for the guilt offering, the priest will take some of the blood of the guilt offering and put it on the right earlobe of the one being made clean, on their right thumb, and on the big toe of their right foot.
003	LEV	014	026	Then the priest will pour some of the olive oil into his left palm
003	LEV	014	027	and using his right index finger, will sprinkle some of the oil from his left palm seven times before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	028	The priest shall also put some of the olive oil in his palm on the right earlobe of the person being made clean, on their right thumb, and on the big toe of their right foot, in the same places as the blood of the guilt offering.
003	LEV	014	029	What is left of the olive oil in his palm, the priest will put on the head of the person being made clean and then make them right before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	030	Then they must sacrifice one of the turtledoves or young pigeons, whichever they can afford,
003	LEV	014	031	one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering, along with the grain offering. This is how the priest will make the person right and clean before the Lord.
003	LEV	014	032	These are the regulations for those who have a skin disease and can't afford the usual offerings to make people clean.”
003	LEV	014	033	Then the Lord told Moses and Aaron,
003	LEV	014	034	“When you get to Canaan, the land I'm giving you to own, if I put some mold into a house there and contaminate it,
003	LEV	014	035	the owner of the house must come and tell the priest, ‘It seems my house has something like mold.’
003	LEV	014	036	The priest must order the house to be emptied before he goes in to inspect the mold, so that nothing in the house will be declared unclean. Once that's done, the priest is to go in and inspect the house.
003	LEV	014	037	He will examine the house and see if the mold on the walls is made up of green or red indentations that go under the surface,
003	LEV	014	038	the priest shall go out of the door and seal the house for seven days.
003	LEV	014	039	On the seventh day the priest will return and inspect the house again. If the mold has spread on the walls,
003	LEV	014	040	he will order the affected stones to be removed and disposed of in an unclean area outside the town.
003	LEV	014	041	Then he will order all the plaster inside of the house to be scraped off and dumped in an unclean area outside the town.
003	LEV	014	042	Different stones must be used to replace the ones removed, and new plaster will be needed to replaster the house.
003	LEV	014	043	If the mold returns and affects the house again even after the stones have been removed and the house has been scraped and replastered,
003	LEV	014	044	the priest must come and inspect it. If he sees the mold has spread in the house, it is a harmful mold; the house is unclean.
003	LEV	014	045	It must be demolished, and all its stones, timbers, and plaster must be taken and dumped in an unclean area outside the town.
003	LEV	014	046	Anyone who goes into the house during any time that it is sealed will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	014	047	Anyone who sleeps or eats in the house must wash their clothes.
003	LEV	014	048	However, if when the priest comes and inspects it and finds that the mold hasn't reappeared after the house was replastered, he shall declare the house clean because the mold is gone.
003	LEV	014	049	He will bring two birds, cedar wood, crimson thread, and hyssop to make the house clean.
003	LEV	014	050	He will kill one of the birds over a clay pot filled with fresh water.
003	LEV	014	051	He will dip the live bird, the cedar wood, crimson thread, and hyssop, in the blood of the bird that was killed and the fresh water, and sprinkle the house seven times.
003	LEV	014	052	He will make the house clean with the bird's blood, the fresh water, the live bird, the cedar wood, the hyssop, and the crimson thread.
003	LEV	014	053	Then he will let the live bird fly away outside the town. This is how he will make the house right, and it will be clean.
003	LEV	014	054	These are the regulations for any infectious skin disease, for a scabby infection,
003	LEV	014	055	for mold on clothing and in a house,
003	LEV	014	056	as well as for a swelling, rash, or spot.
003	LEV	014	057	They are used to decide whether something is clean or unclean. These are the regulations regarding skin diseases and mold.”
003	LEV	015	001	The Lord told Moses and Aaron,
003	LEV	015	002	“Tell the Israelites, When any man has a discharge from his genitals, the discharge is unclean.
003	LEV	015	003	The uncleanness comes from his discharge, whether his body allows it to flow out or blocks it. It makes him unclean.
003	LEV	015	004	Any bed the man with the discharge lies on will be unclean, and anything he sits on will be unclean.
003	LEV	015	005	Anyone who touches his bed has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	006	Anyone who sits on whatever the man was sitting on has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	007	Anyone who touches the man's body has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	008	If the man with the discharge spits on anyone who is clean, they have to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	009	Whatever the man sits on when he's riding will be unclean.
003	LEV	015	010	Anyone who touches whatever was under him will be unclean until the evening. Anyone who picks these things up has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	011	If the man with the discharge touches anyone without washing his hands with water first, the person who was touched has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	012	Any clay item touched by the man must be broken, and any wooden item must be washed with water.
003	LEV	015	013	Once the discharge has healed, the man must allocate seven days for his cleaning process, wash his clothes, and wash himself in fresh water, and he will be clean.
003	LEV	015	014	On the eighth day he must take two turtledoves or two young pigeons, come before the Lord at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, and give them to the priest.
003	LEV	015	015	The priest will sacrifice them, one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering. This is how the priest will make the man right before the Lord because of his discharge.
003	LEV	015	016	When a man has a release of semen, he must wash his whole body with water, and he will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	017	Any clothing or leather that the release of semen falls on must be washed with water, and it will remain unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	018	If a man sleeps with a woman and there is a release of semen, both of them must wash with water, and they will remain unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	019	When a woman has a discharge of blood from her body, she will be unclean because of her period for seven days, and anyone who touches her will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	020	Anything she lies or sits on during her period will be unclean,
003	LEV	015	021	and anyone who touches her bed must wash their clothes and wash themselves with water, and will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	022	Anyone who touches what she was sitting on has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	023	Whether it's a bed or something she was sitting on, anyone who touches it will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	024	If a man sleeps with her and the blood from her period touches him, he will be unclean for seven days, and any bed he lies on will be unclean.
003	LEV	015	025	When a woman has a discharge of blood for several days when it's not the time for her period, or if it continues past her period, she will be unclean for the whole time she is bleeding, not just for the days of her period.
003	LEV	015	026	Any bed she lies on or anything she sits on while she has her discharge will be unclean, just as her bed is during her period.
003	LEV	015	027	Anyone who touches them has to wash their clothes, and wash themselves with water, and they will be unclean until the evening.
003	LEV	015	028	Once the woman's discharge has healed, she must allocate seven days for her cleaning process, wash her clothes, and wash herself in fresh water, and she shall be clean.
003	LEV	015	029	On the eighth day she must take two turtledoves or two young pigeons, come before the Lord at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, and give them to the priest.
003	LEV	015	030	The priest will sacrifice them, one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering. This is how the priest will make her right before the Lord because of her discharge.
003	LEV	015	031	This is how you must stop the Israelites from becoming ceremonially unclean, so that they don't die by making my Tabernacle unclean, the place where I live with them.
003	LEV	015	032	These are the regulations regarding a man who has a discharge, a man who has a release of semen that makes him unclean,
003	LEV	015	033	a woman during her period, any male or female who has a discharge, and a man who sleeps with an unclean woman.”
003	LEV	016	001	The Lord spoke to Moses after the death of two of Aaron's sons when they went into the Lord's presence.
003	LEV	016	002	The Lord told Moses: “Warn your brother Aaron not to come into the Most Holy Place whenever he wants, otherwise he'll die. For that's where I appear in the cloud above the atonement cover of the Ark, behind the veil.
003	LEV	016	003	These are the instructions as to how Aaron is to enter the sanctuary. He is to come with a young bull for a sin offering and a ram for a burnt offering.
003	LEV	016	004	He is to be wearing the holy linen tunic, with linen underwear. He has to tie a linen sash around him and put on the linen turban. These are holy clothes. He must wash himself with water before he puts them on.
003	LEV	016	005	From the people of Israel he is to bring two male goats for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering.
003	LEV	016	006	Aaron will present the bull as his own sin offering to make himself and his household right.
003	LEV	016	007	Then he will bring the two goats and present them before the Lord at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
003	LEV	016	008	Aaron will cast lots to choose between the goats, one for the Lord and the other for the scapegoat.
003	LEV	016	009	He will present the goat that was chosen by lot for the Lord and sacrifice it as a sin offering.
003	LEV	016	010	The goat chosen by lot as the scapegoat is to be presented alive before the Lord to make things right by sending it away into the wilderness as the scapegoat.
003	LEV	016	011	Aaron is to present the bull for his sin offering to make things right for himself and his household by killing the bull as his own sin offering.
003	LEV	016	012	Then he will fill up an incense burner with burning coals from the altar that is before the Lord, and with his hands full of finely ground sweet-smelling incense, take them behind the veil.
003	LEV	016	013	In the presence of the Lord he will put the incense on the burning coals, and the smoke from the incense will cover the atonement cover above the Testimony, so that he will not die.
003	LEV	016	014	He will take some of the bull's blood and with his finger sprinkle it on the east side of the atonement cover. He shall also sprinkle some of it with his finger seven times in front of the atonement cover.
003	LEV	016	015	Then Aaron will slaughter the goat for the sin offering for the people and bring its blood behind the veil, and with its blood he must do as he did with the bull's blood. He is to sprinkle it against the atonement cover and in front of it.
003	LEV	016	016	This is how he will set right the Most Holy Place and purify it from the uncleanness of the Israelites, their acts of rebellion, and all their sins. He will do the same for the Tent of Meeting which is in the middle of their camp, surrounded by their unclean lives.
003	LEV	016	017	No one can be in the Tent of Meeting from the time Aaron enters to purify the Most Holy Place until he leaves, after he has made things right for himself, his household, and all the Israelites.
003	LEV	016	018	Then he shall go to the altar that is before the Lord and purify it. He is to take some of the blood from the bull and the goat and put it on all the horns of the altar.
003	LEV	016	019	He is to sprinkle some of the blood on it with his finger seven times to dedicate it and purify it from the uncleanness of the Israelites.
003	LEV	016	020	Once Aaron has finished purifying the Most Holy Place, the Tent of Meeting, and the altar, he is to present the live goat.
003	LEV	016	021	Then he will put both hands on the head of the live goat and confess over it all the wrongs of the Israelites, all their acts of rebellion, and all their sins. He is to put them on the goat's head and send it away into the desert, taken there by a man chosen to do it.
003	LEV	016	022	The goat will take upon itself all their sins and go into a distant place, and the man will send it away into the desert.
003	LEV	016	023	Aaron is to return to the Tent of Meeting, take off the linen clothes he put on before he went into the Most Holy Place, and leave them there.
003	LEV	016	024	He is to wash himself with water in the sanctuary and put on his own clothes. Then he will go out and sacrifice his burnt offering and the people's burnt offering that makes him and the people right.
003	LEV	016	025	He also must burn the fat of the sin offering on the altar.
003	LEV	016	026	The man who went and sent away the scapegoat must wash his clothes and wash himself with water; then he may come back into the camp.
003	LEV	016	027	The remains of the bull used for the sin offering and the goat for the sin offering, whose blood was brought into the Most Holy Place to purify it, must be taken outside the camp. Their skin, meat, and waste must be burned.
003	LEV	016	028	The person who burns them must wash his clothes and wash himself with water; then he may come back into the camp.
003	LEV	016	029	This regulation applies to you for all time. The tenth day of the seventh month is a day of self-denial for you. You are not to do any work. This applies to all who are native-born and also any foreigner who living among you,
003	LEV	016	030	for on this day the process of making you right will be done, to make you clean from all your sins, clean before the Lord.
