003	LEV	023	001	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	023	002	“Tell the Israelites that these are my religious festivals, the festivals of the Lord that you are to call as the holy times when we meet together.
003	LEV	023	003	You have six days to work, but the seventh day is a Sabbath of complete rest, a holy day of meeting together. Don't do any work. It is the Lord's Sabbath everywhere you live.
003	LEV	023	004	These are the Lord's religious festivals, the holy meetings that you are to announce at their specific times.
003	LEV	023	005	The Lord's Passover starts on the evening of the fourteenth day of the first month.
003	LEV	023	006	The Lord's Festival of Unleavened Bread begins on the fifteenth day of the first month. For seven days the bread you eat must be made without yeast.
003	LEV	023	007	On the first day you are to hold a holy meeting. You must not do any of your usual work.
003	LEV	023	008	For seven days you shall present food offerings to the Lord. There is to be a holy meeting on the seventh day. You must not do any of your usual work.”
003	LEV	023	009	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	023	010	“Tell the Israelites that when you enter the land that I'm giving you and you harvest your crops, take a stack of grain from the firstfruits of your harvest to the priest.
003	LEV	023	011	He will wave the stack of grain before the Lord so that it may be accepted on your behalf. The priest is to do this the day following the Sabbath.
