003	LEV	023	013	together with its grain offering of two-tenths of an ephah of the best flour mixed with olive oil (a food offering to the Lord to be accepted by him) and its drink offering of a quarter of a hin of wine.
003	LEV	023	014	Don't eat any bread, roasted grain, or new grain until the time you bring this offering to your God. This regulation is for all time and for future generations everywhere you live.
003	LEV	023	015	Count seven full weeks from the day after the Sabbath—the day you brought the stack of grain as a wave offering.
003	LEV	023	016	Count fifty days until the day after the seventh Sabbath, and on that day present an offering of new grain to the Lord.
003	LEV	023	017	Bring two loaves of bread from your homes as a wave offering. Make them from two-tenths of an ephah of the best flour, baked with yeast, as the firstfruits to the Lord.
003	LEV	023	018	As well as the bread, present seven one-year-old male lambs without defects, one young bull, and two rams. They will be a burnt offering to the Lord, as well as their grain offerings and drink offerings, a food offering to the Lord to be accepted by him.
003	LEV	023	019	Present one male goat as a sin offering and two one-year-old male lambs as a peace offering.
003	LEV	023	020	The priest will wave the lambs as a wave offering before the Lord, along with the bread of the firstfruits. The bread and the two lambs are holy to the Lord and belong to the priest.
003	LEV	023	021	That same day you are to announce a holy meeting, and you must not do any of your usual work. This regulation is for all time and for future generations everywhere you live.
003	LEV	023	022	When you harvest the crops grown on your land, don't harvest right up to the edges of your field, or collect what has been missed. Leave them for the poor people and foreigners. I am the Lord your God.”
003	LEV	023	023	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	023	024	“Tell the Israelites that on the first day of the seventh month you are to have a special Sabbath of complete rest, a holy meeting that is announced by the sound of trumpets.
003	LEV	023	025	Don't do any of your usual work; instead you are to present a food offering to the Lord.”
003	LEV	023	026	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	023	027	“The Day of Atonement is on the tenth day of this seventh month. You are to have a holy meeting, deny yourselves, and present a food offering to the Lord
003	LEV	023	028	On this day you must not do any of your usual work because it is the Day of Atonement, when things are made right for you before the Lord your God.
003	LEV	023	029	Anyone who does not practice self-denial on this day must be expelled from their people.
003	LEV	023	030	I will destroy anyone of you who does any work on this day.
003	LEV	023	031	Don't do any kind of work at all. This regulation is for all time and for future generations everywhere you live.
003	LEV	023	032	It is to be a Sabbath of complete rest for you, and you shall practice self-denial. You are to observe your Sabbath from the evening of the ninth day of the month until evening the next day.”
003	LEV	023	033	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	023	034	“Tell the Israelites that the Feast of Tabernacles to honor the Lord begins on the fifteenth day of the seventh month and lasts for seven days.
003	LEV	023	035	On the first day have a holy meeting. You must not do any of your usual work.
003	LEV	023	036	For seven days you shall present food offerings to the Lord. On the eighth day you are to have another holy meeting and present a food offering to the Lord. It is a meeting for worship. You must not do any of your usual work.
003	LEV	023	037	These are the Lord's holy festivals, which you are to announce as holy meetings for presenting food offerings to the Lord. These include burnt offerings, grain offerings, sacrifices and drink offerings, each according to the specific day.
003	LEV	023	038	All of these offerings are in addition to those for the Lord's Sabbaths. They are also in addition to your gifts, to all your offerings to fulfill promises, and to all the freewill offerings you present to the Lord.
003	LEV	023	039	You shall celebrate a feast to honor the Lord for seven days on the fifteenth day of the seventh month, once you have harvested your crops. The first day and the eighth day are Sabbaths of complete rest.
003	LEV	023	040	On the first day you are to gather branches from large trees, from palm trees, from leafy trees and of river willows, and celebrate before the Lord your God for seven days.
003	LEV	023	041	You are to hold this festival to honor the Lord for seven days every year. This regulation is for all time and for all future generations.
003	LEV	023	042	You are to live in temporary shelters for seven days. Every Israelite born in the country must live in shelters,
003	LEV	023	043	so that your descendants will remember that I made the Israelites live in shelters when I led them out of Egypt. I am the Lord your God.”
003	LEV	023	044	So Moses told the Israelites all about the Lord's festivals.
003	LEV	024	001	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	024	002	“Order the Israelites to bring you pure, pressed olive oil for the lamps, so they will always stay lit.
003	LEV	024	003	From evening until morning Aaron is to constantly look after the lamps before the Lord, outside the veil of the Testimony in the Tent of Meeting. This regulation is for all time and for all future generations.
003	LEV	024	004	He is to constantly look after the lamps placed on the pure gold lampstand before the Lord.
003	LEV	024	005	Using the best flour bake twelve loaves, with two-tenths of an ephah of flour per loaf.
003	LEV	024	006	Place them in two piles, six in each pile, on the table made of pure gold that stands before the Lord.
003	LEV	024	007	Place pure frankincense beside each pile to go with the bread to act as the ‘reminder part,’ a food offering to the Lord.
003	LEV	024	008	Every Sabbath day the bread shall be placed before the Lord, given by the Israelites as an ongoing sign of the eternal agreement.
003	LEV	024	009	It is for Aaron and his descendants. They are to eat it in a holy place; for they must treat it as a most holy part of the food offerings given to the Lord. It is their share of the food offerings for all time.”
003	LEV	024	010	One day a man who had an Israelite mother and an Egyptian father went into the Israelite camp and had a fight with an Israelite.
003	LEV	024	011	The Israelite woman's son cursed the name of the Lord. So they took him before Moses. (His mother's name was Shelomith, daughter of Dibri, from the tribe of Dan.)
003	LEV	024	012	They detained him until it was clear what the Lord wanted them to do about it.
003	LEV	024	013	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	024	014	“Take the man who cursed me outside the camp. Have all who heard him curse put their hands on his head; then have everyone stone him to death.
003	LEV	024	015	Tell the Israelites that anyone who curses their God will be punished for their sin.
003	LEV	024	016	Anyone who curses the name of the Lord must be executed. All of you must stone them to death, whether they are a foreigner who lives with you or an Israelite. If they curse my name, they must be executed.
003	LEV	024	017	Anyone who kills someone else must be executed.
003	LEV	024	018	Anyone who kills an animal has to replace it—a life for a life.
003	LEV	024	019	If anyone injures someone else, whatever they've done must be done to them:
003	LEV	024	020	a broken bone for a broken bone, an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth. Whatever way they injured the victim, the same must be done to them.
003	LEV	024	021	Anyone who kills an animal has to replace it, but anyone who kills someone else must be executed.
003	LEV	024	022	The same laws apply to foreigners who live with you as to Israelites, for I am the Lord your God.”
003	LEV	024	023	Moses told this to the Israelites, and they took the man who cursed the Lord outside the camp and stoned him to death. The Israelites did what the Lord ordered Moses to do.
003	LEV	025	001	The Lord told Moses on Mount Sinai,
003	LEV	025	002	“Tell the Israelites: When you enter the land that I'm giving you, the land itself must also observe a Sabbath rest in honor of the Lord.
003	LEV	025	003	Six years you can cultivate your fields, take care of your vineyards, and harvest your crops.
003	LEV	025	004	But the seventh year is to be a Sabbath of complete rest for the land, a Sabbath in honor of the Lord. Don't plant your fields or care for your vineyards.
003	LEV	025	005	Don't harvest what may have grown up in your fields, or collect the grapes from your vineyards that you haven't cared for. The land is to have a year of complete rest.
003	LEV	025	006	You can eat whatever the land produces during the Sabbath year. This applies to yourself, your male and female slaves, paid workers and foreigners who live with you,
003	LEV	025	007	and to your livestock and the wild animals living in your land. Whatever grows can be used for food.
003	LEV	025	008	Count seven ‘sabbaths’ of years, in other words, seven times seven years, so that the seven sabbaths of years come to forty-nine years.
003	LEV	025	009	Then blow the trumpet all through the country on the tenth day of the seventh month, which is the Day of Atonement. Make sure this signal is heard throughout your whole country.
003	LEV	025	010	You are to dedicate the fiftieth year and announce freedom everywhere in the country for all who live there. This is to be your Jubilee, when each of you is to return to reclaim your property and to be part of your family once more.
003	LEV	025	011	The fiftieth year will be a Jubilee for you. Don't sow the land; don't harvest what may have grown up in your fields, or collect the grapes from your vineyards that you haven't cared for.
003	LEV	025	012	It is a Jubilee and it is to be holy to you. You can eat whatever the land produces.
003	LEV	025	013	In this Jubilee Year, every one of you shall return to your own property.
003	LEV	025	014	If you sell land to your neighbor, or buy land from him, don't exploit one another.
003	LEV	025	015	When you buy from your neighbor work out how many years have passed since the last Jubilee, for he is to sell to you depending on how many years of harvest remain.
003	LEV	025	016	The more years that are left, the more you shall pay; the fewer years that are left, the less you shall pay, because he is actually selling you a specific number of harvests.
003	LEV	025	017	Don't exploit one another, but have respect for your God, because I am the Lord your God.
003	LEV	025	018	Keep my rules and observe my regulations, so you can live in safety in the land.
003	LEV	025	019	Then the land will produce good harvests, so you will have plenty to eat and live in safety there.
003	LEV	025	020	But if you ask, ‘What are we going to do in the seventh year if we do not sow or harvest our crops?’
003	LEV	025	021	I will bless you in the sixth year, so that the land will produce a crop that will be enough for three years.
003	LEV	025	022	As you sow in the eighth year, you will still be eating from that harvest, which will last until your harvest in the ninth year.
003	LEV	025	023	Land must not be permanently sold, because it really belongs to me. To me you are only foreigners and travelers passing through.
003	LEV	025	024	So whatever land you buy to own, you must make arrangements so it can be returned to its original owner.
003	LEV	025	025	If one of your people becomes poor and sells you some of their land, their close family can come and buy back what they have sold.
003	LEV	025	026	However, if they don't have anyone who can buy it back, but in the meantime their financial situation improves and they have enough to buy back the land,
003	LEV	025	027	they will work however many years it has been since the sale, and pay back the balance to the person who bought it, and go back to their property
003	LEV	025	028	If they can't raise enough to pay the person back for the land, the buyer will remain its owner until the Jubilee Year. But in the Jubilee Year the land will be returned so that the original owners can go back to their property.
003	LEV	025	029	If someone sells a house located in a walled town, they have the right to buy it back for a full year after selling it. It can be bought back any time during that year.
003	LEV	025	030	If it isn't bought back by the end of a full year, then ownership of the house in the walled town is permanently transferred to the one who bought it and their descendants. It won't be returned in the Jubilee.
003	LEV	025	031	But houses in villages that don't have walls around them are to be treated as located in the fields. They can be bought back, and will be returned in the Jubilee.
003	LEV	025	032	However, the Levites always have the right to buy back their houses in the towns that belong to them.
003	LEV	025	033	Whatever the Levites own can be bought back, even houses sold in their towns, and must be returned in the Jubilee. That's because the houses in the towns of the Levites are what they were given to own as their share among the Israelites.
003	LEV	025	034	However, the fields surrounding their towns must not be sold because they belong to the Levites permanently.
003	LEV	025	035	If any of your people become poor and can't survive, you must help them in the same way you would help a foreigner or a stranger, so that they can go on living in your neighborhood.
003	LEV	025	036	Don't make them pay you any interest or demand more than they borrowed, but respect your God so that they can remain living in your area.
003	LEV	025	037	Don't lend them silver with interest or sell them food at an inflated price.
003	LEV	025	038	Remember, I am the Lord your God who led you out of Egypt to give you the land of Canaan and to be your God.
003	LEV	025	039	If any of your people become poor and have to sell themselves to work for you, don't force them to work as a slave.
003	LEV	025	040	Have them live with you like a paid worker who is staying with you for a while. They are to work for you until the Jubilee Year.
003	LEV	025	041	Then they and their children must be freed, and they can go back to their family and to their family's property.
003	LEV	025	042	Israelites are not to be sold as slaves because they belong to me as my slaves—I led them out of Egypt.
003	LEV	025	043	Don't treat them with brutality. Have respect for your God.
003	LEV	025	044	Buy your male and female slaves from the surrounding nations.
003	LEV	025	045	You can also buy them from foreigners who have come to live among you, or from their descendants born in your land. You can treat them as your property.
003	LEV	025	046	You can pass them on to your children to inherit as property after you die. You can make them slaves for life, but you must not brutally treat any of your own people, the Israelites, as a slave.
003	LEV	025	047	If a foreigner among you becomes successful, and one of your people living nearby becomes poor and sells themselves to the foreigner or to a member of the foreigner's family,
003	LEV	025	048	they still have the right of being bought back after the sale. A member of their family can buy them back—
003	LEV	025	049	an uncle or cousin or any close relative from their family can buy them back. If they become successful, they can buy themselves back.
003	LEV	025	050	The person concerned and their buyer will work out the time from the year of the sale up to the Jubilee Year. The price will depend on the number of years, calculated using the daily rate for a paid worker.
003	LEV	025	051	If there are many years left, they must pay a larger percentage of the purchase price.
003	LEV	025	052	If there are only a few years remaining before the Jubilee Year, then they only have to pay a percentage depending on the number of years still left.
003	LEV	025	053	They are to live with their foreign owner just like a paid worker, hired from year to year, but see to it that the owner doesn't treat him brutally.
003	LEV	025	054	If they are not bought back in any of the ways described, they and their children shall be freed in the Jubilee Year.
003	LEV	025	055	For the Israelites belong to me as my slaves. They are my slaves—I led them out of Egypt. I am the Lord your God.”
003	LEV	026	001	“Don't make yourselves idols anywhere in your land and bow down to worship them, whether they are images or sacred pillars or stone sculptures. For I am the Lord your God.
003	LEV	026	002	Keep my Sabbaths and show respect for my sanctuary. I am the Lord.
003	LEV	026	003	If you follow my rules and keep my regulations,
003	LEV	026	004	I will make sure it rains at the right time so that the ground will grow good crops and the fruit trees will be productive.
003	LEV	026	005	Your time of threshing will last right up to the grape harvest, and the grape harvest until the time you have to sow again. You will have more than enough to eat and you will live in safety in your land.
003	LEV	026	006	I will make sure your land is at peace. You will be able to sleep without being afraid of anything. I will get rid of dangerous animals from the land, and you will not suffer from any violent enemy attacks.
003	LEV	026	007	You will chase your enemies, and kill them with the sword.
003	LEV	026	008	Five of you will kill one hundred, and one hundred of you will kill ten thousand. You will destroy your enemies.
003	LEV	026	009	I will come to help you, so you will reproduce and increase in numbers, and I will confirm my agreement with you.
003	LEV	026	010	You'll still be eating your old stock of grain when you need to get rid of it so you can store the new grain.
003	LEV	026	011	I will come and live with you—I certainly won't reject you.
003	LEV	026	012	I shall always be right there with you. I will be your God, and you will be my people.
003	LEV	026	013	I am the Lord your God, who led you out of Egypt so you wouldn't have to be slaves to the Egyptians any longer. I smashed the yoke that kept you bent down and helped you to stand up straight.
003	LEV	026	014	But if you don't pay attention to me and do what I tell you;
003	LEV	026	015	if you reject my laws, hate my regulations, and refuse to follow my commandments, and consequently break my agreement,
003	LEV	026	016	then this is what I am going to do to you: I will make you panic, and suffer from diseases like tuberculosis and fever that make you blind and drain your life away. It will be pointless for you to sow seed in your fields because your enemies will eat the harvest.
003	LEV	026	017	I will turn against you, and you'll be defeated by your enemies. People who hate you will rule over you, and you'll run away even when there's no one chasing you!
003	LEV	026	018	If after all this you still refuse to obey me, I will move to punishing you seven times over for your sins.
003	LEV	026	019	I will break your self-reliant strength you're so proud of, and make your sky hard as iron and your land hard as bronze.
003	LEV	026	020	Your strength will be completely wasted because your land won't produce crops, and your trees won't produce fruit.
003	LEV	026	021	If you go on opposing me and refusing to do what I tell you, I will make your punishments seven times worse, based on your sins.
003	LEV	026	022	I will send wild animals to kill your children, wipe out your livestock, and make you so few in number that there won't be anyone on your roads.
003	LEV	026	023	However, if in spite of all this correction you still don't change but go on opposing me,
003	LEV	026	024	then I will take action against you. I will punish you seven times over for your sins.
003	LEV	026	025	I will send enemies with swords to attack you in retaliation for breaking the agreement. Even though you retreat into your towns for defense, I will plague you with disease, and you will be handed over to your enemies.
003	LEV	026	026	I will send a famine so bread is in short supply. One oven will serve the needs of ten women baking bread. It will be distributed by weight so that you'll eat but won't have enough.
003	LEV	026	027	However, if in spite of all this you don't obey me, but go on opposing me,
003	LEV	026	028	then I will take action against you in a rage of fury, and I will punish you myself seven times over for your sins.
003	LEV	026	029	You will eat the bodies of your own sons and daughters.
003	LEV	026	030	I will destroy your high places of worship, smash your altars of incense, and pile up your dead bodies on what remains of your idols, which also have no life at all. I will really despise you.
003	LEV	026	031	I will demolish your towns and destroy your pagan sanctuaries, and I will refuse to accept your sacrifices.
003	LEV	026	032	I will devastate your land myself, so that your enemies who come and live in it will be horrified at what has happened.
003	LEV	026	033	I'm going to scatter you among the nations. You will be chased out by armies with swords as your land is ruined and your towns are destroyed.
003	LEV	026	034	At least then the land will be able to enjoy its Sabbaths all the time it's abandoned while you are in exile in the land of your enemies. The land will finally be able to rest and enjoy its Sabbaths.
003	LEV	026	035	The whole time it's abandoned the land will observe the Sabbaths of rest that it wasn't able to do while you were living there.
003	LEV	026	036	I will make those of you who survive so discouraged that as you live in the lands of your enemies even the sound of a leaf blowing in the wind will scare you into running away! You'll run away like you're being chased by someone with a sword, and fall down even though no one is after you.
003	LEV	026	037	You'll trip over each other as you run away from the attack, even though no one's there. You'll have no power to resist your enemies.
003	LEV	026	038	You'll die in exile and you'll be buried in a foreign country.
003	LEV	026	039	Those of you who do manage to survive in the countries of your enemies will wither away because of their guilt, decaying as they share the sins of their fathers.
003	LEV	026	040	They need to confess their sins and those of their fathers, acting in such an unfaithful way towards me, opposing me.
003	LEV	026	041	Because of this I took action against them and exiled them in the countries of their enemies. However, if they humbly give up their stubborn attitude and accept their punishment for their sins,
003	LEV	026	042	then I will fulfill the agreement I made with Jacob, Isaac, and Abraham, and I will not forget my promise about the land.
003	LEV	026	043	For the land will be left empty by them, and it will enjoy its Sabbaths being abandoned. They will pay for their sins, because they rejected my rules and regulations.
003	LEV	026	044	But despite all this, even while they are living in land of their enemies, I will not reject or hate them so much as to destroy them and break my agreement with them, because I am the Lord their God.
003	LEV	026	045	Because of them I will renew the agreement I made with their fathers, those I led out of Egypt as the other nations watched, in order that I might be their God. I am the Lord.”
003	LEV	026	046	These are the rules, regulations, and laws that the Lord set up between himself and the Israelites through Moses on Mount Sinai.
003	LEV	027	001	The Lord told Moses,
003	LEV	027	002	“Tell the Israelites: When you make a special promise to dedicate someone to the Lord, these are the values you are to use.
003	LEV	027	003	The value of a man aged twenty to sixty is fifty shekels of silver (using the sanctuary shekel standard).
003	LEV	027	004	The value of a woman is thirty shekels.
003	LEV	027	005	The value of someone aged five to twenty is twenty shekels for a male and ten shekels for a female.
003	LEV	027	006	The value of someone aged one month to five years is five shekels of silver for a male and three shekels of silver for a female.
003	LEV	027	007	The value of someone aged sixty or older is fifteen shekels for a male and ten shekels of silver for a female.
003	LEV	027	008	However, if when you fulfill your promise you are poorer than the fixed value, you are to present the person before the priest, who will then set the value depending on what you can afford.
003	LEV	027	009	If when you fulfill your promise you bring an animal that is permitted as an offering to the Lord, the animal given to the Lord shall be considered holy.
003	LEV	027	010	You are not allowed to replace it or swap it, either for one that is better or one that is worse. However, if you do replace it then both animals become holy.
003	LEV	027	011	If when you fulfill your promise you bring any unclean animal that is not permitted as an offering to the Lord, then you must show the animal to the priest.
003	LEV	027	012	The priest will decide its value, whether high or low. Whatever value the priest places on it is final.
003	LEV	027	013	If you then decide to buy the animal back, you have to add one-fifth to its value in payment.
003	LEV	027	014	If you dedicate your house as holy to the Lord, then the priest will decide its value, whether high or low. Whatever value the priest places on it remains final.
003	LEV	027	015	But if you want to buy back your house, you have to add one-fifth to its value in payment. Then it will belong to you again.
003	LEV	027	016	If you dedicate some of your land to the Lord, then its value shall be determined by the amount of seed required to sow it: fifty shekels of silver for every homer of barley seed used.
003	LEV	027	017	If you dedicate your field during the Jubilee Year, the value will be the full amount calculated.
003	LEV	027	018	But if you dedicate your field after the Jubilee, the priest will work out the value depending on the number of years left until the next Jubilee Year, so reducing the value.
003	LEV	027	019	But if you want to buy your field back, you have to add one-fifth to its value in payment. Then it will belong to you again.
003	LEV	027	020	But if you don't buy the field back, or if you've already sold it to someone else, it can't ever be bought back.
003	LEV	027	021	When the Jubilee comes, the field will become holy, in the same way as a field devoted to the Lord. It will become the property of the priests.
003	LEV	027	022	If you dedicate to the Lord a field you've bought that was not part of your original property,
003	LEV	027	023	the priest will work out the value until the next Jubilee Year. You will pay on that day the exact value, giving it as a holy offering to the Lord.
003	LEV	027	024	In the Jubilee Year, ownership of the field shall revert back to the person you bought it from—to the original owner of the land.
003	LEV	027	025	(All values will use the sanctuary shekel standard of twenty gerahs to the shekel.)
003	LEV	027	026	No one is allowed to dedicate the firstborn of the livestock, because the firstborn belongs to the Lord. Whether they are cattle, sheep, or goats, they are the Lord's.
003	LEV	027	027	But if it is an unclean animal, then you can buy it back according to its value, adding on one-fifth extra. If it's not bought back, then it is to be sold according to its value.
003	LEV	027	028	Anything that you specially dedicate to the Lord from what you own, whether it's a person, an animal, or your land, can't be sold or bought back. Anything specially dedicated is most holy to the Lord.
003	LEV	027	029	No one who is specially dedicated to destruction can be bought back. They must be killed.
003	LEV	027	030	Tithe from your crops or fruit belongs to the Lord; it is holy to the Lord.
003	LEV	027	031	If you want to buy back some of your tithe, you must add on one-fifth to its value.
003	LEV	027	032	When you count your herds and flocks, every tenth animal that passes under the shepherd's rod is holy to the Lord.
003	LEV	027	033	You must not examine it to see if it's good or bad, and you must not replace it. However, if you do replace it then both animals become holy; they can't be bought back.”
003	LEV	027	034	These are the laws the Lord gave to Moses for the Israelites on Mount Sinai.
