# BOOK	004	NUM	Numbers	Numbers
004	NUM	001	001	The Lord spoke to Moses in the Tent of Meeting while they were in the Sinai desert. This was on the first day of the second month of the second year after the Israelites had left Egypt. He told him,
004	NUM	001	002	“Census all the Israelites according to their tribe and family. Count every man and keep a record of each individual's name.
004	NUM	001	003	Those aged twenty or older who can do military service are to be registered by you and Aaron in their Israelite army divisions.
004	NUM	001	004	A representative from each tribe, the head of a family, must be there with you.
004	NUM	001	005	These are the names of the men who will work with you: From the tribe of Reuben, Elizur, son of Shedeur;
004	NUM	001	006	from the tribe of Simeon, Shelumiel, son of Zurishaddai;
004	NUM	001	007	from the tribe of Judah, Nahshon, son of Amminadab;
004	NUM	001	008	from the tribe of Issachar, Nethanel, son of Zuar;
004	NUM	001	009	from the tribe of Zebulun, Eliab, son of Helon;
004	NUM	001	010	from the sons of Joseph: from the tribe of Ephraim, Elishama, son of Ammihud, and from the tribe of Manasseh, Gamaliel, son of Pedahzur;
004	NUM	001	011	from the tribe of Benjamin, Abidan, son of Gideoni;
004	NUM	001	012	from the tribe of Dan, Ahiezer, son of Ammishaddai;
004	NUM	001	013	from the tribe of Asher, Pagiel, son of Ocran;
004	NUM	001	014	from the tribe of Gad, Eliasaph, son of Deuel;
004	NUM	001	015	and from the tribe of Naphtali, Ahira, son of Enan.”
004	NUM	001	016	These were the men chosen from the Israelite community. They were the leaders of their fathers' tribes; the heads of the families of Israel.
004	NUM	001	017	Moses and Aaron summoned these men who had been selected by name.
004	NUM	001	018	They had all the Israelites gather together on the first day of the second month, and recorded the people's genealogy according to their tribe and family, and counted up the names of all those aged twenty or older,
004	NUM	001	019	as the Lord had told Moses to do. Moses conducted this census in the Sinai desert.
004	NUM	001	020	The descendants of Reuben (he was Israel's firstborn son), men aged twenty or over, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	021	from the tribe of Reuben totaled 46,500.
004	NUM	001	022	The descendants of Simeon, men aged twenty or over, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	023	from the tribe of Simeon totaled 59,300.
004	NUM	001	024	The descendants of Gad, men aged twenty or over, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	025	from the tribe of Gad totaled 45,650.
004	NUM	001	026	The descendants of Judah, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	027	from the tribe of Judah, totaled 74,600.
004	NUM	001	028	The descendants of Issachar, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	029	from the tribe of Issachar, totaled 54,400.
004	NUM	001	030	The descendants of Zebulun, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	031	from the tribe of Zebulun, totaled 57,400.
004	NUM	001	032	The descendants of Joseph: the descendants of Ephraim, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	033	from the tribe of Ephraim, totaled 40,500.
004	NUM	001	034	And the descendants of Manasseh, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	035	from the tribe of Manasseh, totaled 32,200.
004	NUM	001	036	The descendants of Benjamin, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	037	from the tribe of Benjamin, totaled 35,400.
004	NUM	001	038	The descendants of Dan, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	039	from the tribe of Dan, totaled 62,700.
004	NUM	001	040	The descendants of Asher, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	041	from the tribe of Asher, totaled 41,500.
004	NUM	001	042	The descendants of Naphtali, men aged twenty or older, were recorded by name according to the genealogical records of their tribe and families. All those registered who could serve in the army
004	NUM	001	043	from the tribe of Naphtali, totaled 53,400.
004	NUM	001	044	These were the totals of the men counted and registered by Moses and Aaron, with the help of the twelve leaders of Israel, who each represented their family.
