004	NUM	003	001	This is the account concerning Aaron and Moses when the Lord spoke to Moses on Mount Sinai.
004	NUM	003	002	The names of the sons of Aaron were: Nadab (firstborn), Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
004	NUM	003	003	These were the names of Aaron's sons who were anointed and ordained to serve as priests.
004	NUM	003	004	Nadab and Abihu died in the Lord's presence when they offered forbidden fire before the Lord in the Sinai desert. Since they didn't have any sons, Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests while their father Aaron was alive.
004	NUM	003	005	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	003	006	“Gather the tribe of Levi together and present them to Aaron the priest to help him with the ministry.
004	NUM	003	007	They are to carry out duties on his behalf and for all the Israelites at the Tent of Meeting, looking after the service of the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	008	They are responsible for caring for all the furniture of the Tent of Meeting, serving the Israelites through what they do in the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	009	The Levites are to work exclusively for Aaron and his sons because this is their assignment among the Israelites.
004	NUM	003	010	You are to appoint Aaron and his sons to have the responsibility of the priesthood. Anyone else who tries to act as a priest must be executed.”
004	NUM	003	011	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	003	012	“I've taken the Levites from the Israelites in place of every one of their firstborn. The Levites belong to me
004	NUM	003	013	because all the firstborn are mine. When I killed every firstborn in Egypt I set apart as holy to me all the firstborn of Israel, human and animal. They are mine. I am the Lord.”
004	NUM	003	014	The Lord spoke to Moses in the Sinai desert. He told him,
004	NUM	003	015	“Register the Levites by their father's line and family. Count every male aged one month or older.”
004	NUM	003	016	So Moses registered them following the Lord's instructions, just as he had been told.
004	NUM	003	017	These were the names of Levi's sons: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.
004	NUM	003	018	These were the names of Gershon's sons by family: Libni and Shimei.
004	NUM	003	019	Kohath's sons by family were Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.
004	NUM	003	020	Merari's sons by family were Mahli and Mushi. These were the families of the Levites, according to their father's line.
004	NUM	003	021	The family of Libni and the family of Shimei came from Gershon. These were the families of Gershon.
004	NUM	003	022	The total of all males aged one month or older was 7,500.
004	NUM	003	023	The camp of families of Gershon was to the west, behind the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	024	The leader of the Gershon families was Eliasaph, son of Lael.
004	NUM	003	025	Their assigned responsibility for the Tent of Meeting was to take care of the Tabernacle and tent, its covering, the curtain at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting,
004	NUM	003	026	the courtyard curtains, the curtain at the entrance to the courtyard surrounding the Tabernacle and altar, the ropes, and everything connected with their use.
004	NUM	003	027	The families of Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel came from Kohath. These were the families of Kohath.
004	NUM	003	028	The total of all males aged one month or older was 8,600. Their assigned responsibility was to take care of the sanctuary.
004	NUM	003	029	The camp of families of Kohath was on the south side of the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	030	The leader of the Kohath families was Elizaphan son of Uzziel.
004	NUM	003	031	Their assigned responsibility was to care for the Ark, the table, the lampstand, the altars, the articles of the sanctuary used with them, the veil, and everything connected with these items.
004	NUM	003	032	The chief of the leaders of the Levites was Eleazar, son of Aaron the priest. He was in charge of those responsible for serving in the sanctuary.
004	NUM	003	033	The family of Mahli and the family of Mushi came from Merari. These were the families of Merari.
004	NUM	003	034	The total of all males aged one month or older was 6,200.
004	NUM	003	035	The leader of the Merari families was Zuriel, son of Abihail. Their camp was on the north side of the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	036	Their assigned responsibility was to take care of the Tabernacle's frames, crossbars, posts, stands, all its equipment, and everything connected with their use,
004	NUM	003	037	as well as the posts of the surrounding courtyard with their stands, tent pegs, and ropes.
004	NUM	003	038	The camp of Moses, Aaron, and Aaron's sons was to the east of the Tabernacle, in the direction of the sunrise, in front of the Tent of Meeting. They were responsible for the sanctuary on behalf of the Israelites. Anyone else who tried to act as a priest was to be executed.
004	NUM	003	039	The sum total of Levites registered by Moses and Aaron as the Lord ordered was 22,000. This included all males aged one month or older.
004	NUM	003	040	The Lord told Moses, “Conduct a census of all the firstborn Israelite males aged one month or older, and register their names.
004	NUM	003	041	Assign the Levites to me. I am the Lord. They are in place of all of the Israelites' firstborn children. The livestock of the Levites are in place of all the Israelites' firstborn livestock.”
004	NUM	003	042	Moses conducted a census of all the firstborn of the Israelites, as the Lord had instructed him.
004	NUM	003	043	The sum total of the firstborn males a month old or more, registered by name, was 22,273.
004	NUM	003	044	The Lord spoke to Moses and told him,
004	NUM	003	045	“You are to take the Levites in place of all the firstborn children of Israel, and the livestock of the Levites in place of their livestock, because the Levites belong to me. I am the Lord.
004	NUM	003	046	In order to buy back the 273 firstborn Israelites who are more than the number of Levites,
004	NUM	003	047	collect five shekels for each of them (using the sanctuary shekel standard of twenty gerahs).
004	NUM	003	048	He handed the money over to Aaron and his sons as the redemption price for the extra Israelites.”
004	NUM	003	049	Moses collected the redemption money for those extra Israelites that were more than the number redeemed by the Levites.
004	NUM	003	050	He collected the money given on behalf of the Israelites' firstborn children. It came to 1,365 shekels (using the sanctuary shekel standard).
004	NUM	003	051	Moses gave this redemption money to Aaron and his sons as the Lord had told him to, following the Lord's instructions.
004	NUM	004	001	The Lord told Moses and Aaron,
004	NUM	004	002	“Register the descendants of Kohath from the tribe of Levi, according to their family and father's line.
004	NUM	004	003	Count men aged thirty to fifty—all who are entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	004	This work that they are to do in the Tent of Meetings involves the things that are most holy.
004	NUM	004	005	Whenever you move camp, Aaron and his sons will go in, take down the veil, and place it over the Ark of the Testimony.
004	NUM	004	006	On top of this they are to put a fine leather covering, spread a cloth of solid blue over it, and then insert its carrying poles.
004	NUM	004	007	Have them spread a blue cloth over the table of the Presence as well, and put the plates and cups on it, as well as the bowls and jugs for the drink offering. The current bread offering is to stay on it.
004	NUM	004	008	Over everything they are to spread a crimson cloth, next a fine leather covering, and then insert its carrying poles.
004	NUM	004	009	Using a blue cloth, they are to cover the lampstand of light, together with its lamps, wick tongs, and trays, as well as the jars of olive oil used to fill them.
004	NUM	004	010	Then have them wrap it together with all its utensils inside a fine leather covering and place it on the carrying frame.
004	NUM	004	011	They are to spread a blue cloth over the gold altar, cover it with fine leather, and then insert its carrying poles.
004	NUM	004	012	They are to place all the utensils used for the service in the sanctuary in a blue cloth, cover them with fine leather, and place them on the carrying frame.
004	NUM	004	013	Have them clean the ashes from the bronze altar and spread a purple cloth over it,
004	NUM	004	014	and put on it all the equipment used in the services on the altar: the firepans, meat forks, shovels, and sprinkling bowls. Spread over it a fine leather covering and then insert its carrying poles.
004	NUM	004	015	Once Aaron and his sons have finished covering these holy things and all the equipment connected with them, when the camp is ready to move, the priests of the Kohath family are to come and carry them. But they are forbidden to touch anything holy, otherwise they'll die. These are their responsibilities for moving the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	016	Eleazar, son of Aaron the priest, is to supervise obtaining olive oil for the lamps, the aromatic incense, the daily grain offering, and the anointing oil. He is in charge of the whole Tabernacle and everything in it—all the holy things and equipment.”
004	NUM	004	017	The Lord told Moses and Aaron,
004	NUM	004	018	“Make sure the families of Kohath are not wiped out from the Levites.
004	NUM	004	019	This is what you have to do so that they'll live and won't die by getting too close to something holy. Aaron and his sons must go in and tell each of them what they have to do and what they have to carry.
004	NUM	004	020	But they must not go in and look at the things that are most holy, even for just a moment, otherwise they'll die.”
004	NUM	004	021	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	004	022	“Register the descendants of Gershon, according to their family and father's line
004	NUM	004	023	Count men aged thirty to fifty—all who are entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	024	This is how the families of Gershon will serve in terms of working and carrying:
004	NUM	004	025	Have them carry the Tabernacle curtains, the Tent of Meeting with its fine leather covering, the curtains for the entrance to the Tent of Meeting,
004	NUM	004	026	the courtyard curtains, the curtain at the entrance to the courtyard surrounding the Tabernacle and altar, the ropes, and everything connected with their use. The families of Gershon are responsible for everything required involving these items.
004	NUM	004	027	All that they do is to be under the supervision of Aaron and his sons—all their work and carrying assignments. You are to tell them all they are required to carry.
004	NUM	004	028	These are their responsibilities for moving the Tent of Meeting, carried out under the direction of Ithamar, son of Aaron the priest.
004	NUM	004	029	Register the descendants of Merari, according to their family and father's line.
004	NUM	004	030	Count men aged thirty to fifty—all who are entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	031	This is how they will serve in handling the Tent of Meeting: they are to carry the frames of the Tabernacle with its crossbars, posts, and stands,
004	NUM	004	032	the posts of the surrounding courtyard with their stands, tent pegs, and ropes, all their equipment and everything connected with their use. You are to tell them by name what they are responsible for carrying.
004	NUM	004	033	These are their responsibilities for all their work in moving the Tent of Meeting, carried out under the direction of Ithamar, son of Aaron the priest.”
004	NUM	004	034	Moses, Aaron, and the Israelite leaders registered the families of Kohath according to their family and father's line.
004	NUM	004	035	They counted men aged thirty to fifty—all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	036	The total by families was 2,750.
004	NUM	004	037	This was the total of the families of Kohath—all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting. Moses and Aaron registered them in accordance with the Lord's instructions to Moses.
004	NUM	004	038	The families of Gershon were counted, according to their family and father's line,
004	NUM	004	039	men aged thirty to fifty—all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	040	The total by families and father's line was 2,630.
004	NUM	004	041	This was the total of the families of Gershon —all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting. They were registered by Moses and Aaron in accordance with the Lord's instructions.
004	NUM	004	042	The families of Merari were counted, according to their family and father's line,
004	NUM	004	043	men aged thirty to fifty—all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	004	044	The total by families was 3,200.
004	NUM	004	045	This was the total of the families of Merari registered by Moses and Aaron in accordance with the Lord's instructions.
004	NUM	004	046	This is how Moses, Aaron, and the Israelite leaders registered all the Levites according to their family and father's line.
004	NUM	004	047	They counted men aged thirty to fifty—all who were entitled to do the work of serving in the Tent of Meeting and carrying it.
004	NUM	004	048	The sum total was 8,580.
004	NUM	004	049	It was in response to the Lord's instructions that they were registered by Moses. Each of those registered were told what to do and what to carry, as the Lord had ordered Moses.
004	NUM	005	001	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	005	002	“Order the Israelites to expel from the camp anyone who has a skin disease, or who has a discharge, or who is unclean from touching a dead body.
004	NUM	005	003	Whether male or female, you must expel them so they won't make their camp unclean, for that is where I live with them.”
004	NUM	005	004	The Israelites followed these instructions, and expelled such people from the camp. They did what the Lord had told Moses they should do.
004	NUM	005	005	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	005	006	“Tell the Israelites that when a man or woman is unfaithful to the Lord by sinning against someone else, they are guilty
004	NUM	005	007	and must confess their sin. They have to pay the full amount of compensation plus one-fifth of its value, and give this to the person they have wronged.
004	NUM	005	008	However, if that person doesn't have a relative who can be paid the compensation, it belongs to the Lord and shall be given to the priest, together with a sacrificial ram by which the guilty person is set right.
004	NUM	005	009	All holy offerings that the Israelites bring to the priest belong to him.
004	NUM	005	010	Your holy offerings belong to you, but once you give them to the priest they belong to him.”
004	NUM	005	011	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	005	012	“Tell the Israelites that these are the instructions to follow if a man's wife has an affair, being unfaithful to him
004	NUM	005	013	by sleeping with someone else. It may be that her husband doesn't find out and her unclean act wasn't witnessed—she wasn't caught out.
004	NUM	005	014	But if her husband becomes jealous and suspicious of his wife, whether she's guilty or not,
004	NUM	005	015	he is to take her before the priest. He is also to take with him on her behalf an offering of one tenth of an ephath of barley flour. He must also bring for her an offering of an ephath of barley flour. He's not to pour olive oil over it or put frankincense on it, since it's a grain offering for jealousy, a reminder offering to remind people about sin.
004	NUM	005	016	The priest is to lead the wife forward and have her stand before the Lord.
004	NUM	005	017	Then he shall fill a clay jar with holy water in a clay jar and sprinkle on it some dust from the floor of the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	005	018	Once the priest has had the woman stand before the Lord, he shall let her hair loose and have her hold the reminder grain offering—the grain offering used in cases of jealousy. The priest shall hold the bitter water that curses.
004	NUM	005	019	He shall place the woman under oath and tell her, ‘If no one else has slept with you and you have not been unfaithful and become unclean while married to your husband, may you not be harmed by this bitter water that curses.
004	NUM	005	020	But if you have been unfaithful while married to your husband and have become unclean and have had sex with someone else…’”
004	NUM	005	021	(Here the priest shall place the woman under the oath of the curse as follows.) “May the Lord place a curse on you that everyone knows about by having your thighs shrink and your belly swell up.
004	NUM	005	022	May this water that curses go into your stomach and make your belly swell up and your thighs shrink. The woman is to answer, ‘I agree, I agree.’
004	NUM	005	023	The priest is to write these curses on a scroll and then wash them off into the bitter water.
004	NUM	005	024	He shall make the woman drink the bitter water that curses, and it will cause her bitter pain if she is guilty.
004	NUM	005	025	The priest shall take back from her the grain offering for jealousy, wave it before the Lord, and take it to the altar.
004	NUM	005	026	Then the priest shall take a handful of the grain offering as a reminder portion and burn it on the altar, and make the woman drink the water.
004	NUM	005	027	After he has made her drink the water, if she has made herself unclean and has been unfaithful to her husband, then the water that curses will cause her bitter pain. Her belly will swell up and her thighs will shrink. She will become a cursed woman among her people.
004	NUM	005	028	But if the woman has not made herself unclean by being unfaithful and is clean, she will not experience this punishment and she will still be able to have children.
004	NUM	005	029	This is the rule to follow in cases of jealousy when a wife has an affair and makes herself unclean while married to her husband,
004	NUM	005	030	or when a husband starts feeling jealous and becomes suspicious of his wife. He shall have his wife stand before the Lord, and the priest is to carry out every part of this rule.
004	NUM	005	031	If she is found guilty, her husband will not be held responsible. But the woman will bear the consequences of her sin.”
004	NUM	006	001	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	006	002	“Tell the Israelites: If a man or a woman makes a special promise to become a Nazirite, to dedicate themselves to the Lord,
004	NUM	006	003	they must not drink any wine or other alcoholic drink. They must not even drink vinegar made from wine or other alcoholic drink, or any grape juice or eat grapes or raisins.
004	NUM	006	004	The whole time they are dedicated to the Lord they must not eat anything from a grapevine, not even grape seeds or skins.
004	NUM	006	005	They must not use a razor on their heads during the whole time of this promise of dedication. They must remain holy until their time of dedication to the Lord is finished. They must let their hair grow long.
004	NUM	006	006	During this time of dedication to the Lord they must not go near a dead body.
004	NUM	006	007	Even if it's their father, mother, brother or sister who has died, they are not to make themselves unclean, because their uncut hair announces their dedication to God.
004	NUM	006	008	Through the whole time of their dedication they are to be holy to the Lord.
004	NUM	006	009	However, if someone dies suddenly close to them, making them unclean, they must wait seven days, and on the seventh day when they are made clean again they are to shave their heads.
004	NUM	006	010	On the eighth day they shall take two turtledoves or two young pigeons to the priest at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	006	011	The priest will offer one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering to make them right, because they became guilty by being near the dead body. On that day they must re-dedicate themselves and let their hair grow again.
004	NUM	006	012	They must re-dedicate themselves to the Lord for the full time they originally promised and bring a one-year-old male lamb as a guilt offering. The previous days don't count towards the time of dedication because they became unclean.
004	NUM	006	013	These are the rules to be observed when the Nazirite's time of dedication is finished. They are to be taken to the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.
004	NUM	006	014	There they are to present an offering to the Lord of a one-year-old male lamb without defects as a burnt offering, a one-year-old female lamb without defects as a sin offering, and a ram without defects as a peace offering.
004	NUM	006	015	In addition they are to bring a basket of bread without yeast made from the best flour mixed with olive oil and wafers without yeast coated with olive oil as well as their grain offerings and drink offerings.
004	NUM	006	016	The priest will present all these before the Lord as well as sacrificing the sin offering and the burnt offering.
004	NUM	006	017	He will also sacrifice a ram as a peace offering to the Lord, together with the basket of bread made without yeast. In addition the priest will present the grain offering and drink offering.
004	NUM	006	018	Then the Nazirites are to shave their heads at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting. They shall take the hair from their heads that were dedicated, and place it on the fire under the peace offering.
004	NUM	006	019	Once the Nazirites have shaved, the priest will take the boiled shoulder from the ram, one bread without yeast from the basket, and one wafer without yeast, and place them in their hands.
004	NUM	006	020	The priest will wave them as a wave offering before the Lord. These items are holy and belong to the priest, as well as the breast of the wave offering and the thigh that was offered. Once this is finished, Nazirites may drink wine.
004	NUM	006	021	These are the rules to be observed when a Nazirite promises to give offerings to the Lord regarding their dedication. They can also bring additional offerings if they can afford it. Every Nazirite must fulfill whatever promises they have made when they dedicated themselves.”
004	NUM	006	022	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	006	023	“Tell Aaron and his sons: This is how you are to bless the Israelites. This is what they are to say:
004	NUM	006	024	‘May the Lord bless you and take care of you.
004	NUM	006	025	May the Lord smile on you and be gracious to you.
004	NUM	006	026	May the Lord watch over you and give you peace.’
004	NUM	006	027	Whenever the priests bless the Israelites in my name, I will bless them.”
004	NUM	007	001	On the same day that Moses finished putting up the Tabernacle, he anointed it and dedicated it, along with all its furniture, the altar, and all its utensils.
004	NUM	007	002	The Israelite leaders who were the heads of their families came and gave an offering. They were the same leaders of the tribes who had worked on the registration of the Israelites.
004	NUM	007	003	They brought to the Lord an offering of six covered wagons and twelve oxen. Each leader gave an ox, and two leaders shared in giving a wagon. They presented them in front of the Tabernacle.
004	NUM	007	004	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	007	005	“Accept what they're giving you and use them in the work of the Tent of Meeting. Give them to the Levites to use as required.”
004	NUM	007	006	Moses accepted the wagons and oxen and handed them over to the Levites.
004	NUM	007	007	He gave two wagons and four oxen to the families of Gershon to use as they required.
004	NUM	007	008	He gave four wagons and eight oxen to the families of Merari, to use as they required. The work was all to be done under the direction of Ithamar, son of Aaron the priest.
004	NUM	007	009	He didn't give any wagons or oxen to the Kohathites because their responsibility was to carry on their shoulders the holy objects assigned to their care.
004	NUM	007	010	The day the altar was anointed, the leaders came forward with their dedicatory offerings, presenting them in front of it.
004	NUM	007	011	The Lord told Moses, “Have one leader come every day and present his offering for the dedication of the altar.”
004	NUM	007	012	The first day Nahshon, son of Amminadab, of the tribe of Judah came forward with his offering.
004	NUM	007	013	His offering was a silver plate that weighed a hundred and thirty shekels, and a silver bowl that weighed seventy shekels (using the sanctuary shekel standard). They were both filled with the best flour mixed with olive oil as a grain offering.
004	NUM	007	014	He also presented a gold dish that weighed ten shekels filled with incense. As sacrifices he brought
004	NUM	007	015	a young bull, a ram, and a one-year-old male lamb as a burnt offering,
