004	NUM	027	001	The daughters of Zelophehad came to present their case. Their father Zelophehad was the son of Hepher, son of Gilead, son of Machir, son of Manasseh, and was from the tribe of Manasseh, son of Joseph. The names of his daughters were Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah. They came
004	NUM	027	002	and stood before Moses, Eleazar the priest, the leaders, and all the Israelites at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting. They said,
004	NUM	027	003	“Our father died in the desert, but he wasn't one of Korah's followers who joined together to rebel against the Lord. No, he died from his own sins, and he didn't have any sons.
004	NUM	027	004	Why should our family name be lost simply because he didn't have a son? Give us land to own alongside our uncles.”
004	NUM	027	005	Moses took their case before the Lord.
004	NUM	027	006	The Lord gave him this answer,
004	NUM	027	007	“What the daughters of Zelophehad are saying is right. You really must give them land to own alongside their uncles—give to them what would have been allocated to their father.
004	NUM	027	008	In addition, tell the Israelites, ‘If a man dies and doesn't have a son, give his property to his daughter.
004	NUM	027	009	If he doesn't have a daughter, give his property to his brothers.
