004	NUM	029	034	Also present a male goat as a sin offering in addition to the continual burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.
004	NUM	029	035	On the eighth day all of you are to meet together. Don't do any of your normal work.
004	NUM	029	036	Present the following as a burnt offering acceptable to the Lord: one bull, two rams, and seven male lambs a year old, all of them without defects.
004	NUM	029	037	They are to be accompanied by their grain offerings and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, all according to the number required.
004	NUM	029	038	Also present a male goat as a sin offering in addition to the continual burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.
004	NUM	029	039	Present these offerings to the Lord at the times you are required to do so, in addition to your offerings to fulfill a promise and freewill offerings, whether they are burnt offerings, grain offerings, drink offerings, or peace offerings.”
004	NUM	029	040	Moses repeated all this to the Israelites as the Lord ordered him to do.
004	NUM	030	001	Moses told the tribal leaders of Israel, “This is what the Lord commands:
004	NUM	030	002	If a man makes a solemn promise to the Lord, or pledges to do something by swearing an oath, he must not break his promise. He must do everything he said he would.
004	NUM	030	003	If a woman who's young and still living in her father's house makes a solemn promise to the Lord or pledges to do something by swearing an oath
004	NUM	030	004	and her father finds out about her promise or pledge but doesn't say anything to her, all the promises or pledges she has sworn to do will stand.
004	NUM	030	005	But if her father disallows them as soon as he finds out, then none of her promises or pledges remain valid. The Lord will release her from keeping them because her father has disallowed them.
004	NUM	030	006	If a woman marries after having made a solemn promise or sworn an oath without thinking
004	NUM	030	007	and her husband finds out about it but doesn't say anything to her right away, all the promises or pledges she has sworn to do will stand.
004	NUM	030	008	But if her husband disallows them when he finds out about it, then none of her promises or oaths remain valid and the Lord will release her from keeping them.
004	NUM	030	009	Every solemn promise made by a widow or a woman who is divorced must be kept.
004	NUM	030	010	If a woman living with her husband makes a solemn promise to the Lord or pledges to do something by swearing an oath,
004	NUM	030	011	and her husband finds out about her promise or pledge but doesn't say anything to her and doesn't disallow them, then all of her promises or pledges remain valid.
004	NUM	030	012	But if her husband disallows them as soon as he finds out about it, then none of her promises or oaths remain valid. The Lord will release her from keeping them because her husband has disallowed them.
004	NUM	030	013	Her husband may also confirm or disallow any solemn promise or pledge the woman may make for self-denial.
004	NUM	030	014	But if her husband doesn't ever say a word to her about it, then he is assumed to have confirmed all the solemn promises and pledges she has made.
004	NUM	030	015	However, if he disallows them some time later after finding out about them, then he will bear the responsibility for her breaking them.”
004	NUM	030	016	These are the regulations that the Lord gave to Moses regarding the relationship between a man and his wife, and between a father and a daughter who is young and still living at home.
004	NUM	031	001	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	031	002	“Punish the Midianites because of what they did to the Israelites. After that you will join your forefathers in death.”
004	NUM	031	003	Moses instructed the people, “Have some of your men get ready for battle, so they can go and attack the Midianites and carry out the Lord's punishment on them.
004	NUM	031	004	You are to contribute one thousand men from each Israelite tribe.”
004	NUM	031	005	So one thousand men were chosen from each Israelite tribe, making twelve thousand troops ready for battle.
004	NUM	031	006	Moses sent them into battle, one thousand from each tribe, together with Phinehas, son of Eleazar the priest. He carried with him the holy objects from the sanctuary and the trumpets used for giving signals.
004	NUM	031	007	They attacked the Midianites, as the Lord had told Moses to do, and they killed all the men.
004	NUM	031	008	Among those killed were the five kings of Midian, Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba. They also killed Balaam, son of Beor, with the sword.
004	NUM	031	009	The Israelites captured the Midianite women and children, and they took as plunder all their herds, flocks, and possessions.
004	NUM	031	010	They set fire to all the Midianite towns and camps where they had lived,
004	NUM	031	011	and carried away all the plunder and loot, including people and animals.
004	NUM	031	012	They brought the prisoners, loot, and plunder to Moses, to Eleazar the priest, and to the rest of the Israelites where they were camped on the plains of Moab, beside the Jordan opposite Jericho.
004	NUM	031	013	Moses, Eleazar the priest, and all the Israelite leaders went out of the camp to meet them.
004	NUM	031	014	Moses was angry with the army officers, the commanders of thousands and commanders of hundreds, who returned from the battle.
004	NUM	031	015	“Why did you let all the women live?” he asked them.
004	NUM	031	016	“You realize that these were the same women who seduced the Israelite men, leading them to be unfaithful to the Lord at Peor, following Balaam's advice! That's why the Lord's people suffered from the plague!
004	NUM	031	017	So go and kill all the boys, and every woman who has slept with a man.
004	NUM	031	018	Let all the girls who are virgins live. They are yours.
004	NUM	031	019	All those of you who killed someone or touched a dead body must stay outside the camp for seven days. Purify yourselves and your prisoners on the third day and the seventh day.
004	NUM	031	020	Also purify all your clothing and anything made of leather, goat's hair, or wood.”
004	NUM	031	021	Eleazar the priest told the soldiers who had gone into battle, “These are the legal regulations that the Lord has ordered Moses to be carried out:
004	NUM	031	022	All that's made of gold, silver, bronze, iron, tin, and lead—
004	NUM	031	023	anything that doesn't burn—must be put through fire to make it clean. But it still has to be purified using water of purification. Anything that burns must be put through the water.
004	NUM	031	024	Wash your clothes on the seventh day and you will be clean. Then you can enter the camp.”
004	NUM	031	025	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	031	026	“You, Eleazar the priest, and the Israelite family leaders are to take a record of the people and animals that were captured.
004	NUM	031	027	Then divide them between the troops who went into battle and the rest of the Israelites.
004	NUM	031	028	Take as a contribution to the Lord from what is allocated to the troops who went into battle one out of every five hundred people, cattle, donkeys, or sheep.
004	NUM	031	029	Take this from their half share and give it to Eleazar the priest as an offering to the Lord.
004	NUM	031	030	From the Israelites half share, take one out of every fifty people, cattle, donkeys, or sheep, or other animals, and give them to the Levites who take care of the Lord's Tabernacle.”
004	NUM	031	031	Moses and Eleazar the priest did as the Lord had ordered Moses.
004	NUM	031	032	This was the list of plunder remaining that had been looted by the troops: 675,000 sheep,
004	NUM	031	033	72,000 cattle,
004	NUM	031	034	61,000 donkeys,
004	NUM	031	035	and 32,000 virgins.
004	NUM	031	036	This was the half share for those who had gone to fight: 337,500 sheep,
004	NUM	031	037	with a contribution for the Lord of 675,
004	NUM	031	038	36,000 cattle, with a Lord's contribution of 72,
004	NUM	031	039	30,500 donkeys, with a Lord's contribution of 61,
004	NUM	031	040	and 16,000 people, with a Lord's contribution of 32.
004	NUM	031	041	Moses gave the contribution to Eleazar the priest as an offering to the Lord as the Lord had ordered Moses.
004	NUM	031	042	The Israelites' half share left after Moses had given the half share to the troops who had gone to fight,
004	NUM	031	043	consisted of: 337,500 sheep,
004	NUM	031	044	36,000 cattle,
004	NUM	031	045	30,500 donkeys,
004	NUM	031	046	and 16,000 people.
004	NUM	031	047	Moses took from the Israelites' half one out of every fifty people and animals and gave them to the Levites who take care of the Lord's Tabernacle, as the Lord had ordered him.
004	NUM	031	048	The army officers, the commanders of thousands and commanders of hundreds, came to Moses
004	NUM	031	049	and told him, “We, your servants, have checked the troops we command and not a single man is missing.
004	NUM	031	050	So we have brought the Lord an offering of the gold objects each man received—armlets, bracelets, rings, earrings, and necklaces—in order that we may be right before the Lord.”
004	NUM	031	051	Moses and Eleazar the priest accepted from them all the objects made out of gold.
004	NUM	031	052	The gold that the commanders of thousands and of hundreds gave as an offering to the Lord weighed in total 16,750 shekels.
004	NUM	031	053	(The men who had fought in the battle had each taken plunder for himself.)
004	NUM	031	054	Moses and Eleazar the priest accepted the gold from the commanders of thousands and of hundreds and took it into the Tent of Meeting as a memorial offering for the Israelites in the presence of the Lord.
004	NUM	032	001	The tribes of Reuben and Gad had large numbers of livestock and saw that the land of Jazer and Gilead was a good place to rear them.
004	NUM	032	002	So they came to Moses, Eleazar the priest, and the Israelite leaders and said,
004	NUM	032	003	“The towns of Ataroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon,
004	NUM	032	004	which the Lord conquered in full view of the Israelites, are well-suited for the livestock that we your servants own.”
004	NUM	032	005	They continued, “Please respond to our request favorably: give us this land. Don't make us cross the Jordan.”
004	NUM	032	006	In reply Moses asked the tribes of Gad and Reuben, “Are you expecting your brothers to go and fight while you just sit here?
004	NUM	032	007	Why discourage the Israelites from crossing into the country that the Lord has given them?
004	NUM	032	008	This is just what your fathers did when I sent them out from Kadesh-barnea to explore the land.
004	NUM	032	009	After your fathers traveled up the valley of Eshcol and explored the land, they discouraged the Israelites, persuading them not to enter the country that the Lord had given them.
004	NUM	032	010	As a result, they made the Lord very angry that day, and he swore this oath,
004	NUM	032	011	‘Not a single one of those I saved from Egypt who is twenty years old or older will ever see the land I promised with an oath to give to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, because they were not completely committed to me—
004	NUM	032	012	no one except Caleb, son of Jephunneh, the Kenizzite, and Joshua, son of Nun, because they were completely committed to me.’
004	NUM	032	013	The Lord was angry with Israel, and made them wander around in the desert for forty years, until the whole generation who had done evil in his sight had died.
004	NUM	032	014	Now look at you, you brood of sinners who have come to take your fathers' place to make the Lord even angrier with Israel!
004	NUM	032	015	If you give up following him, he will abandon these people in the desert once again, and their deaths will be your fault!”
004	NUM	032	016	Then the tribes of Gad and Reuben came to Moses and told him, “We would plan to build stone walls to keep our livestock safe and towns for our children.
004	NUM	032	017	But we will still get ourselves ready for battle, and we will be prepared to lead the Israelites until they can safely occupy their land. In the meantime, our children will stay behind, living in the fortified towns to protect them from the local people.
004	NUM	032	018	We won't return to our homes until every Israelite is in possession of their allotted land.
004	NUM	032	019	However, we won't own any land on the other side of the Jordan because we've received this land to own on this eastern side of the Jordan.”
004	NUM	032	020	Moses responded, “If this is what you will actually do, if you will get yourselves ready for battle under the Lord's direction,
004	NUM	032	021	and if all your troops cross the Jordan with the Lord until he has driven out his enemies ahead of him,
004	NUM	032	022	then once the country is conquered with the Lord's help then you may return, and you will have fulfilled your obligations to the Lord and to Israel. You will own this land, granted to you by the Lord.
004	NUM	032	023	But if you fail to do this, you will clearly be sinning against the Lord, and the consequences of your sin will catch up with you.
004	NUM	032	024	Go ahead and build towns for your children and stone walls for your flocks, but make sure you do what you've promised!”
004	NUM	032	025	The tribes of Gad and Reuben promised Moses, “Sir, we your servants will do just as you have ordered.
004	NUM	032	026	Our wives and children, our livestock and all our animals, will all remain here in the towns of Gilead.
004	NUM	032	027	But we your servants are ready for battle, and all our troops will cross over to fight with the Lord's help, just as you have said, sir.”
004	NUM	032	028	Moses gave the following instructions about them to Eleazar the priest, to Joshua, son of Nun, and to the family leaders of the tribes of Israel.
004	NUM	032	029	Moses told them, “If the tribes of Gad and Reuben cross the Jordan with you, with all their troops ready for battle with the Lord's help, and the land is conquered as you advance, then give them the land of Gilead to own.
004	NUM	032	030	But if they don't get themselves ready for battle and cross over with you, then they must accept their allotted land among you in the country of Canaan.”
004	NUM	032	031	The tribes of Gad and Reuben responded, “We will do just as the Lord has told us, your servants.
004	NUM	032	032	We will cross over and enter the country of Canaan ready for battle with the Lord's help, so that we may have our allotted share of land on this side of the Jordan.”
004	NUM	032	033	So Moses gave to the tribes of Gad and Reuben and the half-tribe of Manasseh, son of Joseph, the kingdom of Sihon, king of the Amorites, and the kingdom of Og, king of Bashan. This land included its towns and their surrounding area.
004	NUM	032	034	The people of Gad rebuilt Dibon, Ataroth, Aroer,
004	NUM	032	035	Atroth-shophan, Jazer, Jogbehah,
004	NUM	032	036	Beth-nimrah, and Beth-haran as fortified towns, and they built stone walls for their flocks.
004	NUM	032	037	The people of Reuben rebuilt Heshbon, Elealeh, Kiriathaim,
004	NUM	032	038	as well as Nebo and Baal-meon (changing their names), and Sibmah. In fact they renamed those towns they rebuilt.
004	NUM	032	039	The descendants of Machir, son of Manasseh, attacked Gilead and captured it. They drove out the Amorites who were living there.
004	NUM	032	040	So Moses gave Gilead to the family of Machir, son of Manasseh, and they settled there.
004	NUM	032	041	Jair, a descendant of Manasseh, attacked their villages and captured them. He named them the Villages of Jair.
004	NUM	032	042	Nobah attacked Kenath and captured it, along with its villages. He named it Nobah after himself.
004	NUM	033	001	This is a record of the journeys made by the Israelites as they left Egypt in their tribal divisions led by Moses and Aaron.
004	NUM	033	002	Moses recorded the different parts of their journey as instructed by the Lord. These are the journeys they made listed in order from where they started:
004	NUM	033	003	The Israelites left Rameses on the fifteenth day of the first month, the day after the Passover. They set out in triumph as all the Egyptians watched.
004	NUM	033	004	The Egyptians were burying all their firstborn that the Lord had killed, for the Lord had brought down his judgments on their gods.
004	NUM	033	005	The Israelites left Rameses and set up camp at Succoth.
004	NUM	033	006	They moved on from Succoth and set up camp at Etham, on the edge of the desert.
004	NUM	033	007	They moved on from Etham, turning back towards Pi-hahiroth, opposite Baal-zephon, and set up camp near Migdol.
004	NUM	033	008	They moved on from Pi-hahiroth and crossed through the middle of the sea into the desert. They traveled on for three days into the Desert of Etham and set up camp at Marah.
004	NUM	033	009	They moved on from Marah and arrived at Elim, where there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees, and set up camp there.
004	NUM	033	010	They moved on from Elim and set up camp beside the Red Sea.
004	NUM	033	011	They moved on from the Red Sea and set up camp in the Desert of Sin.
004	NUM	033	012	They moved on from the Desert of Sin and set up camp at Dophkah.
004	NUM	033	013	They moved on from Dophkah and set up camp at Alush.
004	NUM	033	014	They moved on from Alush and set up camp at Rephidim. There wasn't any water there for the people to drink.
004	NUM	033	015	They moved on from Rephidim and set up camp in the Sinai Desert.
004	NUM	033	016	They moved on from the Sinai Desert and set up camp at Kibroth-hattaavah.
004	NUM	033	017	They moved on from Kibroth-hattaavah and set up camp at Hazeroth.
004	NUM	033	018	They moved on from Hazeroth and set up camp at Rithmah.
004	NUM	033	019	They moved on from Rithmah and set up camp at Rimmon-perez.
004	NUM	033	020	They moved on from Rimmon-perez and set up camp at Libnah.
004	NUM	033	021	They moved on from Libnah and set up camp at Rissah.
004	NUM	033	022	They moved on from Rissah and set up camp at Kehelathah.
004	NUM	033	023	They moved on from Kehelathah and set up camp at Mount Shepher.
004	NUM	033	024	They moved on from Mount Shepher and set up camp at Haradah.
004	NUM	033	025	They moved on from Haradah and set up camp at Makheloth.
004	NUM	033	026	They moved on from Makheloth and set up camp at Tahath.
004	NUM	033	027	They moved on from Tahath and set up camp at Terah.
004	NUM	033	028	They moved on from Terah and set up camp at Mithkah.
004	NUM	033	029	They moved on from Mithkah and set up camp at Hashmonah.
004	NUM	033	030	They moved on from Hashmonah and set up camp at Moseroth.
004	NUM	033	031	They moved on from Moseroth and set up camp at Bene-jaakan.
004	NUM	033	032	They moved on from Bene-jaakan and set up camp at Hor-haggidgad.
004	NUM	033	033	They moved on from Hor-haggidgad and set up camp at Jotbathah.
004	NUM	033	034	They moved on from Jotbathah and set up camp at Abronah.
004	NUM	033	035	They moved on from Abronah and set up camp at Ezion-geber.
004	NUM	033	036	They moved on from Ezion-geber and set up camp at Kadesh in the Desert of Zin.
004	NUM	033	037	They moved on from Kadesh and set up camp at Mount Hor, on the edge of Edom.
004	NUM	033	038	Aaron the priest climbed Mount Hor as the Lord had directed, and he died there on the first day of the fifth month, in the fortieth year after the Israelites had left Egypt.
004	NUM	033	039	Aaron was 123 when he died on Mount Hor.
004	NUM	033	040	(The Canaanite king of Arad, who lived in the Negev in the country of Canaan, found out that the Israelites were on their way.)
004	NUM	033	041	The Israelites moved on from Mount Hor and set up camp at Zalmonah.
004	NUM	033	042	They moved on from Zalmonah and set up camp at Punon.
004	NUM	033	043	They moved on from Punon and set up camp at Oboth.
004	NUM	033	044	They moved on from Oboth and set up camp at Iye-abarim on the border of Moab.
004	NUM	033	045	They moved on from Iye-abarim and set up camp at Dibon-gad.
004	NUM	033	046	They moved on from Dibon-gad and set up camp at Almon-diblathaim.
004	NUM	033	047	They moved on from Almon-diblathaim and set up camp in the mountains of Abarim opposite Nebo.
004	NUM	033	048	They moved on from the mountains of Abarim and set up camp on the plains of Moab beside the Jordan opposite Jericho.
004	NUM	033	049	There on the plains of Moab they set up camp beside the Jordan, from Beth-jeshimoth to Abel-shittim.
004	NUM	033	050	This was where, on the plains of Moab beside the Jordan opposite Jericho, that the Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	033	051	“Tell the Israelites, Once you cross the Jordan and enter the country of Canaan,
004	NUM	033	052	you must drive out everyone living in the land, destroy all their carved images and metal idols, and tear down all their pagan temples.
004	NUM	033	053	You are to take over the country and settle there, because I have given you the land and it belongs to you.
004	NUM	033	054	You are to divide the land and allocate it by lot to the different tribal families. Give a larger portion to a larger family, and a smaller portion to a smaller family. Each one's allocation is decided by lot, and you will all receive an allocation depending on your tribe.
004	NUM	033	055	But if you don't drive out everyone living in the land, the people you allow to remain will be like grit in your eyes and thorns in your sides. They will cause you trouble where you settle in the country.
004	NUM	033	056	Eventually the punishment I planned for them I will inflict on you.”
004	NUM	034	001	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	034	002	“Give this command to the Israelites: When you enter the country of Canaan, it will be allocated to you to own with the following boundaries:
004	NUM	034	003	The southern extent of your country will be from the Desert of Zin along the border of Edom. Your southern border will run east from the end of the Dead Sea,
004	NUM	034	004	cross south of Scorpion Pass, on to Zin, and reach its southern limit south of Kadesh-barnea. Then it will go to Hazar-addar and on to Azmon.
004	NUM	034	005	There the boundary will turn from Azmon to the Wadi of Egypt, ending at the Mediterranean Sea.
004	NUM	034	006	Your western border will be the coast of the Mediterranean Sea. This is to be your boundary to the west.
004	NUM	034	007	Your northern border will run from the Mediterranean Sea straight to Mount Hor.
004	NUM	034	008	From Mount Hor the boundary will go to Lebo-hamath, then on to Zedad,
004	NUM	034	009	to Ziphron, ending at Hazar-enan. This will be your boundary to the north.
004	NUM	034	010	Your eastern border will run straight from Hazar-enan to Shepham
004	NUM	034	011	Then the boundary will go down from Shepham to Riblah on the east side of Ain. It will pass down along the slopes east of the Sea of Galilee.
004	NUM	034	012	Then the boundary will go down along the Jordan, ending at the Dead Sea. This is to be your land with its surrounding borders.”
004	NUM	034	013	Moses gave the order to the Israelites, “Allocate ownership of this land by lot. The Lord has commanded it to be given to the nine and a half tribes.
004	NUM	034	014	The tribes of Reuben and Gad, together with the half-tribe of Manasseh, have already received their allocation.
004	NUM	034	015	These two and a half tribes have received their allocation on the east side of the Jordan opposite Jericho.”
004	NUM	034	016	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	034	017	“These are the names of the men who will be in charge of allocating ownership of the land for you: Eleazar the priest and Joshua, son of Nun.
004	NUM	034	018	Have one leader from each tribe help in the distribution of the land.
004	NUM	034	019	These are their names: From the tribe of Judah: Caleb, son of Jephunneh.
004	NUM	034	020	From the tribe of Simeon: Shemuel, son of Ammihud.
004	NUM	034	021	From the tribe of Benjamin: Elidad, son of Chislon.
004	NUM	034	022	A leader from the tribe of Dan: Bukki, son of Jogli.
004	NUM	034	023	A leader from the tribe of Manasseh, son of Joseph: Hanniel son of Ephod.
004	NUM	034	024	A leader from the tribe of Ephraim: Kemuel, son of Shiphtan.
004	NUM	034	025	A leader from the tribe of Zebulun: Eli-zaphan, son of Parnach.
004	NUM	034	026	A leader from the tribe of Issachar: Paltiel, son of Azzan.
004	NUM	034	027	A leader from the tribe of Asher: Ahihud, son of Shelomi.
004	NUM	034	028	A leader from the tribe of Naphtali: Pedahel, son of Ammihud.”
004	NUM	034	029	These are the names of those the Lord put in charge of allocating land ownership in the country of Canaan.
004	NUM	035	001	The Lord spoke to Moses on the plains of Moab beside the Jordan opposite Jericho. He told him,
004	NUM	035	002	“Order the Israelites to provide from their land allocation towns for the Levites to live in and pastures around the towns.
004	NUM	035	003	The towns are for them to live in, and the pastures will be for their herds and their flocks—for all their livestock.
004	NUM	035	004	The pastures around the towns you give to the Levites are to extend out from the wall a thousand cubits on all sides.
004	NUM	035	005	Measure two thousand cubits outside the town on the east, two thousand on the south, two thousand on the west, and two thousand on the north, with the town in the middle. These larger areas will be their pastures around the towns.
004	NUM	035	006	Six of the towns you give the Levites are to be sanctuary towns, where a person who kills someone can run for protection. As well as these towns, give the Levites forty-two more.
004	NUM	035	007	The total number of towns you are to give the Levites is forty-eight, along with their pastures.
004	NUM	035	008	The towns that you allocate to be given to the Levites from the territory of the Israelites will be more from a larger tribe and less from a smaller one. The number will be in proportion to the size of the land allocation of each tribe.”
004	NUM	035	009	The Lord told Moses,
004	NUM	035	010	“Tell the Israelites: ‘When you cross over the Jordan into Canaan,
004	NUM	035	011	choose towns as your sanctuary towns, so a person who kills someone by mistake may run there.
004	NUM	035	012	These towns will be for you places of sanctuary from those seeking revenge, so that the killer will not die until they are tried in court.
004	NUM	035	013	The towns you choose will be your six sanctuary towns.
004	NUM	035	014	Choose three cities on the other side of the Jordan and three in Canaan as cities of refuge.
004	NUM	035	015	These six cities will be places of sanctuary for the Israelites and for foreigners or settlers among them, so that anyone who kills a person by mistake may run there.
004	NUM	035	016	But if anyone deliberately hits someone with something made of iron and kills them, that person is a murderer and must be executed.
004	NUM	035	017	If anyone picks up something made of stone that could be used as a weapon and hits someone with it, and kills them, that person is a murderer and must be executed.
004	NUM	035	018	If anyone picks up something made of wood that could be used as a weapon and hits someone with it, and kills them, that person is a murderer and must be executed.
004	NUM	035	019	The avenger is to execute the murderer. When he finds the murderer, he is to kill him.
004	NUM	035	020	Similarly, if anyone hates someone and knocks them down or deliberately throws something at them, and they're killed;
004	NUM	035	021	or if someone hits another with his hand and they die, the one who hit him must be executed because he is a murderer. When the avenger finds the murderer, he is to kill him.
004	NUM	035	022	But if anyone knocks someone else down without meaning to and without hating them, or throws something at them not meaning to hurt them,
004	NUM	035	023	or carelessly drops a heavy stone that kills them, but not as an enemy or intending to harm them,
004	NUM	035	024	then the community must judge between the killer and the avenger following these regulations.
004	NUM	035	025	The court is to protect the killer from being attacked by the avenger and must return him to the sanctuary town that he ran to, and he must stay there until the death of the high priest, who was anointed with holy oil.
004	NUM	035	026	But if the killer ever leaves the limits of the sanctuary town where he ran to,
004	NUM	035	027	and the avenger finds him outside his sanctuary town and kills him, then the avenger will not be guilty of murder,
004	NUM	035	028	because the killer has to stay in his sanctuary town until the death of the high priest. Only after the death of the high priest is he allowed to return to the land he owns.
004	NUM	035	029	These regulations apply to all future generations wherever you live.
004	NUM	035	030	If anyone kills a person, the murderer is to be executed based on the evidence given by witnesses, plural. No one is to be executed based on the evidence given by a single witness.
004	NUM	035	031	You are not to accept payment instead of executing a murderer who has been found guilty—they must be executed.
004	NUM	035	032	Also you are not allowed to accept payment for a person who runs to a sanctuary town and permit him to return and live on his own land before the death of the high priest.
004	NUM	035	033	Don't pollute the land where you live because bloodshed pollutes the land, and the land where blood is shed can't be purified except by the blood of the one who shed it.
004	NUM	035	034	Don't make the land impure where you live because I live there too. I am the Lord, and I live with the Israelites.’”
004	NUM	036	001	The family heads of the descendants of Gilead, son of Machir, son of Manasseh, one of the tribes of Joseph, came and spoke before Moses and the Israelite leaders, the heads of families.
004	NUM	036	002	They said, “When the Lord ordered you, my lord, to allocate land ownership to the Israelites by lot, he also ordered you to give our brother Zelophehad's share to his daughters.
004	NUM	036	003	However, if they marry men from the other tribes of Israel, their allocation would be taken away from our fathers' share and added to the tribe of the men they marry. That part of our allocation would be lost to us.
004	NUM	036	004	So when the Jubilee for the Israelites comes around, their allocation would be added to the tribe into which they marry, and taken away from our fathers' tribe.”
004	NUM	036	005	Following what the Lord told him, Moses gave these orders to the Israelites, “What the tribe of the sons of Joseph says is right.
004	NUM	036	006	This is what the Lord has ordered in regard to Zelophehad's daughters: They can marry anyone they want as long as they marry within a family that belongs to their father's tribe.
004	NUM	036	007	No land allocation in Israel may be passed from tribe to tribe, because every Israelite is to hold onto the allocation of his father's tribe.
004	NUM	036	008	Every daughter who possesses an inheritance from any Israelite tribe must marry within a clan of the tribe of her father, so that every Israelite will possess the inheritance of his fathers.
004	NUM	036	009	No land allocation may be passed from one tribe to another, for each Israelite tribe must hold onto its own allocation.”
004	NUM	036	010	Zelophehad's daughters followed the Lord's orders through Moses.
004	NUM	036	011	Mahlah, Tirzah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Noah, Zelophehad's daughters, married cousins on their father's side.
004	NUM	036	012	They married within the families of the descendants of Manasseh, son of Joseph, and their land allocation stayed within their father's tribe.
004	NUM	036	013	These are the orders and regulations that the Lord gave the Israelites through Moses on the plains of Moab beside the Jordan opposite Jericho.
#
# BOOK	005	DEU	Deuteronomy	Deuteronomy
005	DEU	001	001	This is the record of what Moses told all the Israelites during their time in the desert to the east of the Jordan. They were in the Arabah near Suph, between Paran on the one side and Tophel, Laban, Hazeroth, and Di-zahab on the other.
005	DEU	001	002	(It takes eleven days to go from Horeb to Kadesh-barnea by the road that passes Mount Seir.)
005	DEU	001	003	On the first day of the eleventh month of the fortieth year, Moses recounted to the Israelites everything that the Lord had instructed him to tell them.
005	DEU	001	004	This happened after he defeated Sihon king of the Amorites, who ruled in Heshbon, and then at Edrei after he defeated Og king of Bashan, who ruled in Ashtaroth.
005	DEU	001	005	Speaking on the east side of the Jordan in the land of Moab, Moses began to explain these instructions, saying:
005	DEU	001	006	The Lord our God told us at Horeb: “You have remained here beside this mountain for long enough.
005	DEU	001	007	Continue your journey and go to the hill country of the Amorites and all their neighbors, into the Jordan Valley, into the hill country, into the foothills, into the Negev, and along the coast to the country of the Canaanites up to Lebanon, as far as the great River Euphrates.
005	DEU	001	008	Look, I'm giving this land to you. Go and take ownership of the land that the Lord promised he would give to your fathers Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and to their descendants who would follow them.”
005	DEU	001	009	That's when I told you, “I can't take responsibility for all of you by myself.
005	DEU	001	010	The Lord your God has increased your numbers so much that today there are as many of you as there are stars in the sky.
005	DEU	001	011	May the Lord, the God of your forefathers, multiply you a thousand times and bless you as he has promised.
005	DEU	001	012	But how can I take on all your troubles, burdens, and arguments just by myself?
005	DEU	001	013	You must choose for yourselves wise, experienced men with good judgment from each of your tribes, and I will put them in charge as your leaders.”
005	DEU	001	014	You replied to me, saying, “Your proposal is a good one.”
005	DEU	001	015	So I summoned your tribal leaders, men with good judgment, and put them in charge of you, as commanders and officials for your tribes. Some were responsible for thousands, some for hundreds, some for fifties, and some for tens.
005	DEU	001	016	At the same time I gave strict instructions to your judges: “Hear the cases brought between your brothers, and make sure you are fair when you judge between a man and his brother or a foreigner living among you.
005	DEU	001	017	Don't show any favoritism when you judge—treat the powerful and the common people just the same. Don't let anyone intimidate you, because judgment is done on God's behalf. Bring me any case that is too hard for you, and I will hear it.”
005	DEU	001	018	This was also the time I instructed you about everything you had to do.
005	DEU	001	019	Following the orders of the Lord our God, we left Horeb and set off towards the hill country of the Amorites, passing through the whole of the large and terrifying desert that you yourselves have experienced. When we reached Kadesh-barnea,
005	DEU	001	020	I explained to you, “You have reached the hill country of the Amorites, which the Lord our God is giving to us.
005	DEU	001	021	Look, the Lord your God has given you the land! Go and take ownership of the land as the Lord, the God of your forefathers, has told you. Don't be frightened or terrified.”
005	DEU	001	022	Then you all came to me and suggested, “Let's send men on ahead to explore the land and report back to us about what route to take and which towns we'll come across.”
005	DEU	001	023	It seemed like a good plan to me, so I chose twelve of your men, one from each tribe.
005	DEU	001	024	They set off and went up into the hill country as far as the Valley of Eshcol, exploring the land.
005	DEU	001	025	They brought back some of the country's fruit, carrying it down to us, and gave us the report: “The Lord our God is giving us good land.”
005	DEU	001	026	But you didn't want to go. You rebelled against the instructions of the Lord your God.
005	DEU	001	027	You complained while you were in your tents and said, “It's because the Lord hates us that he led us out of Egypt in order to hand us over to the Amorites to be wiped out.
005	DEU	001	028	Where are we going? Our brothers terrified us because they told us: ‘The people are bigger and taller than us; the towns are large, with high walls that reach the sky. We even saw the descendants of the giant Anak there!’”
005	DEU	001	029	So I told you, “Don't be frightened or scared of them!
005	DEU	001	030	The Lord your God who leads your way will fight for you in the same way you saw him do for you in Egypt.
005	DEU	001	031	He did the same in the desert—you saw how the Lord your God carried you like a father carries his son during your whole journey until you arrived here.”
005	DEU	001	032	Despite all this, you didn't trust the Lord your God,
005	DEU	001	033	who led you on the journey, present in the fire by night and in the cloud by day, looking to find a place for you to camp and to show you the way to go.
005	DEU	001	034	When the Lord heard what you were saying, he got angry and swore an oath:
005	DEU	001	035	“Not a single one of this evil generation will see the good land I promised to give your forefathers,
005	DEU	001	036	except Caleb, son of Jephunneh. He will see it, and I will give him and his descendants the land he explored, because he was completely committed to the Lord.”
005	DEU	001	037	The Lord also got angry with me because of you. He told me, “Even you won't enter the country.
005	DEU	001	038	However, Joshua, son of Nun, your assistant, will enter it. Encourage him, for he will help Israel to occupy the land.
005	DEU	001	039	Your small children that you claimed would become prisoners, your children who at the time didn't know good from evil, they will be the ones to enter the land that I will give them, and they will occupy it.
005	DEU	001	040	But now turn around and head back into the desert on the road that leads to the Red Sea.”
005	DEU	001	041	But you answered and told me, “We have sinned against the Lord! We will go and we will fight and we will do everything the Lord our God has ordered us to do.” Then you all picked up your weapons and prepared for battle thinking it would be easy to go and fight in the hill country.
005	DEU	001	042	But the Lord instructed me, “Order them not to go and fight because I won't be with you to prevent you from being defeated by your enemies.”
005	DEU	001	043	I told you this, but you refused to listen. You defied the instructions of the Lord and arrogantly went to fight in the hill country.
