005	DEU	002	013	Then the Lord told us, “Go and cross over Zered Brook.” So we crossed over Zered Brook.
005	DEU	002	014	The time it took for us to travel from Kadesh-barnea to when we crossed over the Brook of Zered was thirty-eight years. By this time the entire generation of warriors had died and were no longer part of the camp, as the Lord had sworn to them would happen.
005	DEU	002	015	In fact the Lord worked against them to remove them from the camp, until they were all dead.
005	DEU	002	016	Once the people's warriors had died,
005	DEU	002	017	the Lord told me,
005	DEU	002	018	“Today you will cross out of Moab at the border near Ar.
005	DEU	002	019	However, when you enter Ammonite territory, don't cause them any trouble or fight with them for I'm not going to give you any Ammonite land, because I have given it to the descendants of Lot and it belongs to them.”
005	DEU	002	020	(This land was previously considered as the country of the Rephaim who used to live there. However, the Ammonites called them Zamzummites.
005	DEU	002	021	They were a strong and numerous people, as tall as the Anakim. But the Lord destroyed them when the Ammonites invaded and drove them out and settled there,
005	DEU	002	022	just as he'd done for the descendants of Esau who lived in Seir when he destroyed the Horites. They drove them out and settled where they used to live, and are still there to this day.
005	DEU	002	023	The Avvim, living in villages as far away as Gaza, were destroyed by the Philistines, who came from Crete, and settled where they used to live.)
005	DEU	002	024	Then the Lord told us, “Get up, go and cross the Arnon Valley. Look, I have handed over to you Sihon the Amorite, king of Heshbon, as well as his land. Go and start taking it over, and fight him in battle.
005	DEU	002	025	From this day on, I'm going to make all nations on earth dread you—they will be terrified of you. Because of the news they hear about you they will tremble in terror when you appear.”
005	DEU	002	026	Moses told the Israelites, “From the Kedemoth Desert I sent messengers with an offer of peace to Sihon, king of Heshbon, telling him,
005	DEU	002	027	‘Let us pass through your land. We'll stay on the main road and won't turn off either to the right or to the left.
005	DEU	002	028	Sell us food to eat and water to drink for money. Just let us pass through on foot,
005	DEU	002	029	just like the descendants of Esau living in Seir and the Moabites living in Ar allowed us, until we cross over the Jordan into the country that the Lord our God is giving to us.”
005	DEU	002	030	But Sihon king of Heshbon refused to let us pass through, for the Lord your God gave him a stubborn spirit and an obstinate attitude, so the Lord could hand him over to you, as he has now done.
005	DEU	002	031	Then the Lord told me, “Look, I have started handing Sihon and his land over to you. Now you can begin to conquer and take over his land.”
005	DEU	002	032	Sihon and his whole army came out to fight us at Jahaz.
005	DEU	002	033	The Lord our God handed him over to us, and we killed him, his sons, and all his army.
