# BOOK	007	JDG	Judges	Judges
007	JDG	001	001	After Joshua died, the Israelites asked the Lord, “Which tribe from among us should go first and attack the Canaanites?”
007	JDG	001	002	“Judah is to go first,” the Lord replied. “I have handed the land over to them.”
007	JDG	001	003	The men of Judah said to their relatives of the tribe of Simeon, “Come with us to the land that has been allotted to us, and fight together with us against the Canaanites. Then we'll do the same for you and your allotted land.” So the tribe of Simeon joined with them.
007	JDG	001	004	The men of Judah attacked the Canaanites and Perizzites, and the Lord handed them over in defeat. They killed ten thousand of the enemy at the town of Bezek.
007	JDG	001	005	There they confronted Adoni-bezek and fought with him, defeating the Canaanites and Perizzites.
007	JDG	001	006	Adoni-bezek ran away, but they chased after him and captured him, and then cut off his thumbs and big toes.
007	JDG	001	007	Adoni-bezek said, “I had seventy kings with their thumbs and big toes cut off picking up left-overs from under my table. Now God has paid me back in the same way what I did to them.” They took him to Jerusalem where he died.
007	JDG	001	008	The men of Judah attacked Jerusalem and conquered it. They killed the inhabitants with the sword and burned the town down.
007	JDG	001	009	After this the men of Judah went to fight against the Canaanites living in the hill country, in the Negev, and in the foothills of the lowlands.
007	JDG	001	010	They attacked the Canaanites who lived in Hebron (previously known as Kiriath Arba) and defeated Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai.
007	JDG	001	011	From there they went on to attack the people living in Debir (previously known as Kiriath Sepher).
007	JDG	001	012	Caleb announced, “I will give my daughter Acsah in marriage to whoever attacks and captures Kiriath Sepher.”
007	JDG	001	013	Othniel, son of Kenaz, Caleb's younger brother, was the one who captured it, so he gave him his daughter Acsah in marriage.
007	JDG	001	014	When Acsah came to Othniel, she encouraged him to ask her father for a field. As she got off her donkey, Caleb asked her, “What do you want?”
007	JDG	001	015	“Please give me a blessing,” she replied. “You gave me land that's like the desert, so please give me springs of water as well.” So Caleb gave her the upper and lower springs.
007	JDG	001	016	The descendants of Moses' father-in-law, the Kenite, went with the people of Judah from the city of palms to the wilderness of Judah in the Negev near Arad where they settled among the people.
007	JDG	001	017	Then Judah joined Simeon and defeated the Canaanites living in Zephath. They completely destroyed the town, so they named it Hormah.
007	JDG	001	018	Judah also captured the towns of Gaza, Ashkelon, and Ekron, each with its surrounding territory.
007	JDG	001	019	The Lord was with Judah, and they took over the hill country, but they could not drive out the people living on the plain because they had iron chariots.
007	JDG	001	020	As Moses had stipulated, Hebron was given to Caleb, who drove out from it the descendants of three sons of Anak.
007	JDG	001	021	However, Benjamin could not drive out the Jebusites, the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so the Jebusites live among the people of Benjamin in Jerusalem to this very day.
007	JDG	001	022	The descendants of Joseph went and attacked the town of Bethel, and the Lord was with them.
007	JDG	001	023	They sent spies to investigate Bethel, which was previously known as Luz.
007	JDG	001	024	The spies saw a man leaving the town and told him, “Please show us how to get into town, and we will treat you well.”
007	JDG	001	025	The man showed them the way into the town, and they killed all the inhabitants except the man and his family, whom they let go.
