007	JDG	019	001	At that time Israel didn't have a king. A Levite who was living in a remote area in the hill country of Ephraim married a concubine-wife from Bethlehem in Judah.
007	JDG	019	002	But she was unfaithful to him and left him to return to her father's house in Bethlehem. She was there for four months.
007	JDG	019	003	Then her husband went after her, to talk kindly with her and bring her back home. With him went his servant and two donkeys. She took him to her father's house and when her father met him, he gladly welcomed him.
007	JDG	019	004	Her father pressed him to stay with them, so he remained for three days, eating, drinking, and sleeping there.
007	JDG	019	005	On the fourth day he and his concubine got up early in the morning and prepared to leave, but her father said to his son-in-law, “You'll feel better if you have something to eat before you go.”
007	JDG	019	006	So the two men sat down to eat and drink together. The father said to his son-in law, “Please agree to spend another night here, and you can enjoy yourself!”
007	JDG	019	007	The man got up to leave, but his father-in-law pressed him to stay, so in the end he spent the night there.
007	JDG	019	008	On the fifth day he got up early in the morning to leave. But his father-in-law said, “Eat before you go, then leave later this afternoon.” So they had a meal together.
007	JDG	019	009	When he got up to leave with his concubine and his servant, his father-in-law told him, “Look it's late—it's already evening. Spend the night here. The day's almost over. Stay here the night and enjoy yourself, then tomorrow you can get up early and be on your way home.”
007	JDG	019	010	But the man didn't want to spend another night, so he got up and left. He headed towards the town of Jebus (now called Jerusalem) with his two saddled donkeys and his concubine.
007	JDG	019	011	As they approached Jebus the day was over, and the servant said to his master, “Sir, why don't we stop here at this Jebusite town for the night?”
007	JDG	019	012	But his master replied, “No, we're not going to stop in this town where only foreigners live and no Israelites. We'll continue on to Gibeah.”
007	JDG	019	013	Then he told his servant, “Come on, let's try and get to Gibeah or Ramah and spend the night somewhere there.”
007	JDG	019	014	So they carried on and reached Gibeah in the territory of Benjamin just as the sun was setting.
