008	RUT	003	002	Don't ignore the fact that Boaz, whose women you worked with, is closely related to us. Now tonight he will be busy winnowing grain on the threshing floor.
008	RUT	003	003	Have a bath, put on some perfume, wear your best clothes, and go down to the threshing floor—but don't let him recognize you. Once he's finished eating and drinking,
008	RUT	003	004	watch where he goes to lie down. Then go and uncover his feet and lie down. Then he will tell you what to do.”
008	RUT	003	005	“I'll do everything you told me,” said Ruth.
008	RUT	003	006	She went down to the threshing floor and did what her mother-in-law had told her to do.
008	RUT	003	007	After Boaz had finished eating and drinking, and was feeling contented, he went and lay down beside the grain pile. Ruth quietly approached him, uncovered his feet, and lay down.
008	RUT	003	008	Around midnight Boaz suddenly woke up. Bending forward he was surprised to see a woman lying at his feet.
008	RUT	003	009	“Who are you?” he asked. “I'm Ruth, your servant,” she replied. “Please spread the corner of your cloak over me, for you are my family redeemer.”
008	RUT	003	010	“May the Lord bless you, my daughter,” he said. “You are showing even more loyalty and love to the family than before. You haven't gone looking for a younger man, of whatever social status.
008	RUT	003	011	So don't worry, my daughter. I will do everything you ask—everyone in town knows you are a woman of good character.
008	RUT	003	012	However, even though I'm one of your family redeemers, there's one who is more closely related than I am.
008	RUT	003	013	Stay here tonight, and in the morning if he wants to redeem you, then fine, let him do it. But if he doesn't, then I promise you in the name of the living Lord, I will redeem you. Lie down here until morning.”
008	RUT	003	014	So Ruth lay at his feet until morning. Then she got up before it was light enough to recognize anyone because Boaz had told her, “No one must know that a woman came here to the threshing floor.”
