# BOOK	009	1SA	1 Samuel	1 Samuel
009	1SA	001	001	Once there was a man from Ramathaim-zophim in the hill country of Ephraim. His name was Elkanah, son of Jeroham, son of Elihu, son of Tohu, son of Zuph, from the tribe of Ephraim.
009	1SA	001	002	He had two wives. The name of the first wife was Hannah, and the name of the second, Peninnah. Peninnah had children, but Hannah had none.
009	1SA	001	003	Every year Elkanah would leave his town and go to worship and sacrifice to the Lord Almighty at Shiloh, where Eli's two sons, Hophni and Phinehas, were the Lord's priests.
009	1SA	001	004	Whenever Elkanah offered a sacrifice, he would give portions of it to Peninnah his wife and to all her sons and daughters.
009	1SA	001	005	He would give an extra portion to Hannah, to show his love for her even though the Lord hadn't given her any children.
009	1SA	001	006	Her rival—the other wife—would taunt her badly to upset her because the Lord hadn't given her any children.
009	1SA	001	007	This went on for years. Whenever Hannah went to the Lord's Temple, Peninnah would taunt her until she cried and couldn't eat.
009	1SA	001	008	“Hannah, what are you crying for?” her husband Elkanah would ask. “Why don't you eat? Why are you so upset? Aren't I better to you than ten sons?”
009	1SA	001	009	One time when they had finished eating and drinking in Shiloh, Hannah got up and went to the Temple. Eli the priest was sitting on his seat by the entrance to the Lord's Temple.
009	1SA	001	010	She was terribly upset, and prayed to the Lord as she cried and cried.
009	1SA	001	011	She made a vow, asking, “Lord Almighty, if only you would pay attention to the suffering of your servant and remember me, and not forget me but give me a son, then I will dedicate him to the Lord for his whole life, and no razor shall ever touch his head.”
009	1SA	001	012	As Hannah went on praying before the Lord, Eli watched her mouth.
009	1SA	001	013	Hannah was praying in her head, and though her lips were moving, her voice made no sound. Eli thought she must be drunk.
009	1SA	001	014	“Do you have to come here drunk?” he asked. “Get rid of your wine!”
009	1SA	001	015	“It's not that, my lord,” Hannah replied. “I'm a very miserable woman. I haven't been drinking wine or beer; I'm just pouring my heart out to the Lord.
009	1SA	001	016	Please don't think I'm a bad woman! I have been praying because of all my troubles and grief.”
009	1SA	001	017	“Go in peace, and may the God of Israel give you what you have asked him for,” Eli replied.
009	1SA	001	018	“Thank you for your kindness to your servant,” she said. Then she went on her way, had something to eat, and she didn't look sad any more.
009	1SA	001	019	Elkanah and Hannah got up early the next morning to worship the Lord, and then they went home to Ramah. Elkanah made love to his wife Hannah, and the Lord honored her request.
009	1SA	001	020	In due course she became pregnant and gave birth to a son. She named him Samuel, saying, “Because I asked the Lord for him.”
009	1SA	001	021	Elkanah and all his family went to make the yearly sacrifice to the Lord and to fulfill his vow.
009	1SA	001	022	But Hannah did not go. She told her husband, “Once the boy is weaned I will take him to be presented to the Lord and to remain there forever.”
009	1SA	001	023	“Do as you see fit,” her husband Elkanah replied. “Stay here until you have weaned him. May the Lord fulfill what he has said.” So Hannah stayed behind and nursed her son until she had weaned him.
009	1SA	001	024	When she had weaned him, Hannah took the boy with her, along with a three-year-old bull, an ephah of flour, and a wineskin containing wine. Even though the boy was young, she brought him to the Lord's Temple at Shiloh.
009	1SA	001	025	After they had slaughtered the bull, they presented the boy to Eli.
009	1SA	001	026	“Please, my lord,” said Hannah, “as surely as you live, my lord, I am the woman who stood here with you praying to the Lord.
009	1SA	001	027	I prayed for this boy, and since the Lord has given me what I asked him for,
009	1SA	001	028	now I'm giving him to the Lord. As long as he lives he will be dedicated to the Lord.” And he worshiped the Lord there.
009	1SA	002	001	Hannah prayed, “I'm so happy in the Lord! He has empowered me! Now I have plenty to say in answer to those who hate me. I celebrate your salvation!
009	1SA	002	002	There's no one holy like the Lord—no one apart from you, no Rock like our God!
009	1SA	002	003	Don't speak so conceitedly! Don't talk so arrogantly! For the Lord is a God who knows everything—doesn't he judge what you do?
009	1SA	002	004	The weapons of the powerful are shattered, while those who stumble along are made strong.
009	1SA	002	005	Those who used to have plenty of food now have to work to earn a crust, while those who used to be hungry now have become fat. The woman who was childless now has seven children, while the woman with many children fades away.
009	1SA	002	006	The Lord kills and he revives; he sends some down to the grave, but he raises others up.
009	1SA	002	007	The Lord makes some poor, but others rich; he brings some down, but he lifts others up.
009	1SA	002	008	He helps the poor up from the dust; he raises the lowborn from the trash pile and seats them with the upper class in places of honor. For the foundations of the earth belong to the Lord, and he has placed the world on them.
009	1SA	002	009	He will take care of those who trust him, but the wicked vanish into the darkness, for people don't succeed through their own strength.
009	1SA	002	010	The Lord crushes his enemies, he thunders against them from heaven. He rules the whole earth; he strengthens his king, and gives power to the one he has anointed.”
009	1SA	002	011	Then Elkanah went home to Ramah while the boy stayed with Eli the priest serving the Lord.
009	1SA	002	012	Eli's sons were worthless men who didn't have any time for the Lord
