009	1SA	028	013	“Don't be scared,” the king told her. “What can you see?” “I see a god coming up out of the ground,” the woman replied.
009	1SA	028	014	“What does he look like?” Saul asked. “An old man is coming up,” she replied. “He has a robe wrapped around him.” Saul thought it must be Samuel, and he bowed facedown in respect.
009	1SA	028	015	Samuel said to Saul, “Why are you bothering me by bringing me up?” “I'm in terrible trouble,” Saul replied. “The Philistines are attacking me, and God has abandoned me. He doesn't answer me anymore, either by prophets or by dreams. That's why I have called you up so you tell me what to do.”
009	1SA	028	016	“Why come and ask me when the Lord has abandoned you and has become your enemy?” Samuel asked.
