009	1SA	028	024	The woman had a fattened calf at the house, and she quickly went and slaughtered it. She also got some flour, kneaded it, and baked some unleavened bread.
009	1SA	028	025	She served the meal to Saul and his men, and they ate it. Then they got up and left, the same night.
009	1SA	029	001	The Philistines gathered all their armies at Aphek, and the Israelites set up camp by the spring in Jezreel.
009	1SA	029	002	The Philistine rulers were marching out in their divisions of hundreds and thousands with David and his men at the rear with King Achish.
009	1SA	029	003	But the Philistine commanders asked, “What are these Hebrews doing here?” Achish replied to the Philistine commanders, “That's David, an officer of King Saul of Israel. He's been with me for a long time, years even, and I haven't found any fault in him since the day he came over to our side up till now.”
009	1SA	029	004	But the Philistine commanders got angry with Achish, and told him, “Send him back to the place he came from, to the town you assigned to him. He can't go with us into battle. What if he turns on us during the fighting? What a great way for him to please his master—by handing over the heads of our men!
009	1SA	029	005	Isn't this the David they sing about in their dances: ‘Saul has killed his thousands, and David his tens of thousands’?”
009	1SA	029	006	So Achish called David over and told him, “As the Lord lives, you are honest and you've done what's right as far as I can see. As far as I'm concerned you should march with me into battle because I haven't found any fault in you from the day you arrived until now. But the other leaders don't approve of you.
009	1SA	029	007	So go back home in peace, and that way you won't do anything to upset the Philistine leaders.”
009	1SA	029	008	“But what have I done?” David asked. “What fault have you found in me, your servant, from the day I came to you until now, that would prevent me from going to fight the enemies of my lord the king?”
009	1SA	029	009	“As far as I'm concerned, you're as good as an angel of God,” Achish replied. “But the Philistine commanders have stated, ‘He can't go into battle with us.’
009	1SA	029	010	So get up early tomorrow morning and leave with your men as soon as it's light.”
009	1SA	029	011	David and his men got up early in the morning and went back to the country of the Philistines. But the Philistines advanced on Jezreel.
009	1SA	030	001	Three days later David and his men arrived back in Ziklag. Some Amalekites had raided the Negev and Ziklag. They had attacked Ziklag and burned it down.
009	1SA	030	002	They had captured the women and everyone else there, young and old. They hadn't killed anyone, but they took everyone with them as they left.
009	1SA	030	003	When David and his men arrived back in town, they found it burned to the ground, and their wives and children captured.
009	1SA	030	004	David and his men cried loudly until they couldn't cry any more.
009	1SA	030	005	David's two wives had also been taken as prisoners—Ahinoam from Jezreel and Abigail, Nabal's widow, from Carmel.
009	1SA	030	006	David was in a great deal of trouble, because the men were so upset over losing their children that they began to talk of stoning him. But trusting in the Lord his God,
009	1SA	030	007	David went to Abiathar the priest, the son of Ahimelech, and said, “Bring me the ephod.” Abiathar brought it to him.
009	1SA	030	008	David asked the Lord, “Should I chase after these raiders? Will I catch up with them?” “Yes, chase after them,” the Lord replied, “for you will definitely catch up with them and rescue the prisoners.”
009	1SA	030	009	David and six hundred of his men set off for the Besor Valley.
009	1SA	030	010	Two hundred of them remained behind there because they were too tired to cross the valley while David continued on with four hundred men.
009	1SA	030	011	They came across an Egyptian in the countryside and they took him to David. They gave him some food to eat and water to drink.
009	1SA	030	012	They also gave him a piece of a fig cake and two raisin cakes. He ate them and recovered, because he hadn't had any food or water for three days and nights.
009	1SA	030	013	“Whose slave are you, and where do you come from?” David asked him. “I'm an Egyptian,” he replied, “the slave of an Amalekite. My master left me behind three days ago when I got sick.
009	1SA	030	014	We raided the Kerethites in the Negev, as well as the part that belongs to Judah, and the Negev of Caleb. We burned Ziklag too.”
009	1SA	030	015	“Can you lead me to these raiders?” David asked. “If you swear to me by God that you won't kill me or hand me over to my master, then I'll take you to them,” the man replied.
009	1SA	030	016	He led David to the Amalekites, where they were spread out all over the place, eating, drinking, and dancing because of the large haul of plunder they had taken from the lands of the Philistines and of Judah.
009	1SA	030	017	David attacked them from dusk until the following evening. Nobody escaped, except for four hundred men who managed to get away, riding on camels.
009	1SA	030	018	David got back everything the Amalekites had taken, including his two wives.
009	1SA	030	019	Everything was accounted for—all the adults and children, as well as all the plunder the Amalekites had taken. David brought everything back.
009	1SA	030	020	He also recovered all the flocks and herds. His men drove them ahead of the other livestock, shouting, “This is David's plunder!”
009	1SA	030	021	When David got back to the two hundred men who had been too tired to continue with him from the Besor Valley, they came to meet him and the men with him. As David approached the men to greet them,
009	1SA	030	022	all the unpleasant, good-for-nothing men of those who had gone with David said, “They weren't with us, so we won't share the plunder that we took, except to give them back their wives and children. They can take them and leave.”
009	1SA	030	023	But David intervened, saying, “No, my brothers, you shouldn't do this with what the Lord has given us. He has protected us and handed over to us the raiders that had attacked us.
