009	1SA	031	001	Meanwhile the Philistines had attacked Israel, and the Israelite army ran away from them, and many were killed on Mount Gilboa.
009	1SA	031	002	The Philistines chased down Saul and his sons, killing Saul's sons Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua.
009	1SA	031	003	The fighting became very intense around Saul, and the arrows of the Philistine archers found their target, wounding Saul very badly.
009	1SA	031	004	Saul said to his armor-bearer, “Take your sword and kill me, or these heathen men will come and kill and torture me!” But the armor-bearer didn't want to do it because he was too afraid. So Saul took his own sword and fell on it.
