010	2SA	022	032	For who is God except the Lord? Who is a Rock, except our God?
010	2SA	022	033	God makes me strong and keeps me safe.
010	2SA	022	034	He makes me surefooted like the deer, able to walk the heights in safety.
010	2SA	022	035	He teaches me how to fight in battle; he gives me the strength to draw a bronze bow.
010	2SA	022	036	You protect me with the shield of your salvation; your help has made me great.
010	2SA	022	037	You gave me room to walk, and prevented my feet from slipping.
010	2SA	022	038	I chased my enemies, and caught up with them. I did not turn around until I had destroyed them.
010	2SA	022	039	I struck them down—they couldn't get up. They fell at my feet.
010	2SA	022	040	You made me strong for the battle; you made those who rose up against me kneel low before me.
010	2SA	022	041	You made my enemies run away; I destroyed all my enemies.
