011	1KI	016	020	The rest of what happened in Zimri's reign and his rebellion are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.
011	1KI	016	021	After this the people of Israel were divided. Half supported Tibni, son of Ginath, as king, while the other half supported Omri.
011	1KI	016	022	However, those on Omri's side defeated Tibni's supporters. Tibni was killed and Omri became king.
011	1KI	016	023	Omri became king of Israel in the thirty-first year of the reign of King Asa of Judah. He reigned for a total of twelve years (six of them were in Tirzah).
011	1KI	016	024	He purchased the hill of Samaria from Shemer for two talents of silver. He fortified the hill, and named the city that he built Samaria, after Shemer, the previous owner of the hill.
011	1KI	016	025	Omri did what was evil in the Lord's sight—in fact he did more evil than those who lived before him.
011	1KI	016	026	For he followed all the ways of Jeroboam, son of Nebat, and in his sins which he made Israel commit, worshiping their useless idols which angered the Lord, the God of Israel.
011	1KI	016	027	The rest of what happened in Omri's reign, what he did, and his achievements are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.
011	1KI	016	028	Omri died and was buried in Samaria. His son Ahab succeeded him as king.
011	1KI	016	029	Ahab, son of Omri, became king of Israel in the thirty-eighth year of the reign of King Asa of Judah. He reigned in Samaria for twenty-two years.
011	1KI	016	030	Ahab, son of Omri, did evil in the Lord's sight, more than those who lived before him.
011	1KI	016	031	He didn't see anything to worry about in following the sins of Jeroboam, son of Nebat, and he even married Jezebel, daughter of Ethbaal, king of the Sidonians, and started to serve and worship Baal.
011	1KI	016	032	Ahab made an altar for Baal in the temple of Baal that he had built in Samaria.
011	1KI	016	033	Then he put up an Asherah pole. In this way Ahab did more to anger the Lord, the God of Israel, than all the kings of Israel before him.
011	1KI	016	034	During Ahab's reign Hiel of Bethel rebuilt Jericho. He sacrificed Abiram his firstborn son when he laid its foundation, and sacrificed Segub his youngest son when he constructed its gates. This fulfilled the message the Lord had given through Joshua, son of Nun.
011	1KI	017	001	Elijah the Tishbite (from Tishbe in Gilead), told Ahab, “As the Lord, the God of Israel, lives, the one I serve, in the years to come there will not be any dew or rain unless I say so!”
011	1KI	017	002	Then the Lord told Elijah,
011	1KI	017	003	“Leave here and go east. Hide in the valley of the Cherith brook where it meets the Jordan.
011	1KI	017	004	You can drink from the brook, and I have ordered ravens to bring you food you there.”
011	1KI	017	005	So Elijah did what the Lord told him. He went to the valley of the Cherith brook, where it meets the Jordan, and stayed there.
011	1KI	017	006	Ravens brought him bread and meat both in the morning and in the evening, and he drank from the brook.
011	1KI	017	007	A while later the brook dried up because there had been no rain in the land.
011	1KI	017	008	Then the Lord told Elijah,
011	1KI	017	009	“Leave here and go to Zarephath near Sidon and stay there. I have given instructions to a widow there to provide you with food.”
011	1KI	017	010	So he left for Zarephath. When he arrived at the entrance to the town, he saw a woman, a widow, gathering sticks. He called her over and asked her, “Could you bring me a little water in a cup so I can have a drink?”
011	1KI	017	011	As she was going to get it, he called after her and said, “Oh, and please bring me a piece of bread.”
011	1KI	017	012	She replied, “As the Lord your God lives, I have no bread, only a handful of flour is left in a jar and a little bit of olive oil in a jug. Right now I am gathering a few sticks so I can go and cook what's left for myself and my son so we can eat it, and then we'll die.”
011	1KI	017	013	Elijah said to her, “Don't be afraid. Go home and do what you said. But first make me a small loaf of bread from what you have and bring it to me. Then make something for yourself and your son.
011	1KI	017	014	For this is what the Lord, the God of Israel, says: ‘The jar of flour will not become empty and the jug of olive oil will not run out until the day the Lord sends rain to water the ground.’”
011	1KI	017	015	She went and did as Elijah had told her, and Elijah, the widow, and her household were able to eat for many days.
011	1KI	017	016	The jar of flour did not become empty and the jug of olive oil did not run out, just as the Lord had said through Elijah.
011	1KI	017	017	Later on the woman's son fell sick. (She was the one who owned the house.) He went from bad to worse, and finally he died.
011	1KI	017	018	“What are you doing to me, man of God?” the woman asked Elijah. “Have you come to remind me about my sins and cause my son to die?”
011	1KI	017	019	“Give me your son,” Elijah replied. He picked him up from her arms, carried him upstairs to the room where he was staying, and laid him on his bed.
011	1KI	017	020	Then he cried out to the Lord, saying, “Lord my God, why have you allowed this to happen to this widow who has opened her home to me, this terrible tragedy of causing her son to die?”
011	1KI	017	021	He stretched himself out on the boy three times, and cried out to the Lord, “Lord my God, please let this boy's life return to him!”
011	1KI	017	022	The Lord responded to Elijah's cry. The boy's life returned to him, and he lived!
011	1KI	017	023	Elijah took the boy and brought him down from the room into the house, and gave him to his mother. “See, your son is alive,” Elijah told her.
011	1KI	017	024	“Now I'm convinced that you are a man of God, and that what the Lord speaks through you is the truth,” the woman replied.
011	1KI	018	001	Sometime later, during the third year, a message from the Lord came to Elijah: “Go and appear before Ahab, and I will send rain on the earth.”
011	1KI	018	002	So Elijah went to appear before Ahab. In the meantime the famine had become severe in Samaria.
011	1KI	018	003	Ahab summoned Obadiah, the manager of his palace (Obadiah was a very sincere believer in the Lord.
011	1KI	018	004	While Jezebel was busy killing the Lord's prophets, Obadiah had taken one hundred prophets and hidden them, fifty in each of two caves, and had provided them with food and water.)
011	1KI	018	005	Ahab told Obadiah, “Go throughout the country and check all the springs and valleys. Perhaps we can find some grass to keep the horses and mules alive so we will not lose any of the animals.”
011	1KI	018	006	So they divided the land between them. Ahab went in one direction, and Obadiah the other.
011	1KI	018	007	As Obadiah went on his way, Elijah came to meet him. Obadiah recognized him, bowed down to the ground, and said, “Is it you, my lord Elijah?”
011	1KI	018	008	“It's me,” Elijah replied. “Go and tell your master, ‘Elijah is here.’”
011	1KI	018	009	“How have I sinned that you are handing me, your servant, over to Ahab to be killed?
011	1KI	018	010	As the Lord your God lives, there's no nation or kingdom where my master hasn't sent someone to search for you. When a nation or kingdom said you weren't there, he made them swear that they couldn't find you.
011	1KI	018	011	And now you're telling me to go to my master and announce, ‘Elijah is here!’
011	1KI	018	012	I have no idea where the Spirit of the Lord will take you after I leave you. If I go and tell Ahab and then he can't find you, he's going to kill me, even though I, your servant, have worshiped the Lord since I was young.
011	1KI	018	013	Didn't you hear, my lord, what I did when Jezebel was busy killing the Lord's prophets? I hid a hundred of the Lord's prophets, fifty in each of two caves, and provided them with food and water.
011	1KI	018	014	And now you're telling me to go to my master and announce, ‘Elijah is here.’ He's going to kill me!”
011	1KI	018	015	Elijah replied, “As the Lord Almighty lives, the one I serve, I will definitely appear before Ahab today.”
011	1KI	018	016	So Obadiah went to meet Ahab and told him, and then Ahab went to meet Elijah.
011	1KI	018	017	When Ahab saw Elijah, he said to him, “Is that you—you who are causing trouble for Israel?”
011	1KI	018	018	“I'm not causing trouble for Israel,” Elijah replied. “It's you and your father's family! You have rejected the Lord's commands and are worshiping the Baals.
011	1KI	018	019	Now call together all of Israel and meet me on Mount Carmel, along with the four hundred and fifty prophets of Baal and the four hundred prophets of Asherah, who are supported by Jezebel.”
011	1KI	018	020	So Ahab summoned all of Israel and also gathered the prophets on Mount Carmel.
011	1KI	018	021	Elijah approached the people and asked them, “How long will you hobble along, hesitating between two opposite beliefs? If the Lord is God, then follow him. But if Baal is God, then follow him.” But the people didn't answer.
011	1KI	018	022	Then Elijah told them, “I am the only one left of the Lord's prophets—just me alone—but Baal has four hundred and fifty prophets.
011	1KI	018	023	Provide us with two bulls. Let the prophets of Baal choose for themselves the one they want, and have them cut it into pieces and place it on the firewood. But don't set fire to it. I will prepare the other bull and place it on the firewood but I won't set fire to it.
011	1KI	018	024	Then you call on your god by name, and I will call on the Lord by name. The god who replies by sending fire—he is God.” Then all the people said, “We agree to what you say.”
011	1KI	018	025	Elijah said to the prophets of Baal, “You choose one of the bulls and prepare it first, because there are so many of you. Call on your god by name, but don't light the fire.”
011	1KI	018	026	So they took the bull provided and prepared it. Then they called on Baal by name from morning until noon. “Baal, answer us!” they pleaded. But no voice was heard, no one answered. They hobbled in a dance around the altar they had made.
011	1KI	018	027	At noon Elijah began to mock them. “Shout really loud!” he said. “Isn't he meant to be a god? Maybe he's meditating, or he's gone to the bathroom, or he's away on a trip! Maybe he's asleep and has to be woken up!”
011	1KI	018	028	They shouted even louder and cut themselves with swords and spears until they bled. This was their usual way of worshiping.
011	1KI	018	029	Noon came and went, and they went on with their manic “prophesying” until the time of the evening sacrifice. But no voice was heard, no one answered, no one was listening.
011	1KI	018	030	Then Elijah told everyone, “Come over here to me.” They went over to him, and he repaired the altar of the Lord that had been torn down.
011	1KI	018	031	Elijah took twelve stones to represent the tribes of the sons of Jacob. (Jacob was the one who received the Lord's message that said, “Israel shall be your name.”)
011	1KI	018	032	With the stones he built an altar in the Lord's name. He dug a ditch around it that could hold two seahs of seed.
011	1KI	018	033	He put the wood in place, cut the bull into pieces, and laid it on the wood. Then he told them, “Fill up four large jars with water and pour it over the offering and the wood.”
011	1KI	018	034	“Do it again,” he said. So they did. “Do it for a third time,” he said. So they did it for the third time.
011	1KI	018	035	The water ran down all over the altar and even filled the ditch.
011	1KI	018	036	At the time of the evening sacrifice, the prophet Elijah went over to the altar and prayed: “Lord, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, demonstrate today that you are God in Israel, that I am your servant, and that everything I have done has been at your command.
011	1KI	018	037	Answer me, Lord! Answer me, so that these people will know that you, Lord, are God, and that you are bringing them back to you.”
011	1KI	018	038	Then the fire of the Lord came down and burned up the sacrifice, the wood, the stones, and the soil—it even licked up the water in the ditch!
011	1KI	018	039	When all the people saw this, they fell facedown on the ground and shouted, “The Lord, he is God! The Lord, he is God!”
011	1KI	018	040	Then Elijah ordered them, “Grab hold of the prophets of Baal. Don't let any escape!” They grabbed them, and Elijah brought them down to the Kishon Valley and killed them there.
