# BOOK	012	2KI	2 Kings	2 Kings
012	2KI	001	001	After Ahab died, Moab rebelled against Israel.
012	2KI	001	002	Ahaziah had fallen through the lattice-work of his upper room in Samaria and had hurt himself badly. So he sent out messengers, telling them: “Go and ask Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron, whether I will get better from this injury.”
012	2KI	001	003	But the angel of the Lord told Elijah the Tishbite, “Go and meet the messengers of the king of Samaria and ask them, ‘Is it because there's no God in Israel that you're going to ask advice from Baal-Zebub, the god of Ekron?’
012	2KI	001	004	So this is the Lord's answer: ‘You will not leave the bed on which you are lying. You're definitely going to die.’” And Elijah left.
012	2KI	001	005	The messengers returned to the king, and he asked them, “Why have you come back?”
