012	2KI	014	001	Amaziah, son of Joash, became king of Judah in the second year of the reign of Jehoash, son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel.
012	2KI	014	002	He was twenty-five when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem for twenty-nine years. His mother's name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.
012	2KI	014	003	He did what was right in the Lord's sight, but not in the same way as his forefather David had. He did everything just as his father Joash had done.
012	2KI	014	004	But the high places were not removed. The people still were sacrificing and presenting burnt offerings in those places.
