012	2KI	014	023	Jeroboam, son of Jehoash, became king of Israel in the fifteenth year of the reign of Amaziah, son of Joash, king of Judah. He reigned in Samaria for forty-one years.
012	2KI	014	024	He did what was evil in the Lord's sight and did not end all the sins that Jeroboam, son of Nebat, had made Israel commit.
012	2KI	014	025	He restored the border of Israel to where it had been, from Lebo-hamath as far as the Sea of the Arabah, as the Lord, the God of Israel, had said through his servant Jonah, son of Amittai, the prophet, who came from Gath-hepher.
012	2KI	014	026	The Lord had seen how badly the Israelites were suffering, both slave and free. No one was there to help Israel.
012	2KI	014	027	However, since the Lord had said that he would not wipe out Israel, he saved them through Jeroboam, son of Jehoash.
012	2KI	014	028	The rest of what happened in Jeroboam's reign, all he did, his great achievements and the battles he fought, and how he recovered for Israel both Damascus and Hamath, are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.
012	2KI	014	029	Jeroboam died and was buried with the kings of Israel. His son Zechariah succeeded him as king.
012	2KI	015	001	Azariah, son of Amaziah, became king of Judah in the twenty-seventh year of the reign of Jeroboam, king of Israel.
012	2KI	015	002	He was sixteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem for fifty-two years. His mother's name was Jecoliah of Jerusalem.
012	2KI	015	003	He did what was right in the Lord's sight, just as his father Amaziah had done.
012	2KI	015	004	But the high places were not removed. The people still were sacrificing and presenting burnt offerings in those places.
012	2KI	015	005	The Lord touched the king and he had leprosy until the day he died. He lived in isolation in a separate house. His son Jotham was in charge of the palace and was the country's actual ruler.
012	2KI	015	006	The rest of what happened in Azariah's reign and all he did are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Judah.
012	2KI	015	007	Azariah died and was buried with his forefathers in the City of David. His son Jotham succeeded him as king.
012	2KI	015	008	Zechariah, son of Jeroboam, became king of Israel in the thirty-eighth year of the reign of Azariah, king of Judah. He reigned in Samaria for six months.
012	2KI	015	009	He did what was evil in the Lord's sight, as his forefathers had done. He did not end the sins that Jeroboam, son of Nebat, had made Israel commit.
012	2KI	015	010	Then Shallum, son of Jabesh, plotted against Zechariah. He attacked him, murdering him in front of the people, and took over as king.
012	2KI	015	011	The rest of the events of Zechariah's reign are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.
012	2KI	015	012	In this way what the Lord told Jehu came true: “Your descendants will sit on the throne of Israel to the fourth generation.”
012	2KI	015	013	Shallum, son of Jabesh, became king in the thirty-ninth year of the reign of King Uzziah of Judah. He reigned in Samaria for one month.
012	2KI	015	014	Then Menahem, son of Gadi, went from Tirzah to Samaria, attacked and murdered Shallum, son of Jabesh, and took over as king.
012	2KI	015	015	The rest of the events of Shallum's reign and the rebellion he plotted are recorded in the Book of Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.
012	2KI	015	016	At that time Menahem, starting from Tirzah, attacked Tiphsah and the region nearby, because they would not surrender the town to him. So he destroyed Tiphsah and ripped open all the pregnant women.
012	2KI	015	017	Menahem, son of Gadi, became king of Israel in the thirty-ninth year of the reign of King Azariah of Judah. He reigned in Samaria for ten years.
012	2KI	015	018	Throughout his reign he did what was evil in the Lord's sight. He did not end the sins that Jeroboam, son of Nebat, had made Israel commit.
