012	2KI	018	034	Where were the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where were the gods of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivvah? Were they able to save Samaria from me?
012	2KI	018	035	Which one of all the gods of these countries has saved their land from me? How then could the Lord save Jerusalem from me?”
012	2KI	018	036	But the people remained silent and didn't say anything, for Hezekiah had given the order, “Don't answer him.”
012	2KI	018	037	Then Eliakim, son of Hilkiah, the palace manager, Shebna the scribe, and Joah, son of Asaph, the record-keeper, went to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and they told him what the Assyrian army general had said.
012	2KI	019	001	When Hezekiah heard it, he tore his clothes, put on sackcloth, and went into the Lord's Temple.
