013	1CH	023	001	When David was old, having lived a long life, he made his son Solomon king of Israel.
013	1CH	023	002	He also summoned all the leaders of Israel, the priests, and the Levites.
013	1CH	023	003	The Levites over thirty years old were counted, and there was 38,000 in total.
013	1CH	023	004	“Of these 24,000 will be in charge of the work of the house of the Lord, while 6,000 will be officers and judges,” David instructed.
013	1CH	023	005	“And 4,000 will be gatekeepers, while 4,000 will praise the Lord using the musical instruments I have provided for praise worship.”
013	1CH	023	006	David divided them into sections corresponding to the sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.
013	1CH	023	007	The sons of Gershon: Ladan and Shimei.
013	1CH	023	008	The sons of Ladan: Jehiel (chief), and Zetham, and Joel, three in total.
013	1CH	023	009	The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran, three in total. These were the leaders of the families of Ladan.
013	1CH	023	010	The sons of Shimei: Jahath, Zizah, Jeush, and Beriah—four in total.
013	1CH	023	011	Jahath (chief), and Zizah (second); but because Jeush and Beriah did not have many sons they were counted as a single family.
013	1CH	023	012	The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel—a total of four.
013	1CH	023	013	The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses. Aaron was dedicated to service with the most holy things, that he and his sons should always present offerings to the Lord, and minister before him, and give blessings in his name forever.
013	1CH	023	014	As for Moses, the man of God, his sons were included with the tribe of Levi.
013	1CH	023	015	The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer.
013	1CH	023	016	The sons of Gershom: Shebuel (chief).
013	1CH	023	017	The sons of Eliezer: Rehabiah (chief). Eliezer had no other sons, but Rehabiah had many sons.
013	1CH	023	018	The sons of Izhar: Shelomith (chief).
013	1CH	023	019	The sons of Hebron: Jeriah (chief), Amariah (second), Jahaziel (third), and Jekameam (fourth).
013	1CH	023	020	The sons of Uzziel: Micah (chief) and Isshiah (second).
013	1CH	023	021	The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish.
013	1CH	023	022	Eleazar died without having sons, only daughters. Their cousins, the sons of Kish, married them.
013	1CH	023	023	The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jeremoth—three in total.
013	1CH	023	024	These were the descendants of Levi by family, the heads of families chiefs listed individually by name—those twenty years of age or more who served in the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	023	025	For David said, “The Lord, the God of Israel, has given peace to his people, and he will live in Jerusalem forever.
013	1CH	023	026	So the Levites don't need to carry the Tent any longer, or anything needed for its service.”
013	1CH	023	027	In accordance with David's final instructions, Levites twenty years of age or more were counted.
013	1CH	023	028	Their assignment was to help the descendants of Aaron with the service of the house of the Lord They were responsible for the courtyards and rooms, for cleansing all the holy things, and the work of the service of the house of God.
013	1CH	023	029	They were also responsible for the showbread that was placed on the table, the special flour for the grain offerings, the unleavened bread, the baking, the mixing, and dealing with all amounts and measurements.
013	1CH	023	030	They also had to stand every morning to give thanks and praise to the Lord, and do the same in the evening,
013	1CH	023	031	and whenever burnt offerings were presented to the Lord whether on Sabbaths, new moons, and feast days. They were to serve regularly before the Lord according to the number required for them.
013	1CH	023	032	So the Levites were to carry out the responsibility of caring for the Tent of Meeting and the sanctuary, and with their brothers the descendants of Aaron, they served the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	024	001	The sons of Aaron were placed in divisions as follows. The sons of Aaron were Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	002	But Nadab and Abihu died before their father did, and they had no sons. Only Eleazar and Ithamar carried on as priests.
013	1CH	024	003	With the help of Zadok, a descendant of Eleazar, and Ithamar, a descendant Ahimelech, David placed them in divisions according to their appointed duties.
013	1CH	024	004	Because Eleazar's descendants had more leaders than those of Ithamar, they were divided like this: sixteen family leaders from the descendants of Eleazar, and eight from the descendants of Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	005	They were divided by casting lots, without preference, for there were officers of the sanctuary and officers of God from both the sons of Eleazar and the sons of Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	006	Shemaiah son of Nethanel, a Levite, was the secretary. He wrote down the names and assignments in the presence of the king, the officials, Zadok the priest, Ahimelech son of Abiathar, and the family leaders of the priests and Levites. One family from Eleazar and one from Ithamar were chosen in turn.
013	1CH	024	007	The first lot fell to Jehoiarib. The second to Jedaiah.
013	1CH	024	008	The third to Harim. The fourth to Seorim.
013	1CH	024	009	The fifth to Malkijah. The sixth to Mijamin.
013	1CH	024	010	The seventh to Hakkoz. The eighth to Abijah.
013	1CH	024	011	The ninth to Jeshua. The tenth to Shecaniah.
013	1CH	024	012	The eleventh to Eliashib. The twelfth to Jakim.
013	1CH	024	013	The thirteenth to Huppah. The fourteenth to Jeshebeab.
013	1CH	024	014	The fifteenth to Bilgah. The sixteenth to Immer.
013	1CH	024	015	The seventeenth to Hezir. The eighteenth to Happizzez.
013	1CH	024	016	The nineteenth to Pethahiah. The twentieth to Jehezkel.
013	1CH	024	017	The twenty-first to Jakin. The twenty-second to Gamul.
013	1CH	024	018	The twenty-third to Delaiah. The twenty-fourth to Maaziah.
013	1CH	024	019	This was the order in which each group were to serve when they came into the house of the Lord, following the procedure defined for them by their forefather Aaron, as instructed by the Lord, the God of Israel.
013	1CH	024	020	These were the rest of the sons of Levi: from the sons of Amram: Shubael; from the sons of Shubael: Jehdeiah.
013	1CH	024	021	For Rehabiah, from his sons: Isshiah (first).
013	1CH	024	022	From the Izharites: Shelomoth; from the sons of Shelomoth: Jahath.
013	1CH	024	023	The sons of Hebron: Jeriah (first), Amariah (second), Jahaziel (third), and Jekameam (fourth).
013	1CH	024	024	The son of Uzziel: Micah; from the sons of Micah: Shamir.
013	1CH	024	025	The brother of Micah: Isshiah; from the sons of Isshiah: Zechariah.
013	1CH	024	026	The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The son of Jaaziah: Beno.
013	1CH	024	027	The sons of Merari: from Jaaziah: Beno, Shoham, Zaccur and Ibri.
013	1CH	024	028	From Mahli: Eleazar, who did not have any sons.
013	1CH	024	029	From Kish: the son of Kish, Jerahmeel.
013	1CH	024	030	The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites, according to their families.
013	1CH	024	031	They also cast lots in the same way their relatives the descendants of Aaron did. They did this in the presence of King David, and of Zadok, Ahimelech, and the family leaders of the priests and of the Levites, the family leaders and their youngest brothers alike.
013	1CH	025	001	David and the leaders of the Levites chose men from the families of Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun to serve by prophesying accompanied by lyres, harps, and cymbals. Here is the list of those who performed this service:
013	1CH	025	002	From the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asarelah. These sons of Asaph were under the supervision of Asaph, who prophesied under the supervision of the king.
013	1CH	025	003	From the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six in total, under the supervision of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied accompanied by the harp, giving thanks and praise to the Lord.
013	1CH	025	004	From the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth.
013	1CH	025	005	All these sons of Heman, the king's seer, were given to him through the promises of God to honor him, for God gave Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.
013	1CH	025	006	All of them were under the supervision of their fathers for the music of the house of the Lord with cymbals, harps, and lyres, for the service of the house of God. Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman were under the supervision of the king.
013	1CH	025	007	Along with their relatives, all of them trained and skilled in singing to the Lord, they totaled 288.
013	1CH	025	008	They cast lots for whatever responsibility they had, the least important equal to the most important, the teacher to the student.
013	1CH	025	009	The first lot, which was for Asaph, fell to Joseph, his sons, and his brother, 12 in total. The second fell to Gedaliah, his sons, and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	010	The third fell to Zaccur, his sons, and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	011	The fourth fell to Izri, his sons, and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	012	The fifth to Nethaniah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	013	The sixth fell to Bukkiah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	014	The seventh fell to Jesarelah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	015	The eighth fell to Jeshaiah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	016	The ninth fell to Mattaniah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	017	The tenth fell to Shimei, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	018	The eleventh fell to Azarel, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	019	The twelfth fell to Hashabiah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	020	The thirteenth fell to Shubael, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	021	The fourteenth fell to Mattithiah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	022	The fifteenth fell to Jerimoth, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	023	The sixteenth fell to Hananiah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	024	The seventeenth fell to Joshbekashah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	025	The eighteenth fell to Hanani, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	026	The nineteenth fell to Mallothi, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	027	The twentieth fell to Eliathah, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	028	The twenty-first fell to Hothir, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	029	The twenty-second fell to Giddalti, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	030	The twenty-third fell to Mahazioth, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	025	031	The twenty-fourth fell to Romamti-Ezer, his sons and his brothers, 12 in total.
013	1CH	026	001	This is a list of the divisions of the gatekeepers. From the Korahites: Meshelemiah son of Kore, one of the sons of Asaph.
013	1CH	026	002	The sons of Meshelemiah: Zechariah (first), Jediael (second), Zebadiah (third), Jathniel (fourth),
013	1CH	026	003	Elam (fifth), Jehohanan (sixth), and Eliehoenai (seventh).
013	1CH	026	004	The sons of Obed-edom: Shemaiah (first), Jehozabad (second), Joah (third), Sacar (fourth), Nethanel (fifth),
013	1CH	026	005	Ammiel (sixth), Issachar (seventh), and Peullethai (eighth), for God had blessed Obed-edom.
013	1CH	026	006	Shemaiah, Obed-edom's son, had sons who were capable leaders and had great authority in their father's family
013	1CH	026	007	The sons of Shemaiah: Othni, Rephael, Obed, and Elzabad. His relatives, Elihu and Semakiah, were also capable men.
013	1CH	026	008	All these descendants of Obed-edom, plus their sons and grandsons, a total of sixty-two, were capable men, well qualified for their service.
013	1CH	026	009	Meshelemiah's eighteen sons and brothers were also capable men.
013	1CH	026	010	Hosah, one of the sons of Merari, made Shimri as leader among his sons, though he was not the firstborn.
013	1CH	026	011	His other sons included Hilkiah (second), Tebaliah (third), and Zechariah (fourth). The total of Hosah's sons and relatives was thirteen.
013	1CH	026	012	These divisions of the gatekeepers, through their family leaders, served in the house of the Lord, just like their brothers.
013	1CH	026	013	Every gate was assigned by lot to different families, the least important equal to the most important.
013	1CH	026	014	The lot for the east gate fell to Meshelemiah. Then they cast lots for his son Zechariah, a wise counselor with insight, and the lot for the north gate fell to him.
013	1CH	026	015	The lot for the south gate fell to Obed-edom, and the lot for the storehouse fell to his sons.
013	1CH	026	016	Shuppim and Hosah received the west gate and the gate of Shallecheth on the road that leads up. They were always guarded.
013	1CH	026	017	There were six Levites on duty every day at the east gate, four at the north gate, four at the south gate, and two at a time at the storehouse.
013	1CH	026	018	Six were on duty every day at the west gate, four at the main road, and two at the courtyard.
013	1CH	026	019	These were the divisions of the gatekeepers from the sons of Korah and the sons of Merari.
013	1CH	026	020	Other Levites under Ahijah were in charge of the treasuries of the house of God and the treasuries of what had been dedicated to God.
013	1CH	026	021	From the sons of Ladan, who were the descendants of the Gershonites through Ladan, and were the family leaders of Ladan the Gershonite: Jehieli.
013	1CH	026	022	The sons of Jehieli, Zetham and his brother Joel, were in charge of the treasuries of the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	026	023	From the Amramites, the Izharites, the Hebronites, and the Uzzielites:
013	1CH	026	024	Shebuel, a descendant of Gershom, son of Moses, who was the chief officer in charge of the treasuries.
013	1CH	026	025	His relatives by Eliezer were Rehabiah, Jeshaiah, Joram, Zicri, and Shelomoth.
013	1CH	026	026	Shelomoth and his relatives were in charge of all the treasuries for all that had been dedicated by King David, by the family leaders who were the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and by the army commanders.
013	1CH	026	027	They dedicated a part of the plunder they had won in battle to help maintain the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	026	028	Shelomoth and his relatives also looked after the gifts dedicated to the Lord by Samuel the seer, Saul son of Kish, Abner son of Ner, and Joab son of Zeruiah. All the dedicated gifts were the responsibility of Shelomoth and his relatives.
013	1CH	026	029	From the Izharites: Kenaniah and his sons were given outside duties as officials and judges over Israel.
013	1CH	026	030	From the Hebronites: Hashabiah and his relatives, 1,700 capable men, were put in charge of Israel west of the Jordan, responsible for everything involving the Lord's work and the king's service.
013	1CH	026	031	Also from the Hebronites came Jerijah, the leader of the Hebronites according to the family genealogies. In the fortieth year of David's reign the records were examined, and men of great ability were discovered at Jazer in Gilead.
013	1CH	026	032	Among the relatives of Jerijah were 2,700 capable men who were family leaders. King David put them in charge of the tribes of Reuben and Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh. They were responsible for everything involving the Lord's work and the king's service.
013	1CH	027	001	This is a list of the Israelites, the family leaders, the commanders of thousands, and the commanders of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in everything related to the divisions that were on duty each month during the year. There were 24,000 men in each division.
013	1CH	027	002	In command of the first division for the first month, was Jashobeam, son of Zabdiel. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	003	He was a descendant of Perez, and was in charge of all the army officers for the first month.
013	1CH	027	004	In command of the division for the second month was Dodai the Ahohite. Mikloth was his division leader. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	005	The third army commander for the third month was Benaiah, son of Jehoiada the priest. He was chief and there were 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	006	This was the same Benaiah who was a great warrior among the Thirty, and was in charge of the Thirty. His son Ammizabad was his division leader.
013	1CH	027	007	The fourth, for the fourth month, was Asahel, Joab's brother. His son Zebadiah was his successor. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	008	The fifth, for the fifth month, was the army commander Shamhuth the Izrahite. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	009	The sixth, for the sixth month, was Ira, son of Ikkesh the Tekoite. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	010	The seventh, for the seventh month, was Helez the Pelonite of the tribe of Ephraim. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	011	The eighth, for the eighth month, was Sibbecai the Hushathite, a Zerahite. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	012	The ninth, for the ninth month, was Abiezer the Anathothite of the tribe of Benjamin. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	013	The tenth, for the tenth month, was Maharai the Netophathite, a Zerahite. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	014	The eleventh, for the eleventh month, was Benaiah the Pirathonite of the tribe of Ephraim. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	015	The twelfth, for the twelfth month, was Heldai the Netophathite, from the family of Othniel. He had 24,000 men in his division.
013	1CH	027	016	This is a list of the leaders for the tribes of Israel: for the Reubenites: Eliezer, son of Zicri; for the Simeonites: Shephatiah, son of Maacah;
013	1CH	027	017	for Levi: Hashabiah, son of Kemuel; for Aaron: Zadok;
013	1CH	027	018	for Judah: Elihu, a brother of David; for Issachar: Omri, son of Michael;
013	1CH	027	019	for Zebulun: Ishmaiah, son of Obadiah; for Naphtali: Jerimoth, son of Azriel;
013	1CH	027	020	for the Ephraimites: Hoshea, son of Azaziah; for the half the tribe of Manasseh: Joel, son of Pedaiah;
013	1CH	027	021	for the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead: Iddo, son of Zechariah; for Benjamin: Jaasiel, son of Abner;
013	1CH	027	022	for Dan: Azarel, son of Jeroham. These were the officers for the tribes of Israel.
013	1CH	027	023	David did not census the men under twenty because the Lord had said he would make Israel as numerous as the stars of heaven.
013	1CH	027	024	Joab, son of Zeruiah, had begun the census but did not finish it. Israel was punished because of this census, and the results were not recorded in the official account of King David.
013	1CH	027	025	Azmaveth, son of Adiel, was in charge of the king's storehouses, while Jonathan, son of Uzziah, was in charge of those in the country, towns, villages, and watchtowers.
013	1CH	027	026	Ezri, son of Kelub, was in charge of the farm workers who worked the land.
013	1CH	027	027	Shimei the Ramathite was in charge of the vineyards. Zabdi the Shiphmite was in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine cellars.
013	1CH	027	028	Baal-Hanan the Gederite was in charge of the olive and sycamore-fig trees in the foothills. Joash was in charge of the stores of olive oil.
013	1CH	027	029	Shitrai the Sharonite was in charge of the cattle in the Sharon pastures. Shaphat, son of Adlai, was in charge of the cattle in the valleys.
013	1CH	027	030	Obil the Ishmaelite was in charge of the camels. Jehdeiah the Meronothite was in charge of the donkeys.
013	1CH	027	031	Jaziz the Hagrite was in charge of the sheep and goats. These were all officials in charge of what belonged to King David.
013	1CH	027	032	Jonathan, David's uncle, was an advisor, a man of insight, and a scribe. Jehiel, son of Hacmoni, looked after the king's sons.
013	1CH	027	033	Ahithophel was the king's counselor and Hushai the Archite was the king's friend.
013	1CH	027	034	After Ahithophel came Jehoiada, son of Benaiah and Abiathar. Joab was the commander of the royal army.
013	1CH	028	001	David summoned to Jerusalem all the leaders of Israel—the leaders of the tribes, the army division commanders in service to the king, the commanders of thousands and the commanders of hundreds, and the officials in charge of all the property and livestock of the king and his sons, along with the court officials, the warriors and all the best fighting men.
013	1CH	028	002	King David got to his feet and said, “Listen to me, my brothers and my people! I really wanted to build a house as a resting place for the Ark of the Lord's Agreement, as a footstool for our God. So I made plans to build it.
013	1CH	028	003	But God told me, ‘You are not to build a house to honor me because you are a man of war who has spilled blood.’
013	1CH	028	004	However, the Lord, the God of Israel, chose me out of all my father's family to be king of Israel forever. For he chose Judah as the leading tribe, and from among the families of Judah he chose my father's family. From among my father's sons he was pleased to chose me as king over the whole of Israel.
013	1CH	028	005	From all my sons (for the Lord gave me many) the Lord has chosen Solomon my child to sit on the throne and to rule over the Lord's kingdom Israel.
013	1CH	028	006	He told me, ‘Your son Solomon is the one who will build my house and my courts, because I have chosen him as my son, and I will be his father.
013	1CH	028	007	I will make sure his kingdom lasts forever if he single-mindedly keeps my commandments and regulations like he does today.
013	1CH	028	008	So now, in the sight of all Israel, the assembly of the Lord, and as God listens, be sure to obey all the commandments of the Lord your God so that you may go on possessing this good land and be able to pass it on as an inheritance to your descendants forever.
013	1CH	028	009	Solomon my son, get to know the God of your father. Serve him with complete dedication and with a willing mind, for the Lord examines every motivation and understands the intention of every thought. If you look for him, you will find him; but if you abandon him, he will reject you forever.
013	1CH	028	010	Pay attention now, for the Lord has chosen you to build a house for the sanctuary. Be strong, and take action!’”
013	1CH	028	011	Then David gave his son Solomon the plans for the Temple porch, its buildings, storehouses, upper rooms, inner rooms, and the room for the “place of atonement.”
013	1CH	028	012	He also gave him everything he had planned for the courts of the house of the Lord, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of the house of God and of those things that had been dedicated.
013	1CH	028	013	In addition he passed on instructions regarding the divisions of the priests and the Levites, for all the work of service of the house of the Lord, and for all that was used for worship in the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	028	014	He also laid down how much gold and silver was to be used in making the different objects used in every kind of service,
013	1CH	028	015	the weight of the gold and silver lampstands and their lamps, depending on the use of each lampstand;
013	1CH	028	016	the weight of gold for each table of showbread, and the weight of silver for the silver tables,
013	1CH	028	017	the weight of pure gold for the forks, basins, and cups; the weight of each gold dish; the weight of each silver bowl;
013	1CH	028	018	the weight of the refined gold for the altar of incense; and lastly plans for a golden chariot of cherubim that spread their wings, covering the Ark of the Lord's Agreement.
013	1CH	028	019	“All this is in writing from the hand of the Lord, given to me as instructions—every detail of this plan,” said David.
013	1CH	028	020	Then David also told Solomon, “Be strong, be brave, and take action! Don't be afraid or discouraged, for the Lord God, my God, is with you! He will not let you down or leave you. He will make sure all the work for the service of the house of the Lord is finished.
013	1CH	028	021	The divisions of the priests and the Levites are prepared for all the service of the house of God. People will be willing to use their different skills to help you in all the work—the officials and all the people will do what you tell them.”
013	1CH	029	001	Then King David said to everyone gathered there, “My son Solomon, chosen by God alone, is young and inexperienced, and the work to be done is great because this Temple will not be for man, but for the Lord God.
013	1CH	029	002	Using all my means I have provided for the house of my God—gold for the articles made of gold, silver for the silver, bronze for the bronze, iron for the iron, and wood for the wood; onyx stones and stones for settings: turquoise, different colored stones, every kind of precious stone; and plenty of marble.
013	1CH	029	003	More than this, because of my devotion to the house of my God, I'm now giving my personal fortune of gold and silver, in addition to everything that I have provided for this holy house.
013	1CH	029	004	3,000 talents of gold—the gold of Ophir—and 7,000 talents of refined silver will go to cover the walls of the buildings,
013	1CH	029	005	gold for the gold work, and silver for the silver work, and for all the work done by the craftsmen. Now who willingly wants to commit themselves to giving to the Lord today?”
013	1CH	029	006	They gave willingly—the family leaders, those in charge of the tribes of Israel, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of the king's work.
013	1CH	029	007	They gave to the service of the house of God 5,000 talents and 10,000 darics of gold, 10,000 talents of silver, 18,000 talents of bronze, and 100,000 talents of iron.
013	1CH	029	008	Those who had precious stones gave them to the treasury of the house of the Lord, under the supervision of Jehiel the Gershonite.
013	1CH	029	009	The people celebrated because their leaders had been so willing to give to the Lord, freely and wholeheartedly. King David was also really delighted.
013	1CH	029	010	Then David praised the Lord before the whole assembly: “Praise to you, Lord, the God of Israel our father, for ever and ever!
013	1CH	029	011	Lord, yours is the greatness, the power, the glory, the splendor, and the majesty, for everything in heaven and on earth is yours. Lord, yours is the kingdom, and you are admired as ruler of all.
013	1CH	029	012	Riches and honor come from you and you reign supreme. You possess power and might, and have the ability to make people great and to give strength to all.
013	1CH	029	013	Now our God we thank you, and we praise you and your glorious character.
013	1CH	029	014	But who am I, and who are my people, that we are able to give as willingly as this? For everything we have comes from you—we are only giving back what you have given us.
013	1CH	029	015	In your eyes we are strangers and foreigners, just like our forefathers. Our time here on earth passes like a shadow, we have no hope of staying here long.
013	1CH	029	016	Lord our God, even all this wealth that we have provided to build you a house for your holy name comes from what you give, and it all belongs to you.
013	1CH	029	017	I know, my God, that you look on the inside and are happy when we live right. Everything I have given willingly and with an honest heart, and now I have seen your people here giving happily and willingly to you.
013	1CH	029	018	Lord, the God of Abraham, Isaac, Israel, and our forefathers, please keep these thoughts and commitments in the minds of your people forever, and make sure they stay loyal to you.
013	1CH	029	019	Please also give my son Solomon a desire to whole-heartedly keep your commandments, decrees, and statutes, and to do all he can to build your Temple that I have provided for.”
013	1CH	029	020	Then David said to everyone there, “Praise the Lord your God!” So everyone praised the Lord, the God of their fathers. They bowed down in reverence to the Lord and to the king.
013	1CH	029	021	The following day they presented sacrifices and burnt offerings to the Lord: one thousand bulls, one thousand rams, and one thousand lambs, with their drink offerings and plenty of sacrifices for all of Israel.
013	1CH	029	022	Then they ate and drank in the presence of the Lord with great happiness that day. They made Solomon, the son of David, king for a second time, and they anointed him as ruler for the Lord, and anointed Zadok as priest.
013	1CH	029	023	So Solomon took the throne of the Lord as king in place of David, his father. He was successful, and all the Israelites obeyed him.
013	1CH	029	024	All the officials and warriors, as well as all of King David's sons, gave a solemn promise of loyalty to King Solomon.
013	1CH	029	025	The Lord made Solomon highly respected throughout Israel, and gave him greater royal majesty than had been given to any king of Israel before him.
013	1CH	029	026	So David, son of Jesse, ruled over all of Israel.
013	1CH	029	027	He ruled over Israel forty years—seven in Hebron, and thirty-three in Jerusalem.
013	1CH	029	028	David died at a good old age, having lived a long life, blessed with wealth and honor. Then his son Solomon took over and ruled in his place.
013	1CH	029	029	Everything that King David did, from beginning to end, is written down in the Records of Samuel the Seer, the Records of Nathan the Prophet, and the Records of Gad the Seer.
013	1CH	029	030	These include all the details of his reign, his power, and what happened to him, and to Israel, and all to the kingdoms of the neighboring countries.
