018	JOB	015	016	How much less pure are those who are unclean and corrupt, drinking in sin like water!
018	JOB	015	017	If you are ready to listen to me, I will show you. I will explain my insights.
018	JOB	015	018	This is what wise men have said, confirmed by their ancestors,
018	JOB	015	019	those to whom alone the land was given before foreigners ever were there.
018	JOB	015	020	The wicked writhe in pain all their lives, through all the years these oppressors survive.
018	JOB	015	021	Terrifying sounds fill their ears; even when they think they're safe, the destroyer will attack them.
018	JOB	015	022	They don't believe they will escape the darkness—they know a sword is waiting for them.
018	JOB	015	023	They wander around looking for food, asking ‘Where is it?’ They know that their day of darkness is close at hand.
018	JOB	015	024	Misery and torment overwhelm them like a king preparing for battle.
018	JOB	015	025	They shake their fists in God's face, defiantly challenging the Almighty,
018	JOB	015	026	insolently attacking him with their shields.
018	JOB	015	027	They have become fat in their rebellion, their bellies bloated with fat.
018	JOB	015	028	But their cities will become desolate; they will live in abandoned houses that are crumbling into ruins.
018	JOB	015	029	They will lose their riches, their wealth will not endure, their possessions will not spread over the earth.
018	JOB	015	030	They will not escape from the darkness. Like a tree whose shoots are burned up in a forest fire, the breath of God will blow him away.
018	JOB	015	031	They should not trust in things that are worthless, for their reward will be worthless.
018	JOB	015	032	This will be paid in full before their time has come. They are like tree branches that wither,
018	JOB	015	033	like vines that lose their unripe grapes, or olive trees that lose their flowers.
