018	JOB	015	035	They plan trouble and produce evil, giving birth to deception.”
018	JOB	016	001	Job replied,
018	JOB	016	002	“I've heard all this before. You are comforters who just cause trouble!
018	JOB	016	003	Will your windy speeches never cease? What's bothering you that you have to answer me?
018	JOB	016	004	I could talk like you do if you were in my place, stringing words together to criticize you, ridiculing you with a toss of my head.
018	JOB	016	005	I could build you up by my mouth speaking words; the movement of my lips would ease your pain.
018	JOB	016	006	For me, if I speak it doesn't ease my pain, and if I don't speak the pain is still there.
018	JOB	016	007	God, you have worn me out. You have destroyed my whole family.
018	JOB	016	008	You have made me shrivel up, which is a witness against me; my thin body testifies against me.
018	JOB	016	009	He has torn me apart in his anger; in his hostility he has gnashed his teeth at me; my enemy pierces me with his fierce look.
018	JOB	016	010	People stare at me with their mouths wide open, they slap me on my cheeks to mock me, they crowd around me to attack me.
018	JOB	016	011	God has handed me over to evil people; he has thrown me into their hands.
018	JOB	016	012	I was living in peace and he smashed me to pieces. He grabbed me by the neck and dashed me to pieces. He set me up as his target.
018	JOB	016	013	His archers surround me. His arrows pierce my kidneys without mercy. He pours out my gall on the ground.
018	JOB	016	014	Like a wall he breaks me down, breach upon breach, rushing at me like a warrior.
018	JOB	016	015	I have sown sackcloth to cover my skin; my strength lies broken in the dust.
018	JOB	016	016	My face is red from crying and dark shadows surround my eyes,
018	JOB	016	017	although I have done nothing wrong and my prayer is pure.
018	JOB	016	018	Earth, do not cover up my blood. May my cry find no place to hide.
018	JOB	016	019	Look, right now my witness is in heaven; the one who speaks for me is on high.
018	JOB	016	020	My friends scorn me, but my eyes pour out tears to God.
018	JOB	016	021	I want my witness to speak for me with God as someone does for their friend.
018	JOB	016	022	For in a few short years I shall go down that road from which I shall not return.”
018	JOB	017	001	“My spirit is crushed; my life is extinguished; the grave is ready for me.
018	JOB	017	002	Mockers surround me. I see how bitterly they ridicule me.
018	JOB	017	003	God, you need to put down a pledge for me with yourself, for who else will be my guarantor?
018	JOB	017	004	You have closed their minds to understanding, so do not let them win!
018	JOB	017	005	They betray friends to gain benefit for themselves and their children suffer for it.
018	JOB	017	006	He has made me a proverb of ridicule among the people; they spit in my face.
018	JOB	017	007	My eyes are worn out from crying and my body is a shadow of its former self.
018	JOB	017	008	People who think they are good are shocked to see me. Those who are innocent are troubled by the godless.
018	JOB	017	009	Those who are right keep going, and those whose hands are clean grow stronger and stronger.
018	JOB	017	010	Why don't you come back and repeat again what you've been saying?—yet I still won't find a wise man among you!
018	JOB	017	011	My life is over. My plans are gone. My heart is broken.
018	JOB	017	012	They turn night into day, and say that daylight is close to darkness.
018	JOB	017	013	What am I looking for? To make my home in Sheol, to make my bed in darkness?
018	JOB	017	014	Should I call the grave my father, and the maggot my mother or my sister?
018	JOB	017	015	So then where is my hope? Can anyone see any hope for me?
018	JOB	017	016	Will hope go down with me to the gates of Sheol? Will we go down together into the dust?”
018	JOB	018	001	Then Bildad the Shuhite spoke up and said,
018	JOB	018	002	“How long will you go on talking, hunting for the right words to say? Talk sense if you want us to reply!
018	JOB	018	003	Do you think we're dumb animals? Do we look stupid to you?
018	JOB	018	004	You tear yourself apart with your anger. Do you think the earth has to be abandoned, or the mountains moved, just because of you?
018	JOB	018	005	It's certain that the life of the wicked will end like a lamp that is snuffed out—their flame will shine no more.
018	JOB	018	006	The light in their home goes out, the lamp hanging above is extinguished.
018	JOB	018	007	Instead of taking strong strides they stumble, and their own plans cause them to fall.
018	JOB	018	008	Their own feet trip them up and they are caught in a net; as they walk along they fall into a pit.
018	JOB	018	009	A trap grabs them by the heel; a snare tightens around them.
