018	JOB	018	016	They wither away, roots below and branches above;
018	JOB	018	017	the memory of them fades from the earth; nobody remembers their names any more.
018	JOB	018	018	They are thrown out of light into darkness, driven from the world.
018	JOB	018	019	They have no children or descendants among their people, and no survivors where they used to live.
018	JOB	018	020	People of the west are appalled at what happens to them. People of the east are shocked.
018	JOB	018	021	This is what happens to the homes of the wicked, to the places of those who reject God.”
018	JOB	019	001	Job replied,
018	JOB	019	002	“How long will you go on tormenting me? How long will you go on crushing me with words?
018	JOB	019	003	Ten times already you have humiliated me. Aren't you ashamed for treating me so badly?
