018	JOB	019	007	Even though I cry for help, I get no answer; even though I shout my objections, I get no justice.
018	JOB	019	008	God has walled me in so I can't escape; he has plunged my path into darkness.
018	JOB	019	009	He has stripped my honor from me; he has taken away my reputation.
018	JOB	019	010	He tears me down from all sides until I am finished; he has destroyed my hope like a tree that is uprooted.
018	JOB	019	011	His anger burns against me; he treats me as one of his enemies.
018	JOB	019	012	God's troops assemble to attack me. They build ramparts against me. They encircle and besiege my home.
018	JOB	019	013	He has driven my brothers far away from me; all my former friends are estranged from me.
018	JOB	019	014	My relatives have abandoned me; my close friends have forgotten me.
018	JOB	019	015	My house guests and my maidservants treat me as a stranger—to them I have become a foreigner.
018	JOB	019	016	I call my servant, but he doesn't reply. I have to beg him!
018	JOB	019	017	I am repulsive to my wife, and I am loathsome to my own brothers.
018	JOB	019	018	Even young children despise me; when I stand up they ridicule me.
018	JOB	019	019	All my closest friends despise me, and those I loved have turned on me.
018	JOB	019	020	I've been reduced to skin and bones and I survive by the skin of my teeth.
018	JOB	019	021	Have pity on me, my friends, have pity on me, because God has struck me down!
018	JOB	019	022	Why are you persecuting me like God does? Aren't you satisfied with getting your pound of flesh?
018	JOB	019	023	I wish my words could be written down, recorded in a book,
018	JOB	019	024	or engraved with an iron pen and molten lead in the rock forever.
018	JOB	019	025	I know my Redeemer is alive, and that he shall finally take the stand for me on the earth.
018	JOB	019	026	Even though my skin is destroyed, in my body I shall see God.
018	JOB	019	027	I myself will see him—with my own eyes, and not those of someone else! The thought overcomes me!
018	JOB	019	028	You say to yourselves, ‘How can we make him suffer so he can see he is the source of his problems?’
018	JOB	019	029	You yourselves should fear being punished by God, for you know anger brings God's punishment that accompanies judgment.”
018	JOB	020	001	Then Zophar the Naamathite answered and said,
018	JOB	020	002	“I'm forced to reply because I'm really upset!
018	JOB	020	003	What I hear you say insults me, but I know how to reply to you!
018	JOB	020	004	Don't you know that since ancient times, since human beings were put on this earth,
018	JOB	020	005	that the triumph of the wicked doesn't last long, that those who reject God are only happy for a short time?
