018	JOB	021	001	Job replied,
018	JOB	021	002	“Please listen carefully to what I say—that would be one comfort you could give me.
018	JOB	021	003	Bear with me; let me speak. After I've spoken you can resume mocking me.
018	JOB	021	004	Am I complaining against people? Of course not. Why shouldn't I be impatient?
018	JOB	021	005	Just take a look at me. Aren't you appalled? Cover your mouth with your hand in shock!
018	JOB	021	006	Every time I think of what's happened to me I am horrified and I shake all over with fear.
