018	JOB	021	008	Their children are with them; they watch their grandchildren grow up.
018	JOB	021	009	They live in their homes in safety—they are not afraid. God does not use his rod to beat them.
018	JOB	021	010	Their bulls always breed successfully; their cows give birth to calves and do not miscarry.
018	JOB	021	011	They send out their little ones like lambs to play; their children dance around.
018	JOB	021	012	They sing accompanied by the tambourine and lyre; they celebrate with the music of the flute.
018	JOB	021	013	They live out their lives contentedly, and go down to Sheol in peace.
018	JOB	021	014	Yet they tell God, ‘Get lost! We don't want anything to do with you.
