018	JOB	021	016	Such people believe they make their own fortune, but I don't accept their way of thinking.
018	JOB	021	017	How often is the lamp of the wicked snuffed out? How often does disaster come upon them? How often does God punish the wicked in his anger?
018	JOB	021	018	Are they blown along like straw in the wind? Does a tornado come in and carry them away?
018	JOB	021	019	Some say, ‘God saves up people's punishment for their children.’ But I say, ‘God should punish those people themselves so that they can learn from it.’
018	JOB	021	020	Let them see their destruction themselves, and drink deeply from God's anger.
018	JOB	021	021	For they don't care what happens to their families once they're dead.
