018	JOB	022	007	You refused water to the thirsty; you denied food to the hungry.
018	JOB	022	008	Is it because the land belongs to the powerful, and only the privileged have a right to live there?
018	JOB	022	009	You have sent widows away empty-handed; you have crushed the outstretched arms of orphans, begging for help.
018	JOB	022	010	That's why you're surrounded by traps to catch you, and why you suddenly panic in terror.
018	JOB	022	011	That's why it's so dark you cannot see, and why you feel like you're drowning.
