018	JOB	023	005	I would discover how he would answer me and learn what he has to say to me.
018	JOB	023	006	Would he fight against me using his mighty power? No, he would pay attention to what I have to say.
018	JOB	023	007	There a good person could reason with him, and I would be acquitted forever by my judge.
018	JOB	023	008	If I go to the east, he's not there; if I go the west, I don't find him.
018	JOB	023	009	If he's working in the north, I don't perceive him; if he's moving south, I don't see him.
018	JOB	023	010	Yet he always knows where I'm going. When he has proved me, I will come out shining like gold.
018	JOB	023	011	I have kept in step with him; I have followed his way without turning aside.
