018	JOB	028	008	No wild beasts have passed that way; the lion has not walked there.
018	JOB	028	009	Miners attack the hard rock; they overturn the roots of mountains.
018	JOB	028	010	They tunnel through the rock, looking carefully for every precious stone.
018	JOB	028	011	They dam the sources of the rivers, and bring to light what is hidden.
018	JOB	028	012	But where can wisdom be found? Where is the place to gain understanding?
018	JOB	028	013	Human beings do not know the way to wisdom; it is not found among the living.
018	JOB	028	014	The deep waters say, ‘It's not here,’ and the sea says, ‘It's not here either.’
018	JOB	028	015	It cannot be bought with gold; nor can it be purchased with silver.
018	JOB	028	016	Its value cannot be measured, even with the gold of Ophir; it is more precious than onyx or lapis lazuli.
