018	JOB	029	007	I went out to the city gate and took my seat in the public square.
018	JOB	029	008	The young men saw me and moved out of the way; the elders would stand up for me.
018	JOB	029	009	The leaders remained silent and covered their mouths with their hands.
018	JOB	029	010	The voices of the officials were hushed; they held their tongues in my presence.
