# BOOK	019	PSA	Psalms	Psalms
019	PSA	001	001	Happy are those who don't follow the advice of the wicked. They refuse to adopt the ways of sinful people, and they don't make fun of others.
019	PSA	001	002	Instead they love to do what the law of the Lord says, and they think about it day and night.
019	PSA	001	003	They're like trees growing by flowing rivers, producing fruit every season. Their leaves never wither, and they are successful in all they do.
019	PSA	001	004	But it's not like that for the wicked! They are like chaff, blown away by the wind.
019	PSA	001	005	For this reason the wicked will not survive the judgment—sinners have no place among those who live right.
019	PSA	001	006	For the Lord watches over those who follow the right way, but the way of the wicked leads to death.
019	PSA	002	001	Why are the nations plotting rebellion? The peoples devise schemes, but they're pointless.
019	PSA	002	002	The kings of the world prepare to attack, and the rulers conspire together against the Lord and his anointed one, saying,
019	PSA	002	003	“Let's break the chains and throw away the cords that bind us.”
019	PSA	002	004	But the one who sits enthroned in heaven laughs. The Lord mocks them.
019	PSA	002	005	He will thunder at them, and terrify them in his fury, saying,
019	PSA	002	006	“It is I who placed my king on Zion, my holy mountain.”
019	PSA	002	007	“I will proclaim the Lord's decree,” says the king. “He told me, ‘You are my son. Today I have become your father.
019	PSA	002	008	Ask me, and I will give you the nations as your possessions—the whole earth will belong to you.
019	PSA	002	009	You will break them with a rod of iron, smashing them like pottery.’”
019	PSA	002	010	So then you kings, be wise! Be warned, you rulers of the world!
019	PSA	002	011	Serve the Lord in reverence, celebrate with trembling!
019	PSA	002	012	Submit to his son so that he will not become angry and you die suddenly. His anger flares up quickly, but how happy are all those who go to him for protection.
019	PSA	003	001	A psalm of David concerning the time he had to flee from his son Absalom. Lord, my enemies have become so many; so many are rebelling against me.
019	PSA	003	002	So many are telling me, “God can't save you!” (Selah)
019	PSA	003	003	But you, Lord, are a shield protecting me. You give me victory; you hold my head high.
019	PSA	003	004	I cry out to the Lord for help, and he answers me from his holy mountain. (Selah)
019	PSA	003	005	I lie down to sleep, and in the morning I wake up because the Lord takes care of me.
019	PSA	003	006	I'm not afraid of tens of thousands who surround me, people who are against me.
019	PSA	003	007	Stand up for me, Lord! Save me, my God! Hit all my enemies on the cheek; break the teeth of the wicked!
019	PSA	003	008	Salvation belongs to you, Lord; may you be a blessing to your people. (Selah)
019	PSA	004	001	For the music director. A psalm of David, to be accompanied by string instruments. When I call, please answer me, God who vindicates me. When I was hemmed in by troubles, you gave me a way out. Be gracious to me and hear my prayer.
019	PSA	004	002	How long will you people ruin my reputation? How long will you love what is worthless and tell lies? (Selah)
019	PSA	004	003	You should realize that the Lord shows special favor to the faithful. The Lord listens when I call to him.
019	PSA	004	004	Be in awe; do not sin. When you rest, reflect on this, and keep quiet! (Selah)
019	PSA	004	005	Offer sacrifices with the right attitude. Trust in the Lord.
019	PSA	004	006	Many say, “Who is going to show us some good?” Lord, may your face shine upon us.
019	PSA	004	007	The happiness you give me is better than those who have a plentiful harvest of grain and new wine.
019	PSA	004	008	I will lie down in peace and sleep, for you, Lord, alone keep me safe.
019	PSA	005	001	For the music director. A psalm of David, to be accompanied by flutes. Lord, please listen to me. Don't ignore my groans of distress.
019	PSA	005	002	Hear me pleading for help, my King and my God, because I'm praying to you.
019	PSA	005	003	Please listen to what I have to say in the morning, Lord. Every morning I put my requests to you and wait for your reply.
019	PSA	005	004	For you are not a God who has any pleasure in wickedness; evil has no place with you.
019	PSA	005	005	The proud cannot come into your presence; you hate everyone who does evil.
019	PSA	005	006	You destroy those who tell lies. The Lord loathes bloodthirsty and deceptive people.
019	PSA	005	007	But because of the greatness of your trustworthy love, I can come into your house; in awe of you, I bow down towards your holy Temple.
019	PSA	005	008	Lead me, Lord, you who always does what is right, save me from my enemies. Make your way clear to me.
019	PSA	005	009	Nothing they say can be trusted; their main desire is to destroy. Their throat is like an open grave; their tongues are full of flattery.
019	PSA	005	010	God, condemn them as guilty! Make them fall because of their evil plans. Throw them out because of all their sins, for they have rebelled against you.
019	PSA	005	011	But may all those who trust in you be happy—may they sing for joy forever. May you spread your protection over them so that everyone who loves your character may celebrate.
019	PSA	005	012	For you, Lord, bless those who live right; you protect them with your shield of love.
019	PSA	006	001	For the music director. To be accompanied by stringed instruments, according to the sheminith. A psalm of David. Lord, please don't condemn me because you're angry with me; please don't punish me because you're angry with me!
019	PSA	006	002	Have mercy on me, Lord, for I am weak; heal me, Lord, for I am sick to the bone.
019	PSA	006	003	I'm shaking all over in fear. How long will it be, Lord, before you do something?
019	PSA	006	004	Turn, Lord, and rescue me! Save me because of your trustworthy love!
019	PSA	006	005	For no one remembers you when they're dead. Who is able to praise you from the grave?
019	PSA	006	006	My groaning has exhausted me. Every night I soak my bed with my crying; I drench my couch with my tears.
019	PSA	006	007	With all my crying I can hardly see; my eyes grow weak because of the trouble my enemies cause me.
019	PSA	006	008	Leave me alone, all you people who do evil, for the Lord has heard me crying!
019	PSA	006	009	The Lord has heard me calling out for help; the Lord answers my prayer.
019	PSA	006	010	All who hate me will be shamefully defeated and terrified; they will run away in disgrace.
019	PSA	007	001	A psalm (shiggaion) of David, which he sang to the Lord concerning Cush, from the tribe of Benjamin. Lord my God, you are my protection. Save me from those who persecute me; please rescue me!
019	PSA	007	002	Otherwise they will tear me apart like a lion, ripping me to pieces with no one to save me.
019	PSA	007	003	If I have done what I'm accused of, if my hands are guilty,
019	PSA	007	004	If I have paid back a friend with evil, if I have robbed my enemy for no reason,
019	PSA	007	005	Then let my enemies chase me down; let them trample me in the dust and drag my reputation through the dirt. (Selah)
019	PSA	007	006	Stand up, Lord, in your anger, rise up against the fury of my enemies; wake up, Lord, and bring me justice!
019	PSA	007	007	Bring together the nations before you; rule them from your throne on high.
019	PSA	007	008	The Lord judges all people. Defend me, Lord, because I do what is right, because of my integrity.
019	PSA	007	009	Please bring an end to the evil done by the wicked; vindicate those who do good, for you are the God of right who examines hearts and minds.
019	PSA	007	010	The Most High God is my defense, the one who saves those who live right.
019	PSA	007	011	God is a fair judge who is always hostile to evil.
019	PSA	007	012	If people do not change their minds, he will sharpen his sword. He has bent and strung his bow.
019	PSA	007	013	He has prepared weapons of death, he has his flaming arrows ready.
019	PSA	007	014	See how the wicked conceive evil! They are pregnant with trouble. They give birth to dishonesty.
019	PSA	007	015	They dig a deep hole to catch people, but then fall into it themselves.
019	PSA	007	016	The trouble they cause rebounds to hit them on the head; their violence against others comes down on their own skulls.
019	PSA	007	017	I will thank the Lord because he does what is right; I will sing praises to the name of the Lord Most High.
019	PSA	008	001	For the music director. On the gittith. A psalm of David. Lord, our Lord, your magnificent reputation fills the earth! Your majesty is greater than the heavens above,
019	PSA	008	002	and is sung by the voices of children and infants. Your strength counters your opponents, silencing the enemy and the avenger.
019	PSA	008	003	When I contemplate the heavens that your hands made, the moon and stars that you placed there,
019	PSA	008	004	What are human beings that you should concern yourself with them? What are people that you should care for them?
019	PSA	008	005	You created them a little lower than God, crowning them with glory and majesty.
019	PSA	008	006	You put them in charge of all that you made, giving them authority over everything:
019	PSA	008	007	the sheep, the cattle, and the wild animals,
019	PSA	008	008	the birds in the sky, and the fish in the sea—everything that swims in the ocean.
019	PSA	008	009	Lord, our Lord, your magnificent reputation fills the earth!
019	PSA	009	001	For the music director. According to Muth-labben. A psalm of David. I will praise you, Lord, with all my heart; I will tell of all the amazing things you have done.
019	PSA	009	002	I will be glad and celebrate in you; I will sing praises to your wonderful nature, Most High God.
019	PSA	009	003	Those who hate me retreat; they fall back and die when you confront them.
019	PSA	009	004	For you have judged that I am right; you have decided fairly from your throne of judgment.
019	PSA	009	005	You have condemned the nations; you have destroyed the wicked; you have wiped out their names forever and ever.
019	PSA	009	006	The enemies are finished, ruined forever; their cities are destroyed—even the memory of them is gone.
019	PSA	009	007	But the Lord rules forever, his throne is set up for judgment.
019	PSA	009	008	The Lord judges the world rightly; he judges the nations fairly.
019	PSA	009	009	The Lord is a place of safety for those who are oppressed, a fortress in times of trouble.
019	PSA	009	010	Those who know your nature trust in you, for you don't abandon those who come to you.
019	PSA	009	011	Sing praises to the Lord who reigns in Zion! Tell the nations what he has done!
019	PSA	009	012	He does not forget to punish murderers; he does not ignore the cries of the suffering.
019	PSA	009	013	Be gracious to me, Lord! Look at how my enemies are persecuting me! Grab me back from the gates of death,
019	PSA	009	014	so I can praise you at Zion's gates, happy that you have saved me.
019	PSA	009	015	The nations have fallen into their own pit they dug; their feet are trapped by their own net they set.
019	PSA	009	016	The Lord is known for his fairness; the wicked are trapped by their own actions. (Higgaion, Selah)
019	PSA	009	017	The wicked depart, going to the grave—all nations who turn their backs on God.
019	PSA	009	018	But the needy will not be ignored forever, the hope of those who suffer will not always be dashed.
019	PSA	009	019	Stand up, Lord! Don't let human beings win! Let the nations be brought before you for judgment!
019	PSA	009	020	Lord, terrify them! Let them know they are only human! (Selah)
019	PSA	010	001	Lord, why are you so distant? Why do you hide from me in times of trouble?
019	PSA	010	002	The wicked chase down the poor with impunity. May they be trapped by the evil schemes they themselves invented.
019	PSA	010	003	For the wicked boast about what they want to do. They praise the greedy, but treat the Lord with contempt.
019	PSA	010	004	The wicked are too proud to come to God. In all their thinking they never consider God.
019	PSA	010	005	What they do always seems to go well. They're unaware of God's judgments. They ridicule all their enemies.
019	PSA	010	006	They tell themselves, “Nothing bad is going to happen to me. I'll never be in trouble!”
019	PSA	010	007	Their speech is full of cursing, lies, and threats; their tongues are always ready to spread trouble and cause evil.
019	PSA	010	008	They hide out in ambush in the villages, ready to kill innocent passers-by. They are always on the lookout for their next victim.
019	PSA	010	009	They lie in ambush like a lion ready to attack, ready to leap out from their hiding place to seize their victim. They capture the helpless, throwing a net over them.
019	PSA	010	010	Their victims are knocked down, laid low. They fall under the strength of the wicked.
019	PSA	010	011	They tell themselves, “God won't notice. He's looking the other way. He won't ever see anything.”
019	PSA	010	012	Take a stand, Lord! Raise your hand to strike! Don't forget those who can't defend themselves.
019	PSA	010	013	Why do the wicked think they can treat God with such contempt? Why do they think that God won't make them accountable?
019	PSA	010	014	But you do see the trouble and grief they cause. Take it into your own hands. The helpless trust in you; you defend the orphans.
019	PSA	010	015	Destroy the power of the wicked, those evil people! Call each of them to account until there are none left!
019	PSA	010	016	Lord, you are King forever and ever! The nations will vanish from their lands.
019	PSA	010	017	Lord, you have heard the longing cries of those who are suffering. You will encourage them, for you will listen to them.
019	PSA	010	018	You will defend the rights of orphans and the oppressed so that those who are mere human beings here on earth will never terrorize them again.
019	PSA	011	001	For the music director: A psalm of David. Lord, you are my protection. So how can you tell me, “Fly away to the mountains like a bird”?
019	PSA	011	002	Look, the wicked are drawing their bows, loading them with arrows ready to shoot from the shadows at good people.
019	PSA	011	003	When the foundations of society are destroyed, what can those who live right do?
019	PSA	011	004	The Lord is in his Temple; the Lord's throne is in heaven. He keeps a close eye on everyone, watching them carefully.
019	PSA	011	005	The Lord examines both those who do right and those who do evil, but he hates those who love violence.
019	PSA	011	006	He will make blazing coals and sulfur rain down on the wicked; a scorching wind is what's coming on them.
019	PSA	011	007	The Lord does what is right, and he loves those who live right. Those who do good will see him face to face.
019	PSA	012	001	For the music director. To the Sheminith. A psalm of David. Help, Lord, for all the good people have gone! Those who trust in you have disappeared from among the people on earth.
019	PSA	012	002	Everyone lies to their neighbors. They flatter with nice talk, but they don't mean what they say.
019	PSA	012	003	Stop their flattery, Lord, and silence their boasts—
019	PSA	012	004	these people who say, “We will succeed through what we say; our mouths belong to us. We don't take orders from anyone!”
019	PSA	012	005	“Because of the violence the helpless have suffered, and because of the groans of the poor, I will rise up to defend them,” says the Lord. “I will give them the protection they have been longing for.”
019	PSA	012	006	What the Lord says is trustworthy, as pure as silver refined seven times in a furnace.
019	PSA	012	007	You, Lord will keep the oppressed safe; you will protect us from these kinds of people forever;
019	PSA	012	008	even though the wicked are all around us, and evil is being promoted everywhere.
019	PSA	013	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. How long, Lord, are you going to forget me? Forever? How long will you turn away from me?
019	PSA	013	002	How long must I be in inner turmoil, feeling sad all day long? How long will my enemy be victorious over me?
019	PSA	013	003	Think about this, and answer me, Lord my God. Give me back my strength, otherwise I'm going to die,
019	PSA	013	004	and my enemy will say, “I defeated him!” and my opponents will celebrate my downfall.
019	PSA	013	005	But I trust in your never-failing love, I will be happy because you save me.
019	PSA	013	006	I will sing to the Lord because he has treated me with such generosity!
019	PSA	014	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. Only fools tell themselves, “God doesn't exist.” They are completely immoral; they commit terrible sins; not a single one of them does anything good.
019	PSA	014	002	The Lord watches from heaven to see whether anyone understands—if there's anyone who wants to come to God.
019	PSA	014	003	They have all gone their own way, they are totally depraved; none of them does anything good, not even one.
019	PSA	014	004	Won't these people who do evil ever learn? They consume my people as if they were eating bread, and refuse to pray to the Lord.
019	PSA	014	005	Look, they will become terrified, because God is with those who live right.
019	PSA	014	006	The wicked dismiss the plans of the poor people, but the Lord looks after them.
019	PSA	014	007	If only the Lord's salvation would come from Zion! When the Lord restores his people, the people of Jacob will celebrate, and the people of Israel will be glad.
019	PSA	015	001	A psalm of David. Who may enter your sanctuary, Lord? Who may come into your presence on your holy mountain?
019	PSA	015	002	Those who live without fault and do what is right, those who sincerely tell the truth.
019	PSA	015	003	They do not slander, do not treat their neighbors badly, do not gossip about people they know.
019	PSA	015	004	They reject people the Lord has rejected, but honor those who follow the Lord. They keep their promises even when it's hard to do. They don't change their minds.
019	PSA	015	005	They lend money without charging interest. They don't take bribes to testify against the innocent. Those who act like this will never ever fall.
019	PSA	016	001	A psalm (miktam) of David. Take care of me, Lord, for I come to you for protection.
019	PSA	016	002	I tell the Lord, “Apart from you Lord, I don't have anything that's good.”
019	PSA	016	003	As for the holy people in the land, they are the ones who are truly great. I appreciate them.
019	PSA	016	004	Those who run after other gods will face a lot of trouble. I will not participate in their offerings of blood, I will not even speak the names of their gods.
019	PSA	016	005	Lord, you alone are all I have; you give me what I need; you safeguard my future.
019	PSA	016	006	The land divisions have worked out in my favor—my property is wonderful!
019	PSA	016	007	I will bless the Lord who gives me good advice; even at night my conscience tells me what is right.
019	PSA	016	008	I have always kept the Lord in front of me. I will not be shaken, for he is right beside me.
019	PSA	016	009	That's why I'm so happy! That's why I am full of joy! That's why my body lives in hope!
019	PSA	016	010	For you will not abandon me in the grave, nor will you allow your Holy One to experience decay.
019	PSA	016	011	You have shown me the path of life, filling me with joy with your presence and the delight of living with you forever.
019	PSA	017	001	A prayer of David. Lord, please hear my cry for justice! Please pay attention to my call for help! Listen to the prayer of an honest man!
019	PSA	017	002	Vindicate me before you—for you see what is right.
019	PSA	017	003	You have observed my thoughts, you have visited me at night, you have examined me—and you have found nothing wrong. I promised myself I wouldn't say anything I shouldn't.
019	PSA	017	004	With regard to the actions of others: I have done what you told me and I have avoided what violent people do.
019	PSA	017	005	I have not strayed from your path; my feet have not slipped from it.
019	PSA	017	006	God, I call out to you because I know you will answer; please listen carefully to what I have to say.
019	PSA	017	007	Show me how wonderful your trustworthy love really is, Savior of those who come to you for protection against their enemies!
019	PSA	017	008	Keep me safe as someone you love; hide me underneath your wings.
019	PSA	017	009	Protect me from the attacks of the wicked who want to destroy me, from my enemies who surround me, intent on killing me.
019	PSA	017	010	They have no compassion, and all they have to say is pure arrogance.
019	PSA	017	011	They hunt me down and surround me, looking for the chance to knock me down in the dust.
019	PSA	017	012	They are like lions, longing to tear their prey apart; like fierce lions crouching in ambush.
019	PSA	017	013	Lord, stand up and confront them! Force them to back down! By your sword rescue me from the wicked!
019	PSA	017	014	Lord, by your power, save me from people whose only thought is for this world. May they be filled with what you have in store for them, their children too, with left-overs for their grandchildren!
019	PSA	017	015	As for me, I shall see your face in all its goodness. When I awake, I will be so pleased to see you face to face.
019	PSA	018	001	To the music director. A psalm of David the servant of the Lord, who sang the words of this song to the Lord on the day when the Lord saved him from all his enemies, and from Saul. He sang: I love you, Lord. You are my strength.
019	PSA	018	002	The Lord is my rock, my fortress, and my Savior. He is my God, my rock who protects me. He shields me from harm, his power protects me, he keeps me safe.
019	PSA	018	003	I call for help from the Lord who should be praised, and he saves me from those who hate me.
019	PSA	018	004	Ropes of death encircled me, surging waters of destruction flooded over me;
019	PSA	018	005	The grave wound its ropes around me; death set snares for me.
019	PSA	018	006	In my despair I called on the Lord—I cried out to my God for help. He heard my voice from his Temple—my cry for help reached his ears.
019	PSA	018	007	The earth shook to and fro; the foundations of the mountains trembled, shaking because of his anger.
019	PSA	018	008	Smoke came out of his nostrils, and fire came from his mouth; burning coals blazed before him.
019	PSA	018	009	He parted the heavens and came down, with dark clouds beneath his feet.
019	PSA	018	010	Riding on an angel he flew, swooping on the wings of the wind.
019	PSA	018	011	He hid himself in darkness, covering himself with black thunderclouds.
019	PSA	018	012	Hailstones and burning coals flew out from his brightness, passing through his thick clouds.
019	PSA	018	013	The Lord thundered from heaven; the voice of the Most High sounded among the hailstones and burning coals.
019	PSA	018	014	He fired his arrows, scattering his enemies; he routed them with his lightning bolts.
019	PSA	018	015	You roared, Lord, and by the wind from the breath of your nostrils the valleys of the sea were exposed and the foundations of the earth were uncovered.
019	PSA	018	016	He reached down his hand from above and grabbed hold of me. He pulled me out of the deep water.
019	PSA	018	017	He rescued me from my powerful enemies, from those who hated me and who were much stronger than me.
019	PSA	018	018	They came at me at my worst possible moment, but the Lord supported me.
019	PSA	018	019	He set me free, he rescued me because he's my friend.
019	PSA	018	020	The Lord rewarded me because I do what's right; he repaid me because I am innocent.
019	PSA	018	021	For I have followed the Lord's ways; I have not sinned by turning away from my God.
019	PSA	018	022	I have kept all his laws in mind; I have not ignored his commandments.
019	PSA	018	023	I am blameless in his sight; I keep myself from sinning.
019	PSA	018	024	The Lord rewarded me for doing what's right. I am innocent in his sight.
019	PSA	018	025	You show trust to those who trust; you show integrity to those with integrity,
019	PSA	018	026	You show yourself pure to those who are pure, but you show yourself smart to those who are crafty.
019	PSA	018	027	You save the humble, but you bring down the proud.
019	PSA	018	028	You light my lamp! Lord, my God, you light up my darkness!
019	PSA	018	029	With you, I can charge down a troop of soldiers; with you, my God, I can climb a fortress wall.
019	PSA	018	030	God's way is absolutely right. What the Lord says is trustworthy. He is a shield to all who come to him for protection.
019	PSA	018	031	For who is God except the Lord? Who is the rock, except our God?
019	PSA	018	032	God makes me strong and keeps me safe.
019	PSA	018	033	He makes me surefooted like the deer, able to walk the heights in safety.
019	PSA	018	034	He teaches me how to fight in battle; he gives me the strength to draw a bronze bow.
019	PSA	018	035	You protect me with the shield of your salvation; you support me with your powerful right hand; your help has made me great.
019	PSA	018	036	You gave me space in which to walk, and prevented my feet from slipping.
019	PSA	018	037	I chased my enemies, and caught up with them. I did not turn around until I had destroyed them.
019	PSA	018	038	I struck them down—they couldn't get up. They fell at my feet.
019	PSA	018	039	You made me strong for battle; you made those who rose up against me kneel down before me.
019	PSA	018	040	You made my enemies run away; I destroyed all my enemies.
019	PSA	018	041	They cried out for help, but no one came to rescue them. They even called out to the Lord, but he did not answer them.
019	PSA	018	042	I ground them into dust, like dust in the wind. I threw them out like mud in the street.
019	PSA	018	043	You rescued me from rebellious people; you made me ruler over nations—people I didn't know now serve me.
019	PSA	018	044	As soon as they hear of me, they obey; foreigners cringe before me.
019	PSA	018	045	They lose heart, and come trembling in surrender from their strongholds.
019	PSA	018	046	The Lord lives! Blessed be my rock! May the God who saves me be praised!
019	PSA	018	047	God avenges me, he subdues peoples under me,
019	PSA	018	048	he rescues me from those who hate me. You keep me safe from those who rebel against me, you save me from violent men.
019	PSA	018	049	That's why I will praise you among the nations, Lord; I will sing praises about who you are.
019	PSA	018	050	You have saved the king so often, showing your trustworthy love to David, your anointed, and to his descendants forever.
019	PSA	019	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. The heavens declare God's glory; the skies above announce what he has made.
019	PSA	019	002	Each day speaks constantly about God's glory to the next day; each night shares knowledge of God with the next night.
019	PSA	019	003	They speak without speech or words; their voice is not audible;
019	PSA	019	004	Yet what they say is heard all over the earth; their message goes to the whole world. God has made a home in the heavens for the sun.
019	PSA	019	005	It's like a bridegroom coming out of his room, like a fit athlete happy to run a race.
019	PSA	019	006	It rises on one side of the heavens and travels across to the other. Nothing is hidden from its heat.
019	PSA	019	007	The Lord's law is beneficial, renewing spiritual life. The Lord's teaching is trustworthy, making inexperienced people wise.
019	PSA	019	008	The Lord's instructions are right, making people glad. The Lord's commandments are sincere, helping people see what is good.
019	PSA	019	009	Reverence for the Lord is right, and lasts forever. The Lord's judgments are both true and fair.
019	PSA	019	010	They are more to be valued than gold, even the finest gold; they are sweeter than honey, even the purest honey coming straight from the honeycomb.
019	PSA	019	011	They also warn your servant. By keeping them I'm richly rewarded.
019	PSA	019	012	Who's aware of their own mistakes? Don't punish me for these faults I'm unaware of.
019	PSA	019	013	Don't let your servant commit deliberate sins. Don't let them rule over me. Then I will be without fault, innocent of such rebellion.
019	PSA	019	014	May you be pleased with the words I speak, and the thoughts I think, Lord my rock and my redeemer.
019	PSA	020	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. May the Lord answer you when you are in trouble; may the name of the God of Jacob protect you.
019	PSA	020	002	May the Lord send you help from the sanctuary, and may he support you from Zion.
019	PSA	020	003	May the Lord remember all your offerings, and accept all your burnt sacrifices. (Selah)
019	PSA	020	004	May the Lord give you whatever you really want; may he make all your plans successful.
019	PSA	020	005	May we shout for joy over your victory, and set up banners in the name of our God. May the Lord answer all your requests.
019	PSA	020	006	Now I know that the Lord saves the one he has anointed. He will answer him from his holy heaven, and save his anointed by his powerful right hand.
019	PSA	020	007	Some trust in chariots and some in war horses, but we trust in who the Lord our God is.
019	PSA	020	008	They collapse and fall down, but we rise and stand up.
019	PSA	020	009	May the Lord save the king! Please answer us when we call for help!
019	PSA	021	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. The king celebrates your strength, Lord; he is so happy you made him victorious!
019	PSA	021	002	You gave him everything he wanted; you didn't hold back anything he asked for.
019	PSA	021	003	You welcomed him on his return with special blessings; you placed a crown of pure gold on his head.
019	PSA	021	004	He asked you to give him a good life, and you gave him a long life, forever and ever.
019	PSA	021	005	Your victories brought him great glory; you granted him splendor and majesty.
019	PSA	021	006	You give him blessings forever. He is full of joy because you are with him.
019	PSA	021	007	For the king trusts in the Lord; he stands firm because of the trustworthy love of the Most High.
019	PSA	021	008	You, the king, will find and capture all your enemies; you will seize everyone who hates you.
019	PSA	021	009	When you appear on the scene you will burn them up like in a furnace; the Lord in his anger will destroy them, burning them up with fire.
019	PSA	021	010	You will wipe out their children from the earth, their descendants from humankind.
019	PSA	021	011	Though they plot evil against you, their malicious schemes will not succeed.
019	PSA	021	012	They will turn and run away when they see your arrows fired at them.
019	PSA	021	013	Rise up, Lord, for you are strong! We will sing and praise your power!
019	PSA	022	001	For the music director. To the tune “Doe of the Dawn.” A psalm of David. My God, my God, why have you abandoned me? Why are you so far away when I groan, asking for help?
019	PSA	022	002	My God, every day I cry out to you, but you don't answer; at night too, but I get no rest.
019	PSA	022	003	Yet you are holy, and the praises of Israel are your throne.
019	PSA	022	004	Our forefathers trusted in you; they trusted and you rescued them.
019	PSA	022	005	They cried out to you for help, and they were saved. They trusted in you and were not defeated.
019	PSA	022	006	But I'm a worm, not a man, scorned and despised by everyone.
019	PSA	022	007	People who see me mock me. They laugh at me and shake their heads, saying,
019	PSA	022	008	“He trusts in the Lord—well then, let the Lord save him! If the Lord is such a friend, then let the Lord rescue him!”
019	PSA	022	009	However, you brought me safely through birth, and led me to trust in you at my mother's breasts.
019	PSA	022	010	I was entrusted to you from birth; from the time I was born you have been my God.
019	PSA	022	011	Do not be distant from me, because trouble is close by and no one else can help.
019	PSA	022	012	Enemies surround me like a herd of bulls; strong bulls from Bashan have encircled me.
019	PSA	022	013	Like roaring lions tearing at their prey they open their mouths wide against me.
019	PSA	022	014	I feel like I'm being poured out like water. I'm falling apart as if all my bones have become loose. My mind feels like it's wax melting inside me.
019	PSA	022	015	My strength has dried up like a piece of broken pottery. My tongue is stuck to the roof of my mouth. You're burying me as if I'm already dead.
019	PSA	022	016	Evil men surround me like a pack of dogs. They have pierced my hands and feet.
019	PSA	022	017	I'm so thin I can count all my bones. People stare at me and gloat.
019	PSA	022	018	They divide my clothing among them; they roll dice for my clothes.
019	PSA	022	019	But you, Lord, don't be far away from me! You are my strength—hurry, come and help me!
019	PSA	022	020	Save me from death by the sword! Save my life—the only one I have—from the dogs!
019	PSA	022	021	Rescue me from the mouth of the lion and from the wild bulls!
019	PSA	022	022	I will tell my people all the wonderful things you have done; I will praise you in the congregation.
019	PSA	022	023	Praise the Lord, all who worship him! Honor him, every descendant of Jacob! Be in awe of him, every descendant of Israel!
019	PSA	022	024	For he has not ridiculed or scorned the suffering of the poor; he has not turned away from them, he has listened to their cries for help.
019	PSA	022	025	You are the subject of my praise in the great assembly. I will fulfill my promises before those who worship you.
019	PSA	022	026	The poor shall eat, and they shall be satisfied. All who come to the Lord will praise him—may you all live forever!
019	PSA	022	027	Everyone in the whole world will repent and return to the Lord; all the nations will worship before you.
019	PSA	022	028	For kingly power belongs to the Lord; he is the one who rules over the nations.
019	PSA	022	029	All who prosper come to feast and worship. Bow down before him, all those destined for the grave—for none can keep themselves alive.
019	PSA	022	030	Our descendants will serve him; they will tell the next generation about the Lord.
019	PSA	022	031	They will come and tell those yet to be born how good the Lord is, and all that he has done!
019	PSA	023	001	A psalm of David. Since the Lord is my shepherd, I have everything I need.
019	PSA	023	002	He gives me rest in green fields. He leads me towards quietly flowing streams.
019	PSA	023	003	He revives me. He guides me along the right paths because that's the kind of person he is.
019	PSA	023	004	Even when I walk through the valley dark as death, I'm not afraid of any evil, because you are right there with me; your rod and your staff protect me.
019	PSA	023	005	You prepare a banquet for me before my enemies. You honor me by anointing my head with olive oil. My cup is so full it overflows!
019	PSA	023	006	I'm absolutely certain that your goodness and trustworthy love will be with me all through my life, and I will live in the house of the Lord forever.
019	PSA	024	001	A psalm of David. The earth is the Lord's, and everything that is in it belongs to him. The world is his, and everyone who lives there.
019	PSA	024	002	For he is the one who laid its foundations on the seas, setting it in place on the waters.
019	PSA	024	003	Who is allowed to go up the Lord's mountain? Who is permitted to stand in his holy place?
019	PSA	024	004	Those who have clean hands and pure minds, who don't worship idols, and who don't lie under oath.
019	PSA	024	005	They will take with them the blessing of the Lord, vindicated by the God who saves them.
019	PSA	024	006	These are the kind of people who may go to the Lord and worship before you, God of Jacob. (Selah)
019	PSA	024	007	Open up, you gates! Swing wide, you ancient doors! Let the King of glory come in!
019	PSA	024	008	Who is this King of glory? The Lord, strong and powerful, mighty in battle.
019	PSA	024	009	Open up, you gates! Swing wide, you ancient doors! Let the King of glory come in!
019	PSA	024	010	Who is this King of glory? The Lord Almighty, he is the King of glory! (Selah)
019	PSA	025	001	A psalm of David. Lord, I come to worship you.
019	PSA	025	002	I trust in you, my God. Don't let me be humiliated, and don't let my enemies triumph over me.
019	PSA	025	003	No one who trusts in you will be humiliated, but humiliation comes to those who are deliberately dishonest.
019	PSA	025	004	Show me your ways, Lord; teach me to follow your paths.
019	PSA	025	005	Lead me in your truth and teach me, for you are the God of my salvation. All day long I put my trust in you.
019	PSA	025	006	Remember, Lord, your compassion and trustworthy love—they are eternal!
019	PSA	025	007	Please don't remember the sins of my youth when I rebelled against you. Instead, remember me according to your trustworthy love, remember me because of your goodness, Lord.
019	PSA	025	008	The Lord is good and he is right; that is why he shows the way to those who are lost.
019	PSA	025	009	He leads those who are humble in doing what's right, teaching them his way.
019	PSA	025	010	The Lord's paths are those of trustworthy love and truth for those who keep his agreement and do as he says.
019	PSA	025	011	Lord, because of your nature, forgive my many sins.
019	PSA	025	012	Who are those who respect the Lord? He will show them the path to choose.
019	PSA	025	013	They will continue to be prosperous, and their descendants will inherit the land.
019	PSA	025	014	The Lord is friends with those who respect him, explaining to them his agreement.
019	PSA	025	015	I always look to the Lord, for he rescues me when I'm trapped.
019	PSA	025	016	Watch over me and be good to me, because I am all alone and suffering.
019	PSA	025	017	My problems get bigger and bigger. Please save me from all I'm going through.
019	PSA	025	018	See all my troubles and trials. Please forgive my sins.
019	PSA	025	019	Look at how many enemies I have, and how they really hate me!
019	PSA	025	020	Please look after me and save me! Don't let me be humiliated, for you are the one who protects me.
019	PSA	025	021	May integrity and honesty defend me because I place my confidence in you.
019	PSA	025	022	God, please deliver the people of Israel from all their troubles!
019	PSA	026	001	A psalm of David. Confirm that I'm innocent, Lord, for I have acted with integrity, and I have trusted in the Lord without fail.
019	PSA	026	002	Examine me, Lord, test me; investigate my thoughts and intentions.
019	PSA	026	003	For I always remember your trustworthy love, and I follow your truth.
019	PSA	026	004	I don't join in with liars and I don't associate with hypocrites.
019	PSA	026	005	I refuse to get together with those who do evil, and I won't involve myself with the wicked.
019	PSA	026	006	I wash my hands to show my innocence. I come to worship at your altar, Lord,
019	PSA	026	007	singing my thanks, telling of all the wonderful things you have done.
019	PSA	026	008	Lord, I love your house, the place where you live in your glory.
019	PSA	026	009	Please don't sweep me away along with sinners. Don't include me with those who commit murder,
019	PSA	026	010	whose hands carry out their evil schemes and grab hold of bribes.
019	PSA	026	011	For I don't do that—I act with integrity. Save me and be gracious to me!
019	PSA	026	012	I stand for what's right, and I will praise the Lord when we meet together to worship him.
019	PSA	027	001	A psalm of David. The Lord is my light and my salvation! How could anyone scare me? The Lord is my life's fortress! How could anyone terrify me?
019	PSA	027	002	When evil people come at me to tear me apart, it's my enemies, those who are against me, they're the ones who trip and fall.
019	PSA	027	003	Even if an army surrounds me, I won't be frightened. Even if I am attacked, I will still trust in God.
019	PSA	027	004	I only ask the Lord for one thing: I just want to live in the house of the Lord throughout my life, contemplating the Lord's goodness and thinking about his Temple.
019	PSA	027	005	When troubles come he will protect me and keep me safe, hiding me in his house, as secure as if he'd placed me on a high rock.
019	PSA	027	006	He will hold my head high over my enemies who are all around me. I shall offer sacrifices in his house with shouts of joy, and I will sing praises to the Lord.
019	PSA	027	007	Listen to me, Lord, when I call for help. Be gracious and answer me.
019	PSA	027	008	You told me, “Come to me.” I am coming to you, Lord.
019	PSA	027	009	Don't refuse to talk to me. Don't be angry with your servant and turn away. You are the one who helps me, so please don't reject me and abandon me, God of my salvation.
019	PSA	027	010	Even if my father and my mother abandon me, the Lord will take care of me.
019	PSA	027	011	Lord, teach me your way and lead me along the right path, because my enemies are against me—
019	PSA	027	012	don't hand me over to them and their evil intentions, for they are making false accusations against me and threatening me with violence.
019	PSA	027	013	However, I'm absolutely sure that I will see the Lord's goodness even in this life.
019	PSA	027	014	Trust in the Lord! Be confident—he will give you courage! Trust in the Lord!
019	PSA	028	001	A psalm of David. Lord, my rock, I'm calling out to you. Please listen to me! For if you don't respond, I'll be like those who go down into the grave.
019	PSA	028	002	Listen as I appeal for mercy, as I call for help, as I hold up my hands in prayer towards your holy Temple.
019	PSA	028	003	Don't drag me off with the wicked, with those who do evil, who speak nicely to their neighbors while in their minds they're plotting evil.
019	PSA	028	004	Give them what they deserve for their evil actions. Pay them back for what they've done. Give them the reward they've earned!
019	PSA	028	005	For they don't pay any attention to what the Lord does, or to what he created. So he will destroy them—they will never be restored.
019	PSA	028	006	Praise the Lord! For he has heard my appeal for mercy!
019	PSA	028	007	The Lord is my strength and my shield. I trust in him and he helps me. I'm so happy, and I sing my thanks to him.
019	PSA	028	008	The Lord gives strength to his people; he is a safe refuge for the one he has anointed.
019	PSA	028	009	Save your people! Bless your “special possession”! Be their shepherd and carry them in your arms forever!
019	PSA	029	001	A psalm of David. Honor the Lord, children of God, honor his glory and strength.
019	PSA	029	002	Honor the Lord for his glorious character, bow in reverence to the Lord in his brilliant holiness.
019	PSA	029	003	The Lord's voice sounds over the sea. The God of glory thunders. The Lord thunders over the vast ocean.
019	PSA	029	004	The Lord's voice is powerful; the Lord's voice is majestic;
019	PSA	029	005	the Lord's voice shatters the cedars, even breaking the cedars of Lebanon.
019	PSA	029	006	He makes the mountains of Lebanon skip like a calf, and Mount Hermon like a young wild ox.
019	PSA	029	007	The Lord's voice blazes out like lightning flashes.
019	PSA	029	008	The Lord's voice causes an earthquake in the desert; the desert of Kadesh shakes.
019	PSA	029	009	The Lord's voice makes the pregnant deer go into labor; it strips bare the forests. In his Temple all the worshipers shout, “Glory!”
019	PSA	029	010	The Lord sits on his throne above the floodwaters; the Lord is the eternal King.
019	PSA	029	011	The Lord gives strength to his people; the Lord blesses them with peace.
019	PSA	030	001	A psalm of David. A psalm for the dedication of the Temple. I want to tell everyone how good you are, Lord, for you saved me, and you didn't let my enemies triumph over me.
019	PSA	030	002	Lord, my God, I called out to you for help, and you have healed me.
019	PSA	030	003	Lord, you rescued me from the grave, you brought me back to life, saving me from going down into the pit of death.
019	PSA	030	004	You who trust the Lord, sing praises to him, and be thankful for his holy character!
019	PSA	030	005	For his anger only lasts a moment, but his favor lasts a lifetime. You may spend the night in tears, but happiness comes with the morning.
019	PSA	030	006	When things were going well, I said, “Nothing will ever shake me!”
019	PSA	030	007	Lord, when you showed me your favor I stood as strong as a mountain; when you turned away from me I was terrified.
019	PSA	030	008	I called out to you for help, Lord. I asked the Lord for grace, saying,
019	PSA	030	009	What would you gain if I die, if I go down into the pit of death? Would my dust praise you? Would it tell of your trustworthiness?
019	PSA	030	010	Please listen to me, Lord, and be gracious to me! Lord, you are the one who helps me.
019	PSA	030	011	You have turned my weeping into dancing. You have taken off my clothes of sackcloth and dressed me in happiness,
019	PSA	030	012	so I can sing praises to you and not keep quiet. Lord my God, I will thank you forever!
019	PSA	031	001	A psalm of David. For the music director. Lord, you are the one who keeps me safe; please don't let me ever be humiliated. Save me, because you always do what is right.
019	PSA	031	002	Please listen to me, and be quick to rescue me. Be my rock of protection, my strong fortress of safety.
019	PSA	031	003	You are my rock and my fortress. For the sake of your reputation, please lead me and guide me.
019	PSA	031	004	Help me escape from the hidden net that they set to trap me, for you are the one who protects me.
019	PSA	031	005	I put myself in your hands. Save me, Lord, for you are a trustworthy God.
019	PSA	031	006	I hate those who devote themselves to pointless idols; I trust in the Lord.
019	PSA	031	007	I will celebrate, happy in your love that never fails, for you have seen the problems I face and have paid attention to my troubles.
019	PSA	031	008	You haven't handed me over to my enemies; you have set me free.
019	PSA	031	009	Be kind to me Lord, for I am upset. I can hardly see from so much crying. I am completely wasting away.
019	PSA	031	010	Grief is killing me; my life is cut short by sadness; I am falling apart because of my troubles; I am worn to the bone.
019	PSA	031	011	I am ridiculed by my enemies, particularly by my neighbors. My friends dread meeting me; people who see me in the street run the other way.
019	PSA	031	012	I have been forgotten as if I were dead; I'm ignored like a broken pot.
019	PSA	031	013	I hear many people whispering about me; terror surrounds me. They plot together against me, planning to kill me.
019	PSA	031	014	But I put my trust in you, Lord, saying, “You are my God!”
019	PSA	031	015	My whole life is in your hands! Save me from those who hate me and persecute me!
019	PSA	031	016	May you look kindly on me, your servant. Save me because of your trustworthy love.
019	PSA	031	017	Lord, don't let me be disgraced, for I'm calling out to you. Instead let the wicked be disgraced, let them be silent in the grave.
019	PSA	031	018	Shut the mouths of those who tell lies against good people—those who speak contemptuously in their pride and arrogance!
019	PSA	031	019	How wonderful is the goodness you have reserved for those who honor you! In front of everyone you give this goodness to those who come to you for help.
019	PSA	031	020	You shelter and protect them with your presence, far from their enemies who scheme against them. You keep them safe from attacks and accusations.
019	PSA	031	021	Bless the Lord, for he has shown me his wonderful trustworthy love when my city was being attacked
019	PSA	031	022	Terrified I cried out, “I am being destroyed right in front of you!” But you heard my cry when I called out for you to help me.
019	PSA	031	023	Love the Lord, all you who trust in him! The Lord takes care of those who trust him, but he pays back in full those who are arrogant.
019	PSA	031	024	Be strong and be confident, all you who put your hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	032	001	A psalm of David. How happy are those whose wrongs are forgiven, whose sins are covered.
019	PSA	032	002	How happy are those whose sins the Lord does not count against them, those who do not act deceptively.
019	PSA	032	003	When I kept quiet, my body fell apart as I groaned in distress all day long.
019	PSA	032	004	You beat me day and night, my strength dried up as in the heat of summer. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	005	Then I confessed my sins to you. I did not hide the wrongs I had done. I said to myself, “I will confess my disobedience to the Lord,” and you forgave the guilt of my sins. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	006	Therefore let all who are faithful pray to you while there's time, so when trouble comes in like a flood it will not overwhelm them.
019	PSA	032	007	For you are my refuge, you protect me from trouble. You surround me with songs of salvation. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	008	“I will instruct you, teaching you the way to follow. I will advise you, watching out for you.
019	PSA	032	009	You mustn't be like a horse or a mule that doesn't know which way to go without a bit or a bridle. Otherwise they can't be controlled.”
019	PSA	032	010	The wicked have many problems, but those who trust in the Lord will be surrounded by his never-failing love.
019	PSA	032	011	So be happy in the Lord and celebrate, you who do good. Shout for joy, all you who live right!
019	PSA	033	001	Let those who do good shout for joy—those who live right should praise him!
019	PSA	033	002	Praise the Lord with the lyre, play music to him on the ten-stringed harp.
019	PSA	033	003	Sing a new song to him; play your instruments well and shout for joy.
019	PSA	033	004	For the word of the Lord is true, and he is trustworthy in everything he does.
019	PSA	033	005	He loves all that is good and right; the earth is full of the Lord's trustworthy love.
019	PSA	033	006	The Lord spoke the word and the heavens were made; his mouth breathed all the stars into existence.
019	PSA	033	007	He gathers the waters of the sea together, he keeps the ocean depths in store.
019	PSA	033	008	Let all the earth show reverence to the Lord; let all the world's inhabitants be in awe of him.
019	PSA	033	009	For he spoke and the world came into existence; he gave the command and it was created.
019	PSA	033	010	The Lord foils the decisions of the nations, he frustrates the plans of the peoples,
019	PSA	033	011	But the Lord's plan stands forever—what he decides lasts for all generations.
019	PSA	033	012	Happy is the nation whose God is the Lord, the people he has chosen as specially belonging to him.
019	PSA	033	013	The Lord looks from heaven and sees the whole of humanity,
019	PSA	033	014	from his throne he watches all those who live on earth.
019	PSA	033	015	He created their minds, so he knows everything they do.
019	PSA	033	016	Even the greatest army cannot save a king; the greatest strength cannot save a warrior.
019	PSA	033	017	Don't deceive yourself: a warhorse can't give you victory—even its incredible strength won't save you.
019	PSA	033	018	The Lord watches over those who reverently follow him, those who place their hope in his trustworthy love
019	PSA	033	019	to save them from death and to keep them alive when famine strikes.
019	PSA	033	020	We place our confidence in the Lord; he is our help and our defender.
019	PSA	033	021	We are so happy about him, for we trust in his holy character.
019	PSA	033	022	Lord, let your trustworthy love rest upon us as we hope in you.
019	PSA	034	001	A psalm of David concerning the time he pretended to be mad in front of Abimelech who then sent him away. I will always bless the Lord; my mouth will continually praise him.
019	PSA	034	002	From the bottom of my heart I am proud of the Lord; those who are humble will hear and be happy.
019	PSA	034	003	Glorify God with me; together let's honor his reputation.
019	PSA	034	004	I asked the Lord for help, and he answered me. He set me free from all my fears.
019	PSA	034	005	The faces of those who look to him will shine with joy; they will never be downcast with shame.
019	PSA	034	006	This poor man cried out, and the Lord heard me, and saved me from all my troubles.
019	PSA	034	007	The angel of the Lord stands guard over all those who honor him, keeping them safe.
019	PSA	034	008	Taste, and you will see that the Lord is good! How happy are those who trust in his protection!
019	PSA	034	009	Show your reverence for the Lord, you who are his holy people, for those who respect him have everything they need.
019	PSA	034	010	Lions may grow weak and hungry, but those who trust in the Lord have all that is good.
019	PSA	034	011	Children, listen to me! I will teach you how to respect the Lord.
019	PSA	034	012	Who of you wants to live a long and happy life?
019	PSA	034	013	Then don't let your tongue speak evil, or your lips tell lies.
019	PSA	034	014	Reject what is evil, do what is good. Look for peace, and work to make it a reality.
019	PSA	034	015	The Lord watches over those who do right, and he hears when they cry for help.
019	PSA	034	016	The Lord sets himself against those who do evil. He will wipe out even the memory of them from the earth.
019	PSA	034	017	But when his people call out for help, he hears them and rescues them from all their troubles.
019	PSA	034	018	The Lord is close beside those who are broken-hearted; he saves those whose spirits are crushed.
019	PSA	034	019	Those who do right have many problems, but the Lord solves all of them.
019	PSA	034	020	He keeps them safe—not a single one of their bones will be broken.
019	PSA	034	021	Evil kills the wicked. Those who hate good people will suffer for their wrongdoing.
019	PSA	034	022	The Lord saves the lives of his servants. Those who trust in his protection will not suffer for their wrongdoings.
019	PSA	035	001	A psalm of David. Oppose my opponents, Lord; fight those who are fighting against me.
019	PSA	035	002	Put your armor on, and pick up your shield. Get ready, come and help me.
019	PSA	035	003	Draw your spear and your javelin, confront those who are chasing me. Tell me, “I am your salvation!”
019	PSA	035	004	Shame them! Humiliate those who are trying to kill me! Turn them back! Disgrace those who are planning to hurt me!
019	PSA	035	005	Let them be like chaff blown by the wind; let the angel of the Lord drive them away.
019	PSA	035	006	May their path be dark and slippery, with the angel of the Lord chasing them down.
019	PSA	035	007	For no reason they set a net to catch me; for no reason they dug a pit to trap me.
019	PSA	035	008	Let disaster come on them suddenly; let the net they set catch them instead; let the pit they dug trap them instead.
019	PSA	035	009	Then I will be glad in the Lord; I will be happy in his salvation.
019	PSA	035	010	Every part of me will say, Who can compare to you, Lord? You rescue the weak from the strong; the poor and needy from robbers.
019	PSA	035	011	Hostile witnesses stand up to testify against me, accusing me of crimes I don't know anything about.
019	PSA	035	012	They pay me back with evil instead of good. I feel like giving up.
019	PSA	035	013	But when they were sick, I put on clothes of sackcloth in sympathy. I denied myself through fasting. May my prayer for them return to bless me too.
019	PSA	035	014	I was upset for them, as if they were my own friends or family; I bowed down in grief as if I was mourning my own mother.
019	PSA	035	015	But when I was in trouble, they gathered around and laughed at me. Even strangers I don't know attacked me, constantly tearing me apart.
019	PSA	035	016	Like irreligious people mocking a cripple they mock me and call me names, gnashing their teeth at me.
019	PSA	035	017	How long, Lord, will you sit by and just watch? Save me from their vicious attacks; defend the only life I have from these lions.
019	PSA	035	018	Then I will thank you in front of the whole congregation and praise you in front of all the people.
019	PSA	035	019	Don't let my enemies take pleasure in my troubles, those people who hate me and tell lies about me, gloating over me for no reason.
019	PSA	035	020	They are not looking for peace; they invent malicious and deceptive schemes against innocent peace-loving people.
019	PSA	035	021	They open their mouths wide to make accusations against me, saying, “Look! Look! We saw it with our own eyes!”
019	PSA	035	022	But Lord, you've seen all this! Say something! Don't give up on me, Lord!
019	PSA	035	023	Wake up! Get up and defend me, my Lord and my God! Take up my case and make sure justice is done!
019	PSA	035	024	Vindicate me, my Lord and my God, because you are just and right. Don't let them gloat over me.
019	PSA	035	025	Don't let them say to themselves, “Look! We got what we wanted!” Don't let them say, “We completely destroyed him!”
019	PSA	035	026	Make them totally ashamed, all those who are happy for the trouble I'm in. Let those who are celebrating over me be covered with shame and dishonor.
019	PSA	035	027	Instead let those who are pleased I've been vindicated celebrate and shout for joy. Let them always say, “How great is the Lord! He is happy when his servants live in peace and have what they need.”
019	PSA	035	028	I will tell others about your character of truth and right, praising you all day long!
019	PSA	036	001	For the music director. A psalm of David, servant of the Lord. Evil speaks to the wicked, deep down in their minds, for in their eyes they have no need to respect God.
019	PSA	036	002	In their own eyes they're so wonderful that they can't even see their sin and do something about it.
019	PSA	036	003	Whatever they say is deceptive and deceitful. They no longer do anything wisely or for good.
019	PSA	036	004	Even when they're lying in bed they think up evil schemes. They commit themselves to a way of life that is no good. They choose evil, and don't reject it.
019	PSA	036	005	Lord, your faithful love reaches to the heavens, your trustworthiness to the clouds.
019	PSA	036	006	Your goodness is like the highest mountains, your fairness is like the deepest oceans. Lord, you save both the people and the animals.
019	PSA	036	007	God, how priceless is your trustworthy love! Everyone can find protection under the shelter of your wings.
019	PSA	036	008	They gain strength from the wonderful food you provide in your house; you give them drink from your refreshing river.
019	PSA	036	009	You are the source of life; you are the light by which we see.
019	PSA	036	010	Extend your trustworthy love to those who know you, and your goodness to those who truly live right.
019	PSA	036	011	Don't let the arrogant trample me down; don't let the wicked drive me out.
019	PSA	036	012	Now look! See how those who do evil have fallen—thrown down, unable to get up.
019	PSA	037	001	A psalm of David. Don't be upset over wicked people, or be jealous of those who do wrong.
019	PSA	037	002	For like grass, they will quickly dry up; like plants, they will soon wither away.
019	PSA	037	003	Trust in the Lord, and do good. Live in the land and feed on faithfulness.
019	PSA	037	004	Find your happiness in the Lord, and he will give you what you want the most.
019	PSA	037	005	Entrust all that you do to the Lord. Place your confidence in him and he will help you.
019	PSA	037	006	He will make your vindication shine like a light, the rightness of your cause like the noonday sun.
019	PSA	037	007	Be still in God's presence; wait patiently for him. Don't be upset over people who prosper when they carry out their evil schemes.
019	PSA	037	008	Give up your anger! Let go of your rage! Don't get mad—it only results in evil!
019	PSA	037	009	For the wicked will be destroyed, and those who trust in the Lord will take possession of the land.
019	PSA	037	010	In a little while the wicked will be no more—though you look for them you won't find them.
019	PSA	037	011	The humble will own the land; they will live there happily, in peace and prosperity.
019	PSA	037	012	The wicked plot evil against those who do good, gnashing their teeth at them.
019	PSA	037	013	But the Lord laughs at them, for he sees their coming day of judgment.
019	PSA	037	014	The wicked draw their swords, and bend their bows to destroy the poor and needy, to kill those who live right.
019	PSA	037	015	But the swords of the wicked will slice through their own hearts, and their bows will be broken.
019	PSA	037	016	It's better to do right and only have a little, than to be wicked and rich.
019	PSA	037	017	For the power of the wicked will be broken, but the Lord supports those who do right.
019	PSA	037	018	The Lord knows what is happening to the innocent and grants them an eternal inheritance.
019	PSA	037	019	They will not be humiliated in bad times; even in days of famine they will have plenty to eat.
019	PSA	037	020	But the wicked will die. The enemies of the Lord are like the flowers of the field—they will vanish like smoke.
019	PSA	037	021	The wicked borrow, but don't repay; while those who do right give generously.
019	PSA	037	022	Those who are blessed by God will own the land, but those he curses will die.
019	PSA	037	023	The Lord shows the right path to those who follow him, and is happy with the way they live.
019	PSA	037	024	Though they may trip up, they will not fall to the ground, for the Lord holds their hand.
019	PSA	037	025	Once I was young, and now I've grown old, yet I've never seen those who do right abandoned, nor their children having to beg for bread.
019	PSA	037	026	They are always kind, and generous with their loans; their children are a blessing.
019	PSA	037	027	Reject evil, do what is good, and you will live forever in the land.
019	PSA	037	028	For the Lord loves fairness and he will never abandon those who are trustworthy. He will protect them forever. But the children of the wicked will die.
019	PSA	037	029	Those who do right will own the land and will live there forever.
019	PSA	037	030	People who do right give good advice, explaining what is fair.
019	PSA	037	031	God's law lives in their minds, so they will not slip from his way.
019	PSA	037	032	The wicked lie in wait for those who do good, intending to kill them.
019	PSA	037	033	But the Lord will not let them fall into the hands of the wicked, and he will not let those who do good be condemned when they are put on trial.
019	PSA	037	034	Trust in the Lord, and stay on his path. He will lift you up and give you the land to own. You will see when the wicked are destroyed.
019	PSA	037	035	I have watched the wicked acting brutally, spreading like a large tree in its native land.
019	PSA	037	036	But when I passed that way the next time, they were gone. I searched for them but couldn't find them.
019	PSA	037	037	Observe the innocent, look at those who do right! Those who love peace have a future!
019	PSA	037	038	But those who are rebellious will be altogether destroyed; the wicked have no future.
019	PSA	037	039	The Lord saves those who live right; he is their protection in times of trouble.
019	PSA	037	040	The Lord helps them and rescues them from the wicked. He saves them because they go to him for protection.
019	PSA	038	001	A psalm of David, for a memorial. Lord, please don't condemn me because you're angry with me; don't punish me because you're furious with me!
019	PSA	038	002	Your arrows have pierced me deeply, your hand has come down hard on me.
019	PSA	038	003	Because you're so upset with me, not a single part of my body is healthy; I am completely sick because of my sins.
019	PSA	038	004	I'm drowning in guilt—the burden is too heavy to bear.
019	PSA	038	005	My wounds are infected—they're smelling—all because of my stupidity.
019	PSA	038	006	I am bent over, doubled up in pain. The whole day I walk around crying my eyes out.
019	PSA	038	007	Inside I'm burning up with fever; no part of my body is healthy.
019	PSA	038	008	I'm worn out, totally down. I groan because of the anguish I feel in my heart.
019	PSA	038	009	Lord, you know what I desperately want, you hear every sigh I make.
019	PSA	038	010	My heart is racing, leaving me with no strength; my eyesight is failing.
019	PSA	038	011	My loved ones and my friends don't come near me because they're afraid of what I've got. Even my family keeps me at a distance.
019	PSA	038	012	Those who are trying to kill me set traps for me; those who want to hurt me make threats against me, working on their deceitful schemes all day long.
019	PSA	038	013	I act as if I'm deaf to what they're saying, and pretend to be dumb so I don't have to speak.
019	PSA	038	014	Like a man who can't hear, and who doesn't reply—that's me!
019	PSA	038	015	For I'm waiting on you, Lord! You will answer for me, my Lord and my God.
019	PSA	038	016	I'm asking you, Lord, please don't let my enemies gloat over me, don't let them be glad when I trip up.
019	PSA	038	017	For I'm about ready to collapse—the pain never stops.
019	PSA	038	018	I do confess my sins; I am terribly sorry for what I've done.
019	PSA	038	019	I have many powerful enemies—they are very active, hating me for no reason.
019	PSA	038	020	They pay me back evil for good; they accuse me for the good I try to do.
019	PSA	038	021	Don't give up on me, my Lord and my God, don't stay away from me.
019	PSA	038	022	Hurry, come and help me, Lord my salvation.
019	PSA	039	001	For Jeduthun, the music director. A psalm of David. I told myself, “I will be careful in what I do, and not sin in what I say. I will keep my mouth shut when the wicked are around.”
019	PSA	039	002	So I was completely silent—I didn't even say anything good. But the pain inside only got worse.
019	PSA	039	003	My mind burned as if on fire; I had to say what I was thinking:
019	PSA	039	004	Lord, remind me. How short is my life? How long do I have? Remind me how quickly my life will pass.
019	PSA	039	005	Just look at the tiny amount of days you have given me! In your eyes my whole lifetime is like nothing. Our lives here are just a breath… (Selah)
019	PSA	039	006	Human beings are just shadows walking around. They pointlessly rush through life, trying to pile up possessions without knowing who will get them.
019	PSA	039	007	So Lord, what am I looking for? I put my hope in you.
019	PSA	039	008	Save me from my rebellion. Don't let me be mocked by fools.
019	PSA	039	009	I will stay quiet, I won't say a word, for it's you who has done this to me.
019	PSA	039	010	Please stop hitting me! Your beating has worn me out!
019	PSA	039	011	When you discipline us, reprimanding us for our sins, it's like a moth eating up what is precious to us. All of us are just a breath… (Selah)
019	PSA	039	012	Please hear my prayer, Lord! Listen to my cry for help! Don't be deaf to my weeping. Please treat me as your guest, passing through, just like my forefathers.
019	PSA	039	013	Please leave me alone so I can be cheerful again, before I am dead and gone.
019	PSA	040	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. I waited for the Lord patiently, and he turned to me—he heard my cry for help.
019	PSA	040	002	He pulled me out of the pit of destruction, out from the mud and the slime. He set me on a rock, and gave me a safe place to stand.
019	PSA	040	003	He gave me a new song to sing, a song of praise to our God. Many people will see and be in awe, and they will put their trust in him.
019	PSA	040	004	Happy are those who trust in the Lord, who do not look for help from the arrogant or from those who worship idols.
019	PSA	040	005	Lord my God, you have done so many wonderful things for us, and you have so many plans for us. No one compares to you. I want to tell all that you've done—blessings too many to count.
019	PSA	040	006	You don't want sacrifices and offerings. Now you have helped me understand—you're not asking for burnt offerings or sin offerings.
019	PSA	040	007	Then I said, “Look! Here I am! I've come to do what is written about me in the scroll of the Book.
019	PSA	040	008	I am pleased to do your will, my God—your Law guides my mind.”
019	PSA	040	009	I have announced the good news of salvation to the whole congregation. I don't keep quiet, Lord, as you know.
019	PSA	040	010	I have not kept the truth of your goodness hidden inside me—I have spoken of your trustworthiness and your salvation. I have not concealed your unfailing love and your faithfulness from the whole congregation.
019	PSA	040	011	Lord, please don't keep back your mercy from me. May your trustworthy love and faithfulness always be my protection.
019	PSA	040	012	For I'm experiencing so many problems—I can't even count them! My sins have piled up so high I can't see over them. They're more than the number of hairs on my head! I feel like giving up!
019	PSA	040	013	Lord, please save me! Hurry, Lord, help me!
019	PSA	040	014	Please defeat and humiliate the people who are trying to kill me; turn back in disgrace those who want to hurt me.
019	PSA	040	015	May they be shocked at their defeat, those who taunted me.
019	PSA	040	016	But may everyone who comes to you be happy and glad; may those who love your salvation always say, “The Lord is great!”
019	PSA	040	017	As for me, I am poor and needy. May the Lord think about me. Help me! Save me! My God, please don't wait!
019	PSA	041	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. How happy are those who take care of the poor! When they are in trouble the Lord will save them.
019	PSA	041	002	The Lord protects them and keeps them alive. They will live happily in the land, and they will not be handed over to their enemies.
019	PSA	041	003	The Lord looks after them when they're sick; he makes them well from their illness.
019	PSA	041	004	“Lord, please be gracious to me,” I asked. “Please heal me, for I have sinned against you.”
019	PSA	041	005	Those who hate me only say evil things about me. “When is he going to die, and people forget all about him?” they ask.
019	PSA	041	006	They come to visit me, but their sympathy is not sincere. They're only interested in the bad news, which they spread around as soon as they leave.
019	PSA	041	007	All who hate me talk in whispers about my condition, hoping for the worst.
019	PSA	041	008	“He's been cursed with some terrible disease,” they say. “Now he's bed-ridden he'll never recover!”
019	PSA	041	009	Even my best friend, the one I trusted, who shared meals with me—even he has turned against me.
019	PSA	041	010	But you Lord, please be gracious to me, make me well so I can repay them!
019	PSA	041	011	I know you are pleased with me because you have not let my enemies win and shout in triumph over me.
019	PSA	041	012	You have supported me because of my integrity, you have brought me into your presence forever.
019	PSA	041	013	Praise the Lord, the God of Israel, from eternity to eternity! Amen and amen!
019	PSA	042	001	For the music director. A psalm (maskil) of the sons of Korah. As a deer longs for flowing streams, so I long for you, God.
019	PSA	042	002	I am thirsty for God, the living God. When can I go and see God's face?
019	PSA	042	003	My tears have been my only food, day and night, while people ask me all day long, “Where is your God?”
019	PSA	042	004	I am crushed as I remember how I walked with the crowds, leading them in a procession to the house of God, with shouts of joy and songs of thanks among the worshipers at the festival.
019	PSA	042	005	Why am I so discouraged? Why do I feel so sad? I will hope in God; I will praise him because he is the one who saves me—
019	PSA	042	006	my God! Even though I am very discouraged, I still remember you: from the land of Jordan and Hermon, and from Mount Mizar.
019	PSA	042	007	You thunder through the raging waters, through the noise of the waterfalls. Your crashing waves surge over me—I feel like I'm drowning.
019	PSA	042	008	But every day the Lord shows me his trustworthy love; every night he gives me songs to sing—a prayer to the God of my life.
019	PSA	042	009	I cry out, “My God, my rock, why have you forgotten me? Why must I go around weeping because of the attacks of my enemies?”
019	PSA	042	010	The mocking of my attackers crushes my bones. They're always asking me, “Where is your God?”
019	PSA	042	011	Why am I so discouraged? Why do I feel so sad? I will hope in God; I will praise him because he is the one who saves me—my God!
019	PSA	043	001	God, please vindicate me! Plead my case against an unfaithful nation; save me from these wicked and dishonest people.
019	PSA	043	002	For you, God, are my protection—so why have you turned your back on me? Why must I go around weeping because of the attacks of my enemies?
019	PSA	043	003	Send your light and your truth so they can guide me; let them lead me to your holy mountain, to the place where you live.
019	PSA	043	004	I will go to God's altar, to God who makes me truly happy. I will praise you on the harp, God, my God.
019	PSA	043	005	Why am I so discouraged? Why do I feel so sad? I will hope in God; I will praise him because he is the one who saves me—my God!
019	PSA	044	001	For the music director. A psalm (maskil) of the sons of Korah. God, we have heard with our own ears—our forefathers have told us—all you did in their times, long ago.
019	PSA	044	002	Through your power you drove out the other nations so you could settle our ancestors there; you defeated the nations and you sent our ancestors to occupy the land.
019	PSA	044	003	They did not conquer the land using their swords; it was not through their own strength that the victory was won—it was by your strength, your power, and your presence with them, because you loved them.
019	PSA	044	004	God, you are my King; command victories for Jacob!
019	PSA	044	005	Only through you can we repel our enemies; only in your name can we defeat our opponents.
019	PSA	044	006	I do not trust my bow; I do not have confidence in my sword to save me.
019	PSA	044	007	You are the one who saves us from our enemies; you defeat those who hate us.
019	PSA	044	008	God, we proudly thank you all day long, and praise your name forever. (Selah)
019	PSA	044	009	But now you have rejected and disgraced us; you no longer accompany our armies.
019	PSA	044	010	You made us run from our enemies, and those who hate us have taken whatever they wanted.
019	PSA	044	011	You have handed us over like sheep to be slaughtered; you have scattered us among the other nations.
019	PSA	044	012	You have sold your own people for next to nothing, making no profit on the sale.
019	PSA	044	013	You have made a mockery of us before our neighbors, we are ridiculed and laughed at by those around us.
019	PSA	044	014	You have made us a joke to the other nations; they scornfully shake their heads at us.
019	PSA	044	015	We are humiliated all day long; we hold our heads in shame,
019	PSA	044	016	because of all the insults from the people mocking us, because our vengeful enemies are right in front of us.
019	PSA	044	017	All this has happened to us even though we didn't forget you; we haven't been unfaithful to the promises we made to you.
019	PSA	044	018	We have not turned away from you, not in thought, nor in action.
019	PSA	044	019	Even so, you crushed us, and made us into a jackal's den. You have covered us with the darkness of death.
019	PSA	044	020	If we had forgotten the name of our God, or worshiped other gods,
019	PSA	044	021	wouldn't God have been aware of this, because he knows everyone's thoughts?
019	PSA	044	022	But because of you we are killed all day long; we're considered just sheep to be slaughtered.
019	PSA	044	023	Lord, wake up! Why are you sleeping? Get up! Don't turn your back on us forever!
019	PSA	044	024	Why do you look away from us and take no notice of our suffering and misery?
019	PSA	044	025	We lie ruined in the dust, our bodies facedown in the dirt.
019	PSA	044	026	Stand up! Come and help us! Save us because of your trustworthy love!
019	PSA	045	001	For the music director. To the tune “Lilies.” A psalm (maskil) of the sons of Korah. A love song. I am moved to write about this wonderful subject. Let me share what I have written for the king. What I say comes from the pen of a skilled author.
019	PSA	045	002	You are more handsome than anyone else. You always speak graciously, for God has blessed you forever.
019	PSA	045	003	Strap on your sword, mighty warrior, stride out in glory and majesty!
019	PSA	045	004	In your majesty ride out to victory, in the defense of truth, humility, and right, because you are strong and act powerfully.
019	PSA	045	005	Your sharp arrows pierce the hearts of your enemies; the nations fall under you.
019	PSA	045	006	Your throne comes from God, and lasts forever and ever. The scepter with which you rule is a scepter of fairness.
019	PSA	045	007	You love what is right and hate what is wrong. That is why God, your God, has placed you above everyone else by anointing you with the oil of joy.
019	PSA	045	008	Your robes are perfumed with aloes, myrrh, and cassia; music played on stringed instruments in palaces decorated with ivory makes you happy.
019	PSA	045	009	The daughters of kings are among the noblewomen; the queen stands beside you on your right, wearing jewelry made of gold from Ophir.
019	PSA	045	010	Listen to what I have to say, daughter; please pay attention. Don't pine for your people and your family.
019	PSA	045	011	May the king desire you in your beauty; respect him, for he is your lord.
019	PSA	045	012	The people of Tyre will come with gifts; rich people will look for your favor.
019	PSA	045	013	Inside her preparation room the princess bride looks wonderful in her golden gown.
019	PSA	045	014	Wearing her beautiful clothes she is brought to the king, followed by her bridesmaids.
019	PSA	045	015	What a happy, joyful procession enters the king's palace!
019	PSA	045	016	Your sons will take the place of your fathers; as princes you will make them rulers throughout the land.
019	PSA	045	017	Through my words you will be famous through all generations, and nations will praise you forever and ever.
019	PSA	046	001	For the music director by the sons of Korah. According to alamoth, a song. God is our protection and our strength; always ready to help when troubles come.
019	PSA	046	002	So we will not be afraid though the earth shakes, though the mountains fall into the depths of the sea,
019	PSA	046	003	though the waters roar and foam, though the mountains tremble as the waters surge violently! (Selah)
019	PSA	046	004	A river flows to bring happiness to those in God's city, the holy place where the Most High lives.
019	PSA	046	005	God is in the midst of the city; it will never fall. God protects it as soon as it is light.
