019	PSA	049	007	but no one can pay to rescue another from death; no one can pay a ransom to God.
019	PSA	049	008	Redemption is beyond price; no one could ever pay enough
019	PSA	049	009	that they could live forever and not face the grave.
019	PSA	049	010	Everyone knows that the wise die, those who are foolish and stupid too, leaving what they have to the next generation.
019	PSA	049	011	They think their homes will last forever, that where they live will continue for all generations.
019	PSA	049	012	But human beings, for all their fame, don't understand. They die, just like the animals.
