019	PSA	049	019	but their destiny is the same as their forefathers: they will never again see the light of day.
019	PSA	049	020	Human beings, for all their fame, don't understand, and they die, just like the animals.
019	PSA	050	001	A psalm of Asaph. The Lord, the Almighty God, speaks! He summons everyone on earth, from the east to the west.
019	PSA	050	002	God shines out of Mount Zion, perfect in beauty.
019	PSA	050	003	Our God arrives, and does not stay quiet. Fire flames before him, burning everything up; a violent storm rages around him.
019	PSA	050	004	He summons the heavens above and the earth to witness the judgment of his people.
019	PSA	050	005	“Bring me those who trust in me—those who confirmed the agreement with me through sacrifice.”
019	PSA	050	006	The heavens declare his decisions are right, for God himself is the judge. (Selah)
019	PSA	050	007	“My people, listen to what I have to say. I am bringing charges against you, Israel. I am God, your God!
019	PSA	050	008	I'm not complaining about your sacrifices or burnt offerings that you offer all the time.
019	PSA	050	009	I do not require bulls from your barns or goats from your pens,
019	PSA	050	010	for I own all the animals of the forest, and the cattle on a thousand hills belong to me.
019	PSA	050	011	I know every bird of the mountains; all living things in the fields are mine.
019	PSA	050	012	If I were hungry, I wouldn't tell you, for the earth and everything in it are mine.
019	PSA	050	013	Do I eat the flesh of bulls or drink the blood of goats?
019	PSA	050	014	Give an offering of thanks to God; keep the promises you made to the Most High,
019	PSA	050	015	and call on me when you're in trouble. I will rescue you, and you will thank me.”
019	PSA	050	016	But to the wicked God says, “What's the point of mechanically repeating my laws or making empty promises about obeying the agreement?
019	PSA	050	017	You hate my discipline, and you toss my words away, leaving them behind you.
