019	PSA	054	005	The evil my enemies have done will come back upon them. I depend on you to destroy them.
019	PSA	054	006	I will happily offer a sacrifice to you; I will praise the kind of person you are, Lord, for you are good.
019	PSA	054	007	For he has saved me from all my troubles; and I have seen those who hated me defeated.
019	PSA	055	001	For the music director. With stringed instruments. A psalm (maskil) of David. God, please hear my prayer; don't ignore my cry for help!
019	PSA	055	002	Please listen, and give me an answer. I'm terribly troubled by my problems! I'm frantic!
019	PSA	055	003	For my enemies are screaming at me; the wicked are intimidating me. They rain down suffering on me, angrily assaulting me in their hatred.
019	PSA	055	004	My heart thumps in agony! Terrified, I feel I'm about to die!
019	PSA	055	005	I'm in a panic, trembling with fear; feelings of horror wash over me.
019	PSA	055	006	I tell myself, If only God would give me wings like a dove so I could fly away and be at peace!
019	PSA	055	007	I would fly far away to escape, and stay in the wilderness. (Selah)
019	PSA	055	008	I would hurry to a place to hide, out of the wind, safe from the raging storm.
019	PSA	055	009	Confuse them, Lord! Muddle what they're saying, for I see violence and conflict in the city.
019	PSA	055	010	They patrol the city walls day and night, and wickedness and trouble are within the city.
019	PSA	055	011	The ones causing destruction are inside the city; frauds and cheats are always on the streets.
019	PSA	055	012	The problem is that it's not an enemy who mocks me—I could stand that. It's not someone who hates me who insults me—I could avoid them.
019	PSA	055	013	No, it's you, a man just like me, my best friend who I know so well!
019	PSA	055	014	Our friendship was so close. We used to have great talks together as we walked with everyone to the house of God.
019	PSA	055	015	May death come quickly to them; may they go down into the grave alive, because evil finds its home in them.
019	PSA	055	016	As for me, I cry out to God, and the Lord will save me.
019	PSA	055	017	I weep and groan morning, noon, and night, and he listens to me.
019	PSA	055	018	He rescues me, keeping me safe and sound from my attackers, because there are so many against me.
019	PSA	055	019	God who has ruled from the beginning will hear me and answer them. (Selah) For they refuse to change and don't respect God.
019	PSA	055	020	As for my best friend, he attacked his friends who had no quarrel with him; he broke the promises he had made to them.
019	PSA	055	021	What he says is as smooth as butter, but inside he plans war; his words are as soothing as oil, but they cut like sharp swords.
019	PSA	055	022	Throw your burdens onto the Lord and he will take care of you. He will never allow those who live right to fall.
019	PSA	055	023	But you, God, will bring down murderers and liars, throwing them into the pit of destruction before they have even lived half their lives. As for me, I will trust in you.
019	PSA	056	001	For the music director. According to “Dove on Distant Oaks.” A psalm (miktam) of David concerning the time the Philistines captured him in Gath. God, please be gracious to me, for people are persecuting me; my attackers fight against me all day long.
019	PSA	056	002	My enemies chase me down all the time—there are many of them, attacking me in their arrogance.
019	PSA	056	003	But when I'm afraid, I trust in you.
019	PSA	056	004	I thank God for his promises. I trust in God, so why should I be fearful? What can mere human beings do to me?
019	PSA	056	005	They constantly twist my words against me; they spend all their time thinking of evil things to do to me.
019	PSA	056	006	They gather together in their hiding places to keep watch on me, hoping to kill me.
019	PSA	056	007	Will they escape when they do so much evil? God, in anger bring these people down!
019	PSA	056	008	You've kept track of all my wanderings. You've collected all my tears in your bottle. You've kept a record of each one.
019	PSA	056	009	Then those who hate me will run away when I call for your help. For I know this: God is for me!
019	PSA	056	010	I thank God for his promises. I thank the Lord for his promises.
019	PSA	056	011	I trust in God, so why should I be fearful? What can mere human beings do to me?
019	PSA	056	012	God, I will keep my promises to you. I will give thank offerings to you,
019	PSA	056	013	for you have saved me from death and kept me from falling. Now I walk in the presence of God, in the light that gives life.
019	PSA	057	001	For the music director. According to “Do Not Destroy.” A psalm (miktam) of David concerning the time he fled from Saul and hid in the cave. Please be kind to me, God! Be kind to me because I come to you for protection. I will shelter under the shadow of your wings until the danger is past.
019	PSA	057	002	I cry out for help to God Most High, to God who vindicates me.
019	PSA	057	003	From heaven he sends his help, and he saves me. He defeats those who persecute me. (Selah) God sends me his unfailing love, showing he is completely trustworthy.
019	PSA	057	004	I am surrounded by man-eating lions—I am forced to live with them! Their teeth are spears and arrows, and their tongues are swords.
019	PSA	057	005	God, your greatness is above the highest heavens; and your glory covers the whole earth!
019	PSA	057	006	They set a trap to catch me. I was so depressed. They dug a pit on my path but they were the ones who fell into it. (Selah)
019	PSA	057	007	I have confidence in you, God, I have confidence in you. I will sing songs of praise to you.
019	PSA	057	008	I say to myself, “Wake up!” Wake up, harp and lyre! I will wake up the dawn!
019	PSA	057	009	I will thank you among the peoples, Lord; I will sing your praises among the nations.
019	PSA	057	010	Your faithful love reaches to the heavens; your trustworthiness to the clouds.
019	PSA	057	011	God, your greatness is above the highest heavens; and your glory covers the whole earth!
019	PSA	058	001	For the music director. According to “Do Not Destroy.” A psalm (miktam) of David. You leaders, do you really say what is right? Do you judge people fairly?
019	PSA	058	002	No, for in your minds you plan evil. You cause violence everywhere!
019	PSA	058	003	The wicked are sinners from birth; from the moment they're born they tell lies.
019	PSA	058	004	They have venom like that of a poisonous snake, and just like a cobra they stop listening,
019	PSA	058	005	refusing to hear the voice of the snake charmers or the spellbinders.
019	PSA	058	006	God, break their teeth, and smash the jaws of these lions, Lord.
019	PSA	058	007	May they vanish like water that flows away; when they shoot their arrows may they miss their mark.
019	PSA	058	008	May they be like the slime of snails that dissolves away, like a stillborn child that never saw the light of day.
019	PSA	058	009	Before the cooking pot is hot from burning thorns, whether fresh or dry, God will blow them away.
019	PSA	058	010	Those who live right will be happy when they see there is punishment; they will wash their feet in the blood of the wicked.
019	PSA	058	011	They will say, “There is definitely a reward for those who live right; there is certainly a God who judges fairly on earth.”
019	PSA	059	001	For the music director. According to “Do Not Destroy.” A psalm (miktam) of David, concerning the time Saul sent out soldiers to watch David's house in order to kill him. Rescue me from my enemies, God! Protect me from those who are attacking me!
019	PSA	059	002	Rescue me from these evil people! Save me from these murderers!
019	PSA	059	003	See how they're lying in wait to kill me! Powerful men are gathered against me, Lord, even though I have not sinned or done anything wrong.
019	PSA	059	004	Even though I'm not guilty they hurry to prepare an attack on me. Please stand up, come and help me, and see what's going on.
019	PSA	059	005	You are God, the Lord Almighty, God of Israel. Stand up, and punish all the nations. Don't have any mercy on these evil traitors. (Selah)
019	PSA	059	006	In the evening they return, snarling like dogs as they roam around the city.
019	PSA	059	007	See what evil talk comes pouring out of their mouths! Words sharp as swords, for they say to themselves, “Who can hear us?”
019	PSA	059	008	But you, Lord, you laugh at them; you pour scorn on all the nations.
019	PSA	059	009	You are my strength! I will look to you, God, for you are the one who protects me.
019	PSA	059	010	In his trustworthy love, God will come and save me. He will show me how my enemies are defeated.
019	PSA	059	011	Don't kill them right away, otherwise my people will quickly forget what you have done. By your power make them stagger around and then fall down, Lord our protection.
019	PSA	059	012	Let them be caught out by the evil things they say, the words they proudly speak—brought down by their curses and the lies they tell!
019	PSA	059	013	Destroy them in your anger! Destroy them completely! Then everyone will know that God rules in Israel!
019	PSA	059	014	In the evening they return, snarling like dogs as they roam around the city.
019	PSA	059	015	They wander around, looking for things to eat, and howl when they're not satisfied.
019	PSA	059	016	But I will sing of your strength; in the morning I will sing for joy about your trustworthy love. For you have been my protection; my place of safety in my time of trouble.
019	PSA	059	017	You are my strength, I sing praises to you, for you are the one who protects me—the God who shows me his trustworthy love!
019	PSA	060	001	For the music director. According to “Lily of the Testimony.” A psalm (miktam) of David, useful for teaching, about the time he fought against Aram-naharaim and Aram-zobah, and then Joab returned and killed 12,000 Edomites in the Valley of Salt. You, God, have rejected us! You have broken us; you have been angry with us; but now you have to welcome us back!
019	PSA	060	002	You have sent earthquakes on our land and split it apart. Now heal the cracks, for the land is still having tremors.
019	PSA	060	003	You have been very hard on your people; you gave us wine that made us stagger around.
019	PSA	060	004	But you have given those who respect you the banner of truth to unfurl and rally around. (Selah)
019	PSA	060	005	Rescue those you love! Answer us, and save us by your power!
019	PSA	060	006	God has spoken from his Temple: “Triumphantly I divide up Shechem, and portion out the Valley of Succoth.
019	PSA	060	007	Both Gilead and Manasseh belong to me. Ephraim is my helmet, and Judah is my scepter.
019	PSA	060	008	I will treat Moab as my washbasin; I will place my sandal on Edom; I will shout in triumph over Philistia.”
019	PSA	060	009	Who will bring me into the fortified city? Who will lead me into Edom?
019	PSA	060	010	Have you rejected us, God? Won't you lead our armies?
019	PSA	060	011	Please give us help against our enemies, for human help is worthless.
019	PSA	060	012	Our strength is in God, and he will crush our enemies.
019	PSA	061	001	For the music director. With stringed instruments. A psalm of David. God, please hear my cry for help; please listen to my prayer.
019	PSA	061	002	From this distant place, far from home, I cry out to you as my courage fails. Take me to a rock high above me where I will be safe,
019	PSA	061	003	for you are my protection, a strong tower where my enemies cannot attack me.
019	PSA	061	004	Let me live with you forever; protect me under the shelter of your wings. (Selah)
019	PSA	061	005	For you, God, have heard the promises I've made. You have given all those who love your character your special blessing.
019	PSA	061	006	Please give the king many extra years; may his reign last through generations.
019	PSA	061	007	May he always live in your presence; may your trustworthy love and faithfulness protect him.
019	PSA	061	008	Then I will always sing praises to you, and every day I will keep my promises to you.
019	PSA	062	001	For Jeduthun, the music director. A psalm of David. Only in God do I find peace; my salvation comes from him.
019	PSA	062	002	He is the one who protects me and saves me; he keeps me safe so I will never be in danger.
019	PSA	062	003	How long are you going to attack me? All of you against one man! To you I'm just a broken wall, a collapsed fence.
019	PSA	062	004	They plan to throw me down from my high position; they love to tell lies. They say nice things to me, but inside they're cursing me. (Selah)
019	PSA	062	005	Only in God do I find peace; my hope comes from him.
019	PSA	062	006	He is the one who protects me and saves me; he keeps me safe so I will not be in danger.
019	PSA	062	007	My salvation and my success come from God alone; God is my security and my protection.
019	PSA	062	008	My people, always trust in him. Pour out all your thoughts to him, for he is the one who looks after us. (Selah)
019	PSA	062	009	Ordinary people are mere breaths, while leaders are just fakes. Put them all together and weigh them on scales and they wouldn't weigh more than air!
019	PSA	062	010	Don't trust in money made by extortion or robbery. Don't be proud of your wealth even if you are successful—don't make money what you live for.
019	PSA	062	011	God has already made it clear—I have heard it many times—power belongs to you, God.
019	PSA	062	012	You show us trustworthy love. You give back to people in return for what they've done.
019	PSA	063	001	A psalm of David, when he was in the Judean desert. God, you are my God, I eagerly look for you. I am thirsty for you; all that I am longs for you in this dry, weary, waterless land.
019	PSA	063	002	I see you in the Temple; I watch your power and glory.
019	PSA	063	003	Your trustworthy love is better than life itself; I will praise you.
019	PSA	063	004	I will thank you as long as I live; I lift up my hands as I celebrate your wonderful character.
019	PSA	063	005	You satisfy me more than the richest food; I will praise you with joyful songs.
019	PSA	063	006	I think of you all night long as I lie on my bed meditating about you.
019	PSA	063	007	For you are the one who helps me; I sing happily from under your wings.
019	PSA	063	008	I hold on to you; your strong arms lift me up.
019	PSA	063	009	Those who are trying to destroy me will go down into the grave.
019	PSA	063	010	They will be killed by the sword; they will become food for jackals.
019	PSA	063	011	But the king will be happy for what God has done. All who follow God will praise him, but those who tell lies will be silenced.
019	PSA	064	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. God, please listen to my complaint. Protect me because my enemies scare me.
019	PSA	064	002	Shelter me from the plots of the wicked, from this evil mob.
019	PSA	064	003	What they say cuts like swords; they fire off poisonous words like arrows.
019	PSA	064	004	They shoot from their hiding places at innocent people—doing this without warning, not afraid of being caught.
019	PSA	064	005	They encourage one another to do evil, planning how to secretly trap people, telling themselves, “Nobody will notice.”
019	PSA	064	006	They plot wicked things. “What a great plan we've created!” they say. There are no limits to the depths to which human minds and thoughts can sink.
019	PSA	064	007	But God will shoot them with arrows; all of a sudden they will be wounded.
019	PSA	064	008	What they themselves say will trip them up; people who see them will mock them, shaking their heads at them.
019	PSA	064	009	Then everyone will be frightened. They will say that this is the work of God, and they will think about what he has done.
019	PSA	064	010	Those who are right with the Lord will be happy in him, they will go to him for protection. Those who live right will praise him.
019	PSA	065	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. A song. God, you deserve to be praised, and in Zion we will keep our promises to you.
019	PSA	065	002	You hear our prayers; everyone comes to you.
019	PSA	065	003	Even though we're drowning in our sins and our disobedience, you forgive us.
019	PSA	065	004	Happy are those you choose to keep close to you, those who live in your courts! We are delighted with the blessings we receive in your house, your holy Temple!
019	PSA	065	005	In your goodness you answer us through the wonderful things you do, God of our salvation. You can be trusted by everyone on earth, including those sailing distant oceans.
019	PSA	065	006	You made the mountains by your power, for you have great strength.
019	PSA	065	007	You calm the raging seas and crashing waves, you silence the noisy shouts of the nations.
019	PSA	065	008	Everyone, even those in distant lands, are amazed by the wonderful things you do, from the east to the west they sing for joy.
019	PSA	065	009	You care for the earth and water it; you make it very productive. God, your river is full of water to grow the grain—this is what you have planned.
019	PSA	065	010	You fill the plowed furrows with water, you soften the ridges; you bless the growing crops.
019	PSA	065	011	You make the high point of the year a wonderful harvest, filling the wagons with good things.
019	PSA	065	012	The pastures in the wilderness grow lush; the hillsides are clothed in bright flowers.
019	PSA	065	013	The meadows are covered with flocks of sheep, and the valleys with fields of grain. Everything triumphantly sings for joy.
019	PSA	066	001	For the music director. A song. A psalm. Everyone on earth, shout for joy to God!
019	PSA	066	002	Sing about his marvelous reputation; praise him for his goodness!
019	PSA	066	003	Tell God, “What you do is awesome! Your enemies are forced to bow before you because of your power.
019	PSA	066	004	Everyone on earth worships you, singing your praises—singing praises because of who you are.” (Selah)
019	PSA	066	005	Come and see what God has done! What he does for people is truly awesome!
019	PSA	066	006	He turned the Red Sea into dry land, and his people walked across through the waters. We celebrated there because of what he did.
019	PSA	066	007	He rules forever through his power. He keeps an eye on the nations, watching to make sure no rebels rise up in opposition. (Selah)
019	PSA	066	008	Let all people everywhere bless our God, and loudly sing praises to him.
019	PSA	066	009	He has kept us alive, and he has not let us fall.
019	PSA	066	010	God, you have tested us, refining us like silver.
019	PSA	066	011	You caught us in your net; you placed heavy burdens on our backs.
019	PSA	066	012	You let people ride roughshod over us; we suffered through fire and flooding, but you brought us to a safe place.
019	PSA	066	013	I will come to your Temple with burnt offerings; I will fulfill my promises to you,
019	PSA	066	014	the promises I made when I was in trouble.
019	PSA	066	015	I will sacrifice burnt offerings to you of fattened livestock—the smoke of the sacrifice of rams, offerings of bulls and goats. (Selah)
019	PSA	066	016	Come and listen, everyone who honors God, and I will tell you all he has done for me.
019	PSA	066	017	I called out to him, and praised him with my voice.
019	PSA	066	018	If I had focused my mind on evil, the Lord would not have listened to me.
019	PSA	066	019	But God did hear me! He listened to what I had to say in my prayer!
019	PSA	066	020	Praise God, who did not disregard my prayer or take his trustworthy love from me.
019	PSA	067	001	For the music director. To be accompanied by stringed instruments. A psalm. A song. May God be gracious to us and bless us. May he look favorably on us. (Selah)
019	PSA	067	002	May everyone on earth come to know your ways, your salvation among all people.
019	PSA	067	003	May the people praise you, God; may all the people praise you.
019	PSA	067	004	May they be happy and sing for joy because you judge people fairly, and you guide everyone on earth. (Selah)
019	PSA	067	005	May the people praise you, God; may all the people praise you.
019	PSA	067	006	The earth has produced its crops; and God, our God, has blessed us.
019	PSA	067	007	God will bless us, and all people everywhere will respect him.
019	PSA	068	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. A song. Stand up, God, and scatter your enemies. Let those who hate him run away from him!
019	PSA	068	002	Blow them away as if they were smoke; melt them like beeswax in a fire. Let the wicked die in God's presence.
019	PSA	068	003	But those who are right with God are happy, and they celebrate in God's presence, full of joy.
019	PSA	068	004	Sing praises to God! Sing praises to his wonderful reputation! Praise the rider of the clouds—his name is the Lord! Be happy in his presence!
019	PSA	068	005	He is a father to the orphans, a protector of widows. This is who God is, who lives in his holy place.
019	PSA	068	006	God gives those who are abandoned a family to live with. He sets prisoners free with celebration. But those who rebel live in a desert wasteland.
019	PSA	068	007	God, when you led your people out, when you marched through the desert, (Selah)
019	PSA	068	008	the earth quaked, and the heavens shook before God, the one of Sinai; before God, the God of Israel.
019	PSA	068	009	You sent plenty of rain to water the promised land; refreshing it when it was dry.
019	PSA	068	010	Your people settled there, and because of your kindness, God, you looked after the poor. (Selah)
019	PSA	068	011	The Lord gives the command, and a great army of women spread the good news.
019	PSA	068	012	The kings of the foreign armies are quick to run away, and the women who stayed at home divide the plunder!
019	PSA	068	013	Why are you staying at home? There are ornaments in the shape of a dove with wings of silver and feathers of fine gold to be taken.
019	PSA	068	014	The Almighty scattered the foreign kings like a snowstorm on Mount Zalmon.
019	PSA	068	015	“Mountain of God,” Mount Bashan, with your many high peaks, Mount Bashan,
019	PSA	068	016	why do you look enviously, mountain with many peaks, at the mountain God chose as his home, where the Lord will live forever?
019	PSA	068	017	God's chariots can't be counted; there are thousands and thousands of them. He comes among them from Sinai into his Temple.
019	PSA	068	018	As you ascended to your high throne you led a procession of prisoners. You received gifts from the people, even from those who had rebelled against the home of the Lord God.
019	PSA	068	019	May the Lord be blessed, for every day he carries our burdens. God is our salvation. (Selah)
019	PSA	068	020	For us, God is a God who saves. The Lord God provides our escape from death.
019	PSA	068	021	But God will crush the heads of his enemies, the hairy heads of those who continue to sin.
019	PSA	068	022	The Lord says, “I will drag them down from Bashan; I will drag them up from the depths of the sea,
019	PSA	068	023	so that you may walk in their blood. Even your dogs will have their share of your enemies.”
019	PSA	068	024	People watch your processions, God—the processions of my God and King as they go into the Temple.
019	PSA	068	025	The singers are at the front, the musicians at the back, and in the middle girls playing tambourines.
019	PSA	068	026	Praise God, everyone who has come to worship; praise the Lord, everyone who belongs to Israel.
019	PSA	068	027	There is the little tribe of Benjamin, followed by the many leaders from Judah; then come the leaders of Zebulun and Naphtali.
019	PSA	068	028	Display your power, God! Reveal your strength, Lord, as you have done for us in the past.
019	PSA	068	029	Because of your Temple in Jerusalem, kings bring tribute to you.
019	PSA	068	030	Condemn the beasts of the reeds, the bulls and calves! May they be humbled and bring bars of silver in tribute! Scatter the war-loving nations!
019	PSA	068	031	Let Egypt come with bronze gifts; let Ethiopia come quickly and hand over their tributes to God!
019	PSA	068	032	Sing to God, kingdoms of the earth, sing praises to the Lord. (Selah)
019	PSA	068	033	Sing to the rider of the ancient heavens, his strong voice sounding like thunder!
019	PSA	068	034	Let everyone know of God's power: how his majesty extends over Israel, how his strength is revealed in the heavens.
019	PSA	068	035	How awesome is God in his Temple! The God of Israel gives strength and power to his people! Praise God!
019	PSA	069	001	For the music director. To the tune “Lilies.” A psalm of David. God, please save me, because the water is up to my neck!
019	PSA	069	002	I'm sinking deeper into the mud—there's no solid ground for me to stand. I find myself in deep water; floods wash over me.
019	PSA	069	003	I'm so tired of screaming out for help my throat is totally raw. My eyes are worn out looking for my God to help me.
019	PSA	069	004	Those who hate me for no reason are more than the number of hairs on my head. Many enemies try to destroy me by telling lies. How can I give back what I didn't steal?
019	PSA	069	005	God, you know how foolish I am! My sins are not hidden from you.
019	PSA	069	006	Don't let those who trust you be ashamed because of me, Lord God Almighty. Don't let those who follow you be disgraced because of me, God of Israel.
019	PSA	069	007	For your sake I put up with the insults; my face shows my embarrassment.
019	PSA	069	008	I have become a foreigner to my brother Israelites; a stranger to my very own brothers.
019	PSA	069	009	My devotion for your house is burning me up inside; the insults of those who insulted you have fallen on me.
019	PSA	069	010	I wept and I fasted, but they mocked me;
019	PSA	069	011	I mourned in sackcloth, but they laughed at me.
019	PSA	069	012	People sitting by the town gate gossip about me. I'm the subject of rude songs sung by drunks.
019	PSA	069	013	But my prayer is to you, Lord, believing this is a good time to respond to me. God, in your wonderful trustworthy love, answer me with your sure salvation.
019	PSA	069	014	Please rescue me from the mud—don't let me sink! Save me from those who hate me and from drowning in the deep waters!
019	PSA	069	015	Don't let the flood waters wash over me. Don't let the deep waters pull me down. Don't let the grave close over me.
019	PSA	069	016	Please answer my prayers, Lord, for you are good and love me with your trustworthy love; because of your kindness, please help me.
019	PSA	069	017	Don't turn away from me, your servant. Please answer me quickly because I'm in trouble.
019	PSA	069	018	Come here and rescue me; set me free from my enemies.
019	PSA	069	019	You—you know my shame, my disgrace, my humiliation. You see everything my enemies are doing.
019	PSA	069	020	Insults have broken my heart—I am so sick there is no cure. I looked for some sympathy, but there was no one! Nobody showed me any compassion.
019	PSA	069	021	Instead they gave me bitter herbs to eat and vinegar to drink.
019	PSA	069	022	May the table set before them become a trap for them, a net that catches them, bringing punishment.
019	PSA	069	023	May their eyes become blind so they cannot see, and may their backs always be bent low in dejection.
019	PSA	069	024	Pour out your judgment on them; chase them down in your fierce anger.
019	PSA	069	025	Let the places where they live be deserted. Let their homes be abandoned.
019	PSA	069	026	For they persecute those you have punished, and make it even more painful for those you have disciplined.
019	PSA	069	027	Punish them for the evil they have done. Don't acquit them.
019	PSA	069	028	Blot out their names from the Book of Life. Don't let them be listed with those who do right.
019	PSA	069	029	But I am suffering and in physical pain. God, please save me and keep me safe.
019	PSA	069	030	I will praise God's character in song; I will say how incredible he is and how thankful I am.
019	PSA	069	031	The Lord is happier with this than with offering animals as sacrifices: cattle, or bulls with horns and hooves.
019	PSA	069	032	The humble will see this and be happy. May God encourage everyone who comes to him.
019	PSA	069	033	God hears the poor, and he does not ignore his people who are in prison.
019	PSA	069	034	Praise him heaven and earth, the seas and everything that lives in them!
019	PSA	069	035	For God will save Zion, and rebuild the cities of Judah. They will live there and own the land.
019	PSA	069	036	The descendants of those who follow him will inherit the land, and those who love him will live there.
019	PSA	070	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. For a memorial. God, save me! Hurry, Lord, help me!
019	PSA	070	002	Please defeat and humiliate the people who are trying to kill me; turn back in disgrace those who want to hurt me.
019	PSA	070	003	May they be shocked at their defeat, those who taunted me.
019	PSA	070	004	But may everyone who comes to you be happy and glad; may those who love your salvation always say, “God is great!”
019	PSA	070	005	As for me, I am poor and needy. Hurry, God, help me! Save me! Lord, don't wait!
019	PSA	071	001	Lord, you are the one who keeps me safe; please don't disappoint me.
019	PSA	071	002	Save me, rescue me, because you always do what is right.
019	PSA	071	003	Please listen to me, and save me. Be my rock of protection where I can always go and hide. You gave the command to save me; for you are my rock and fortress.
019	PSA	071	004	My God, rescue me from the power of the wicked, from the clutches of those who are evil and brutal.
019	PSA	071	005	For you, Lord God, are my hope. You are the one I have trusted since I was young.
019	PSA	071	006	I have depended on you since birth; you have taken care of me from my mother's womb. That's why I'm always praising you!
019	PSA	071	007	My life has been like a miracle to many people, for you have been my powerful protector.
019	PSA	071	008	All day long I am full of praise for you, telling how wonderful you are!
019	PSA	071	009	Don't reject me now I'm getting old. When my strength is gone, please don't abandon me.
019	PSA	071	010	For my enemies are talking about me; those who want to kill me are plotting together.
019	PSA	071	011	They say, “God has given up on him. Let's go after him because there's no one to save him.”
019	PSA	071	012	God, please don't stay away from me. My God, hurry to help me!
019	PSA	071	013	Defeat my accusers, get rid of them! May those who want to cause me trouble be covered with shame and disgrace!
019	PSA	071	014	As for me, I will go on hoping in you, and I will praise you more and more.
019	PSA	071	015	I will talk about your goodness and your salvation every day, even though it's more than I can understand.
019	PSA	071	016	I will come and explain what the Lord has done. I will remind people that you alone do what is right.
019	PSA	071	017	God, you have taught me since I was young, and I still tell others about all the wonderful things you do.
019	PSA	071	018	Even though I'm old and gray, please don't abandon me, God. Let me tell the new generation about your power. Let me explain to all who are to come the great things you do.
019	PSA	071	019	God, your trustworthy and true nature is higher than the highest heaven! You have done incredible things! God, who is like you?
019	PSA	071	020	You had me face many troubles and plenty of misery, but you will bring me back to life; you will rise me up from the depths of the earth.
019	PSA	071	021	You will give me even greater prestige, and you will make me happy again.
019	PSA	071	022	Then I will praise you on the harp for your trustworthiness, my God. I will sing praises to you on the lyre, Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	071	023	I will shout for joy as I sing praises to you, for you have redeemed me.
019	PSA	071	024	All day long I will tell about all the good things you have done, for those who tried to cause me misery have been disgraced and humiliated.
019	PSA	072	001	A psalm of Solomon. God, please give the king fairness, and give the king's son the ability to do what's right.
019	PSA	072	002	May he rightly judge your people, and may he be fair to the poor.
019	PSA	072	003	May the mountains bring peace to the people, and the hills bring goodness.
019	PSA	072	004	May he defend the poor and save their children, may he crush those who oppress them.
019	PSA	072	005	May they respect him as long as the sun and the moon shine above, for all generations.
019	PSA	072	006	May his reign be like rain falling on new grass, like showers that water the earth.
019	PSA	072	007	May those who live right prosper under his rule; may there be great prosperity until the moon is no more.
019	PSA	072	008	May he rule from sea to sea, from the river to the ends of the earth.
019	PSA	072	009	Desert tribes will kneel before him; and his enemies will bite the dust.
019	PSA	072	010	The kings of Tarshish and the islands will bring him tribute; the kings of Sheba and Seba will present him with gifts.
019	PSA	072	011	Every king will bow down to him; every nation will serve him.
019	PSA	072	012	He will help the poor when they cry out to him, and help those who are suffering that have no one to support them.
019	PSA	072	013	He has pity on the poor and needy—he saves their lives!
019	PSA	072	014	He rescues them from violence and oppression, for their lives mean so much to him.
019	PSA	072	015	May he live long! May the gold from Sheba be given to him. May people always pray for him and bless him all day long.
019	PSA	072	016	May there be plenty of grain in the land, even growing on mountain-tops. May the fruit on the trees sway like the trees of Lebanon. May the people in the city flourish like grass in a field.
019	PSA	072	017	May his fame live forever, may it last as long as the sun. May all nations be blessed through him, and may they praise him.
019	PSA	072	018	Praise the Lord God, the God of Israel, who is the only one who can do such fantastic things!
019	PSA	072	019	Praise his wonderful nature forever! May the whole world be full of his glory! Amen and amen!
019	PSA	072	020	(This is the end of the psalms of David, son of Jesse.)
019	PSA	073	001	A psalm of Asaph. Truly God is good to Israel, to those whose minds are pure.
019	PSA	073	002	But I was stumbling, my feet were starting to slide,
019	PSA	073	003	because I was jealous of self-important people—I saw how well the wicked were doing.
019	PSA	073	004	They don't ever seem to get sick; they are strong and healthy.
019	PSA	073	005	They don't have problems like other people; they don't get hit by disasters like everybody else.
019	PSA	073	006	They wear their pride like a necklace; they clothe themselves with violence.
019	PSA	073	007	Their eyes bulge out because they're so fat; their minds are full of selfish vanity.
019	PSA	073	008	They mock people, and speak maliciously; they arrogantly threaten cruelty.
019	PSA	073	009	They talk irreverently against heaven above, and defame people here on earth.
019	PSA	073	010	As a result people turn to them and drink in everything they say.
019	PSA	073	011	“God won't find out,” they say. “The Most High doesn't even know what's going on!”
019	PSA	073	012	Look at these wicked people! They don't have a care in the world, and they're always making money!
019	PSA	073	013	It's been pointless to keep my mind pure and my hands clean.
019	PSA	073	014	I'm cursed with suffering all day long; every morning I'm punished.
019	PSA	073	015	If I'd talked like this to others, I would have betrayed your people.
019	PSA	073	016	So I thought about it and tried to understand, but it looked like a lot of hard work to me—
019	PSA	073	017	until I went into God's Temple. Then I understood what happens to the wicked in the end.
019	PSA	073	018	For you send them on a slippery path; you throw them down to destruction.
019	PSA	073	019	How quickly they're destroyed! They come to a terrifying end.
019	PSA	073	020	Like waking up from a dream, Lord—when you get up you will forget all about them!
019	PSA	073	021	At that time my thoughts were bitter. I felt like I had been stabbed.
019	PSA	073	022	I was stupid and ignorant. I was like a brute beast to you.
019	PSA	073	023	Yet I'm always with you; you hold me by the hand.
019	PSA	073	024	You tell me what to do; and ultimately you will welcome me in glory.
019	PSA	073	025	Who is there in heaven for me except you? And I want nothing on earth except you.
019	PSA	073	026	My body and my mind may fail, but God is the foundation of my life. He is mine forever!
019	PSA	073	027	Those people who are far from God will die. You destroy all those unfaithful to you.
019	PSA	073	028	But I love to stay close to God! I have chosen the Lord God to protect me. I will share all that you have done.
019	PSA	074	001	A psalm (maskil) of Asaph. God, why have you rejected us? Is it forever? Why does your anger burn so hot against the sheep of your own field?
019	PSA	074	002	Remember the people you made your own long ago, the tribe you redeemed and made your own. Remember too Mount Zion, the place where you live.
019	PSA	074	003	Come and walk through the complete devastation. The enemy has totally destroyed your Temple.
019	PSA	074	004	The enemy shouted in triumph right where you met with us. There they set up their war banners as signs of their victory.
019	PSA	074	005	They acted like men chopping down a forest with axes.
019	PSA	074	006	With axes and hammers they smashed in the carved wooden panels.
019	PSA	074	007	Then they set fire to your Temple, burning it to the ground. They defiled the place where you live, the place that bears your name.
019	PSA	074	008	They said to themselves, “Let's destroy it all!” So they burned down every place where God was worshiped throughout the land.
019	PSA	074	009	We no longer see any signs. There are no prophets left. And no one among us knows how long this will last.
019	PSA	074	010	How long will the enemy ridicule you, God? Will they insult your character forever?
019	PSA	074	011	Why do you hold back from doing something? Take action and destroy them!
019	PSA	074	012	But you, God, are our king from long ago. You have saved us many times in the land.
019	PSA	074	013	You were the one who split apart the sea by your strength; you broke the heads of the sea monsters.
019	PSA	074	014	You were the one who crushed the heads of Leviathan, and you gave its body to the desert animals to eat.
019	PSA	074	015	You were the one who made springs and rivers flow with water. You made permanent rivers dry up.
019	PSA	074	016	You created the day, and also the night; you made the moon and the sun.
019	PSA	074	017	You set the boundaries of the earth; you made summer and winter.
019	PSA	074	018	So keep in mind how the enemy ridiculed you, Lord, and how irreverent people insulted your reputation.
019	PSA	074	019	Don't let wild animals kill your turtledoves! Don't abandon your people forever!
019	PSA	074	020	Remember your promises in the agreement, because the land is full of dark places and violence.
019	PSA	074	021	Don't let those who suffer be mistreated again. Let the poor and needy praise you for you who are.
019	PSA	074	022	Stand up, God, and plead your case. Don't forget how these foolish people insulted you all the time.
019	PSA	074	023	Don't ignore what your enemies have said, for their loud accusations against you are getting worse and worse!
019	PSA	075	001	For the music director. A psalm of Asaph. According to “Do Not Destroy.” A song. We thank you, God, we thank you because you are close beside us. People tell about the wonderful things you have done.
019	PSA	075	002	God says, “When the time I have decided comes, I will judge fairly.
019	PSA	075	003	When the earth quakes, and all its inhabitants tremble, I am the one who holds it steady. (Selah)
019	PSA	075	004	To those who boast I say, ‘Don't boast!’ I tell the wicked, ‘Don't be proud!’
019	PSA	075	005	No, don't be proud and arrogant, insulting heaven.”
019	PSA	075	006	For no one, from the east to the west, or from the wilderness, should think so highly of themselves.
019	PSA	075	007	God is the one who decides—who he will bring down and who he will lift up.
019	PSA	075	008	For the Lord has a cup in his hand, full of bubbling wine mixed with spices. He pours it out, and all the wicked drink it deeply, down to the last drop.
019	PSA	075	009	But I will speak about you forever. I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	075	010	For God says, “I will break the power of the wicked; but I will give my support to those who do what is good.”
019	PSA	076	001	For the music director. To be accompanied by stringed instruments. A psalm of Asaph. A song. God is famous in Judah; his reputation is great throughout Israel.
019	PSA	076	002	He lives in Jerusalem; his home is in Zion.
019	PSA	076	003	There he broke the flaming arrows, the shields, the swords, and the weapons of war. (Selah)
019	PSA	076	004	You shine with light; you are more majestic than the everlasting mountains.
019	PSA	076	005	Our most courageous enemies have been plundered. They sleep the sleep of death. Even the strongest of them could not raise a hand against us.
019	PSA	076	006	At your command, God of Jacob, both horse and rider fell down dead.
019	PSA	076	007	You are terrifying—who can stand before you when you are angry?
019	PSA	076	008	From heaven you announced judgment. Everyone on earth was afraid and stood still,
019	PSA	076	009	when you stood up to judge, to save the oppressed people of the earth. (Selah)
019	PSA	076	010	Even human anger against you makes you look glorious, for you wear it alike a crown.
019	PSA	076	011	Make your promises to God and be sure to keep them. Everyone bring gifts to the awe-inspiring one.
019	PSA	076	012	For he humbles proud leaders; he terrifies the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	077	001	For Jeduthun, the music director. A psalm of Asaph. I cry out to God for help—I even shout. If only he would listen to me!
019	PSA	077	002	When I was in trouble I prayed to the Lord. All night long I stretched out my hands to him in prayer but nothing brought me any comfort.
019	PSA	077	003	I thought about God, groaning loudly; I meditated on him, but I was discouraged. (Selah)
019	PSA	077	004	You stop me going to sleep; I'm so upset I can't even talk.
019	PSA	077	005	I think of the old days, years ago.
019	PSA	077	006	I remember the songs I sang in the night. I meditate and ask myself:
019	PSA	077	007	Has the Lord given up on me forever? Won't he ever be pleased with me again?
019	PSA	077	008	Has his trustworthy love disappeared forever? Have his promises permanently ended?
019	PSA	077	009	Has God forgotten to be kind? Has he angrily slammed the door shut on his compassion? (Selah)
019	PSA	077	010	Then I said, “This is what hurts me the most: the Most High doesn't treat me the way he used to.”
019	PSA	077	011	I remember what you have done, Lord; I remember all the wonderful things you did long ago.
019	PSA	077	012	I will think about all you have accomplished; I will think deeply about how you have acted.
019	PSA	077	013	God, your ways are holy; is any god as great as you?
019	PSA	077	014	You are the God who does wonderful things! You have revealed your power to the nations.
019	PSA	077	015	Through your strength you saved your people, the descendants of Jacob and Joseph. (Selah)
019	PSA	077	016	When the waters saw you, God, when they looked they trembled! Yes, they shook down to the very depths!
019	PSA	077	017	The clouds poured rain down; the skies crashed with thunder; your lightning flew like arrows.
019	PSA	077	018	Your thunder rumbled from the whirlwind; lightning flashes lit up the world; the earth quaked and shook.
019	PSA	077	019	Your way led through the sea; your path passed through the deep sea; yet your footprints were invisible.
019	PSA	077	020	You led your people like a flock, shepherded by Moses and Aaron.
019	PSA	078	001	A psalm (maskil) of Asaph. Listen to what I have to teach you, my people; hear what I have to say.
019	PSA	078	002	I will tell you wise sayings; I will explain mysteries from the past
019	PSA	078	003	that we have heard before and reflected on; stories our forefathers passed down to us.
019	PSA	078	004	We will not keep them from our children; we will tell the next generation about God's marvelous actions—about his power and the amazing things he has done.
019	PSA	078	005	He gave his laws to the descendants of Jacob; his instructions to the people of Israel. He commanded our forefathers to teach them to their children,
019	PSA	078	006	so that the next generation—children yet to be born—would understand and grow up to teach their children.
019	PSA	078	007	In this way they should place their trust in God and not forget what God has done, and keep his commandments.
019	PSA	078	008	Then they would not be like their forefathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation that was untrustworthy and unfaithful.
019	PSA	078	009	The soldiers of Ephraim, though armed with bows, ran away on the day of battle.
019	PSA	078	010	They did not keep God's agreement, and refused to follow his laws.
019	PSA	078	011	They ignored what he had done, and the amazing things he had shown them—
019	PSA	078	012	the miracles he had performed for their forefathers near Zoan in Egypt.
019	PSA	078	013	He split the sea in two and led them through, making the water stand like walls on either side.
019	PSA	078	014	He led them with a cloud by day, and by night with a light of fire.
019	PSA	078	015	He split open rocks in the desert to give his people plenty to drink, water as deep as the ocean.
019	PSA	078	016	He made streams flow from the stone; water rushing down like rivers!
019	PSA	078	017	But they repeatedly sinned against him, rebelling against the Most High in the desert.
019	PSA	078	018	They deliberately provoked God by demanding the foods they longed for.
019	PSA	078	019	They insulted God by saying, “Can God provide food here in the desert?
019	PSA	078	020	Yes, he can strike a rock so that water gushes out like flowing rivers, but can he give us bread? Can he supply his people with meat?”
019	PSA	078	021	When he heard this, the Lord became very angry, burning like fire against the descendants of Jacob, furious with the people of Israel,
019	PSA	078	022	for they didn't believe in God and didn't trust him to take care of them.
019	PSA	078	023	Even so he commanded the skies above and the doors of heaven to open,
019	PSA	078	024	and he made manna rain down on them to eat, giving them bread from heaven.
019	PSA	078	025	Human beings ate the bread of angels; he sent them more than enough food.
019	PSA	078	026	He sent the east wind blowing across the sky; by his power he drove the south wind.
019	PSA	078	027	He rained down meat on them as plentiful as dust; birds as numerous as sand on a beach.
019	PSA	078	028	He made them fall right in the middle of their camp, all around where they were living.
019	PSA	078	029	They ate until they were full. He gave them the food they longed for.
019	PSA	078	030	But before they satisfied their appetite, while the meat was still in their mouths,
019	PSA	078	031	God became angry with them and he killed their strongest men, striking them down in the prime of life.
019	PSA	078	032	Despite all this they went right on sinning. Despite the miracles, they refused to trust him.
019	PSA	078	033	So he snuffed out their futile lives, bringing them to an end in terror.
019	PSA	078	034	When he began killing them, the rest came back to God in repentance, praying to him.
019	PSA	078	035	They remembered that God was their rock, that God Most High was their Savior.
019	PSA	078	036	They flattered him by what they told him, but they were only lying.
019	PSA	078	037	Deep down they were not sincere, and did not keep the agreement they had with him.
019	PSA	078	038	But being compassionate he pardoned their guilt and did not destroy all of them. He often held back his anger—he did not pour out all his fury.
019	PSA	078	039	He remembered their mortality—that they were like a puff of wind that would not return.
019	PSA	078	040	How often they rebelled against him in the wilderness, giving him grief in the desert!
019	PSA	078	041	Again and again they provoked God, causing pain to the Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	078	042	They did not remember his strength when he rescued them from their oppressors,
019	PSA	078	043	performing miracles in Egypt, doing wonderful things on the plain of Zoan.
019	PSA	078	044	There he turned their rivers and their streams into blood so that no one could drink from them.
019	PSA	078	045	He sent flies among them to destroy them, and frogs to ruin everything.
019	PSA	078	046	He gave their crops to locusts; everything they worked had for was taken by locusts.
019	PSA	078	047	He destroyed their vines with hail, and their fig trees with freezing rain.
019	PSA	078	048	He handed over their cattle to hail and their flocks to lightning bolts.
019	PSA	078	049	He poured out on them his fierce anger—rage and hostility and anguish—sending a band of destroying angels against them.
019	PSA	078	050	He sent his unrestrained anger against them; he did not spare them from death, handing them over to the plague.
019	PSA	078	051	He struck down all the firstborn of Egypt, the first to be conceived in the tents of Ham.
019	PSA	078	052	But he led out his people like sheep, and guided them like a flock in the wilderness.
019	PSA	078	053	He led them to safety, and they were not afraid. He drowned their enemies in the sea.
019	PSA	078	054	He brought them to the border of his holy land, to this mountainous land that he had conquered for them.
019	PSA	078	055	He drove out the heathen nations before them. He divided up the land for them to own. He settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.
019	PSA	078	056	But they provoked God Most High, rebelling against him. They did not follow what he had told them.
019	PSA	078	057	Just like their forefathers they turned away from God and were unfaithful to him, as twisted as a defective bow.
019	PSA	078	058	They made him angry with their pagan high places of worship; they made him jealous with their idols.
019	PSA	078	059	When God heard their worship he became furious and he totally rejected Israel.
019	PSA	078	060	He abandoned his place at Shiloh, the Tabernacle where he lived among the people.
019	PSA	078	061	He surrendered the Ark of his power, allowing it to be captured; handing it over into enemy hands.
019	PSA	078	062	He handed over his people to be slaughtered by the sword; he was furious with his chosen people.
019	PSA	078	063	Their young men were destroyed by fire; their young women had no wedding songs.
019	PSA	078	064	Their priests were killed by the sword; their widows were unable to mourn.
019	PSA	078	065	Then the Lord woke up as if from sleep, as a warrior sobering up from drinking wine.
019	PSA	078	066	He defeated his enemies, striking them on the back, causing them everlasting shame.
019	PSA	078	067	He rejected the descendants of Joseph, and did not choose the tribe of Ephraim.
019	PSA	078	068	Instead he chose the tribe of Judah, and Mount Zion which he loves.
019	PSA	078	069	There he built his sanctuary, high like the heavens, on earth that he made to last forever.
019	PSA	078	070	He chose his servant David, taking him from the sheep pens,
019	PSA	078	071	taking him from caring for the sheep and lambs to be a shepherd to the descendants of Jacob—God's special people, Israel.
019	PSA	078	072	Like a shepherd, he took care of them with sincere devotion, leading them with skillful hands.
019	PSA	079	001	A psalm of Asaph. God, heathen nations have invaded your land. They have defiled your holy Temple. They have turned Jerusalem into heaps of rubble.
019	PSA	079	002	They have given the dead bodies of your servants as food to the birds of the air, the flesh of your faithful people to the beasts of the earth.
019	PSA	079	003	They have poured out the blood of Jerusalem's people like water all through the city; no one remains to bury the dead.
019	PSA	079	004	We have been made a mockery before our neighbors, ridiculed and laughed at by those around us.
019	PSA	079	005	How long, Lord? Will you be angry with us forever? Will your jealousy always burn like fire?
019	PSA	079	006	Pour out your anger on the heathen nations that don't know you, and on those kingdoms that don't worship you!
019	PSA	079	007	For they have destroyed the descendants of Jacob, and turned our country into a wasteland.
019	PSA	079	008	Don't hold the sins of our forefathers against us! Come to us quickly for we desperately need your compassion.
019	PSA	079	009	Help us, God of our salvation, because of your wonderful character! Save us and forgive us our sins because that's the kind of person you are!
019	PSA	079	010	Why should the heathen nations be able to say, “Where is their God?” May they experience your punishment for shedding the blood of your servants, and may we see it.
019	PSA	079	011	Listen to the groans of the prisoners; with your great power save those condemned to die.
019	PSA	079	012	Pay each of these neighbors back seven times for the scorn and ridicule they directed against you, Lord.
019	PSA	079	013	Then we your people, the flock of your pasture, will praise you forever. We will thank you for all generations to come.
019	PSA	080	001	For the music director. A psalm of Asaph. To the tune “Lilies of the Covenant.” Please hear us, Shepherd of Israel, you who lead the descendants of Joseph like a flock. You who sit on your throne above the cherubim, shine out
019	PSA	080	002	in the presence of Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh. Gather together your power and come to save us!
019	PSA	080	003	God, please restore us! Let your face shine on us so we can be saved.
019	PSA	080	004	Lord God Almighty, how long will you be angry with the prayers of your people?
019	PSA	080	005	You fed them with the bread of tears, and gave them a full bowl of tears to drink.
019	PSA	080	006	You turn us into victims our neighbors fight over; our enemies mock us.
019	PSA	080	007	God Almighty, please restore us! Let your face shine on us so we can be saved!
019	PSA	080	008	You carried us out of Egypt like a vine. You drove out the heathen nations, and then you planted the vine.
019	PSA	080	009	You prepared the ground for the vine. It took root and filled the land.
019	PSA	080	010	The mountains were covered by its shade; its branches covered the great cedars.
019	PSA	080	011	It sent its branches as far west as the Mediterranean Sea, and its shoots as far east as the Euphrates River.
019	PSA	080	012	So why have you broken down the walls that protect it so that everyone who passes by can steal its fruit?
019	PSA	080	013	Wild pigs from the forest eat it, wild animals feed on it.
019	PSA	080	014	God Almighty, please return to us! Look down from heaven and see what's happening to us! Come and care for this vine
019	PSA	080	015	that you planted yourself, this son that you brought up yourself.
019	PSA	080	016	We, your vine, have been chopped down and burned. May those who did this die when you glare at them.
019	PSA	080	017	Protect the man who stands beside you; strengthen the son you have chosen.
019	PSA	080	018	Then we will not turn away from you. Revive us so we can pray to you.
019	PSA	080	019	Lord God Almighty, please restore us! Let your face shine on us so we can be saved.
019	PSA	081	001	For the music director. On the gittith. A psalm of Asaph. Sing aloud to God our strength; shout for joy to the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	002	Start the song! Play the tambourine, sweet-sounding lyre, and harp.
019	PSA	081	003	Blow the trumpet at the new moon, and at full moon, to begin our festivals,
019	PSA	081	004	for this is a rule for Israel, a regulation of the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	005	God made this statute for Joseph when he opposed the land of Egypt. I heard a voice I didn't know, saying:
019	PSA	081	006	“I took the load from your shoulders; I freed your hands from carrying heavy baskets.
019	PSA	081	007	In your suffering you cried out to me, and I saved you. I answered you from the thundercloud. I tested you at the waters of Meribah. (Selah)
019	PSA	081	008	My people, listen to my warnings! Israel, please listen to me!
019	PSA	081	009	There must not be a strange god among you; you must never bow down to foreign gods and worship them.
019	PSA	081	010	I am the Lord your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt. Open your mouth wide and I will fill it.
019	PSA	081	011	But my people didn't listen to me. Israel didn't want anything to do with me.
019	PSA	081	012	So I sent them away to follow their stubborn thinking, living as they chose.
019	PSA	081	013	If only my people would listen to me; if only Israel would follow my ways!
019	PSA	081	014	It wouldn't take me long to conquer their enemies, to strike down their foes.
019	PSA	081	015	Those who hate the Lord would cringe before him, forever doomed.
019	PSA	081	016	But I would feed you the best wheat and satisfy you with honey from the rock.”
019	PSA	082	001	A psalm of Asaph. God stands in the midst of his great assembly to judge among the gods.
019	PSA	082	002	How long will you make unfair judgments and show favoritism to the wicked? (Selah)
019	PSA	082	003	Defend the poor and orphans; support the rights of those who are oppressed and suffering.
019	PSA	082	004	Rescue the poor and those unable to help themselves; save them from the clutches of evil people.
019	PSA	082	005	They don't have any wisdom; they live in the dark; the foundations of the earth are shaken.
019	PSA	082	006	I say, “You are gods; all of you are children of the Most High.
019	PSA	082	007	But you will die like any human being, you will fall like any other leader.”
019	PSA	082	008	Stand up, Lord, and judge the earth, for all the nations belong to you.
019	PSA	083	001	A song. A psalm of Asaph. God, please do not stay silent! You can't remain unmoved! God, you must not keep quiet!
019	PSA	083	002	Can't you hear the roars of your enemies? Can't you see how those who hate you are defiantly lifting up their heads?
019	PSA	083	003	They invent cunning plans to conspire against your people; they plot against those you treasure.
019	PSA	083	004	They say, “Come on! Let's destroy them as a nation so the name ‘Israel’ will be completely forgotten.”
019	PSA	083	005	They all agree in their conspiracy; they've made a treaty together to attack you—
019	PSA	083	006	the people of Edom, the Ishmaelites, Moab, and the Hagirites;
019	PSA	083	007	the people of Gebal and Ammon and Amalek, Philistia, and the inhabitants of Tyre.
019	PSA	083	008	Assyria too has joined them, allied with the descendants of Lot. (Selah)
019	PSA	083	009	Do to them what you did to Midian, what you did to Sisera and Jabin at the Kishon River.
019	PSA	083	010	They were destroyed at Endor and became like manure to fertilize the ground.
019	PSA	083	011	Make their leaders like Oreb and Zeeb; all their rulers like Zebah and Zalmunna,
019	PSA	083	012	for they said, “Let's take the pastures of God for ourselves!”
019	PSA	083	013	My God, make them like whirling tumbleweeds, chaff blown away by the wind.
019	PSA	083	014	Just like fire that burns the forest, a flame that sets fire to the mountains,
019	PSA	083	015	in the same way chase them down with your storm, terrify them with your whirlwind.
019	PSA	083	016	Shame them in defeat so that they come to you, Lord!
019	PSA	083	017	Make them ashamed, terrify them forever so that they die in disgrace.
019	PSA	083	018	Let them understand that you alone, called the Lord, are the Most High who rules over all the earth.
019	PSA	084	001	For the music director. A psalm of the descendants of Korah. On the gittith. How wonderful is the place where you live, Lord Almighty!
019	PSA	084	002	I long, I ache, to be in the courts of the Lord. My mind and my body sing for joy to the living God.
019	PSA	084	003	Even a sparrow finds a home there, and a swallow builds a nest for herself where she can raise her chicks near to your altars, Lord Almighty, my king and my God.
019	PSA	084	004	How happy are those who live in your house—they are always praising you! (Selah)
019	PSA	084	005	How happy are those whose strength is in you, those who are determined to make a pilgrimage.
019	PSA	084	006	As they walk through the Valley of Tears it becomes a spring of water; autumn rains cover it with pools.
019	PSA	084	007	They go from strength to strength, and each one will appear before God in Jerusalem.
019	PSA	084	008	Lord God Almighty, please hear my prayer; please listen, God of Jacob. (Selah)
019	PSA	084	009	Please God, look at our defender, look at the face of your anointed one.
019	PSA	084	010	One day in your courts is better than a thousand anywhere else. I'd rather stand as a doorkeeper in the house of my God than live comfortably in the homes of the wicked.
019	PSA	084	011	For the Lord God is our sun and shield, and he gives us grace and honor. The Lord doesn't hold back anything good from those who do right.
019	PSA	084	012	Lord Almighty, how happy are those who trust in you.
019	PSA	085	001	For the music director. A psalm of the descendants of Korah Lord, you have shown your kindness to your land; you have restored Jacob's prosperity.
019	PSA	085	002	You took away your people's guilt; you forgave all their sins. (Selah)
019	PSA	085	003	You took back your fury; you turned away from your fierce anger.
019	PSA	085	004	Bring us back to you, God of our salvation! Take away your anger towards us.
019	PSA	085	005	Are you going to be furious with us forever? Will you stay angry with us for all future generations?
019	PSA	085	006	Won't you restore our lives so your people can find happiness in you?
019	PSA	085	007	Show us your trustworthy love, Lord! Give us your salvation!
019	PSA	085	008	Let me hear what God has to say. God speaks peace to his people, to those who trust in him. But they must not return to their foolish ways.
019	PSA	085	009	Truly God's salvation is with those who do as he says. His glorious presence will live with us in our land.
019	PSA	085	010	Trustworthiness and faithful love join together; goodness and peace have kissed each other.
019	PSA	085	011	What is true grows up from the earth; what is right looks down from heaven.
019	PSA	085	012	The Lord will certainly give us all that is good, and our land will produce fine crops.
019	PSA	085	013	Truth and right go ahead of him to prepare a path for him to walk on.
019	PSA	086	001	A prayer of David. Please listen to me, Lord! Please answer me, for I am weak and really need your help!
019	PSA	086	002	Don't let me die, for I am faithful to you. Save me, for I am your servant and I trust in you. You are my God.
019	PSA	086	003	Be kind to me, Lord, for I call out to you all day long.
019	PSA	086	004	Make me happy, Lord, for I've dedicated my life to you.
019	PSA	086	005	For you, Lord, are good; you are forgiving and full of trustworthy love for all who come to you.
019	PSA	086	006	Lord, please listen to my prayer. Hear my call for help.
019	PSA	086	007	When I'm in trouble I cry out to you because I know you will answer me.
019	PSA	086	008	There's no one like you among the “gods,” Lord. No one can do the things you do.
019	PSA	086	009	You created all the nations, and they will come and bow down before you, Lord. They will declare how wonderful you are.
019	PSA	086	010	For you are great, and do wonderful things! Only you are God.
019	PSA	086	011	Lord, please teach me your way, so I can depend on your trustworthiness. Make me single-minded, so I can consistently honor the kind of person you are.
019	PSA	086	012	Lord my God, I thank you from the bottom of my heart. I will praise your character forever.
019	PSA	086	013	For your trustworthy love for me is so great; you have saved me from death.
019	PSA	086	014	God, arrogant people are attacking me, vicious people are trying to kill me. To them you count for nothing.
019	PSA	086	015	But you, Lord, are a compassionate and gracious God, slow to become angry, full of trustworthy love and faithfulness.
019	PSA	086	016	Turn to me, have mercy on me. Give me your strength, your servant; save the son of your servant-girl.
019	PSA	086	017	Show me a sign that you approve of me! Those who hate me will see it, and they will be ashamed because you, Lord, have helped me.
019	PSA	087	001	A song. A psalm of the descendants of Korah. The Lord founded the city on his holy mountain.
019	PSA	087	002	Jerusalem is the city that the Lord loves more than any other city in Israel.
019	PSA	087	003	Many wonderful things are said of you, city of God! (Selah)
019	PSA	087	004	I mention Egypt and Babylon as those who know me, and in addition Philistia, Tyre, and Ethiopia—“this man was born there.”
019	PSA	087	005	It will be said concerning Jerusalem, “Everyone was born there,” and the Most High will make it secure.
019	PSA	087	006	When the Lord registers the nations, he will write, “They were born there.” (Selah)
019	PSA	087	007	Singers and dancers alike say, “Living here I am at home.”
019	PSA	088	001	A song. A psalm of the descendants of Korah. For the music director. To the tune “Mahalath Leannoth.” A maskil by Heman the Ezrahite Lord, God of my salvation, I cry out to you day and night.
019	PSA	088	002	Please listen to my prayer; hear my words as I plead with you.
019	PSA	088	003	My life is full of troubles, and my death is approaching.
019	PSA	088	004	I'm counted among the dying; a man with no strength.
019	PSA	088	005	I am abandoned among the dead, lying like a corpse in the grave, forgotten and beyond your care.
019	PSA	088	006	You have placed me in a deep pit, in the depths of darkness.
019	PSA	088	007	Your hostility crushes me; you are drowning me under your crashing waves. (Selah)
019	PSA	088	008	You have made my friends avoid me by making me look repulsive to them. I'm trapped, I can't go out.
019	PSA	088	009	I've cried my eyes out begging you every day for your help, Lord, holding out my hands to you.
019	PSA	088	010	Do you do miracles among the dead? Do the dead stand up to praise you? (Selah)
019	PSA	088	011	Your faithful love—is it mentioned in the grave? Your trustworthiness—is it discussed in the place of destruction?
019	PSA	088	012	Are the wonderful things you do known in the darkness? Is your goodness known in the land of forgetfulness?
019	PSA	088	013	But I cry out to you for help; every morning I pray to you.
019	PSA	088	014	Lord, why do you reject me? Why do you turn away from me?
019	PSA	088	015	I have been sick since I was young, often at death's door. I have had to bear the terrible things you've done to me. I'm in despair!
019	PSA	088	016	Your anger has overcome me; the terrible things you do have destroyed me.
019	PSA	088	017	They surround me all the time like floodwaters, swallowing me up.
019	PSA	088	018	You have made my family and friends avoid me. Darkness is my only friend.
019	PSA	089	001	A psalm (maskil) of Ethan the Ezraite I will sing of the Lord's trustworthy love forever; I will tell all generations of your faithfulness.
019	PSA	089	002	For I have said, “Your unfailing love lasts forever; your faithfulness endures as long as the heavens.”
019	PSA	089	003	You said, “I have made an agreement with my chosen one, I gave a binding promise to my servant David:
019	PSA	089	004	I will make sure your lineage lasts forever; I will keep your throne secure for all generations.” (Selah)
019	PSA	089	005	All the heavenly beings will sing of the wonderful things you have done, Lord; angels will gather to sing of your faithfulness.
019	PSA	089	006	For who in heaven can compare to the Lord? Who is like the Lord even among the angels?
019	PSA	089	007	The heavenly council are in awe of God; all who surround him are overwhelmed by him.
019	PSA	089	008	Lord God Almighty, who is as powerful as you? In all this, Lord, you are completely trustworthy.
019	PSA	089	009	You rule the restless seas; you calm their stormy waves.
019	PSA	089	010	You crushed Rahab the sea-monster to death; by your power you scattered your enemies.
019	PSA	089	011	The heavens belong to you, and the earth too; you made the world and everything in it.
019	PSA	089	012	You created north and south; Mount Tabor and Mount Hermon celebrate you.
019	PSA	089	013	Your arm is powerful. Your hand is strong. Your right hand is held up high in command.
019	PSA	089	014	Your character of goodness and fairness is the basis for the way you rule; dependable love and trustworthiness are always with you.
019	PSA	089	015	How happy are those who know how to shout your praises, Lord. They live in the light of your presence.
019	PSA	089	016	They celebrate the person you are all day long, so glad that you do what's right.
019	PSA	089	017	They rely on you, their glory and strength; by your grace you lift us up.
019	PSA	089	018	Yes, the Lord is the one who shields us, and our king belongs to the Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	089	019	Once you spoke in a vision to your faithful servant and said, “I have given strength to the warrior I have chosen from the people to become king.
019	PSA	089	020	I have selected David my servant, and I have anointed him with the oil of my holiness.
019	PSA	089	021	I have placed my hand on him to steady him; and I have made him strong by my powerful arm.
019	PSA	089	022	His enemies will not deceive him; the wicked will not bring him down.
019	PSA	089	023	I will wipe out his enemies before him; I will strike down those who hate him.
019	PSA	089	024	My trustworthiness and unfailing love will be with him, and through me he will be victorious.
019	PSA	089	025	I will extend his rule from the Mediterranean Sea to the Euphrates River.
019	PSA	089	026	He will call out to me, ‘You are my Father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.’
019	PSA	089	027	I will also make him my first-born son, the highest of the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	089	028	I will love him faithfully forever; my agreement with him shall never come to an end.
019	PSA	089	029	I will make sure his royal line lasts forever; his dynasty will continue as long as the heavens endure.
019	PSA	089	030	But if his descendants abandon my laws, if they do not follow my rules,
019	PSA	089	031	if they break my decrees, and do not keep my commandments,
019	PSA	089	032	I will punish their rebellion by beating them with a rod, and their sin by lashing them with a whip.
019	PSA	089	033	However, I will not take away my love from him; I will not break my promise to him.
019	PSA	089	034	I will not annul the agreement I have with him; I will not alter a single word I've said.
019	PSA	089	035	By my holy character I have made a vow to David that I will not lie to him.
019	PSA	089	036	His royal line will last forever, and his dynasty will continue before me as long as the sun endures.
019	PSA	089	037	It will continue forever like the moon, an enduring witness in the heavens.” (Selah)
019	PSA	089	038	But you have rejected and abandoned him! You are angry with your chosen king!
019	PSA	089	039	You have broken the agreement you had with him; you have thrown his crown to the ground!
019	PSA	089	040	You have torn down his defensive walls; you have ruined his fortresses.
019	PSA	089	041	Everyone who passes by has robbed him; he has become an object of mockery to the nations nearby.
019	PSA	089	042	You have made his enemies strong; you have made them celebrate their victory.
019	PSA	089	043	You have repelled his sharp sword; you have not helped him in battle.
019	PSA	089	044	You took away his glory; you threw his throne to the ground.
019	PSA	089	045	You have made him grow old before his time; you have totally humiliated him. (Selah)
019	PSA	089	046	How long, Lord? Will you hide yourself from us forever, your anger burning like fire?
019	PSA	089	047	Remember me—my life is so short! Why did you bother creating futile humanity?
019	PSA	089	048	There's no one who doesn't die—no one can save themselves from the power of the grave. (Selah)
019	PSA	089	049	Where is the trustworthy love you used to have, Lord, that you faithfully promised to David?
019	PSA	089	050	Don't forget, Lord, how your servants are being humiliated! I'm burdened down with the insults of so many nations!
019	PSA	089	051	Your enemies taunt me, Lord, mocking your king wherever he goes.
019	PSA	089	052	May the Lord be blessed for ever. Amen and amen.
019	PSA	090	001	A prayer of Moses, the man of God. Lord, through every generation, you have been “home” for us!
019	PSA	090	002	Before the mountains were born, before you gave birth to the earth and the universe, from eternity past to eternity future, you are God.
019	PSA	090	003	You turn people back into dust, saying, “Return to dust, human beings.”
019	PSA	090	004	In your eyes, a thousand years are like a day that's already gone; like a few passing hours of the night.
019	PSA	090	005	You bring people's lives to a sudden end, like dreams that vanish. They are like grass that grows up in the morning—
019	PSA	090	006	it sprouts in the morning, fresh and new, but by the evening it is withered and dead.
019	PSA	090	007	We are burned up by your anger, terrified by your fury.
019	PSA	090	008	You have set out our sins before you—our secret sins are visible in the light of your presence.
019	PSA	090	009	Our lives fade away under your anger, coming to an end as quickly as a sigh.
019	PSA	090	010	We live for seventy years—eighty if we have the strength. But even in the prime of life all that we have is hardship and suffering. Soon our lives are over and we're gone.
019	PSA	090	011	Who can know the power of your anger? Who understands your fury so you can be shown reverence?
019	PSA	090	012	Teach us to value every one of our days so we can live wisely!
019	PSA	090	013	Lord, how long will it be before you come back to us and have pity on us your servants?
019	PSA	090	014	Show us every morning your trustworthy love so we may be happy, full of joy throughout our lives.
019	PSA	090	015	Make us glad for as many days as you made us sad, for all the years we suffered!
019	PSA	090	016	May we, your servants, see you at work for us again; may our children see your glory.
019	PSA	090	017	May our Lord God be pleased with us, blessing what we do, blessing what we do.
019	PSA	091	001	Those who live under the protection of the Most High are kept safe by the Almighty.
019	PSA	091	002	This is what I say about the Lord: “He is the one who defends and protects me. He is my God, and I trust in him.”
019	PSA	091	003	For he will save you from hidden traps and deadly diseases.
019	PSA	091	004	He will hide you under his feathers, and shelter you with his wings. His trustworthiness shields and protects you.
019	PSA	091	005	You will not be afraid of terror at night or an arrow that flies in the day,
019	PSA	091	006	or disease that attacks at night, or catastrophe that falls at noon.
019	PSA	091	007	A thousand may fall beside you, ten thousand die at your right hand, but you won't be harmed.
019	PSA	091	008	You only have to open your eyes and you will see how the wicked are repaid.
019	PSA	091	009	Because you have made the Lord your protection, and the Most High your home,
019	PSA	091	010	nothing evil will happen to you; no plague will come near where you live.
019	PSA	091	011	For he will command his angels to take care of you in everything you do.
019	PSA	091	012	They will hold you up with their hands so you won't trip and fall down.
019	PSA	091	013	You will trample lions and snakes; you will tread young lions and serpents underfoot.
019	PSA	091	014	I will save anyone who loves me; I will protect anyone who accepts me.
019	PSA	091	015	When they call out to me for help, I will answer; when they are in trouble, I will be with them. I will save and honor them.
019	PSA	091	016	I will grant them long lives, and show them my salvation.
019	PSA	092	001	A psalm. A song for the Sabbath day. How good it is to thank the Lord, to sing praises to you, Most High,
019	PSA	092	002	to tell of your trustworthy love in the morning, and your faithfulness in the night,
019	PSA	092	003	to the music of a ten-stringed harp and the melody of a lyre.
019	PSA	092	004	You've made me so happy, Lord, because of all you've done for me! I sing for joy at what you've done!
019	PSA	092	005	Lord, what you do is amazing; your thoughts are very profound!
019	PSA	092	006	Only senseless people and fools don't know and understand this:
019	PSA	092	007	even though the wicked grow up quickly like grass, and even though people who do evil flourish, they will be destroyed forever!
019	PSA	092	008	But you, Lord, rule on high forever.
019	PSA	092	009	Your enemies, Lord, your enemies will die; everyone who does evil will be destroyed!
019	PSA	092	010	But you have made me as powerful as a wild bull; you have anointed me with the best olive oil.
019	PSA	092	011	My eyes look with pleasure to see my enemies defeated; my ears have heard the downfall of those who tried to attack me.
019	PSA	092	012	Those who live right flourish like a palm tree; they grow tall like a cedar tree in Lebanon.
019	PSA	092	013	They are planted in the house of the Lord; they thrive in the courts of our God.
019	PSA	092	014	Even when they are old they will still produce fruit, staying fresh and green.
019	PSA	092	015	They will declare, “The Lord does what is right! He is my rock! There is no wrong in him!”
019	PSA	093	001	The Lord reigns, clothed in majesty! He wears his royal robes, with his power worn like a belt. The world is held together firmly—it cannot be broken apart.
019	PSA	093	002	Your throne has existed from ages past; you are from eternity.
019	PSA	093	003	The floods have raised up, Lord; the floods have raised their voices; the floods have raised up their crashing waves.
019	PSA	093	004	But greater than the most violent ocean, greater than the largest waves of the sea, the greatest is the Lord above.
019	PSA	093	005	Your laws are totally trustworthy. Your house, Lord, is holy forever.
019	PSA	094	001	The Lord is a God of vengeance! God of vengeance, shine out!
019	PSA	094	002	Stand up, judge of the earth, and pay back those who are proud what they deserve.
019	PSA	094	003	How long, Lord? How long will the wicked celebrate in triumph?
019	PSA	094	004	How long will you let them pour out their arrogant words? How long will these evil people go on boasting?
019	PSA	094	005	Lord, they crush your people; they oppress those you call your own.
019	PSA	094	006	They kill widows and foreigners; they murder orphans.
019	PSA	094	007	They say, “The Lord can't see what we're doing. Israel's God doesn't pay any attention to us.”
019	PSA	094	008	Take another look, you stupid people! Fools—when will you ever get the point?
019	PSA	094	009	Do you think the creator of the ear can't hear? Do you think the maker of the eye can't see?
019	PSA	094	010	Do you think that the one who punishes nations won't punish you too? Do you think that the one who teaches human beings knowledge doesn't know anything?
019	PSA	094	011	The Lord knows the thoughts of human beings—he knows they are pointless.
019	PSA	094	012	Those you discipline are happy, Lord; those you teach from your Law.
019	PSA	094	013	You give them peace in days of trouble, until a pit is dug to trap the wicked.
019	PSA	094	014	For the Lord will not give up on his people; he will not abandon his own.
019	PSA	094	015	Justice will once again be based on what is right; those who are sincere will support it.
019	PSA	094	016	Who came to my defense against the wicked; who stood up for me against those who do evil?
019	PSA	094	017	If the Lord hadn't helped me, I would have soon gone down into the silence of the grave.
019	PSA	094	018	I shouted out, “My foot's slipping!” and your trustworthy love, Lord, kept me from falling.
019	PSA	094	019	When my mind was full of worries, you comforted me and encouraged me.
019	PSA	094	020	Can unjust judges really be on your side, Lord, when their corrupt use of the law causes misery?
019	PSA	094	021	They work together to destroy good people; they condemn those who are innocent to death.
019	PSA	094	022	But the Lord protects me like a fortress; my God is the rock that keeps me safe.
019	PSA	094	023	He will turn the wickedness of evil people back upon them; he will destroy them because of their sins; the Lord our God will destroy them.
019	PSA	095	001	Come, let's sing for joy to the Lord! Let's shout in triumph to the rock of our salvation!
019	PSA	095	002	Let's go before him with thanksgiving! Let's sing loudly to him in celebration!
019	PSA	095	003	For the Lord is a great God, a great king above all gods.
019	PSA	095	004	He rules over the depths of the earth and the heights of the mountains.
019	PSA	095	005	The sea is his, because he made it; the dry land, because he formed it.
019	PSA	095	006	Come, let's enter in and worship, let's kneel before the Lord our Creator.
019	PSA	095	007	For he is our God, and we are the people he looks after like a shepherd, the flock he cares for. If you hear his voice calling you today,
019	PSA	095	008	don't have a hard-hearted attitude, “as you did at Meribah, as you did that day at Massah in the desert,
019	PSA	095	009	when your forefathers provoked me, testing my patience, even though they had seen everything I'd done.
019	PSA	095	010	For forty years I was disgusted with that generation, and I said, ‘They are people who are unfaithful to me in their minds, and they refuse to accept my ways.’
019	PSA	095	011	So in my frustration I vowed, ‘They will certainly not enter my rest.’”
019	PSA	096	001	Sing to the Lord a new song! All the earth, sing to the Lord!
019	PSA	096	002	Sing to the Lord, and of his wonderful reputation! Each day let everyone know of his salvation!
019	PSA	096	003	Declare his glorious acts among the nations, the amazing things he does among all peoples.
019	PSA	096	004	For the Lord is great, and deserves the best praise! He is to be respected with awe above all gods.
019	PSA	096	005	For all the gods of other nations are idols; but the Lord made the heavens!
019	PSA	096	006	Splendor and majesty are his; power and glory are in his sanctuary.
019	PSA	096	007	Give the Lord acclamation, nations of the world, acclaim him with glory and strength.
019	PSA	096	008	Give the Lord the glory he deserves; bring an offering and come into his courts.
019	PSA	096	009	Worship the Lord in his magnificent holiness; let all the earth tremble in his presence.
019	PSA	096	010	Tell the nations, “The Lord is in charge!” The world is held together firmly—it cannot be broken apart. He will judge everyone fairly.
019	PSA	096	011	Let the heavens sing for joy, let the earth be happy, let the sea and everything in it shout with praise!
019	PSA	096	012	Let the fields and everything there celebrate; let all the trees in the forest sing for joy.
019	PSA	096	013	In fact, let everything that stands before the Lord sing praises, for he is coming, coming to judge the earth. He will judge the world with fairness, and the nations with his truth.
019	PSA	097	001	The Lord reigns! Let the earth be glad, and distant lands be full of joy!
019	PSA	097	002	He is surrounded by clouds and thick darkness; his throne is founded on justice and right.
019	PSA	097	003	Flames proceed him, burning up his enemies on every side.
019	PSA	097	004	His flashes of lightning light up the world; the earth watches and trembles.
019	PSA	097	005	The mountains melt like wax in the presence of the Lord, before the Lord of all the earth.
019	PSA	097	006	The heavens proclaim his goodness; everyone sees his glory.
019	PSA	097	007	All those who worship idols are humiliated, those who are proud of their idols—for all “gods” bow down before him.
019	PSA	097	008	Jerusalem hears this and celebrates; all the towns of Judah are happy because of your judgments, Lord.
019	PSA	097	009	For you, Lord, are the highest of all, ruling over the whole earth; your position is far above any other god.
019	PSA	097	010	You who love the Lord, hate evil! He protects the lives of those who are faithful to him, and saves them from the power of wicked people.
019	PSA	097	011	Light shines on those who do good, giving joy to those who live right.
019	PSA	097	012	Be happy in the Lord, you who do right, and thank him for his holy nature!
019	PSA	098	001	A psalm. Sing the Lord a new song, for he has done wonderful things: by his powerful right hand and his strong arm he has won the victory.
019	PSA	098	002	The Lord has revealed his salvation to the nations, and shown them his goodness.
019	PSA	098	003	He has not forgotten to show his trustworthy love and faithfulness to the descendants of Israel. Our God has made his salvation clear to the ends of the earth.
019	PSA	098	004	Everyone on earth, shout in triumph to the Lord; break out in joyful songs of praise!
019	PSA	098	005	Sing praises to the Lord with the harp, with the harp and melodious voices;
019	PSA	098	006	with trumpets and the sound of the ram's horn sing in happiness before the Lord, the King.
019	PSA	098	007	Let the sea and everything in it shout with praise, together with the earth and everything living in it.
019	PSA	098	008	Let the rivers celebrate, let the hills join in the celebration
019	PSA	098	009	before the Lord, for he is coming to judge the earth. He will judge the world justly, and the nations fairly.
019	PSA	099	001	The Lord reigns; let the nations tremble! He sits on his throne above the cherubim; let the earth shake!
019	PSA	099	002	The Lord rules supreme in Zion, he is sovereign over all the nations.
019	PSA	099	003	Let them praise his greatness, and respect him for who he is—for he is holy,
019	PSA	099	004	having kingly power. You love justice; you make impartial decisions. You have made sure everything is done in fairness and according to what's right.
019	PSA	099	005	Give respect to the Lord our God! Bow down at his feet, for he is holy!
019	PSA	099	006	Moses and Aaron were among his priests; Samuel also prayed to him. They called out to the Lord for help, and he answered them.
019	PSA	099	007	He spoke to the people from the pillar of cloud, and they kept the laws and decrees he gave them.
019	PSA	099	008	Lord our God, you answered them. You were a forgiving God to them, but you punished them when they did wrong.
019	PSA	099	009	Honor the Lord our God, and worship at his holy mountain. For the Lord our God is holy!
019	PSA	100	001	A psalm of thanksgiving. Everyone on earth shout for joy to the Lord!
019	PSA	100	002	Worship the Lord with gladness; come into his presence with joyful songs!
019	PSA	100	003	Know that the Lord is God! He made us, so we belong to him. We are his people, the flock he cares for.
019	PSA	100	004	Go in through his gate with thanks; enter his courts with praise. Thank him; praise him for who he is.
019	PSA	100	005	For the Lord is good. His trustworthy love lasts forever; his faithfulness continues for all generations.
019	PSA	101	001	A psalm of David. I will sing of your faithful love and good judgment. I will sing praises to you, Lord.
019	PSA	101	002	I will make sure my life is blameless. When will you come and help me? My life will be one of integrity even in private.
019	PSA	101	003	I will not look at anything evil. I hate doing wrong—I won't have anything to do with it.
019	PSA	101	004	I won't think bad thoughts—I won't even consider anything evil.
019	PSA	101	005	I will silence anyone who secretly slanders their neighbor. I won't tolerate anyone who is proud and arrogant.
019	PSA	101	006	I look for faithful people to live with me; only those who are trustworthy will serve me.
019	PSA	101	007	No one who is dishonest will live in my house; no liars will be allowed in my presence.
019	PSA	101	008	I work every day to silence the wicked in the land, to rid the city of the Lord of all who do evil.
019	PSA	102	001	A prayer from someone who is suffering and is tired out, pouring out their troubles to the Lord. Lord, please hear my prayer, my cry for help!
019	PSA	102	002	Don't hide your face from me in my time of trouble! Turn and listen to me, and answer me quickly when I call.
019	PSA	102	003	My life is disappearing like smoke; my body feels like it's on fire!
019	PSA	102	004	I'm like grass that's dried up, withered away—I even forget to eat!
019	PSA	102	005	All my groaning has worn me out; my bones show through my skin.
019	PSA	102	006	I'm like a desert owl, like a little owl among the ruins.
019	PSA	102	007	I can't sleep. I'm like a lonely bird on a rooftop.
019	PSA	102	008	My enemies taunt me all day long. They mock me and swear at me.
019	PSA	102	009	Ashes are the food I eat; my tears drip into my drink,
019	PSA	102	010	because of your anger and hostility, for you have picked me up and tossed me away.
019	PSA	102	011	My life is fading away like a shadow that lengthens—I'm withering away like grass.
019	PSA	102	012	But you, Lord, reign forever, your fame will last for all generations.
019	PSA	102	013	You will take action and have pity on Jerusalem, for it's time to be kind to the city, the time has come.
019	PSA	102	014	For the people who follow you love its stones; they value even its dust!
019	PSA	102	015	Then the nations will be in awe of who you are, Lord; all the kings of the earth will be in awe of your glory.
019	PSA	102	016	For the Lord will rebuild Jerusalem; he will appear in glory.
019	PSA	102	017	He will pay attention to the prayers of the homeless; he will not disregard their requests.
019	PSA	102	018	Let this be recorded for generations to come, so that people yet to be born may praise the Lord:
019	PSA	102	019	The Lord looked down from above, from the heights of his holy place; he looked down from heaven to the earth,
019	PSA	102	020	to respond to the groans of prisoners, to set free the children of death.
019	PSA	102	021	As a result the wonderful nature of the Lord will be celebrated with praise in Jerusalem,
019	PSA	102	022	when the people of many kingdoms gather together to worship the Lord.
019	PSA	102	023	But as for me, he broke my health while I was still young, cutting my life short.
019	PSA	102	024	I cried out, “My God, don't take my life while I'm young! You are the one who lives forever.
019	PSA	102	025	Long ago you created the earth; you made the heavens.
019	PSA	102	026	They will come to an end, but you will not. They will all wear out, like clothes—you will change them, and throw them away.
019	PSA	102	027	But you are the one who always is; your years never come to an end.
019	PSA	102	028	Our children will live with you, and our children's children will grow in your presence.”
019	PSA	103	001	A psalm of David. Let every part of me praise the Lord; let my whole being praise his holy character.
019	PSA	103	002	Let every part of me praise the Lord; don't let me forget the wonderful things he's done for me.
019	PSA	103	003	He forgives my sins, and he heals all my diseases.
019	PSA	103	004	He saves me from death; he honors me with trustworthy love and mercy.
019	PSA	103	005	He fills my life with all that's good; he makes me young again, strong as an eagle.
019	PSA	103	006	The Lord does what is right, and vindicates those who are exploited.
019	PSA	103	007	He explained his ways to Moses: he told the people of Israel what he was going to do.
019	PSA	103	008	The Lord is kind and gracious, not quick-tempered, and full of trustworthy love.
019	PSA	103	009	He doesn't keep on accusing us; he doesn't stay angry with us forever.
019	PSA	103	010	He does not punish us for our sins as he ought to; he does not pay us back for our wrongdoing as we deserve.
019	PSA	103	011	For as high as the heavens are above the earth is the extent of his trustworthy love to those who honor him.
019	PSA	103	012	As far as the east is from the west is how far the Lord has taken our sins away from us.
019	PSA	103	013	Like a loving father, the Lord is kind and compassionate to those who follow him.
019	PSA	103	014	For he knows how we are made; he remembers we are only dust.
019	PSA	103	015	Human lifetimes are like grass: we blossom like flowers in a field,
019	PSA	103	016	but then the wind blows and we are gone, disappearing without a trace.
019	PSA	103	017	But the Lord's trustworthy love lasts for all eternity to those who accept him; his goodness to all generations,
019	PSA	103	018	to those who keep his agreement and who remember to follow his commandments.
019	PSA	103	019	The Lord has set up his throne in the heavens, and he rules over all.
019	PSA	103	020	Praise the Lord, you angels, you powerful ones who do what he says, listening to what he tells you!
019	PSA	103	021	Praise the Lord, you heavenly armies who serve him and carry out his will!
019	PSA	103	022	Praise the Lord, everything in his creation, everyone under his rule, and let every part of me praise the Lord!
019	PSA	104	001	Let every part of me praise the Lord! Lord my God, you are so great, clothed with majesty and splendor!
019	PSA	104	002	You wear light as your clothing; you stretch out the fabric of the heavens.
019	PSA	104	003	You place the roof-beams of your house in the rainclouds. You make the clouds your chariots. You ride on the wings of the wind.
019	PSA	104	004	You make your angels winds, and your servants flames of fire.
019	PSA	104	005	You set the earth on its foundations; it will never be shaken.
019	PSA	104	006	It was clothed with ocean depths—the waters even covered the mountains—
019	PSA	104	007	but at your command the waters fled; at the sound of your thunder they rushed away.
019	PSA	104	008	The mountains rose up and the valleys sank down to where you had determined.
019	PSA	104	009	You set a boundary for the oceans so they would not come back and cover the earth.
019	PSA	104	010	You make springs flow into the streams, running down between the hills.
019	PSA	104	011	They provide water for all the wild animals, and wild donkeys quench their thirst.
019	PSA	104	012	Birds build their nests in trees along the streams, singing from among the leaves.
019	PSA	104	013	You send down rain on the mountains from your home high above; you fill the earth with good things.
019	PSA	104	014	You make the grass grow for the cattle, and plants for people to eat—crops produced by the earth for food,
019	PSA	104	015	and wine to make them happy, olive oil to make their faces shine, and bread to make them strong.
019	PSA	104	016	The Lord's trees are well-watered, the cedars of Lebanon that he planted.
019	PSA	104	017	Sparrows make their nests there; herons make their homes in the tall trees.
019	PSA	104	018	Wild goats live high in the mountains; hyraxes hide among the rocks.
019	PSA	104	019	You made the moon to mark the months, and the sun knows when to set.
019	PSA	104	020	You make darkness fall and the night comes, the time when the forest animals come out to hunt.
019	PSA	104	021	The young lions roar as they seek their prey, looking for the food that God provides for them.
019	PSA	104	022	When the sun rises they return to their dens to rest.
019	PSA	104	023	Then people leave for work, working until the evening.
019	PSA	104	024	Lord, how many different things you have made—all of them wisely created! The earth is full of your creatures.
019	PSA	104	025	Consider the sea, deep and wide, full of all kinds of living things, large and small.
