019	PSA	107	040	He pours out his contempt on their leaders, making them wander, lost in the wilderness.
019	PSA	107	041	But he lifts the poor out of their troubles, and makes their families as big as flocks.
019	PSA	107	042	Those who live right will observe what is happening and be glad, but the wicked will be silenced.
019	PSA	107	043	Those who are wise will pay attention to all this, and thoughtfully reflect on the Lord's trustworthy love.
019	PSA	108	001	A song. A psalm of David. God, I have complete confidence in you! My whole being sings praises to you!
019	PSA	108	002	Wake up, harp and lyre! I will wake up the dawn!
019	PSA	108	003	I will thank you among the peoples, Lord, I will sing your praises among the nations.
019	PSA	108	004	For your trustworthy love reaches higher than the heavens, your faithfulness is higher than the clouds.
019	PSA	108	005	God, your greatness is above the highest heavens; and your glory is over all the earth!
019	PSA	108	006	Rescue those you love! Answer us, and save us by your power!
019	PSA	108	007	God has spoken from his Temple: “Triumphantly I divide up Shechem, and portion out the Valley of Succoth.
019	PSA	108	008	Both Gilead and Manasseh belong to me. Ephraim is my helmet, and Judah is my scepter.
019	PSA	108	009	I will treat Moab as my washbasin; I will place my sandal on Edom; I will shout in triumph over Philistia.”
019	PSA	108	010	Who will bring me into the fortified city? Who will lead me into Edom?
019	PSA	108	011	Have you rejected us, God? Won't you go out with our armies?
019	PSA	108	012	Please give us help against our enemies, for human help is worthless.
019	PSA	108	013	Our strength is in God, and he will crush our enemies.
019	PSA	109	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. God, the one I praise, please don't remain silent,
019	PSA	109	002	because wicked and deceitful people are attacking me, telling lies about me.
019	PSA	109	003	They surround me with words of hate, fighting against me for no reason.
019	PSA	109	004	I love them, but they respond with hostility towards me, even while I'm praying for them!
019	PSA	109	005	They pay me back with evil instead of good, with hatred instead of love.
019	PSA	109	006	“Appoint someone wicked over him. Have someone stand as an accuser against him.
019	PSA	109	007	When he is judged and sentenced, may he be found guilty. Let his prayers be counted as sins.
019	PSA	109	008	May his life be short; let someone else take over his position.
019	PSA	109	009	May his children be left fatherless, and his wife become a widow.
019	PSA	109	010	May his children be homeless, wandering beggars, driven from their ruined houses.
019	PSA	109	011	May creditors seize all that he owns; may strangers take all that he worked for.
019	PSA	109	012	May no one be kind to him; may no one take pity on his fatherless children.
019	PSA	109	013	May his descendants die; may his family name be wiped out in the next generation.
019	PSA	109	014	May the Lord be reminded of the sins of his fathers; may his mother's sins not be blotted out.
019	PSA	109	015	May their sins be constantly before the Lord; may his name be totally forgotten by people.
019	PSA	109	016	For he didn't think to be kind to others, instead he harassed and killed the poor, the needy, the brokenhearted.
019	PSA	109	017	He loved to put a curse on others—let it come back on him. He had no time for blessings—so may he never receive any.
019	PSA	109	018	He cursed as often as he got dressed. May his curses go into him like the water he drinks, like the olive oil he rubs on his skin that enters his bones.
019	PSA	109	019	May his curses stick to him like clothing, may they be pulled tight around him like a belt.”
019	PSA	109	020	May all this be the punishment of the Lord on my enemies, on those who speak evil of me.
019	PSA	109	021	But treat me well, Lord God, because of your own reputation. Save me because you are faithful and good.
019	PSA	109	022	For I am poor and needy, and my heart is breaking.
019	PSA	109	023	I am fading away like an evening shadow; I am like a locust that is shaken off.
019	PSA	109	024	I am so weak from lack of food that my legs give way; my body is just skin and bones.
019	PSA	109	025	People ridicule me—they look at me and shake their heads!
019	PSA	109	026	Help me, Lord my God; save me because of your trustworthy love.
019	PSA	109	027	May they recognize that this is what you are doing—that you are the one who saves me.
019	PSA	109	028	When they curse me, you will bless me. When they attack me, you will defeat them. And I, your servant, will be happy.
019	PSA	109	029	May those who accuse me be clothed with disgrace; may they cover themselves with a cloak of shame.
019	PSA	109	030	But I will keep on thanking the Lord, praising him to everyone around me.
019	PSA	109	031	For he takes a stand to defend the needy, to save them from those who condemn them.
019	PSA	110	001	A psalm of David. The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at my right hand, until I make your enemies a footstool for you.”
019	PSA	110	002	The Lord will expand your royal power from Zion; you will rule over your enemies.
019	PSA	110	003	Your people willingly follow you on the day when your power is revealed on the holy mountains, renewed in strength every morning like dew at dawn.
019	PSA	110	004	The Lord has made a vow he will not break: “You are a priest forever, following the order of Melchizedek.”
019	PSA	110	005	The Lord stands right beside you to support you; he will strike down kings in his anger.
019	PSA	110	006	He will execute judgment on the nations, filling their lands with corpses. He will strike down those who rule all over the earth.
019	PSA	110	007	He will drink from streams beside the path. Therefore he will be victorious.
019	PSA	111	001	Praise the Lord! I will thank the Lord with all my heart in the congregation of the faithful.
019	PSA	111	002	All the wonderful things the Lord has done are studied by everyone who loves them.
019	PSA	111	003	His majesty and honor are revealed by what he does; his goodness lasts forever.
019	PSA	111	004	He wants the wonderful things he has done to be remembered; the Lord is gracious and kind.
019	PSA	111	005	He feeds those who respect him; he always remembers the agreement he made.
019	PSA	111	006	He demonstrated to his people the powerful things he could do by giving them the lands of other nations.
019	PSA	111	007	Everything he does can be depended on, and is right; all his commandments are trustworthy.
019	PSA	111	008	They remain rock-solid forever. He was true and right in saying what should be done.
019	PSA	111	009	He delivered his people. He commanded that his agreement would continue forever. How holy and awesome is his reputation!
019	PSA	111	010	The beginning of wisdom is honoring the Lord. Those who follow what he says do well. He is to be praised forever!
019	PSA	112	001	Praise the Lord! Happy are those who respect the Lord, who love to do what he says!
019	PSA	112	002	Their descendants will prosper in the land; the children of those who do good will be blessed.
019	PSA	112	003	Their families will be wealthy; the good they do has eternal results.
019	PSA	112	004	Light shines in the darkness for those who live right, for those who are gracious, compassionate, and good.
019	PSA	112	005	Good things come to those who are generous in their lending and are honest in doing business.
019	PSA	112	006	They will never fall. Those who live right won't be forgotten.
019	PSA	112	007	They aren't afraid of bad news because they rely totally on the Lord.
019	PSA	112	008	They are confident and brave, and see their enemies defeated.
019	PSA	112	009	They share generously, giving to the poor; the good they do has eternal results. They are greatly respected.
019	PSA	112	010	The wicked observe all this and are mad; they gnash their teeth in anger. They waste away, and all that they hoped for comes to nothing.
019	PSA	113	001	Praise the Lord! Praise him, servants of the Lord! Praise the Lord as he is!
019	PSA	113	002	Let the Lord's nature be praised, now and forever.
019	PSA	113	003	Let everyone everywhere, from the east to the west, praise the Lord as he is!
019	PSA	113	004	The Lord rules supreme over all nations; his glory extends higher than the heavens.
019	PSA	113	005	Who is like the Lord our God? He is the one who lives on high, seated on his throne.
019	PSA	113	006	He has to stoop low to look down on the heavens and the earth.
019	PSA	113	007	He helps the poor up from the dust; he lifts the needy from the dump.
019	PSA	113	008	He gives them positions of honor together with important leaders, with leaders of his own people.
019	PSA	113	009	He makes the childless woman happy in her home by giving her children. Praise the Lord!
019	PSA	114	001	At the time of the exodus of Israel from Egypt, when the descendants of Jacob left that foreign country,
