019	PSA	120	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. I called out to the Lord for help in all my troubles, and he answered me.
019	PSA	120	002	Lord, please save me from liars and cheats!
019	PSA	120	003	What will the Lord do to you, you liars? How will he punish you?
019	PSA	120	004	With the sharp arrows of a warrior and burning coals made from a broom tree.
019	PSA	120	005	I'm sorry for myself, because I live as a foreigner in Meshech, or among the tent-dwellers of Kedar.
019	PSA	120	006	I have lived for far too long among people who hate peace.
019	PSA	120	007	I want peace, but when I talk of peace, they want war.
019	PSA	121	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. I look to the hills—but is that where my help comes from?
019	PSA	121	002	My help comes from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	121	003	He will not let you fall; he who watches over you won't fall asleep.
019	PSA	121	004	In fact he who watches over you doesn't take naps or fall asleep.
019	PSA	121	005	The Lord keeps watch over you; the Lord protects you; he stands right beside you.
019	PSA	121	006	The sun won't hurt you during the day, nor the moon at night.
019	PSA	121	007	The Lord will protect you from all kinds of evil; he will keep you safe and sound.
019	PSA	121	008	The Lord will look after you when you leave, and when you return, now and forever.
019	PSA	122	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. A psalm of David. I was so happy when they said to me, “Let's go the house of the Lord.”
019	PSA	122	002	Now we're standing inside your gates, Jerusalem!
019	PSA	122	003	Jerusalem is built as a city where people can be together.
019	PSA	122	004	All the tribes—the tribes of the Lord—go up there, following the command given to Israel to give thanks to the Lord.
019	PSA	122	005	This is where the thrones are placed, where judgment is given, the thrones of the house of David.
019	PSA	122	006	Pray that Jerusalem may be at peace. May everyone who loves Jerusalem be kept safe.
019	PSA	122	007	May there be peace within your walls, and safety within your fortresses.
019	PSA	122	008	On behalf of my family and friends, I will now say, “May you be at peace.”
019	PSA	122	009	On behalf of the house of the Lord our God, I pray that everything goes well for you.
019	PSA	123	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. I look up to you, the one who rules from heaven.
019	PSA	123	002	Just as servants look to their master, or a maid looks to her mistress, so we keep our eyes on you, Lord our God, waiting for you to be merciful to us.
019	PSA	123	003	Please have mercy on us, Lord, have mercy. We've had enough of people's contempt.
019	PSA	123	004	We've had more than enough of the scorn of the proud, and the contempt of the arrogant.
019	PSA	124	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. A psalm of David. If the Lord hadn't been for us, what would have happened? Let everyone in Israel say:
019	PSA	124	002	If the Lord hadn't been for us, what would have happened when people came and attacked us?
019	PSA	124	003	They would have swallowed us alive when their anger raged against us.
019	PSA	124	004	Like a flood they would have swept over us; like a rushing torrent they would have submerged us.
019	PSA	124	005	They would have rushed over us like raging waters, drowning us.
019	PSA	124	006	Praise the Lord, who didn't hand us over to them as prey to be ripped apart by their teeth.
019	PSA	124	007	We escaped from them like a bird flying out of a hunter's trap. The trap was broken and we flew away!
019	PSA	124	008	Our help comes from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	125	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. Those who trust in the Lord are like Mount Zion, for it is unshakeable and endures forever.
019	PSA	125	002	In the same way that the mountains surround Jerusalem, the Lord surrounds his people, now and forever.
019	PSA	125	003	The wicked will not always rule over the land of the faithful, otherwise the faithful might also end up doing wrong.
019	PSA	125	004	Lord, please do good to those who do good, those who sincerely do what is right.
019	PSA	125	005	But as for those who turn aside to follow their own crooked ways—the Lord will lead them away together with those who do evil. May Israel be at peace!
019	PSA	126	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. When the Lord brought his people back from captivity to Zion, it was as if we were dreaming!
019	PSA	126	002	We laughed so much, we sang for joy. The other nations said, “The Lord has done wonderful things for these people.”
019	PSA	126	003	The Lord certainly has done wonderful things for us. How happy we were!
019	PSA	126	004	Please return and help us again, Lord. Renew us like streams of water that renew the Negev desert.
019	PSA	126	005	Those who sow in tears will reap with shouts of joy!
019	PSA	126	006	Those who weep as they go out to sow their seed will be singing in celebration when they carry the harvest home.
019	PSA	127	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. A psalm of Solomon. If the Lord doesn't build the house, the work of the builders is futile. If the Lord doesn't guard the city, the work of the guards is pointless.
019	PSA	127	002	It's useless to get up early in the morning and go to work, and stay late into the evening, worrying about earning enough to eat, when the Lord gives rest to those he loves.
019	PSA	127	003	Children certainly are a gift from the Lord, for a family is a blessing.
019	PSA	127	004	Like arrows in the hand of a warrior are the children of a young man.
019	PSA	127	005	Happy is the father who fills his quiver with them! Such fathers will not be embarrassed when they confront their enemies at the city gate.
019	PSA	128	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. Happy are all those who worship the Lord, everyone who follows his ways!
019	PSA	128	002	You will eat what your own hands have produced. You will be happy and do well.
019	PSA	128	003	Your wife will be like a fruitful vine growing in your home. Your children will be like the shoots of an olive tree around your table.
019	PSA	128	004	This will certainly be the Lord's blessing on those who worship him.
019	PSA	128	005	May the Lord go on blessing you from Zion; may you see Jerusalem prosper all the days of your life.
019	PSA	128	006	May you see your children's children. May Israel be at peace!
019	PSA	129	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. Many enemies have attacked from the time I was young. Let everyone in Israel say:
019	PSA	129	002	Many enemies have attacked from the time I was young, but they never defeated me.
019	PSA	129	003	They beat me on my back, leaving long furrows as if it had been plowed by a farmer.
019	PSA	129	004	But the Lord does what is right: he has cut me free from the ropes of the wicked.
019	PSA	129	005	May everyone who hates Zion be driven back in humiliating defeat.
019	PSA	129	006	May they be like grass that grows on a roof that withers before it can be harvested,
019	PSA	129	007	There's not enough even for a reaper to hold, not enough even for the binder to bind.
019	PSA	129	008	May passers-by not say to them, “The blessing of the Lord be on you; we bless you in the name of the Lord.”
019	PSA	130	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. Lord, I cry out to you from the depths of my pain.
019	PSA	130	002	Please listen to my cry, and pay attention to what I'm asking.
019	PSA	130	003	Lord, if you kept a list of sins, who could escape being condemned?
019	PSA	130	004	But you are forgiving so that we might respect you.
019	PSA	130	005	I'm waiting for the Lord, longingly waiting, for I trust in his word.
019	PSA	130	006	I long for the Lord to come, more than watchmen longing for the dawn to come, more than watchmen longing for the dawn to come.
019	PSA	130	007	Israel, put your hope in the Lord, for the Lord loves us with a trustworthy love and his salvation knows no limits.
019	PSA	130	008	He will save Israel from every sin.
019	PSA	131	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. A psalm of David. Lord, I'm not proud or arrogant. I don't worry about things that are beyond me, matters that are far beyond my experience.
019	PSA	131	002	On the contrary, I have chosen to be calm and quiet, like a weaned child with its mother. I am like a weaned child with its mother.
019	PSA	131	003	Israel, hope in the Lord, now and forever!
019	PSA	132	001	A song for pilgrims going up to Jerusalem. Lord, remember David, and all that he went through.
