019	PSA	136	003	Thank the Lord of lords! For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	004	To him who alone does amazing things! For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	005	To him who knew how to make the heavens. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	006	To him who spread out the earth over the waters. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	007	To him who made the lights above. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	008	The sun to rule the day. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	009	The moon and stars to rule the night. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	010	To him who struck down the firstborn in Egypt. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	011	He led his people out of Egypt. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	012	He did this with his strong hand and outstretched arm. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	013	To him who parted the Red Sea. For his trustworthy love lasts forever,
019	PSA	136	014	And led Israel through it. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	015	But threw Pharaoh and his army into the Red Sea. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	016	To him who led his people through the wilderness. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	017	To him who struck down powerful kings. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	018	To him who killed powerful kings. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	019	Sihon, king of the Amorites. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	020	Og, king of Bashan. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	021	He gave Israel their land to possess. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	022	He granted ownership to his servant Israel. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	023	He remembered us even in our humiliation. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	024	He rescued us from our enemies. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	025	To the one who provides food for every living creature. For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	136	026	Thank the God of heaven! For his trustworthy love lasts forever.
019	PSA	137	001	When we sat down by the rivers of Babylon we wept as we remembered Zion.
019	PSA	137	002	We hung up our harps on the willow trees.
019	PSA	137	003	For those who had taken us captive asked us for a song—our tormentors wanted us to sing a happy song from Jerusalem.
019	PSA	137	004	But how could we sing a song dedicated to the Lord in a pagan land?
019	PSA	137	005	If I forget Jerusalem, may my right hand forget how to play;
019	PSA	137	006	May my tongue stick to the roof of my mouth if I don't remember you—if I don't consider Jerusalem my greatest joy.
019	PSA	137	007	Lord, please remember what the people of Edom did on the day Jerusalem fell, the ones who said “Tear it down! Destroy it down to its foundations!”
019	PSA	137	008	Daughter of Babylon, you will be destroyed! Happy is the one who pays you back, who does to you what you did to us!
019	PSA	137	009	Happy is the one who grabs your children and smashes them against the rocks!
019	PSA	138	001	A psalm of David. I thank you with my whole being; I sing your praises before the heavenly beings.
019	PSA	138	002	I bow down before your holy Temple, and I am thankful because of who you are—for your trustworthy love and faithfulness—and for the fact that your promises are even greater than what people expect of you.
019	PSA	138	003	On the day I cried out to you for help, you answered me. You encouraged me and made me strong.
019	PSA	138	004	All the kings of the earth will praise you, Lord, for they have heard what you have said.
019	PSA	138	005	They will sing about what the Lord has done and about the great glory of the Lord.
019	PSA	138	006	Though the Lord is high above, he pays attention to the lowly; but he recognizes the proud a long way off.
019	PSA	138	007	Even though I walk into a great deal of trouble, you protect me. You reach out to defend me from the anger of those who hate me—your strong hand saves me.
019	PSA	138	008	The Lord vindicates me! Lord, your trustworthy love lasts forever! Don't give up on what you have made!
019	PSA	139	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. Lord, you have examined me from the inside out—you know everything about me!
019	PSA	139	002	You know when I sit down and when I get up. You know what I'm thinking even when I'm a long way away.
019	PSA	139	003	You observe where I go and when I rest. You're familiar with everything I do.
019	PSA	139	004	Lord, you even know what I'm going to say before I say it.
019	PSA	139	005	You're always there—behind me, in front of me, and all around me. You place your caring hand on me.
019	PSA	139	006	This amazing knowledge you have is far beyond me, way beyond my understanding!
019	PSA	139	007	Where can I go that you're not already there? Where can I run to escape your presence?
019	PSA	139	008	If I go up to heaven, you are there. If I lie down in Sheol, look—you are there too!
019	PSA	139	009	If I were to fly away on wings of the dawn to the east; if I were to live on the far western shore of the sea,
019	PSA	139	010	even there your hand would lead me, your right hand would support me.
019	PSA	139	011	If I asked the darkness to hide me, and light to become night around me,
019	PSA	139	012	Even darkness would not be dark for you, and the night would be bright as day, for darkness is like light to you.
019	PSA	139	013	You made me from the inside out, shaping me in my mother's womb.
019	PSA	139	014	I praise you for making me in such an awesome and wonderful way. What you do is incredible—I realize this completely!
019	PSA	139	015	My growing body was not hidden from you as I was formed in secret, as I was intricately put together “in the depths of the earth.”
019	PSA	139	016	You saw me as an embryo, and in your book all my days were written down—the days that were made for me before any of them existed.
019	PSA	139	017	God, your thoughts are so valuable to me! Taken together, they can't be counted!
019	PSA	139	018	If I tried to count them, they would be more than every grain of sand. Yet when I awake I am still with you.
019	PSA	139	019	God, if you would only kill the wicked! Murderers, get away from me!
019	PSA	139	020	When they speak of you they're being deceptively evil. Since they are your enemies, they call on you in vain.
019	PSA	139	021	Lord, don't I hate those who hate you? I despise those who rebel against you!
019	PSA	139	022	I hate them with absolute hatred—they have become my enemies!
019	PSA	139	023	Examine me carefully, God, so you can be sure of my true feelings. Check me out so you can know what I really think.
019	PSA	139	024	Please show me if I'm following any kind of idol, and lead me along the path of eternal life.
019	PSA	140	001	For the music director. A psalm of David. Lord, please save me from those who do evil; protect me especially from those who are violent!
019	PSA	140	002	Their minds are busy plotting evil things, stirring up trouble all day long.
019	PSA	140	003	Their tongues are as sharp as those of snakes; viper's venom is on their lips. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	004	Lord, please keep me from falling into the hands of the wicked; protect me especially from those who are violent, who are plotting my downfall.
019	PSA	140	005	Proud people have hidden a trap for me—they have strung out a net on the path, they have set snares to catch me. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	006	I told the Lord, “You are my God! Lord, please listen to my cries for help!”
019	PSA	140	007	Lord God, my powerful Savior, you covered my head like a helmet on the day of battle.
019	PSA	140	008	God, don't allow the wicked to get what they want—don't let them be successful in what they plan so they don't become proud. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	009	May the harm spoken against me by those who surround me fall back on them,
019	PSA	140	010	Let burning coals rain down on them! Let them be thrown into the fire, or into bottomless pits, never to rise again.
019	PSA	140	011	Don't let people who slander others live in our land. May disaster strike down violent people.
019	PSA	140	012	Yet I know the Lord defends the rights of those who are persecuted, and gives justice to the poor.
019	PSA	140	013	Truly those who live right are thankful for the kind of person you are, and those who are honest will live in your presence.
019	PSA	141	001	A psalm of David. Lord, I'm calling out to you! Please hurry up and help me! Please listen to me when I cry out to you!
019	PSA	141	002	May my prayer be like incense before you, my uplifted hands like an evening offering.
019	PSA	141	003	Lord, make sure I don't say anything I shouldn't—keep a watch over my conversations.
019	PSA	141	004	Don't let me think about evil things or take part in doing anything wrong with wicked people. I won't join in eating fancy food at their feasts.
019	PSA	141	005	Let a good person punish me in love—let them correct me. It will be like an anointing—I won't refuse it. But I still pray against those who do evil.
019	PSA	141	006	They shall be thrown down by the power of the rock that judges them, and then they will recognize what I said was true!
019	PSA	141	007	Just as the earth is broken up by the plow, so shall their bones be scattered at the mouth of Sheol.
019	PSA	141	008	But I'm looking to you, Lord God, for I find protection in you. Don't let me die!
019	PSA	141	009	Keep me safe from the traps they have set to catch me, from the snares of evil people.
019	PSA	141	010	Let them fall into their own traps while I pass by unharmed.
019	PSA	142	001	A maskil of David, when he was in the cave. A prayer. I call out to the Lord for help; pleading with the Lord for mercy.
019	PSA	142	002	I pour out my complaints before him; I tell him what's troubling me.
019	PSA	142	003	When I'm totally discouraged, you know the direction I should take. But whichever way I go, people set traps for me.
019	PSA	142	004	I look to my right for someone to support me—but no one pays me any attention. There's no safe place for me—no one cares about me at all.
019	PSA	142	005	I cry out to you, Lord, for help, saying, “You are the one who keeps me safe; you are all I need in life.
019	PSA	142	006	Please listen to my sad cry, for I'm feeling very low. Please save me from those who are after me, for they're too strong for me.
019	PSA	142	007	Release me from my prison so I can praise you for the person you are! Those who live right will gather round me because you have treated me so well.”
019	PSA	143	001	A psalm of David. Lord, please hear my prayer. Because you are faithful, please listen to my appeal for mercy. Answer me because you do what is right!
019	PSA	143	002	Please don't place me, your servant, on trial, because nobody is innocent in your sight.
019	PSA	143	003	The enemy has chased me down. He crushes me to the ground. He makes me live in darkness like those who died a long time ago.
019	PSA	143	004	I sense myself fading away inside; I am overwhelmed by a sense of desolation.
019	PSA	143	005	I think of days long ago, and as I meditate I talk to myself about all you have done, I reflect on what you have accomplished.
019	PSA	143	006	I stretch out my hands to you, thirsting for you like dried-out land. (Selah)
019	PSA	143	007	Please answer me quickly, Lord! I'm dying! Don't turn away otherwise I'll be just like those who are going down into the grave.
019	PSA	143	008	Tell me every morning about your trustworthy love, because I put my confidence in you. Show me the way I should go, because I dedicate myself to you.
019	PSA	143	009	Save me from those who hate me, Lord—I run to you for protection.
019	PSA	143	010	Teach me your will for you are my God. May your spirit of goodness lead me and make my way smooth.
019	PSA	143	011	Because of the kind of person you are, let me go on living. Because you always do what's right, get me out of the trouble I'm in.
019	PSA	143	012	In your trustworthy love, get rid of those who hate me, destroy all my enemies, for I am your servant.
019	PSA	144	001	A psalm of David. Praise the Lord—he is my rock. He trains me for battle, he gives me skill for war.
019	PSA	144	002	He is the one who faithfully loves me, protects me, and defends me. He is the one who rescues me, shields me from danger, and keeps me safe. He defeats nations and places them under my rule.
019	PSA	144	003	Lord, what are human beings that you should care about them? What are people that you should concern yourself with them?
019	PSA	144	004	Humanity is like a breath; their lives are like a passing shadow.
019	PSA	144	005	Part your heavens and come down. Touch the mountains so that they give off smoke.
019	PSA	144	006	Scatter your enemies with flashes of lightning! Let your arrows fly and send them running in confusion!
019	PSA	144	007	Stretch down your hand from heaven and set me free. Rescue me from raging waters, from the oppression of foreign enemies.
019	PSA	144	008	They are such liars, even telling lies under oath.
019	PSA	144	009	God, I will sing a new song to you, accompanied by a ten-stringed harp,
019	PSA	144	010	to you, the one who gives victory to kings. You saved your servant David from death by the sword.
019	PSA	144	011	Set me free. Rescue me from the oppression of foreign enemies. They are such liars, even telling lies under oath.
019	PSA	144	012	Then our sons will grow up like plants in their youth and become mature, and our daughters will be like beautiful pillars carved to support a palace.
019	PSA	144	013	Our storehouses will be full of all kinds of crops; our flocks of sheep will grow by thousands, increasing by tens of thousands in the pastures.
019	PSA	144	014	Our cattle will grow fat. No one will break down our city walls, there will be no exile, no cries of mourning in our town squares.
019	PSA	144	015	The people who live like this will be happy. Happy are those whose God is the Lord.
019	PSA	145	001	A psalm of David. A song of praise. I will glorify you, my God and King! I will praise who you are forever and ever!
019	PSA	145	002	I will praise you every day; I will praise your character forever and ever!
019	PSA	145	003	The Lord is great and deserves much praise! His greatness cannot be measured!
019	PSA	145	004	Let every generation tell the next all that you do, sharing the stories of your amazing miracles!
019	PSA	145	005	They will speak of your majesty, your glorious splendor, and I will meditate on the wonderful things you have done.
019	PSA	145	006	They will speak of the power of your awesome actions, and I will say how wonderful you are.
019	PSA	145	007	They will explain to everyone how famous you are for your tremendous goodness, and joyfully celebrate how you always do what is right.
019	PSA	145	008	The Lord is gracious and merciful, not easily angered, and full of trustworthy love.
019	PSA	145	009	The Lord is good to everyone, and he shows mercy to all his created beings.
019	PSA	145	010	All the created beings will thank you, Lord, and all who faithfully follow you will praise you.
019	PSA	145	011	They will praise the glory of your kingdom, and talk about your power.
019	PSA	145	012	They will explain to people your wonderful miracles, and the glorious splendor of your kingdom.
019	PSA	145	013	Your kingdom never ends, and your rule continues for all generations. What the Lord promises can always be trusted; he is merciful in all he does.
019	PSA	145	014	The Lord helps up all those who fall down; he lifts up all those who are bowed down.
019	PSA	145	015	All eyes are on you, waiting in hope, and you give food at just the right time.
019	PSA	145	016	You give generously and satisfy the needs of every living thing.
019	PSA	145	017	The Lord does right in everything—his actions are always trustworthy.
019	PSA	145	018	The Lord is close to all who ask for his help, to all who ask in sincerity.
019	PSA	145	019	He satisfies the needs of those who follow him. He hears their cries for help and he saves them.
019	PSA	145	020	The Lord takes care of all those who love him, but he will destroy all those who are wicked.
019	PSA	145	021	I will speak in praise of the Lord, and may everyone honor his holy character, forever and ever.
019	PSA	146	001	Praise the Lord! With my whole being I praise the Lord!
019	PSA	146	002	I will praise the Lord while I live; I will sing praises to my God while I have breath.
019	PSA	146	003	Don't put your confidence in human leaders—they can't save you.
019	PSA	146	004	Once they breathe no more, they go back to dust. On that very day everything they planned dies with them.
019	PSA	146	005	Happy are those who have the God of Jacob to help them—their hope is in the Lord their God—
019	PSA	146	006	the one who made heaven and earth, and the sea along with everything it contains. He is trustworthy forever.
019	PSA	146	007	He makes sure the oppressed receive justice. He gives food to the hungry. The Lord sets the prisoners free.
019	PSA	146	008	The Lord makes the blind see. The Lord lifts up those who are bowed down. The Lord loves those who do what's right.
019	PSA	146	009	The Lord takes care of strangers among us. He looks after widows and orphans. But he makes life difficult for the wicked.
019	PSA	146	010	The Lord will reign forever. Zion, he will be your God for all generations. Praise the Lord!
019	PSA	147	001	Praise the Lord, for it's good to sing praises to our God! Praise is wonderful and beautiful!
019	PSA	147	002	The Lord is rebuilding Jerusalem, gathering together the people of Israel who have been scattered.
019	PSA	147	003	He heals the broken-hearted, and bandages the wounded.
019	PSA	147	004	He knows how many stars he made, and commands all of them by name.
019	PSA	147	005	Our Lord is great! His power is immense! There's no limit to what he understands!
019	PSA	147	006	The Lord helps those who are bowed down to get up; but he grinds the wicked into the ground.
019	PSA	147	007	Sing thanks to the Lord! Sing praises to our God with a harp!
019	PSA	147	008	He covers the sky with clouds to bring rain to the earth, and makes the grass grow on the hills.
019	PSA	147	009	He gives food to the animals, and to the baby ravens when they call.
019	PSA	147	010	The Lord doesn't appreciate the strength of war-horses or value human power.
019	PSA	147	011	What the Lord values are those who follow him, those who put their confidence in his trustworthy love.
019	PSA	147	012	Jerusalem, praise the Lord! Zion, praise your God!
019	PSA	147	013	He makes the bars on your city gates strong, and blesses your children around you.
019	PSA	147	014	He keeps the borders of your land safe from attack; he provides you with plenty of the finest wheat.
019	PSA	147	015	He sends his commands around the world—they're quickly implemented.
019	PSA	147	016	He sends snow as white as wool, and scatters frost like ashes.
019	PSA	147	017	He throws hail like stones. Who can stand the cold he sends?
019	PSA	147	018	Then he sends out his command and it melts; he blows on it and the water flows.
019	PSA	147	019	He proclaims his word to Jacob; his rules and laws to Israel.
019	PSA	147	020	He has not done this for any other nation—they don't know his laws. Praise the Lord!
019	PSA	148	001	Praise the Lord! Praise the Lord from heaven; praise him in the heights above!
019	PSA	148	002	Praise him, all his angels; praise him, all his heavenly armies!
019	PSA	148	003	Praise him, sun and moon! Praise him, all you shining stars!
019	PSA	148	004	Praise him, highest heavens, and the waters above the heavens!
019	PSA	148	005	Let them all praise the Lord and his nature, for he gave the order and they were created.
019	PSA	148	006	He placed them in their positions forever and ever; he established a law that will never end.
019	PSA	148	007	Praise the Lord from the earth, and creatures from all the depths of the seas,
019	PSA	148	008	lightning and hail, snow and clouds, and stormy wind—everything that does as he commands.
019	PSA	148	009	Mountains and all the hills, fruit trees and all the trees of the forest,
019	PSA	148	010	wild animals and all livestock, crawling animals and wild birds,
019	PSA	148	011	earthly kings and all peoples, leaders and rulers of the world,
019	PSA	148	012	young men and women, old people and children—
019	PSA	148	013	Let them all praise the Lord, for his reputation is unequalled; his glory is above anything on earth or in heaven.
019	PSA	148	014	He has given his people a source of strength, bringing praise to his faithful followers, the people of Israel who are dear to him. Praise the Lord!
019	PSA	149	001	Praise the Lord! Sing a new song to the Lord! Praise him wherever his faithful followers gather!
019	PSA	149	002	Let Israel celebrate their Creator; let the people of Zion be happy in their King.
019	PSA	149	003	Praise his nature with dancing; sing praises to him, accompanied by tambourine and harp.
019	PSA	149	004	For the Lord enjoys his people; he honors the oppressed with salvation.
019	PSA	149	005	Let the faithful celebrate how he honors them; let them sing happily even from their beds.
019	PSA	149	006	May their praises of God always be on their lips, a double-edged sword in their hands,
019	PSA	149	007	ready to take revenge on the nations, to punish the foreign peoples,
019	PSA	149	008	to imprison their kings in shackles and their leaders in iron chains,
019	PSA	149	009	to impose the judgment decreed against them. This is an honor for all his faithful followers. Praise the Lord!
019	PSA	150	001	Praise the Lord! Praise God in his holy place! Praise him in the great expanse of heaven!
019	PSA	150	002	Praise him for the amazing things he does! Praise him for how wonderfully great he is!
019	PSA	150	003	Praise him with the sound of the trumpet, praise him with harp and lyre!
019	PSA	150	004	Praise him with tambourine and dancing, praise him with strings and flutes!
019	PSA	150	005	Praise him with the clash of cymbals, praise him with really loud cymbals!
019	PSA	150	006	Let everything that breathes praise the Lord! Praise the Lord!
#
# BOOK	020	PRO	Proverbs	Proverbs
020	PRO	001	001	The proverbs of Solomon, son of David, king of Israel.
020	PRO	001	002	They are for achieving wisdom and instruction, and to recognize sayings that bring insight.
020	PRO	001	003	They provide education in what makes sense, living right, judging correctly, and acting fairly.
020	PRO	001	004	They give discernment to the immature, knowledge and discretion to the young.
020	PRO	001	005	Wise people will listen and gain in learning, and those who have good judgment will gain skills in guidance,
020	PRO	001	006	understanding the proverbs and puzzles, the sayings and questions of the wise.
020	PRO	001	007	Honoring the Lord is where true knowledge begins, but fools treat wisdom and good advice with contempt.
020	PRO	001	008	My son, pay attention to your father's instruction, and don't reject your mother's teaching.
020	PRO	001	009	They are a wreath of grace to decorate your head; they are pendants for your neck.
020	PRO	001	010	My son, if evil people try to tempt you, don't give into them.
020	PRO	001	011	They may tell you, “Come with us. Let's go and hide, ready to kill someone. Let's ambush someone for fun!
020	PRO	001	012	Let's bury them alive; let's put them in the grave while they're still healthy!
020	PRO	001	013	We'll take from them all kinds of valuable things and fill our homes with the stuff we steal!
020	PRO	001	014	Come and join us and we'll all share what we get!”
020	PRO	001	015	My son, don't follow their ways. Don't go in that direction with them.
020	PRO	001	016	For they rush to do evil; they hurry to commit violence and murder.
020	PRO	001	017	There's no point in trying to lure birds into a net when they can see it.
020	PRO	001	018	However, these evil people hide ready to kill others, but they themselves are the victims. They're only ambushing themselves!
020	PRO	001	019	This is what happens to you if you try to become rich through crime—it kills you!
020	PRO	001	020	Wisdom calls out in the streets; she shouts aloud in the squares.
020	PRO	001	021	She cries out at busy corners; she explains her message at the town gates:
020	PRO	001	022	“How long will you stupid people love stupidity? How long will scornful people enjoy their mocking? How long will fools hate knowledge?
020	PRO	001	023	Pay attention to my warnings, and I'll pour out my deepest thoughts to you—I'll explain what I know to you.
020	PRO	001	024	For I have called you, but you refused to listen; I reached out my hand to you, but you didn't care.
020	PRO	001	025	You ignored everything I said; you wouldn't accept any of my warnings.
020	PRO	001	026	So I'll laugh at you when you're in trouble; I'll mock you when you're in a panic.
020	PRO	001	027	When panic rains down on you like a storm, when trouble hits you like a whirlwind, when sorrow and pain come on you,
020	PRO	001	028	then you'll call out to me for help, but I won't answer; you'll search hard for me, but won't find me.
020	PRO	001	029	Why?—because they hated knowledge, and they didn't choose to respect the Lord.
020	PRO	001	030	They're not willing to accept my advice; they despise all my warnings.
020	PRO	001	031	So they'll have to eat the fruit of their own choices, bloated by their own devious schemes.
020	PRO	001	032	Stupid people are killed by their rebellion; foolish people are destroyed by their lack of concern.
020	PRO	001	033	But everyone who listens to me will be kept safe, and will live without worrying about problems.”
020	PRO	002	001	My son, if you accept what I say and value my instructions,
020	PRO	002	002	if you pay attention to wisdom and really try to understand;
020	PRO	002	003	if you cry out for insight and call loudly for help in understanding;
020	PRO	002	004	if you look for it as if it were silver and search for it as if it were hidden treasure;
020	PRO	002	005	then you will understand how to relate to the Lord and discover the truth about God.
020	PRO	002	006	The Lord is the source of wisdom; what he says provides knowledge that makes sense.
020	PRO	002	007	He gives good judgment to those who live right; he defends those who have good sense.
020	PRO	002	008	He supports those who act fairly and protects those who trust in him.
020	PRO	002	009	Then you will be able to recognize what is right and just and fair, in fact all that is good in the way you should live.
020	PRO	002	010	For wisdom will fill your mind, and knowledge will make you happy.
020	PRO	002	011	Good decisions will keep you on track; thinking logically will keep you safe.
020	PRO	002	012	Doing this will save you from the ways of evil, from men who tell twisted lies,
020	PRO	002	013	who turn away from following what is right to walk down paths of darkness.
020	PRO	002	014	They happily do wrong; they love how twisted evil is.
020	PRO	002	015	They live crooked lives doing deceitful things.
020	PRO	002	016	Doing this will also save you from a woman who acts immorally, from a woman who like a prostitute tries to seduce you with flattering words.
020	PRO	002	017	Such a woman has left her husband she married when she was young, forgetting the promises she made before God.
020	PRO	002	018	What happens in her house leads to death; following her way leads to the grave.
020	PRO	002	019	No one who goes to her comes back; they don't ever find the way back to life again.
020	PRO	002	020	So you should follow the way of the good, and make sure you stay on the paths of those who do right.
020	PRO	002	021	For only people who live right will live in the land; only honest people will remain there.
020	PRO	002	022	But the wicked will be thrown out of the land; those who are untrustworthy will be pulled out by the roots.
020	PRO	003	001	My son, don't forget my instructions. Always keep my commands in mind.
020	PRO	003	002	Then you will live a long time, and have a full life.
020	PRO	003	003	Hold on to kindness and truth. Tie them around your neck; write them in your mind.
020	PRO	003	004	That way you'll gain a good reputation and be appreciated by both God and people.
020	PRO	003	005	Put your trust totally in the Lord—don't rely on what you think you know!
020	PRO	003	006	Remember him in everything you do, and he'll show you the right way.
020	PRO	003	007	Don't think you're wise—respect God and avoid evil.
020	PRO	003	008	Then you will be healed and made strong.
020	PRO	003	009	Honor the Lord with your wealth and with the firstfruits of all the crops you grow.
020	PRO	003	010	Then your barns will be filled with produce, and your vats will overflow with new wine.
020	PRO	003	011	My son, don't reject the Lord's discipline or resent it when he corrects you,
020	PRO	003	012	for the Lord corrects those he loves, as a father corrects a son who pleases him.
020	PRO	003	013	Happy are those who find wisdom and gain understanding,
020	PRO	003	014	for wisdom is worth more than silver, and pays better than gold.
020	PRO	003	015	She is more valuable than rubies—everything you could ever want just doesn't compare!
020	PRO	003	016	She offers long life in one hand, and riches and honor in the other.
020	PRO	003	017	She brings true happiness, and leads to peaceful prosperity.
020	PRO	003	018	Wisdom is a tree of life to everyone who embraces her, blessing those who accept her.
020	PRO	003	019	It was through wisdom that the Lord created the earth, and through understanding he set the heavens in place.
020	PRO	003	020	It was through his knowledge the waters of the deep were broken open, and the clouds sent down the dew.
020	PRO	003	021	My son, hold on to good judgment and wise decisions—don't let them out of your sight,
020	PRO	003	022	for they will be life to you, and an ornament for your neck.
020	PRO	003	023	You will be able to walk confidently on your way, and you won't trip up.
020	PRO	003	024	When you rest, you won't be afraid; when you lie down, your sleep will be sweet.
020	PRO	003	025	You won't be afraid of a sudden panic, or of disasters that hit the wicked,
020	PRO	003	026	for the Lord will be the one you can trust in, and he will prevent you being caught in a trap.
020	PRO	003	027	Don't hold back good from those who deserve it when it's something you have the power to do.
020	PRO	003	028	Don't tell your neighbor, “Go away. Come back tomorrow and then I'll give it to you,” when you've already got it.
020	PRO	003	029	Don't plan to harm your neighbor who lives nearby and trusts you.
020	PRO	003	030	Don't quarrel with anybody for no reason, when they haven't done anything to hurt you.
020	PRO	003	031	Don't be jealous of violent people—don't choose to follow their example!
020	PRO	003	032	For the Lord hates deceitful people, but he is a friend to those who do what is good.
020	PRO	003	033	The houses of the wicked are cursed by the Lord, but he blesses the homes of those who live right.
020	PRO	003	034	He mocks those who mock, but he is kind to the humble.
020	PRO	003	035	The wise will receive honor, but fools are held up in disgrace.
020	PRO	004	001	Listen, sons, to a father's instruction; pay attention and discover what makes sense,
020	PRO	004	002	for what I am passing on to you is reliable. Don't reject my teachings.
020	PRO	004	003	When I was a son with my father—a tender young boy, my mother's only child—
020	PRO	004	004	he was the one who taught me. He told me, “Pay attention to the words I say and keep them in mind; do what I tell you and you will live.
020	PRO	004	005	Get wisdom, find out what makes sense. Don't forget my words or reject them.
020	PRO	004	006	Don't give up on wisdom for she will keep you safe. Love wisdom and she will protect you.
020	PRO	004	007	The first thing in becoming wise is to get wisdom! Whatever else you gain, gain insight.
020	PRO	004	008	Treasure wisdom, and she will praise you; embrace her, and she will honor you.
020	PRO	004	009	She will place on your head a wreath of grace; she will present to you a crown of glory.”
020	PRO	004	010	Listen, my son, if you accept what I tell you, then you will live a long life.
020	PRO	004	011	I have explained to you the way of wisdom; I have guided you along the right paths.
020	PRO	004	012	Nothing will block your way when you walk, you won't stumble when you run.
020	PRO	004	013	Hold on to these instructions—don't let them go. Protect them, for they are life's foundation.
020	PRO	004	014	Don't go the way of the wicked or follow the example of those who do evil.
020	PRO	004	015	Avoid that way completely. Don't go there! Turn away, and walk on.
020	PRO	004	016	Evil people won't rest until they've done something wrong; they can't sleep unless they've tripped someone up.
020	PRO	004	017	For they eat the bread of wickedness and drink the wine of violence.
020	PRO	004	018	The way of life of the good is like the light of the sunrise, glowing brighter and brighter until the full light of day shines out.
020	PRO	004	019	But the way of life of the wicked is like complete darkness; they don't even know what they're tripping over.
020	PRO	004	020	My son, pay attention to what I tell you; listen to the words I'm saying.
020	PRO	004	021	Don't lose sight of them; think about them deeply,
020	PRO	004	022	for they are life to anyone who finds them, and make the whole body healthy.
020	PRO	004	023	Most of all, protect your mind, for everything in life flows from it.
020	PRO	004	024	Don't ever lie, and don't say anything dishonest.
020	PRO	004	025	Focus on what's ahead of you; look at what's in front of you.
020	PRO	004	026	Pay attention to the path you decide to follow, and you'll be safe wherever you go.
020	PRO	004	027	Don't deviate to the right or the left, and turn away from evil.
020	PRO	005	001	My son, pay attention to my wisdom, listen carefully as I explain what makes sense,
020	PRO	005	002	so you can make good decisions and protect knowledge with your lips.
020	PRO	005	003	For the lips of an immoral woman may taste as sweet as honey, the kisses of her mouth may be as smooth as oil,
020	PRO	005	004	but in the end what you get from her is the bitterness of wormwood and the sharp pain of being cut with a two-edged sword.
020	PRO	005	005	She leads you down to death; she takes you down to the grave.
020	PRO	005	006	She doesn't follow the path that leads to life—she wanders away and doesn't even know she's lost.
020	PRO	005	007	Now, my son, listen to me; don't reject what I have taught you.
020	PRO	005	008	Stay far away from her! Don't go near the door of her house!
020	PRO	005	009	Otherwise you'll surrender your honor to others, and your character to cruel people.
020	PRO	005	010	Strangers will spend your wealth; everything you've worked for will go to someone else.
020	PRO	005	011	When you come to the end of your life you'll moan in pain as disease destroys your body.
020	PRO	005	012	You'll say, “How I used to hate discipline, and my mind rebelled against being corrected!
020	PRO	005	013	I didn't listen to what my teacher said. I didn't pay attention to my instructors.
020	PRO	005	014	Now I'm on the verge of being completely disgraced before everyone in the community.”
020	PRO	005	015	Drink water from your own cistern, flowing water from your own well.
020	PRO	005	016	Why should your springs be spilled outside, your streams of water poured out in the streets?
020	PRO	005	017	Keep them for yourselves alone. They're not for you to share with strangers.
020	PRO	005	018	May your spring of water be blessed, and may you enjoy the wife you married when you were young.
020	PRO	005	019	May she be to you a loving deer, a graceful doe. May her breasts always be intoxicating to you; may you be drunk on her love forever.
020	PRO	005	020	Why, my son, become intoxicated with an immoral woman? Why embrace the breasts of a woman who acts like a prostitute?
020	PRO	005	021	For the Lord sees everything people do, the Lord investigates everywhere they go.
020	PRO	005	022	The wicked are trapped by their evil actions; the cords of their sins tie them up.
020	PRO	005	023	They will die because they lack self-control, lost because of their great stupidity.
020	PRO	006	001	My son, suppose you have pledged to guarantee your neighbor's debt, or you have shaken hands in agreement with a stranger,
020	PRO	006	002	then you've trapped yourself by what you promised, you've been caught by what you said.
020	PRO	006	003	So this is what you have to do. You need to get out of it, because you've put yourself in that person's power. Go to your neighbor in all humility and ask him to release you from the commitment.
020	PRO	006	004	Don't delay, saying that you'll sleep on it. Don't rest until you've done it.
020	PRO	006	005	Get out of it like a gazelle escaping from a trap, like a bird from a bird-catcher's net.
020	PRO	006	006	Go and observe the ants, you slacker! Learn from what they do and become wise.
020	PRO	006	007	They don't have a leader, an officer, or a ruler,
020	PRO	006	008	yet they work hard during the summer getting their food, gathering what they need during the harvest.
020	PRO	006	009	So how long are you going to lie there, you slacker? When are you going to get up from your sleep?
020	PRO	006	010	You may say, “Please, just a little more sleep, a little longer snooze, a little more folding of the arms to rest”—
020	PRO	006	011	and poverty will attack you like a robber, destitution like an armed warrior.
020	PRO	006	012	Rebellious and wicked people go around telling lies,
020	PRO	006	013	winking slyly, giving sneaky foot gestures, rudely pointing with their fingers.
020	PRO	006	014	Their warped minds plot evil schemes; they're always causing trouble.
020	PRO	006	015	As a result, disaster falls suddenly on such people; in just a moment they're destroyed without hope of healing.
020	PRO	006	016	There are six things that the Lord hates, seven things that he absolutely detests:
020	PRO	006	017	arrogant eyes, a lying tongue, hands that murder the innocent,
020	PRO	006	018	a mind that plots evil schemes, feet that hurriedly run to do wrong,
020	PRO	006	019	a false witness that speaks lies, those who caused arguments in families.
020	PRO	006	020	My son, pay attention to your father's instruction, and don't reject your mother's teaching.
020	PRO	006	021	Keep them always in mind. Tie them around your neck.
020	PRO	006	022	They will lead you as you walk along; they will watch over you as you sleep; when you wake up they will talk with you.
020	PRO	006	023	For the instruction is a lamp, and the teaching is a light. The correction that comes from discipline is the way to life.
020	PRO	006	024	It will protect you from an evil woman and the seductive words of a prostitute.
020	PRO	006	025	Don't let your mind lust after her beauty, or let her hypnotize you with her fluttering eyelashes.
020	PRO	006	026	You can buy a prostitute for the price of a loaf of bread, but adultery with another man's wife can cost you your life.
020	PRO	006	027	Can you put fire in your lap and not burn your clothes?
020	PRO	006	028	Can you walk on hot coals and not scorch your feet?
020	PRO	006	029	It's the same for anyone who sleeps with another man's wife. No one who touches her will remain unpunished.
020	PRO	006	030	People don't condemn a thief if he steals to satisfy himself when he's hungry.
020	PRO	006	031	But if he's caught, he has to pay back seven times what he stole, even if it means handing over everything he has in his house.
020	PRO	006	032	Any man who commits adultery with a woman has no sense; he who does so destroys himself.
020	PRO	006	033	He will be wounded and dishonored. His disgrace will never be removed.
020	PRO	006	034	For jealousy makes a husband furious, and he won't hold back when he takes revenge.
020	PRO	006	035	He refuses any compensation, and won't be paid off, however big the amount.
020	PRO	007	001	My son, accept what I say and value my instructions.
020	PRO	007	002	Do what I tell you and you will live. Observe my teachings, valuing them as your main focus in life.
020	PRO	007	003	Tie them to your fingers; write them in your mind.
020	PRO	007	004	Tell wisdom, “You're my sister,” and call insight your best friend.
020	PRO	007	005	They will protect you from the immoral woman, from the prostitute with her seductive words.
020	PRO	007	006	One time I looked through the lattice of the window in my house,
020	PRO	007	007	and I saw among the immature young men one who had no sense at all.
020	PRO	007	008	He was walking down the street near the corner where she lived and took the road passing her house.
020	PRO	007	009	It was at dusk in the evening, as the light was fading and the dark night closed in.
020	PRO	007	010	Then out came a woman to meet him. She was dressed as a prostitute and had deceptive intentions.
020	PRO	007	011	(She was loud and provocative, never wanting to stay at home.
020	PRO	007	012	One moment she'd be walking the streets, the next she'd be there in the town squares, loitering at every corner.)
020	PRO	007	013	She grabbed hold of him and kissed him, and with a bold face she told him,
020	PRO	007	014	“I sacrificed my peace offering today, and paid my vows.
020	PRO	007	015	That's why I came out to meet you. I was looking for you and now I've found you!
020	PRO	007	016	My bed is made, covered with colorful linens from Egypt.
020	PRO	007	017	I've sprinkled perfume on my bed—myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
020	PRO	007	018	Come with me, let's make love until the morning. Let's enjoy one another in our love-making!
020	PRO	007	019	My husband isn't home; he's gone on a long trip.
020	PRO	007	020	He took a bag of money with him, and he won't be coming back until the full moon.”
020	PRO	007	021	She convinced him with all that she said; she seduced him with her smooth talking.
020	PRO	007	022	He followed her right away, like an ox to the slaughter. Like a stag that's caught in a snare
020	PRO	007	023	until an arrow pierces its liver, like a bird flying into a trap, he's unaware he will pay with his life.
020	PRO	007	024	So now listen to me, my sons, and pay attention to what I'm saying.
020	PRO	007	025	Don't even think about following her. Don't stray down her road.
020	PRO	007	026	For she has brought down and destroyed a lot of men; she's killed so many.
020	PRO	007	027	Her house leads to the grave—it goes down to the rooms of death.
020	PRO	008	001	Isn't wisdom calling? Isn't understanding raising her voice?
020	PRO	008	002	On the top of the hill by the road, she stands up at the crossroads.
020	PRO	008	003	Beside the gates of the town, right there at the entrance, she cries out:
020	PRO	008	004	“I'm calling out to you, everyone! My call is to everyone in the whole world!
020	PRO	008	005	If you're immature, learn how to grow up. If you're stupid, learn what makes good sense.
020	PRO	008	006	Listen to me because I have valuable things to explain to you.
020	PRO	008	007	I say what's right, because I tell the truth and I hate wickedness in all its forms.
020	PRO	008	008	All the words I say are true; none are false or misleading.
020	PRO	008	009	My words are straightforward to anyone with understanding; they are correct to those who have knowledge.
020	PRO	008	010	Choose my instruction over silver; choose knowledge over pure gold.
020	PRO	008	011	For wisdom is more valuable than rubies; everything you could ever want just doesn't compare!
020	PRO	008	012	I, wisdom, am at home with good decisions. I know how to find knowledge and discernment.
020	PRO	008	013	Honoring the Lord means hating evil. So I hate pride and arrogance, wicked behavior and telling lies.
020	PRO	008	014	I have advice and good judgment; I know what makes sense, and I have power.
020	PRO	008	015	It's because of me that kings reign, and rulers issue fair decrees.
020	PRO	008	016	It's because of me that leaders and nobles govern—all who rule justly.
020	PRO	008	017	I love those who love me, and those who really look for me will find me.
020	PRO	008	018	With me go riches and honor, lasting wealth and prosperity.
020	PRO	008	019	The fruit I produce is better than gold, even pure gold, and my harvest is better than even the best silver.
020	PRO	008	020	I live in a way that's right; I follow the paths of justice.
020	PRO	008	021	I grant wealth to those who love me; I fill their treasure storehouses.
020	PRO	008	022	The Lord created me first of all; I was made before anything else.
020	PRO	008	023	I was formed a long time ago, at the first, before the world began.
020	PRO	008	024	I was born when there were no ocean depths, when there were no springs pouring out water.
020	PRO	008	025	I was born before the mountains or the hills had been formed,
020	PRO	008	026	when he hadn't made the earth and its fields or any of the earth's dust.
020	PRO	008	027	I was there when he placed the heavens in position, when he drew the horizon over the ocean,
020	PRO	008	028	when he made the clouds in the sky above, when he created the springs of the oceans,
020	PRO	008	029	when he set limits on the sea so that the waters would not go farther than he ordered, and when he laid out the foundations of the earth.
020	PRO	008	030	Then I was beside him as a master craftsman. I made him happy every day, and I was always full of joy in his presence.
020	PRO	008	031	I was so happy in the world he created, celebrating together with human beings.
020	PRO	008	032	And now, my sons, listen to me, for happy are those who follow my ways.
020	PRO	008	033	Listen to my instruction and be wise—do not reject it.
020	PRO	008	034	Happy are those who listen to me, watching for me every day at my doors, waiting at my entrance way.
020	PRO	008	035	For those who find me, find life, and are accepted by the Lord.
020	PRO	008	036	But those who don't find me hurt themselves; everyone who hates me loves death.”
020	PRO	009	001	Wisdom has built her house; she has prepared its seven pillars.
020	PRO	009	002	She has slaughtered her animals for meat; she has mixed her wine; and she has set her table.
020	PRO	009	003	She has sent out her servant girls with invitations. She calls out from the highest places of the town,
020	PRO	009	004	“Everybody who needs to learn, come and see me!” To people who don't have any sense she says,
020	PRO	009	005	“Come, eat my food, and drink the wine I have mixed.
020	PRO	009	006	Leave your foolish ways and you will live; follow the path that makes sense.”
020	PRO	009	007	If you correct a mocker all you get are insults; if you argue with the wicked all you get is abuse.
020	PRO	009	008	So don't argue with mockers or they'll only hate you; argue with the wise and they'll love you.
020	PRO	009	009	Educate the wise and they'll become even wiser; teach those who live right and they will increase their learning.
020	PRO	009	010	Honoring the Lord is the beginning of wisdom; knowledge of the Holy One brings insight.
020	PRO	009	011	Through wisdom you'll have many more days, increasing the years of your life.
020	PRO	009	012	If you are wise, you are the one to profit from it; if you scoff, you alone will have to suffer the consequences.
020	PRO	009	013	Stupidity is like a loud, ignorant woman who doesn't know anything.
020	PRO	009	014	She sits at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the town,
020	PRO	009	015	calling out to those passing by, going about their business,
020	PRO	009	016	“Everybody who needs to learn, come and see me!” To people who don't have any sense she says,
020	PRO	009	017	“Stolen water is sweet, and food eaten in secret tastes good!”
020	PRO	009	018	But they don't know that the dead are there, that those she's invited are in the depths of the grave.
020	PRO	010	001	Solomon's proverbs. A wise son makes his father happy, but a stupid son only brings his mother grief.
020	PRO	010	002	Wealth gained through evil does you no good; but living right saves you from death.
020	PRO	010	003	The Lord doesn't let good people go hungry, but he stops the wicked from getting what they want.
020	PRO	010	004	Lazy hands make you poor, but hard-working hands make you rich.
020	PRO	010	005	A son who gathers crops during the summer is sensible, but the one who sleeps during harvest brings disgrace.
020	PRO	010	006	Those who are good are blessed, but what the wicked say hides their violent nature.
020	PRO	010	007	The good are remembered as a blessing, but the reputation of the wicked will rot.
020	PRO	010	008	Those who think wisely pay attention to instruction, but a stupid chatterbox ends up in disaster.
020	PRO	010	009	Honest people will live in safety, but those who behave deceitfully will be caught out.
020	PRO	010	010	People who wink slyly cause trouble, but someone who gives a strong rebuke brings peace.
020	PRO	010	011	What good people say is a spring that gives life, but what the wicked say hides their violent nature.
020	PRO	010	012	Hatred causes conflict, but love covers all wrongs.
020	PRO	010	013	Wisdom comes from people with good judgment, but stupid people are punished with a rod.
020	PRO	010	014	Wise people accumulate knowledge, but the chattering of stupid people is a prelude to disaster.
020	PRO	010	015	The wealth of the rich provides them protection, while the poverty of the poor ruins them.
020	PRO	010	016	If you do right you're rewarded with life, but if you're wicked all you gain is sin.
020	PRO	010	017	If you accept instruction, you're on the path to life, but if you reject correction you'll go astray.
020	PRO	010	018	Anyone who hides their hatred is lying, and anyone who spreads slander is stupid.
020	PRO	010	019	If you talk too much, you'll say something wrong. Be wise and take care what you say.
020	PRO	010	020	What good people say is like the best silver, but the mind of the wicked isn't worth much.
020	PRO	010	021	Advice from good people helps feed many others, but stupid people die because they have no sense.
020	PRO	010	022	The Lord's blessing makes you rich, and he doesn't add any sadness to accompany it.
020	PRO	010	023	Stupid people think it's fun to do wrong, but someone who has wisdom understands what's right.
020	PRO	010	024	What the wicked fear will happen to them, while what good people hope for will be granted.
020	PRO	010	025	When the storm hits, the wicked are no more, but the good are safe and secure forever.
020	PRO	010	026	In the same way vinegar irritates the teeth and smoke irritates the eyes, lazy people irritate their employers.
020	PRO	010	027	Honoring the Lord makes your life longer, but the years the wicked live will be cut short.
020	PRO	010	028	Good people look forward to happiness, but the hopes of the wicked come to nothing.
020	PRO	010	029	The way of the Lord protects those who do right, but he destroys those who do evil.
020	PRO	010	030	The good will never be removed from the land, but the wicked will not remain there.
020	PRO	010	031	What good people say produces wisdom, but liars will have their tongues cut out.
020	PRO	010	032	Good people know the right thing to say, but the wicked always lie.
020	PRO	011	001	The Lord hates dishonest scales, but accurate weights please him.
020	PRO	011	002	With pride comes disgrace, but with humility comes wisdom.
020	PRO	011	003	Honesty guides the good, but deceit destroys liars.
020	PRO	011	004	Wealth won't help you on judgment day, but goodness saves you from death.
020	PRO	011	005	The goodness of the innocent keeps them on track, but the wicked fall by their own wickedness.
020	PRO	011	006	The goodness of those who live right will save them, but the dishonest are trapped by their own desires.
020	PRO	011	007	When a wicked person dies, their hopes die with them; what the godless look forward to is gone.
020	PRO	011	008	The good are saved from trouble, while the wicked get into trouble.
020	PRO	011	009	Godless people mouth off and destroy their neighbors, but the good are saved by wisdom.
020	PRO	011	010	The whole town celebrates when good people are successful; they also shout for joy when the wicked die.
020	PRO	011	011	Ethical people are a blessing to a town, but what the wicked say destroys it.
020	PRO	011	012	People who run down their neighbors have no sense; someone who's sensible keeps quiet.
020	PRO	011	013	A gossip goes around telling secrets, but trustworthy people keep confidences.
020	PRO	011	014	A nation falls without good guidance, but they are saved through much wise counsel.
020	PRO	011	015	You'll get into trouble if you guarantee a stranger's loans—you're far safer if you refuse to make such pledges.
020	PRO	011	016	A gracious woman holds on to her honor just as ruthless men hold on to their wealth.
020	PRO	011	017	If you're kind, you'll be rewarded; but if you're cruel, you'll hurt yourself.
020	PRO	011	018	The wicked earn wages that cheat them, but those who sow goodness reap a genuine reward.
020	PRO	011	019	Do what's right, and you will live; chase after evil and you will die.
020	PRO	011	020	The Lord hates perverted minds, but is happy with those who live moral lives.
020	PRO	011	021	You can be certain of this: the wicked won't go unpunished, but the good will be saved.
020	PRO	011	022	A beautiful woman who lacks good judgment is like a gold ring in a pig's snout.
020	PRO	011	023	Good people want what's best, but what the wicked hope for ends in death.
020	PRO	011	024	If you give generously you receive more, but if you keep back what you should give, you end up poor.
020	PRO	011	025	If you're generous, you'll become rich; give someone a drink of water, and you'll be given one in return.
020	PRO	011	026	People curse those who hoard grain; but they bless those who sell.
020	PRO	011	027	If you look to do good, you'll be appreciated; but if you look for evil, you'll find it!
020	PRO	011	028	If you trust in your riches, you'll fall; but if you do good, you'll flourish like green leaves.
020	PRO	011	029	If you cause trouble in your family, you'll inherit nothing but air. Stupid people end up as servants to those who think wisely.
020	PRO	011	030	The fruit of the good is a tree of life, and the wise person saves people.
020	PRO	011	031	If the good are repaid here on earth, how much more will the wicked who sin be repaid!
020	PRO	012	001	If you love knowledge, you will love discipline. Anyone who hates being corrected is stupid!
020	PRO	012	002	The Lord blesses the good, but he condemns anyone with evil schemes.
020	PRO	012	003	Wickedness doesn't provide security, but those who live right are deeply rooted and cannot be moved.
020	PRO	012	004	A good wife is a crown for her husband, but one who brings shame is like rot in his bones.
020	PRO	012	005	Good people make plans that are fair, but the advice of the wicked is deceptive.
020	PRO	012	006	The words of the wicked are like a violent ambush, but those of honest people save them.
020	PRO	012	007	The wicked are destroyed, and they're gone, but the family of the good stands firm.
020	PRO	012	008	People are appreciated for talking sense, but those with perverted minds are despised.
020	PRO	012	009	Better to be a humble man serving himself than a boastful man who has nothing to eat.
020	PRO	012	010	Good people look after their animals, but the care given by wicked is really cruelty.
020	PRO	012	011	If you cultivate the land you'll have plenty of food, but if you chase after worthless things you're stupid.
020	PRO	012	012	Wicked people long for ill-gotten gains, but good people are productive themselves.
020	PRO	012	013	The wicked trap themselves by their own sinful words, but good people escape trouble.
020	PRO	012	014	What you say brings you rewards, and your work returns to bless you.
020	PRO	012	015	Stupid people think they're on the right track, but if you're wise you listen to advice.
020	PRO	012	016	Stupid people get angry immediately, but if you're sensible you ignore an insult.
020	PRO	012	017	Whoever tells the truth is being honest, but a false witness tells lies.
020	PRO	012	018	Some people's hasty words cut like a knife, but the words of the wise bring healing.
020	PRO	012	019	Words of truth last forever, but lies are gone in a moment.
020	PRO	012	020	Deceit is in the mind of those planning evil, but those who plan peace have joy.
020	PRO	012	021	No harm comes to the good, but trouble fills the wicked.
020	PRO	012	022	The Lord hates liars but is happy with those who are trustworthy.
020	PRO	012	023	If you're sensible, you don't show off your knowledge, but stupid people announce their stupidity.
020	PRO	012	024	Hard work brings leadership, but laziness brings slavery.
020	PRO	012	025	If you're anxious, you're weighed down, but an encouraging word will cheer you up.
020	PRO	012	026	Good people look out for their friends, but the way the wicked live leads them astray.
020	PRO	012	027	Lazy people don't catch their prey, but if you work hard you can become rich.
020	PRO	012	028	The path of right leads to life, it doesn't lead to death.
020	PRO	013	001	A wise son accepts his father's discipline, but a mocker doesn't listen to correction.
020	PRO	013	002	You'll be rewarded for saying good things, but dishonest people want violence.
020	PRO	013	003	Watch what you say and save your life—saying too much leads to disaster.
020	PRO	013	004	Lazy people want a lot, but get nothing; if you work hard you'll be well rewarded.
020	PRO	013	005	Good people hate lies, but the wicked cause a stink and bring disgrace.
020	PRO	013	006	Goodness protects those who live right, but sin overcomes the wicked.
020	PRO	013	007	Some pretend to be rich, but don't have anything, while others pretend to be poor and are very rich.
020	PRO	013	008	The rich can pay a ransom to save their lives, but the poor aren't troubled in this way.
020	PRO	013	009	The life of good people shines brightly, but the lamp of the wicked will be snuffed out.
020	PRO	013	010	Pride only causes conflict; but those who take advice are wise.
020	PRO	013	011	Wealth gained by fraud quickly disappears, but those who gather bit by bit prosper.
020	PRO	013	012	Hope that's delayed makes you feel sick, but a wish that comes true revives you.
020	PRO	013	013	If you despise words of advice, you'll pay for it; but if you respect what you're told, you'll be rewarded.
020	PRO	013	014	The teaching of the wise is like a fountain of life, so you can avoid the snares of death.
020	PRO	013	015	Good sense earns appreciation, but the way of the unfaithful is hard.
020	PRO	013	016	All wise people act intelligently, but stupid people demonstrate their stupidity.
020	PRO	013	017	A bad messenger creates trouble, but a faithful representative brings healing.
020	PRO	013	018	Poverty and disgrace come to those who ignore instruction, but those who accept correction are honored.
020	PRO	013	019	It's nice to see a wish come true, but stupid people hate to turn away from evil to achieve this.
020	PRO	013	020	Being friends with wise people will make you wise, but being friends with stupid people will only cause you problems.
020	PRO	013	021	Tragedy chases after the sinner, but prosperity rewards the good.
020	PRO	013	022	Good people leave an inheritance to their grandchildren, but the sinner's wealth is saved for those who live right.
020	PRO	013	023	The unplowed ground of the poor could produce a lot of food, but it's stolen through injustice.
020	PRO	013	024	People who don't discipline their children hate them. Those who love their children carefully discipline them.
020	PRO	013	025	The good eat until they're full; but the belly of the wicked is empty.
020	PRO	014	001	Every wise woman builds her house, but the stupid woman tears it down with her own hands.
020	PRO	014	002	Those who live right respect the Lord, but those who live dishonestly despise him.
020	PRO	014	003	What stupid people say punishes their pride, but what wise people say will protect them.
020	PRO	014	004	Without oxen, the manger is empty, but a good harvest comes through the ox's strength.
020	PRO	014	005	A trustworthy witness doesn't lie, but a false witness is deceptive.
020	PRO	014	006	It's pointless for a scoffer to look for wisdom, but knowledge comes easily to someone who understands.
020	PRO	014	007	Stay away from stupid people—you won't learn anything from them.
020	PRO	014	008	Sensible people use their wisdom to decide where they're going, but the foolishness of stupid people is treacherous.
020	PRO	014	009	Stupid people laugh at sin, but good people want forgiveness.
020	PRO	014	010	The mind alone knows its sadness, and no one else can share its happiness.
020	PRO	014	011	The house of wicked people will be destroyed, but the tent of good people will prosper.
020	PRO	014	012	There's a way that seems to be right, but in the end it's the way of death.
020	PRO	014	013	Even when you're laughing you can be feeling sad—joy can end in grief.
020	PRO	014	014	Disloyal people are repaid for what they do, and good people are rewarded.
020	PRO	014	015	Stupid people believe whatever they're told, but sensible people think about what they're doing.
020	PRO	014	016	Wise people are careful and avoid evil, but stupid people are confidently reckless.
020	PRO	014	017	Quick-tempered people act foolishly, while people who make evil plans are hated.
020	PRO	014	018	The inheritance of stupid people is stupidity, but sensible people are rewarded with knowledge.
020	PRO	014	019	Evil people bow down before good people, and the wicked bow down at the doors of those who do right.
020	PRO	014	020	The poor are hated even by their neighbors, while the rich have many friends.
020	PRO	014	021	People who look down on their neighbors are sinners, but those who are kind to the poor are blessed.
020	PRO	014	022	Aren't people who plan to do evil wrong? But those who plan to do good have trustworthy love and faithfulness.
020	PRO	014	023	There's profit in hard work, but just talking leads to poverty.
020	PRO	014	024	The wise are rewarded with wealth, but stupid people are rewarded with stupidity.
020	PRO	014	025	A truthful witness saves lives, but a false witness is treacherous.
020	PRO	014	026	People who honor the Lord are completely safe; he will protect their children.
020	PRO	014	027	Respecting the Lord is like a fountain of life, so you can avoid the snares of death.
020	PRO	014	028	The glory of a king is the number of his subjects, for a ruler is nothing without them.
020	PRO	014	029	If you're slow to get angry, you're very wise; but if you have a short fuse you glorify stupidity.
020	PRO	014	030	A peaceful mind makes your body healthy, but jealousy makes your bones rot.
020	PRO	014	031	Anyone who oppresses the poor insults their Maker, but anyone who is kind to the needy honors him.
020	PRO	014	032	Wicked people are brought down by their own evil actions, but those who live right are confident even in death.
020	PRO	014	033	Wisdom is at home in a mind that understands, but it's not found among stupid people.
020	PRO	014	034	Doing right makes a nation successful, but sin is a disgrace to any people.
020	PRO	014	035	A servant who acts wisely is appreciated by the king, but he gets angry with a servant who acts disgracefully.
020	PRO	015	001	A kind reply wards off anger, but hurtful words make people mad.
020	PRO	015	002	What wise people say makes knowledge attractive, but stupid people talk a lot of nonsense.
020	PRO	015	003	The Lord sees everywhere, watching the evil and the good.
020	PRO	015	004	Gentle words are a source of life, but telling lies does a lot of damage.
020	PRO	015	005	Only a foolish son despises his father's instruction, but one who accepts correction is sensible.
020	PRO	015	006	There's plenty of treasure where good people live, but the income of the wicked brings them trouble.
020	PRO	015	007	Wise people share their knowledge, but stupid people don't think like that.
