020	PRO	024	028	Don't testify against your neighbors without having a good reason, and don't tell lies.
020	PRO	024	029	Don't say to yourself, “I'm going to do to him what he did to me! I'll pay him back for what he's done!”
020	PRO	024	030	I walked past the field of a lazy man, past a vineyard of someone with no sense.
020	PRO	024	031	It was all overgrown with thorns, the ground was covered with weeds, and the stone wall had fallen down.
020	PRO	024	032	As I looked I thought about it, and what I saw taught me a lesson:
020	PRO	024	033	You may say, “Please, just a little more sleep, a little longer snooze, a little more folding of the arms to rest”—
020	PRO	024	034	and poverty will attack you like a robber, destitution like an armed warrior.
020	PRO	025	001	These are more proverbs of Solomon, collected by the scribes of Hezekiah, king of Judah.
020	PRO	025	002	God's greatness is in doing things that can't be known, while the greatness of kings is in revealing things.
020	PRO	025	003	Just as the height of the heavens or the depth of the earth can't be known, the king's thinking can't be known.
020	PRO	025	004	Remove the waste from the silver, and the silversmith has pure silver to work with.
020	PRO	025	005	Remove the wicked from the king's presence and the king will rule securely and justly.
020	PRO	025	006	Don't try to make yourself look great before the king, and don't pretend to be among the important people,
020	PRO	025	007	for it's better to be told, “Come up here,” than to be humiliated before a nobleman. Even though you've seen something with your own eyes,
020	PRO	025	008	don't rush to take legal action, for what are you going to do in the end when your neighbor shows you're wrong and humiliates you?
020	PRO	025	009	Discuss the case with your neighbor himself, and don't betray someone else's secret,
020	PRO	025	010	otherwise whoever hears it will make you ashamed and you'll never lose your bad reputation.
020	PRO	025	011	Advice given at the right time is like golden apples set in silver.
020	PRO	025	012	Constructive criticism from the wise to someone who listens is like a gold ring and a necklace of fine gold.
020	PRO	025	013	Faithful messengers are as refreshing to their master as cold snow on a hot harvest day.
020	PRO	025	014	Someone who boasts about a gift they never give is like cloud and wind without rain.
020	PRO	025	015	If you're patient you can persuade your superior, and soft words can break down opposition.
020	PRO	025	016	If you find honey, eat just enough, for if you eat too much, you'll be sick.
020	PRO	025	017	Don't set foot in your neighbors' homes too often, otherwise they'll get fed up with you and hate you.
020	PRO	025	018	Telling lies in court against a friend is like attacking them with a mace, or a sword, or an arrow.
020	PRO	025	019	Trusting in unreliable people in times of trouble is like eating with a broken tooth or walking on a bad foot.
020	PRO	025	020	Singing happy songs to someone who's broken-hearted is like taking off your coat on a cold day, or pouring vinegar onto an open wound.
020	PRO	025	021	If your enemy is hungry, give him something to eat; if he's thirsty, give him a drink of water.
020	PRO	025	022	This will make him ashamed as if he had burning coals piled on his head, and the Lord will reward you.
020	PRO	025	023	In the same way that the north wind brings rain, slandering people makes them angry.
020	PRO	025	024	It's better to live in a corner of a housetop than to share a whole house with an argumentative wife.
020	PRO	025	025	Good news from a distant country is like cold water to an exhausted traveler.
020	PRO	025	026	Good people who give in to the wicked are like a muddied spring or a polluted well.
020	PRO	025	027	It's not good to eat too much honey, or to want too much praise.
020	PRO	025	028	Someone without control is as exposed as a town whose walls have been breached.
020	PRO	026	001	Honoring someone stupid is as inappropriate as snow in the summer or rain during harvest.
020	PRO	026	002	A curse that isn't deserved won't land on the person, like a fluttering sparrow or a flitting swallow.
020	PRO	026	003	Horses need a whip, donkeys need a bridle, and stupid people need a rod on their backs!
020	PRO	026	004	Don't answer stupid people following their stupidity, or you'll become as bad as them.
020	PRO	026	005	Answer stupid people following their stupidity, otherwise they'll think they're wise.
020	PRO	026	006	Trusting someone stupid to deliver a message is like cutting off your feet or drinking poison.
020	PRO	026	007	A proverb spoken by someone stupid is as useless as a lame person's legs.
020	PRO	026	008	Honoring someone stupid is as pointless as tying a stone into a sling.
020	PRO	026	009	A proverb spoken by someone stupid is as ridiculous as a thorn bush waved around by a drunk.
020	PRO	026	010	Anyone who hires someone stupid or just a passer-by is like an archer wounding people by shooting arrows at random.
020	PRO	026	011	Stupid people repeat their stupidity like a dog returning to its vomit.
020	PRO	026	012	Have you seen a man who is wise in his own eyes? There's more hope for stupid people than for him!
020	PRO	026	013	Lazy people are the ones who say, “There's a lion on the road—a lion running around the streets!”
020	PRO	026	014	A lazy person turns in bed like a door turns on its hinge.
020	PRO	026	015	Lazy people put their hands in a dish, but are too tired to lift the food to their mouths.
020	PRO	026	016	In their own eyes lazy people are wiser than many sensible advisors.
020	PRO	026	017	Interfering in someone else's quarrel is like grabbing a stray dog by the ears.
020	PRO	026	018	You're like a crazy person firing off blazing arrows and killing people
020	PRO	026	019	if you lie to your friend and then say, “I was only joking!”
020	PRO	026	020	Without wood, the fire goes out; and without gossips, arguments stop.
020	PRO	026	021	An argumentative person fires up quarrels like putting charcoal on hot embers or wood on a fire.
020	PRO	026	022	Listening to gossip is like gulping down bites of your favorite food—they go deep down inside you.
020	PRO	026	023	Smooth talking with evil intent is like a shiny lead glaze on an earthenware pot.
020	PRO	026	024	People say nice things to you even though they hate you; deep down they're just lying to you.
020	PRO	026	025	When people talk nicely to you, don't believe them—their minds are full of hate for you.
020	PRO	026	026	Even though their hatred may be hidden by cunning tricks, their evil will be revealed to everyone.
020	PRO	026	027	Those who dig pits to trap others will fall in themselves, and those who start boulders rolling will be crushed themselves.
020	PRO	026	028	If you tell lies, you show you hate your victims; if you flatter people, you cause disaster.
020	PRO	027	001	Don't boast about what you're going to do tomorrow, because you don't know what the day may bring.
020	PRO	027	002	Let others praise you, not you yourself; someone else, not you personally.
020	PRO	027	003	Stone may be heavy, and sand may weigh a lot, but the annoyance caused by stupid people is the biggest burden of all.
020	PRO	027	004	Fury may be fierce and cruel, anger may be a destructive flood, but who can withstand jealousy?
020	PRO	027	005	Open criticism is better than hidden love.
020	PRO	027	006	A friend's honest comments may hurt you, but an enemy's kisses are over the top.
020	PRO	027	007	If you're full up, you can't face honey; but if you're starving, even bitter food tastes sweet.
020	PRO	027	008	Having to leave home is like a bird having to leave its nest.
020	PRO	027	009	Perfume and scented oils make you feel happy, but good advice from a friend is even better.
020	PRO	027	010	Don't give up on your friends or your family's friends. Don't go to a relative's house when you've got trouble. A friend nearby is more useful than a relative far away.
020	PRO	027	011	My son, make me happy by being wise, so I can respond to anyone who criticizes me.
020	PRO	027	012	If you're sensible you see danger coming and get out of the way; but stupid people just keep going and suffer the consequences.
020	PRO	027	013	If someone guarantees a stranger's debt with their cloak, be sure to take it! Make sure you have whatever is pledged to an immoral woman!
020	PRO	027	014	If when you get up every morning you shout a loud hello to your neighbors, they will see that as a curse!
020	PRO	027	015	An argumentative wife is as irritating as constant dripping on a rainy day.
020	PRO	027	016	Trying to stop her is like trying to make the wind stop or trying to hold olive oil in your hand.
020	PRO	027	017	An iron blade is sharpened with an iron tool, and one person's mind is sharpened by another's.
020	PRO	027	018	Those who care for a fig tree eat its fruit, and those who care for their master are rewarded.
020	PRO	027	019	Just as water reflects your face, your mind reflects who you really are.
020	PRO	027	020	In the same way that the grave and destruction are never satisfied, human desire is never satisfied.
020	PRO	027	021	Just as a crucible tests silver, and a furnace tests gold, people are tested by the praise they receive.
020	PRO	027	022	Even if you ground stupid people in a mortar, crushing them like grain with the pestle, you can't get rid of stupidity from them.
020	PRO	027	023	You should know the condition of your flocks really well and take good care of your herds,
020	PRO	027	024	for wealth doesn't last forever—is a crown passed down through all generations?
020	PRO	027	025	Once the hay is cut, and the new growth begins, and fodder from the mountains is gathered,
020	PRO	027	026	and the lambs have provided you wool to make clothing, and the sale of goats have paid for a field,
020	PRO	027	027	there'll be enough milk from your goats to feed you, your family, and your servant girls.
020	PRO	028	001	The wicked run away even when no one is chasing them, but the good have the trusting boldness of lions.
020	PRO	028	002	When a country is in rebellion, it has many rulers, but a ruler who is wise and knowledgeable provides strength and continuity.
020	PRO	028	003	When someone poor oppresses the poor, it's like heavy rain that beats down the crops.
020	PRO	028	004	People who reject the law praise the wicked, but those who keep the law fight against them.
020	PRO	028	005	Evil people understand nothing about justice, but those who follow the Lord understand it completely.
020	PRO	028	006	Better to be poor and have integrity than to be devious and rich.
020	PRO	028	007	If you keep the law, you're a wise son, but if you keep bad company you shame your father.
020	PRO	028	008	Anyone who gets rich through charging interest and profiteering is only storing it up for someone who is kind to the poor.
020	PRO	028	009	God hates the prayers of people who disregard the law.
020	PRO	028	010	Those who lead good people astray into evil ways will fall into their own traps, but the innocent will receive a good reward.
020	PRO	028	011	The rich see themselves as wise, but poor people with insight see right through them.
020	PRO	028	012	When good people win, everyone celebrates, but when the wicked come to power, people hide.
020	PRO	028	013	People who hide their sins won't succeed, but those who confess and renounce their sins will be shown kindness.
020	PRO	028	014	Blessed are those who always respect the Lord, but those who are stubborn end up in a lot of trouble.
020	PRO	028	015	A wicked ruler lording it over poor people is like a roaring lion or a charging bear.
020	PRO	028	016	An unwise ruler thoroughly extorts his people, but one who refuses to profit illegally will live long.
020	PRO	028	017	Someone guilty of murder will go on running away from it until they die. Don't try and stop them.
020	PRO	028	018	If you have integrity, you'll be kept safe, but if you live deviously, you'll fall.
020	PRO	028	019	If you cultivate the land you'll have plenty of food, but if you chase fantasies you'll end up with nothing.
020	PRO	028	020	If you're trustworthy, you'll be richly rewarded; but if you try to get rich quick, you won't go unpunished.
020	PRO	028	021	Showing favoritism isn't good, but some people will do wrong just for a piece of bread.
020	PRO	028	022	Envious people are in a rush to get rich; they don't realize they'll end up poor.
020	PRO	028	023	Honest criticism is appreciated later far more than flattery.
020	PRO	028	024	A man who robs his father and mother, and says, “It's not a crime,” is one step away from becoming a murderer.
020	PRO	028	025	Greedy people stir up trouble, but those who trust in the Lord will be successful.
020	PRO	028	026	People who trust their own minds are foolish, but those who follow wise ways will be kept safe.
020	PRO	028	027	If you give to the poor, you won't be in need; but if you look the other way, you'll have many curses.
020	PRO	028	028	When the wicked come to power, people hide; but when they fall, the good do well.
020	PRO	029	001	Anyone who goes on stubbornly rejecting many warnings will be suddenly destroyed, without hope of healing.
020	PRO	029	002	When good people are in charge, everybody celebrates; but when the wicked rule, everybody groans.
020	PRO	029	003	A man who loves wisdom makes his father happy, but one who visits prostitutes throws away his money.
020	PRO	029	004	A king who rules justly makes the country secure, but one who asks for bribes will destroy it.
020	PRO	029	005	Those who flatter their friends lay a net to trip them up.
020	PRO	029	006	Evil people are trapped by their own sins, but those who do right sing and celebrate.
020	PRO	029	007	Good people care about treating the poor fairly, but the wicked don't think about it at all.
020	PRO	029	008	Cynical people can inflame a whole city, but the wise calm angry people down.
020	PRO	029	009	When a wise man takes a stupid man to court, there's raging and ridicule, but nothing is settled.
020	PRO	029	010	Murderers hate people of integrity, but those who live right try to help them.
020	PRO	029	011	Stupid people let all their anger out, while wise people quietly hold it in.
020	PRO	029	012	A ruler who listens to lies will have nothing but wicked officials.
020	PRO	029	013	Poor people and their oppressors have this in common: the Lord gives life to all of them.
020	PRO	029	014	If a king judges the poor fairly, he will have a long rule.
020	PRO	029	015	Discipline and correction provide wisdom, but a son left undisciplined is an embarrassment to his mother.
020	PRO	029	016	When the wicked are in power, sin increases; but the good will see their downfall.
020	PRO	029	017	Discipline your children and they won't give you any worries; they will make you very happy.
020	PRO	029	018	Without a revelation from God, the people go out of control, but those who keep the law are happy.
020	PRO	029	019	A servant can't be disciplined by words alone; though they understand, they don't follow what they're told.
020	PRO	029	020	Have you seen a man who speaks without thinking? There's more hope for stupid people than for him!
020	PRO	029	021	A servant indulged from childhood will in the end become unmanageable.
020	PRO	029	022	Angry people stir up trouble, those with short tempers commit many sins.
020	PRO	029	023	If you're proud, you'll be humiliated; but if you're humble, you'll be honored.
020	PRO	029	024	A thief's partner hates his life; even under the threat of being cursed he can't tell the truth.
020	PRO	029	025	Being afraid of people traps you, but if you trust in the Lord you're safe.
020	PRO	029	026	Many people look for favors from a ruler, but justice comes from the Lord.
020	PRO	029	027	Good people hate those who are unjust; the wicked hate those who do what's right.
020	PRO	030	001	These are the words of Agur, son of Jakeh. An oracle. This is what the man says, God, I'm really tired, I'm worn out.
020	PRO	030	002	I'm so stupid I'm not really a man; I can't even think like a human being.
020	PRO	030	003	I have not learned wisdom; I have no knowledge of the Holy One.
020	PRO	030	004	Who has gone up to heaven, and come down? Who holds the winds in the palm of his hands? Who has wrapped up the waters in his cloak? Who has set the earth's boundaries? What is his name, and what is his son's name? Are you sure you don't know?
020	PRO	030	005	Every word God says has been proved true. He defends everyone who comes to him for protection.
020	PRO	030	006	Don't add anything to his words, or he will criticize you and you'll be shown to be a liar.
020	PRO	030	007	God, I want to request two things from you. Please don't refuse to let me have them before I come to die.
020	PRO	030	008	Keep me from being false, help me not to tell lies. Don't make me poor or rich; just provide me with the food I need.
020	PRO	030	009	Otherwise if I have plenty of money, I may give up on you, saying, “Who is the Lord?” while if I'm poor I may steal and bring the name of my God into disrepute.
020	PRO	030	010	Don't slander a servant to his master, or he will curse you and you'll suffer for it.
020	PRO	030	011	There are some who curse their fathers and do not bless their mothers.
020	PRO	030	012	There are some who see themselves as pure but they're still filthy—they have not been washed.
020	PRO	030	013	There are some who think themselves so high and mighty, and who look down on others.
020	PRO	030	014	There are some who have teeth like swords, incisors like knives, ready to devour the poor from the earth, the needy from society.
020	PRO	030	015	The leech has two daughters who cry out, “Give me! Give me!” There are three things that are never satisfied, four that never say, “Enough!”:
020	PRO	030	016	The grave, the womb that doesn't become pregnant, the earth thirsty for water, and the fire that never says, “Enough!”
020	PRO	030	017	People who ridicule their fathers and despise obedience to the mother will have their eyes pecked out by wild ravens and eaten by young vultures.
020	PRO	030	018	These three things are amazingly hard for me, four things I just can't understand:
020	PRO	030	019	The way an eagle soars in the sky, the way a snake slides over a rock, the way a ship sails across the sea, the way a man and a woman fall in love.
020	PRO	030	020	This is the way of a woman who commits adultery: she eats, she wipes her mouth, and then says, “I haven't done anything wrong!”
020	PRO	030	021	Three things make the earth tremble, there are four things it can't support:
020	PRO	030	022	a slave becoming a king, a stupid person eating like a pig,
020	PRO	030	023	an unbearable woman getting married, and a maidservant taking her mistress's place.
020	PRO	030	024	There are four things on earth that are small, but very wise:
020	PRO	030	025	Ants—they're not strong, but they work hard all summer storing up food.
020	PRO	030	026	Hyraxes—they don't have much power, but they make their homes in the rock.
020	PRO	030	027	Locusts—they don't have a king, but they all march in line abreast.
020	PRO	030	028	Lizards—you can catch them in your hands, but they live in the king's palace.
020	PRO	030	029	There are three things that are glorious to watch as they walk, four that look dignified as they move:
020	PRO	030	030	The lion, supreme among wild animals, who isn't frightened of anything.
020	PRO	030	031	The strutting starling, the male goat, and a king with his army.
020	PRO	030	032	If you have been foolishly boasting about yourself, or if you've been planning to do something wrong, stop and put your hand over your mouth.
020	PRO	030	033	Just as churning milk produces butter, and twisting someone's nose makes it bleed, so stirring up anger causes arguments.
020	PRO	031	001	These are the words of King Lemuel, an oracle, taught to him by his mother.
020	PRO	031	002	What shall I tell you, my son?—the son I gave birth to, the son given in response to my vows.
020	PRO	031	003	Don't waste your strength sleeping with women, those that bring down kings.
020	PRO	031	004	Lemuel, kings shouldn't be drinking wine, rulers shouldn't be drinking alcohol.
020	PRO	031	005	For if they drink, they'll forget what the law says, and pervert the rights of those who are suffering.
020	PRO	031	006	Give alcohol to those who are dying, and wine to those who are in terrible distress.
020	PRO	031	007	Let them drink so they can forget their poverty, and not remember their troubles any longer.
020	PRO	031	008	Speak up for those who have no voice, for the rights of those marginalized by society.
020	PRO	031	009	Speak up and judge fairly; defend the poor and destitute.
020	PRO	031	010	Who can find a strong, capable wife? She's worth more than jewels!
020	PRO	031	011	Her husband has complete confidence in her, and with her he'll never be poor.
020	PRO	031	012	She brings him good, not evil, all her life.
020	PRO	031	013	She gets wool and flax, and with her eager hands turns them into clothes.
020	PRO	031	014	Like a merchant's ship, she brings food from far away.
020	PRO	031	015	She gets up while it's still dark to make breakfast for her family, and to plan what her servant girls need to do.
020	PRO	031	016	She looks at a field, and decides to buy it; from the money she's earned she buys a vineyard.
020	PRO	031	017	She's keen to get ready, and works hard with her strong arms.
020	PRO	031	018	She knows that the things she makes are valuable. She keeps busy—her lamp burns late into the night.
020	PRO	031	019	She spins the thread and weaves the cloth.
020	PRO	031	020	She's generous to the poor, and gives help to the needy.
020	PRO	031	021	She doesn't worry if it snows, because her whole family has warm clothing.
020	PRO	031	022	She makes herself bedspreads; she dresses in fine linen and purple clothes.
020	PRO	031	023	Her husband is well-respected in the council at the town gates, where he sits with the town elders.
020	PRO	031	024	She makes linen clothes for sale, and supplies merchants with belts.
020	PRO	031	025	She's clothed with strength and dignity, and she is happy about the future.
020	PRO	031	026	She speaks wise words, and she's kind when she gives instructions.
020	PRO	031	027	She looks after the needs of her whole household, and she's never idle.
020	PRO	031	028	Her children are quick to bless her. Her husband praises her too, saying,
020	PRO	031	029	“Many women do great things, but you are better than all of them!”
020	PRO	031	030	Charm can deceive, and beauty fades, but a woman who honors the Lord should be praised.
