# BOOK	022	SOL	Song of Solomon	Song of Solomon
022	SOL	001	001	Solomon's song of songs.
022	SOL	001	002	Kiss me, kiss me with your mouth again and again, for your love is sweeter than wine.
022	SOL	001	003	I love the way you smell from the perfumed oils you use. You have quite a reputation—it spreads like spilled perfumed oil. It's not surprising that all the young women adore you!
022	SOL	001	004	Take me by the hand—let's run! (The king has brought me to his bedroom.) Let's be happy together and find pleasure in your love. Your love is far better than wine! Women are right to adore you so!
022	SOL	001	005	I'm black, but I'm beautiful, women of Jerusalem, like the tents of Kedar, like the curtains of Solomon.
022	SOL	001	006	Don't look down on me because I'm black, because the sun has burned me. My brothers were angry with me and made me look after the vineyards, so I couldn't look after my own vineyard.
022	SOL	001	007	My love, please tell me where you're taking your flock. Where will you rest them at noon? For why should I have to wear a veil while looking for you among the flocks of your companions?
022	SOL	001	008	If you really don't know, you who are more beautiful than any other woman, then follow the tracks of my flock, and let your goats graze near the shepherd's tents.
022	SOL	001	009	My darling, to me you're like a mare among Pharaoh's horses that pull his chariots,
022	SOL	001	010	Your beautiful cheeks adorned with ornaments, your neck with strings of jewels.
022	SOL	001	011	Let's make you some gold ornaments inlaid with silver.
022	SOL	001	012	As the king lay on his couch, my nard perfume gave off its fragrance.
022	SOL	001	013	My love is like a pouch of myrrh, lying all night between my breasts.
022	SOL	001	014	My love is like a bunch of fragrant henna flowers in the vineyards of Engedi.
022	SOL	001	015	Look at how very beautiful you are, my darling, how beautiful! Your eyes are as gentle as doves.
022	SOL	001	016	And you, my love, are so handsome—how charming you are! The green grass is our bed,
