024	JER	001	001	These are the words of Jeremiah son of Hilkiah, one of the priests living in Anathoth in the territory of Benjamin.
024	JER	001	002	The Lord's message came to Jeremiah beginning in the thirteenth year of the reign of Josiah, son of Amon, king of Judah,
024	JER	001	003	and on through the time of Jehoiakim, son of Josiah, king of Judah, up to the fifth month of the eleventh year of Zedekiah, son of Josiah, king of Judah, which was when the people of Jerusalem went into exile.
024	JER	001	004	The Lord came and told me,
024	JER	001	005	“I knew exactly who you would be before I created you in your mother's womb; I chose you before you were born to be a prophet to the nations.”
024	JER	001	006	“Oh no, Lord God!” I replied. “I really don't know how to speak in public because I'm still too young!”
024	JER	001	007	“Don't say you're too young,” the Lord told me. “Go to everyone I send you to. Tell them everything I order you to say.
