# BOOK	027	DAN	Daniel	Daniel
027	DAN	001	001	During the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, Nebuchadnezzar, king of Babylon, attacked Jerusalem and surrounded it.
027	DAN	001	002	The Lord allowed him to defeat King Jehoiakim, and also to remove some of the objects used in the Temple of God. He took them back to Babylon, to the house of his god, placing them in the treasury of his god.
027	DAN	001	003	Then the king ordered Ashpenaz, his chief eunuch, to take charge of some of the captured Israelites from the royal and noble families.
027	DAN	001	004	“They are to be young men without any physical defect who are good-looking,” he said. “They must be well-educated, quick to learn, have good insight, and be well able to serve in the king's palace and be taught the literature and language of Babylon.”
027	DAN	001	005	The king also provided them with a daily allowance of the same kind of rich food and wine he was served. At the end of their three years of education they would enter the king's service.
027	DAN	001	006	Among those chosen were Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, from the tribe of Judah.
027	DAN	001	007	The chief eunuch gave them new names: Daniel he called Belteshazzar, Hananiah he called Shadrach, Mishael he called Meshach, and Azariah he called Abednego.
027	DAN	001	008	However, Daniel made up his mind not to make himself impure by eating the king's rich food and wine. He asked the chief eunuch to allow him not to make himself impure.
027	DAN	001	009	God had helped Daniel to be viewed with kindness and sympathy by the chief eunuch.
027	DAN	001	010	But the chief eunuch told Daniel, “I'm afraid of what my lord the king would do to me. He's the one who decided what you should eat and drink. What if he were to see you looking pale and sickly compared to the other young men of your age. Because of you the king would have my head!”
027	DAN	001	011	Daniel then spoke with the guard that the chief eunuch had put in charge of Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah.
027	DAN	001	012	“Please put us, your servants, to the test and just give us vegetables to eat and water to drink for ten days,” Daniel told him.
027	DAN	001	013	“After that, compare us with those young men who ate the king's rich food. Then decide on the basis of what you see.”
027	DAN	001	014	The guard agreed to the proposal they made and tested them for ten days.
027	DAN	001	015	When the ten days were up they looked healthier and better fed than all the young men who had eaten the king's rich food.
027	DAN	001	016	After that the guard didn't give them the rich food and wine, just vegetables.
027	DAN	001	017	God gave these four young men the ability to learn and understand in all areas of literature and knowledge, while Daniel was also given the gift of interpreting all kinds of visions and dreams.
027	DAN	001	018	When their time of education ordered by the king was over, the chief eunuch brought all the young men before King Nebuchadnezzar.
027	DAN	001	019	The king talked with them and none could compare with Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah. So they entered the king's service.
027	DAN	001	020	Whatever subject the king asked them about, everything that required wisdom of understanding, he found them ten times better than all the magicians and enchanters in his whole kingdom.
027	DAN	001	021	Daniel remained in this position until the first year of King Cyrus' reign.
027	DAN	002	001	In the second year of Nebuchadnezzar's reign the king had dreams that upset him so much that he found it difficult to sleep.
027	DAN	002	002	So the king summoned the magicians, enchanters, sorcerers, and astrologers to tell him what he had dreamed. They came in and stood before him.
027	DAN	002	003	“I've had a dream that has really upset me,” he told them. “I need to know what it means.”
027	DAN	002	004	The astrologers answered the king in Aramaic, “May Your Majesty the king live forever! Tell us your dream and we your servants will interpret it for you.”
027	DAN	002	005	“I can't recall it,” the king told the astrologers. “If you can't reveal the dream to me, and its meaning, you will be cut into pieces and your houses will be totally destroyed!
027	DAN	002	006	But if you can tell me the dream and its meaning you will receive from me gifts, rewards, and great honor. So tell me the dream and what it means!”
027	DAN	002	007	Again they said the same thing: “If Your Majesty the king would tell us his servants the dream, we will explain what it means.”
027	DAN	002	008	“It's obvious to me that you're just trying to buy time!” said the king. “You can see that I can't remember the dream.
027	DAN	002	009	If you can't reveal the dream to me, you will all receive the same punishment! You have conspired against me, telling me lies, hoping things will change. So tell me what my dream was and then I'll know that you can explain what it means.”
