029	JOE	003	004	Also, what have you got to do with me, Tyre and Sidon, and all the regions of Philistia? Are you trying to get back at me? If you are trying to pay me back, I will quickly pay you back what you deserve for what you've done.
029	JOE	003	005	You stole my silver and my gold and my best treasures, and you put them in your temples.
029	JOE	003	006	You sold the people of Judah and Jerusalem to the Greeks so they could be sent far away from their land.
029	JOE	003	007	But watch out! I will get them moving from the places you sold them to, and bring them back, and I will pay you back what you deserve for what you've done.
029	JOE	003	008	I will sell your sons and daughters to the people of Judah, and they will sell them to the Sabeans, a distant nation. I the Lord have spoken.
029	JOE	003	009	Proclaim this among the nations: “Prepare for war! Call up the mighty warriors! Let all the soldiers get ready and advance!
029	JOE	003	010	Hammer your plow blades and turn them into swords. Turn your pruning hooks into spears. Even the weak should say ‘I am a strong fighter!’
029	JOE	003	011	Hurry up and come, all nations from everywhere, and gather there. Bring down your warriors, Lord!
029	JOE	003	012	Let the nations get ready, let them come to the valley of Jehoshaphat for there I will sit in judgment on all the nations.
029	JOE	003	013	Start swinging the sickle, for the harvest is ripe. Come and tread the grapes for the winepress is full and the vats are overflowing because their wickedness has become so great.
029	JOE	003	014	Huge mobs are in the valley of the Lord's verdict. For the day of the Lord is near in the valley of his verdict.
029	JOE	003	015	The sun and moon will become dark, and the stars will stop shining.
029	JOE	003	016	The Lord will roar from Zion, shouting in a loud voice from Jerusalem, shaking the heavens and the earth. But the Lord will shelter his people, protecting the people of Israel.
029	JOE	003	017	Then you will know that I, the Lord your God, dwell in Zion, my holy mountain, and Jerusalem will be a holy place forever, and no foreigners will ever march through her again.
029	JOE	003	018	At that time new wine will pour down the mountains, and the hills will flow with milk, and all the riverbeds of Judah will run with water. A spring will flow out of the Temple and will water the valley of Shittim.
029	JOE	003	019	But Egypt will become desolate, and Edom a desert wasteland, because of the violence they did against Judah, for in their land they shed innocent blood.
029	JOE	003	020	Judah will be lived in forever, and Jerusalem for all generations.
029	JOE	003	021	Will I pardon and leave unpunished the shedding of innocent blood? The Lord lives in Zion!”
