# BOOK	030	AMO	Amos	Amos
030	AMO	001	001	Here is the message that was given to Amos, a shepherd from Tekoa in Judah. This is what he saw concerning Israel when Uzziah was king of Judah and Jeroboam, son of Jehoash, was king of Israel, two years before the earthquake.
030	AMO	001	002	And he said, The Lord roars from Zion, he shouts from Jerusalem. The shepherds' pastures wither, the top of Mount Carmel dries up.
030	AMO	001	003	This is what the Lord says: The people of Damascus have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, for they beat the people of Gilead with sharp iron threshing tools.
030	AMO	001	004	So I will send fire down on the house of Hazael and burn up Ben-Hadad's fortresses.
030	AMO	001	005	I will smash the gates of Damascus, I will cut down those who live in the Valley of Aven, and the ruler from Beth Eden. The people of Aram will be deported as prisoners to the land of Kir, says the Lord.
030	AMO	001	006	This is what the Lord says: The people of Gaza have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, for they sent into exile whole communities, handing them over to Edom.
030	AMO	001	007	So I will send down fire on the walls of Gaza and burn up its fortresses.
030	AMO	001	008	I will cut down those who live in Ashdod and the ruler of Ashkelon. I will turn to punish Ekron and the Philistines who remain will die, says the Lord God.
030	AMO	001	009	This is what the Lord says: The people of Tyre have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, for they exiled whole communities, handing them over to Edom, and did not keep their agreement to help each other as members of the same family.
030	AMO	001	010	So I will send down fire on the walls of Tyre and burn up its fortresses.
030	AMO	001	011	This is what the Lord says: The people of Edom have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, for they hunted down the Israelites to whom they were related, killing them with swords. They attacked without mercy, tearing the Israelites to pieces in an angry rage that never stopped.
030	AMO	001	012	So I will send down fire on Teman, and I will burn up the fortresses of Bozrah.
030	AMO	001	013	This is what the Lord says: The people of Ammon have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, because they ripped open pregnant women in Gilead as part of their war to enlarge their territory.
030	AMO	001	014	I will set fire to the walls of Rabbah and burn up its fortresses. There will be shouts on the day of battle which will whirl with rage like a windstorm.
030	AMO	001	015	Their king will be sent into exile together with his princes, says the Lord.
030	AMO	002	001	This is what the Lord says: The people of Moab have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, because they desecrated the bones of the king of Edom by burning them, turning them into lime.
030	AMO	002	002	So I will send down fire on Moab, and I will burn up the fortresses of Kerioth, and the people of Moab will die in the midst of uproar, battle cries, and the sound of the trumpet.
030	AMO	002	003	I will cut down their king and all their princes with him, says the Lord.
030	AMO	002	004	This is what the Lord says: The people of Judah have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, because they rejected the law of the Lord and have not kept his commands. Their lies have led them astray, the same lies that their forefathers followed.
030	AMO	002	005	So I will send down fire on Judah, and I will burn up the fortresses of Jerusalem.
030	AMO	002	006	This is what the Lord says: The people of Israel have repeatedly sinned and so I will not hesitate to punish them, because they sell good people for silver, and poor people for a pair of sandals.
030	AMO	002	007	They trample the heads of the poor into the dust, and push the needy out of the way. A man and his father have sex with the same servant girl so that my holy name is profaned.
030	AMO	002	008	At every altar they stretch themselves out in clothes taken from debtors as collateral, in the temple of their god they drink wine taken from the people they fined.
030	AMO	002	009	Yet it was I who was the one who destroyed the Amorites before you, even though they were as tall as cedars and as strong as oaks. I destroyed them root and branch.
030	AMO	002	010	It was I who brought you out of the land of Egypt and led you through the desert for forty years so that you could take the Amorites' land.
030	AMO	002	011	I appointed some of your sons to be prophets, and some of your young men to be Nazirites. Isn't this true, people of Israel?
030	AMO	002	012	But you made the Nazirites sin by drinking wine, and you told the prophets, “Don't tell us what God says.”
030	AMO	002	013	Now see what I am going to do. I will crush you where you are, as if crushed by a heavy cart loaded down with sheaves of grain.
030	AMO	002	014	Not even your fastest runners will escape; strong men will lose their strength. Even the greatest warrior will not be able to save his life.
030	AMO	002	015	The archer will not stand his ground. The quickest on his feet will not be able to get away, and even those on horseback will not save themselves.
030	AMO	002	016	On that day even the bravest of the mighty warriors will run away naked, says the Lord.
030	AMO	003	001	People of Israel, listen to this message that the Lord has spoken against you—all of you, whom I brought out of the land of Egypt.
030	AMO	003	002	I chose a special relationship with you alone out of all the families of the earth, and so I will punish you for your wrongdoing.
030	AMO	003	003	Can two people walk together unless they have arranged to meet?
030	AMO	003	004	Does a lion roar in the forest before finding its prey? Does a young lion growl from its den if it has caught nothing?
030	AMO	003	005	Does a bird fall into a trap and get caught unless the spring is set? Does a trap spring shut if there's nothing there to catch?
030	AMO	003	006	When the trumpet sounds in the city, shouldn't the people be alarmed? When a disaster comes to a city, isn't it the Lord who does it?
030	AMO	003	007	For the Lord God does nothing without revealing his intentions to his servants the prophets.
030	AMO	003	008	The lion has roared—so who isn't scared? The Lord God has spoken—so who can refuse to speak for him?
030	AMO	003	009	Announce this to the fortresses of Ashdod and to the fortresses in the land of Egypt: Assemble yourselves on Samaria's mountains and see all the turmoil and oppression happening in the country.
030	AMO	003	010	They don't know how to do what is right, declares the Lord. They have stored up in their fortresses what they've taken by violence and robbery.
030	AMO	003	011	As a result, says the Lord, an enemy will surround you, break down your strongholds, and plunder your fortresses.
030	AMO	003	012	This is what the Lord says: Just as a shepherd tries to rescue a sheep from a lion's mouth, but only saves a couple of legs or a piece of an ear, so it will be for the people of Israel living in Samaria—all that will be “saved” will be the corner of a couch and a piece of a leg from a bed.
030	AMO	003	013	Listen! Warn the house of Jacob, declares the Lord God of power.
030	AMO	003	014	For on that day I will punish Israel for their sins. I will destroy the altars of Bethel: the corners of the altar will be cut off and fall to the ground.
030	AMO	003	015	I will tear down their winter houses and their summer houses as well, their houses filled with ivory will be ruined—their many houses will be destroyed.
030	AMO	004	001	Listen to this message, you well-fed cows of Bashan who live on Mount Samaria, who oppress the poor and crush the needy, and who order your husbands, “Bring us drinks!”
030	AMO	004	002	The Lord God has sworn by his holiness: Watch out! For the time is coming when they will drag you away with hooks, each one of you will be like a fish on a hook.
030	AMO	004	003	You will leave through breaches in the city walls, thrown out in the direction of Mount Hermon.
030	AMO	004	004	Why don't you go to Bethel and sin? Go to Gilgal and add to your sins even more? Offer your sacrifices in the morning, bring your tithes after three days.
030	AMO	004	005	Burn a thank offering of bread made with yeast, and announce what you're giving as freewill offerings so everyone will know. This is what you love to do! declares the Lord God.
030	AMO	004	006	It was I who made sure you had nothing to eat in all your cities, and a lack of food wherever you lived, but still you wouldn't return to me, says the Lord.
030	AMO	004	007	It was I who kept the rain from falling when there were still three months before harvest. One city would have rain, while another would not. One field would have rain, another would dry up from lack of rain.
030	AMO	004	008	People wandered from town to town looking for water, yet were still thirsty. But still you did not return to me, declares the Lord.
030	AMO	004	009	I struck your many farms and vineyards with blight and mildew; locusts devoured your fig trees and olive trees. But still you did not return to me, declares the Lord.
030	AMO	004	010	I sent a plague on you like I did in Egypt. I killed your young men in battle; I took away your horses; I made you smell the stench of dead bodies in your camps. But still you did not return to me, declares the Lord.
030	AMO	004	011	Some of you I destroyed as I destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah. You were like a burning stick pulled out of a fire. But still you did not return to me, declares the Lord.
030	AMO	004	012	Therefore, this is what I am going to do to you, Israel. Because I am going to do this, Israel, prepare to meet your God!
030	AMO	004	013	Watch! The One who made the mountains, who created the winds, who reveals his thoughts to humankind, who turns the sunlight into darkness, who walks on the high places of the earth—the Lord God of power is his name!
030	AMO	005	001	Listen, people of Israel, to this funeral lament that I sing about you!
030	AMO	005	002	Virgin Israel has fallen, and will never rise again! She lies abandoned on the ground, and there is no one to help her up.
030	AMO	005	003	This is what the Lord says: From a city that sends out a thousand soldiers, only a hundred will return; from a city that sends out a hundred soldiers, only ten will return.
030	AMO	005	004	This is what the Lord says to the people of Israel: Look to me so you may live!
030	AMO	005	005	Do not look to the false gods of Bethel, do not go to the pagan shrines of Gilgal or travel to those of Beersheba. For Gilgal will go into exile, and Bethel will come to nothing.
030	AMO	005	006	Look to the Lord so you may live! Otherwise he will explode like fire against the descendants of Joseph and no one from Bethel will be able to quench it.
030	AMO	005	007	You twist justice and make it bitter, you throw integrity to the ground.
030	AMO	005	008	The One who made the Pleiades and Orion, who turns the darkness into morning, and daytime into night, who calls for the water of the seas, and pours it down as rain upon the earth—the Lord is his name!
030	AMO	005	009	In a flash he cuts down the strong and destroys the fortresses.
030	AMO	005	010	You hate anyone who confronts injustice and loathe anyone who speaks honestly.
030	AMO	005	011	Because you trample down the poor and impose a tax on their grain, building for yourselves impressive houses, you will not live in them, and you will not drink wine from the fine vineyards you have planted.
030	AMO	005	012	For I know the extent of your wrongdoing and your numerous sins. You oppress good people by taking bribes, and you prevent the poor from getting justice in the courts.
030	AMO	005	013	So smart people keep quiet in such evil times.
030	AMO	005	014	Do what is right, and not evil, so you may live. Then the Lord God of power will be with you, as you claim he is.
030	AMO	005	015	Hate evil and love good—and make sure justice wins out in your courts. Maybe the Lord God of power will have mercy on those who are left of Jacob's people.
030	AMO	005	016	For this is what the Lord, the Lord God of power says: There will be weeping in the city squares and wailing in the streets. They will call even the farmers to grieve, as well as the professional mourners.
030	AMO	005	017	There will be wailing in every vineyard, for I will pass through the midst of you, says the Lord.
030	AMO	005	018	How disastrous it will be for those of you who long for the day of the Lord. Why would you want the day of the Lord to come? It will bring darkness, not light.
030	AMO	005	019	It will be like a man running away from a lion only to meet a bear; or a man who goes home and leans his hand on a wall, only to be bitten by a snake.
030	AMO	005	020	Isn't the day of the Lord darkness without light? Yes, pitch dark without a glimmer of light.
030	AMO	005	021	I hate, I despise your festivals and take no delight in your religious assemblies.
030	AMO	005	022	Even though you present me with burnt offerings and grain offerings, I will not accept them. As for your peace offerings of fattened cattle—I will not even look at them.
030	AMO	005	023	Stop your noisy worship songs. I will not listen to the melody of your harps.
030	AMO	005	024	Rather let justice flow like a river, and doing right like an ever-flowing stream.
030	AMO	005	025	Did you bring me sacrifices during those forty years in the desert, people of Israel?
030	AMO	005	026	But now you carry idols of Sakkuth your king and Kaiwan your star god that you made for yourselves.
030	AMO	005	027	So I will send you into exile in a land beyond Damascus, says the Lord, whose name is the God of power.
030	AMO	006	001	How disastrous it will be for you who have an easy life in Zion, and you who feel secure living on Mount Samaria—you who are the most famous men in all of Israel to whom people come for help!
030	AMO	006	002	But go to Calneh, and see what took place there. Then go on to the great city of Hamath, and down to the Philistine city of Gath. Were they better kingdoms than yours? Did they have more territory than you?
030	AMO	006	003	You put out of your minds any thought of coming disaster, yet you are bringing closer the time when violence reigns.
030	AMO	006	004	How disastrous it will be for you people who lie on beds decorated with ivory and lounge on couches, eating lamb from your flocks and fattened calves from the stall.
030	AMO	006	005	You make up songs accompanied by the harp, thinking you're great composers like David.
030	AMO	006	006	You drink wine by the bowlful, and anoint yourselves with the finest oils, but you do not grieve over the ruin of Joseph's descendants.
030	AMO	006	007	So you will be at the head of those led away into exile; the feasting and lazing around will be over.
030	AMO	006	008	The Lord God has sworn an oath on his own life. This is what the Lord God of power declares: I detest Jacob's arrogance and I hate his fortresses; I will hand over this city and all in it to the enemy.
030	AMO	006	009	If there are ten people in a house, they will die.
030	AMO	006	010	And when a relative comes to take away the bodies from the house, he will ask someone inside, “Is there anyone else with you?” The person will reply, “No...” Then the other will say, “Quiet! Don't even mention the Lord's name.”
030	AMO	006	011	Watch out! When the Lord gives the command, large houses will be reduced to rubble, and small houses smashed to pieces.
030	AMO	006	012	Can horses gallop over rocks? Can oxen plow the sea? But you have turned justice into poison, and the fruit of doing good into bitterness!
030	AMO	006	013	You joyfully celebrate your conquest of Lodebar, and say “Didn't we in our own strength capture Karnaim?”
030	AMO	006	014	Watch out, people of Israel! I am going to send an enemy nation to attack you, says the Lord God of power, and they will oppress you from the Pass of Hamath to the Arabah Valley.
030	AMO	007	001	This is what the Lord God showed me. I saw that he was preparing a swarm of locusts just when the spring crops began to grow. (Spring crops begin to grow right after the time when the king's hay is cut.)
030	AMO	007	002	And so when the locusts finished eating every green plant in the fields, I pleaded with the Lord God, “Please forgive your people! How can the descendants of Jacob survive? They are so weak.”
030	AMO	007	003	So the Lord changed his mind. “It won't happen,” said the Lord.
030	AMO	007	004	This is what the Lord God showed me. I saw that the Lord God was calling for a judgment of fire. The fire burned up the depths of the sea and destroyed the farmland.
030	AMO	007	005	I pleaded with the Lord God, “Please stop! How can the descendants of Jacob survive? They are so weak.”
030	AMO	007	006	So the Lord changed his mind. “This too won't happen,” said the Lord.
030	AMO	007	007	This is what he showed me. I saw the Lord was standing beside a wall that had been built with a plumb line. He was holding a plumb line in his hand.
030	AMO	007	008	And the Lord asked me, “Amos, what do you see?” I replied, “A plumb line.” And the Lord God said, “I am placing a plumb line in the midst of my people Israel. I won't ignore their sins anymore.
030	AMO	007	009	The high places of the descendants of Isaac will be torn down, and the holy places of Israel will be destroyed. Sword in hand, I will rise up against the house of Jeroboam.”
030	AMO	007	010	Then Amaziah, priest of Bethel, sent a message to Jeroboam, king of Israel, saying, “Amos is plotting against you among the people of Israel. What he's saying is unbearable!
030	AMO	007	011	For he's saying Jeroboam will be killed by the sword, and the people will be taken away from their land into exile.”
030	AMO	007	012	Amaziah said to Amos, “Go away prophet! Run away to the land of Judah. Go and prophesy there to earn your bread.
030	AMO	007	013	But don't ever prophesy again at Bethel, for this is where the king worships, the national Temple.”
030	AMO	007	014	But Amos replied, “I'm not a trained prophet, or the son of a prophet. I was just a shepherd, and also took care of fig trees.
030	AMO	007	015	The Lord took me from following my flock, and the Lord told me, ‘Go, and give my message to my people of Israel.’”
030	AMO	007	016	So now hear what the Lord is telling you: You say, “Don't prophesy against Israel, and don't preach against the descendants of Isaac.”
030	AMO	007	017	But this is what the Lord says: Your wife will become a prostitute in the city; your sons and daughters will be killed by the sword. Your land will be measured and divided up, and you yourself will die in a foreign land. The people of Israel will definitely be taken from the land and go into exile.
030	AMO	008	001	This is what the Lord God showed me. I saw a basket of fruit.
030	AMO	008	002	He asked me, “What do you see, Amos?” I said, “A basket of fruit.” Then the Lord told me, “This is the end of my people Israel! I won't ignore their sins anymore.
030	AMO	008	003	On that day the Temple songs will become sorrowful wailing. There will be dead bodies scattered everywhere. Silence!” declares the Lord.
030	AMO	008	004	Listen to this, you who trample down the needy, and wipe out the poor of the land.
030	AMO	008	005	You who ask, “When will the holy day be over so we can get back to selling grain? When will the Sabbath be over so we can open our storehouses, and cheat people with short measures and unfair scales?”
030	AMO	008	006	You buy the poor for silver, the needy for a pair of sandals, and you sell grain mixed with chaff.
030	AMO	008	007	The Lord God, of whom the descendants of Jacob are so proud, has sworn an oath: I will never forget the evil you have done.
030	AMO	008	008	Shall not the land tremble because of this, and everyone who lives there mourn? The earth will rise up like the Nile River in flood, be tossed around, and then fall again.
030	AMO	008	009	On that day, declares the Lord God, I will make the sun go down at noon, and darken the land during the daytime.
030	AMO	008	010	I will turn your festivals into times of mourning, your happy songs into laments. I will make you wear sackcloth and shave your heads. I will make your mourning like that for an only son. At the end of it all it will be a bitter day.
030	AMO	008	011	The time is coming, declares the Lord, when I will send a famine on the land—not a famine of bread, or a lack of water, but a famine of hearing the words of the Lord.
030	AMO	008	012	People will wander from sea to sea, from north to east, running to and fro searching for the word of the Lord, but they will not find it.
030	AMO	008	013	On that day, even the beautiful girls and healthy young men will collapse from thirst.
030	AMO	008	014	Those who swear by the disgraceful idols of Samaria, who take oaths like, “By the life of your god, Dan,” or “A pilgrimage to the god of Beersheba”—they will fall, and never rise again.
030	AMO	009	001	Then I saw the Lord standing beside the altar, and he said: Strike the tops of the Temple pillars so that the foundations shake, and shatter them on the heads of all the people below. Those who survive I will kill by the sword. None of them will escape, not a single one.
030	AMO	009	002	Even if they dig down into Sheol, I will catch them and pull them up. Even if they climb up to heaven, I will bring them down.
030	AMO	009	003	Even if they hide themselves at the top of Mount Carmel, I will search for them and catch them. Even if they hide from me at the bottom of the sea, I will command the sea serpent to bite them.
030	AMO	009	004	Even if they are driven into exile by their enemies, I will order them put to death by the sword. I will watch them carefully—and for evil, not for good.
030	AMO	009	005	The Lord God of power touches the earth and it melts, and all who live there mourn. The earth rises up like the Nile River in flood, and then falls again.
030	AMO	009	006	The Lord builds his upper rooms in heaven, and places the foundations on the earth. He calls for the water of the seas, and pours it down as rain upon the earth—the Lord is his name!
030	AMO	009	007	Aren't the Ethiopians as important to me as you, people of Israel? asks the Lord. Yes, I brought the Israelites out of the land of Egypt, but I also brought the Philistines from Caphtor, and the Syrians from Kir.
030	AMO	009	008	Watch out! I'm watching this sinful kingdom. I will eradicate it from the face of the earth. Yet I will not completely destroy the descendants of Jacob.
030	AMO	009	009	See what I'm doing! I will give the command, and the people of Israel will be shaken among the nations like flour through a sieve, and nothing will fall to the ground.
030	AMO	009	010	All the sinners of my people will be killed by the sword—all those who say, “Nothing bad is going to happen; no disaster will fall on us.”
030	AMO	009	011	On that day I will restore the fallen kingdom of David; I will repair the broken walls, I will rebuild the ruins, and I will make it as it was in days of old.
030	AMO	009	012	And they will possess what is left of Edom and all the nations that were once mine, declares the Lord. He will make this happen.
030	AMO	009	013	Look! The time is coming, says the Lord, when the reaper will overtake the plowman, and the one who treads the grapes will overtake the one who sows the seed. The mountains will drip with sweet wine, and flow from all the hills.
030	AMO	009	014	I will bring my people back from captivity, and they will rebuild the ruined cities, and they shall live in them. They shall plant vineyards and drink their wine; they will plant gardens and eat the fruit they produce.
030	AMO	009	015	I will plant them in their own land, and they shall never be uprooted again from the land I have given them, declares the Lord your God.
