035	HAB	003	009	You took out your bow; you filled your quiver with arrows. (Selah) You split the earth open with rivers.
035	HAB	003	010	Mountains saw you and shook. Water poured down and swept by. The deep called out, lifting high its waves.
035	HAB	003	011	The sun and moon stood still in the sky as your sparkling arrows flew and your spears flashed bright.
035	HAB	003	012	Indignant, you marched across the earth, trampling the nations in your anger.
