038	ZEC	014	006	On that day there will be no longer cold and frost.
038	ZEC	014	007	It will be one continuous day (only the Lord knows how this could happen). It won't be day or night, because in the evening it will still be light.
038	ZEC	014	008	On that day living waters will flow out of Jerusalem, half of it going east to the Dead Sea and half going west to the Mediterranean Sea, flowing in summer and winter alike.
038	ZEC	014	009	The Lord will be king over all the earth. On that day there will be one true Lord, and his name the only one.
038	ZEC	014	010	The whole land will be transformed into a plain, from Geba to Rimmon, south of Jerusalem. But Jerusalem will be raised up to where it was, and people will live there from the Benjamin Gate to where the old gate was, to the Corner Gate, and from the Tower of Hananel to the king's winepresses.
038	ZEC	014	011	It will be inhabited and never again condemned to destruction again—people will be able to live in safety in Jerusalem.
038	ZEC	014	012	This will be the plague that the Lord will use to strike all the nations that attacked Jerusalem. Their flesh shall rot while they are still standing on their feet; their eyes will rot in their sockets; their tongues will rot in their mouths.
038	ZEC	014	013	On that day the Lord will strike them with a terrible panic, and they will seize one another, and fight hand-to-hand.
038	ZEC	014	014	Even Judah will fight in Jerusalem. The wealth of the surrounding nations shall be collected: lots of gold, silver, and clothes.
038	ZEC	014	015	A similar plague will strike the horses, mules, camels, donkeys, and all other animals that may be in their camps.
038	ZEC	014	016	After this every one of the survivors from the nations that attacked Jerusalem will go there to worship the King, the Lord Almighty, and to celebrate the Festival of Shelters.
038	ZEC	014	017	If any of the peoples of the world refuse to go to Jerusalem to worship the King, the Lord Almighty, they will have no rain.
038	ZEC	014	018	If the Egyptian people refuse to go and attend, then the Lord will inflict on them the same plague as on the other nations who will not go celebrate the Festival of Shelters.
038	ZEC	014	019	This will be the punishment on Egypt and all the nations if they do not go to Jerusalem and celebrate.
038	ZEC	014	020	On that day the bells worn by horses will be engraved with the words “Holy to the Lord.” The household cooking pots used in the Lord's Temple will be as holy as the bowls used on the altar in the presence of the Lord.
038	ZEC	014	021	Every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah will be holy to the Lord Almighty, so that everyone who comes to sacrifice can take them and cook their sacrificial meat in them. On that day there will no longer be traders in the Lord's Temple.
