# BOOK	039	MAL	Malachi	Malachi
039	MAL	001	001	A prophecy: This message came from the Lord concerning Israel through Malachi.
039	MAL	001	002	I have loved you, says the Lord. But you ask, “How have you loved us?” Wasn't Esau Jacob's brother? the Lord responds. But I loved Jacob
039	MAL	001	003	and despised Esau. I have made Esau's mountain homeland into a wasteland, and turned his inheritance into a desert for jackals.
039	MAL	001	004	The people of Edom may be saying: “We have been beaten down, but we will rebuild the ruins.” But this is what the Lord Almighty says, They may try and build, but I will tear down. They will be called a land of wickedness, and the people those who make the Lord angry forever.
039	MAL	001	005	You will see this destruction with your own eyes, and you will say, “The Lord is great, even beyond the borders of Israel.”
039	MAL	001	006	A son honors his father, and a servant respects his master. So if I am your father, where is my honor? If I am your master, where is my respect? says the Lord Almighty to you priests who show contempt for me. But you ask, “How have we shown contempt for you?”
039	MAL	001	007	By making defiled offerings on my altar. Then you ask, “How have we defiled you?” By saying the Lord's table doesn't deserve respect.
039	MAL	001	008	When you offer a blind animal as a sacrifice, isn't that wrong? Or when you offer an animal that is crippled or sick, isn't that wrong? Would you give such gifts to your governor? Would he be pleased with you? Would he be kind and show favor to you? asks the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	001	009	So why don't you try being kind to God, begging him to be merciful to you? But when you bring such offerings, why should he show favor to you? asks the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	001	010	I really wish one of you would shut the Temple doors to stop you lighting pointless fires on my altar! I am not pleased with you, says the Lord Almighty, and I will not accept offerings from you.
039	MAL	001	011	I am honored by nations from the farthest east to the distant west; everywhere people make offerings to me of incense and pure sacrifices. I am honored among the nations, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	001	012	But you dishonor me when you say the Lord's table doesn't deserve respect, and that its food can be treated with contempt.
039	MAL	001	013	You say, “All this is too much trouble!” and you sniff scornfully at it, says the Lord Almighty. But when you bring animals that are stolen or crippled or sick and offer them as sacrifices, should I accept what you're giving? asks the Lord.
039	MAL	001	014	Cursed are those who cheat by vowing to bring a ram as a sacrifice and then offers an imperfect animal to the Lord. For I am a great King, says the Lord Almighty, and I am respected among the nations!
039	MAL	002	001	Now this command is for you priests!
039	MAL	002	002	If you will not listen and if you will not take it to heart to honor me, says the Lord Almighty, then I will place a curse on you and I will curse your blessings—in fact I have already cursed them because you haven't taken what I said to heart.
039	MAL	002	003	Watch out! I am going to penalize your descendants. I will spread manure on your faces from the animals you sacrifice, the manure from your religious festivals, and you will be thrown out with it.
039	MAL	002	004	Then you will know that I sent you this command so that my agreement with Levi can continue, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	002	005	My agreement with him was one of life and peace, which I gave to him, and respect—he respected me. He stood in awe of me.
039	MAL	002	006	He taught the people the truth; nothing in his teaching was false. He walked with me in peace and did what was right, and he helped many to turn away from sin.
039	MAL	002	007	A priest should explain the truth about God, they should go to him to be taught, for he is the Lord Almighty's messenger.
039	MAL	002	008	But you have turned from my way. You have made many people to fall into sin. By your teaching you have broken the agreement with Levi, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	002	009	So I have destroyed any respect you had, and humiliated you before all the people. For you have not kept my ways, and have shown favoritism in what you teach.
039	MAL	002	010	Don't we all have one Father? Didn't one God create us? So why are we unfaithful to each other, violating the agreement made by our forefathers?
039	MAL	002	011	The people of Judah have been unfaithful and have committed a disgusting sin in Israel and Jerusalem. For the men of Judah have defiled the Lord's Temple (which he loves) by marrying women who worship idols.
039	MAL	002	012	May the Lord expel the family of any man who does this from the nation of Israel! May there be no one left to bring an offering to the Lord Almighty!
039	MAL	002	013	Something else you do is to pour out your tears on the Lord's altar weeping and moaning because he no longer pays attention to your offerings or doesn't want to accept them.
039	MAL	002	014	“Why not?” you ask. Because the Lord witnessed the vows you and your wife exchanged when you were young. You were unfaithful to her, your wife and partner joined to you by marriage contract.
039	MAL	002	015	Did he not make you one, and give some of his Spirit to you? And what does he want? Children of God. So watch what you do, and don't be unfaithful to the wife you married when you were young.
039	MAL	002	016	For I hate divorce, says the Lord God of Israel, for it's a violent attack on the wife, says the Lord Almighty. So watch what you do, and don't be unfaithful.
039	MAL	002	017	You have worn the Lord out with your words. “How have we worn him out?” you ask. By saying everyone who does evil is good in the sight of the Lord and he is happy with them, or by asking, where is the Lord's justice?
039	MAL	003	001	Look! I am sending my messenger, and he will prepare the way for me. The Lord you are seeking will suddenly arrive at his Temple. The messenger of the agreement you say is so happy with you is coming, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	003	002	Who can survive the day when he comes? Who can stand before him when he appears? For he will be like a blazing furnace that refines metal, or like the strong alkali that cleanses stains.
039	MAL	003	003	He will sit down like a refiner who purifies silver; he will purify Levi's descendants and refine them like gold and silver so they can present pure offerings to the Lord.
039	MAL	003	004	Then the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem will please the Lord as they did in the old days, in the former years.
039	MAL	003	005	I will come and put you on trial. I am ready to be a witness against those who: practice witchcraft commit adultery tell lies give false evidence cheat employees oppress widows and orphans abuse foreigners and do not respect me, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	003	006	For I am the Lord, I don't change, and you haven't stopped being descendants of Jacob.
039	MAL	003	007	From the time of your forefathers onward, you have turned away from my laws and not kept them. Return to me, and I will return to you, says the Lord Almighty. But you ask, “How should we return?”
039	MAL	003	008	Should people defraud God? Yet you are defrauding me! But you ask, “How have we defrauded you?” In tithes and offerings.
039	MAL	003	009	You are under a curse, for you and the whole nation are defrauding me.
039	MAL	003	010	Bring the full tithe into the storehouse so that there will be food in my Temple. Put me to the test in this, says the Lord Almighty, and I will open the windows of heaven and pour out so much blessing that you won't have enough room for it.
039	MAL	003	011	I will prevent locusts from destroying your crops, and your vineyards will not fail to bear fruit, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	003	012	All nations will call you blessed because you live in such a wonderful land, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	003	013	You have said hard things about me, says the Lord. But you say, “What have we said against you?”
039	MAL	003	014	You have said, “What's the point of serving God? What benefit is there in keeping his commandments or going before the Lord Almighty with long faces?
039	MAL	003	015	From now on we'll say that the proud are blessed. Evil people do well, and nothing happens when they dare God to punish them.”
039	MAL	003	016	Then those who truly respected the Lord spoke to each other, and the Lord heard what they said. A scroll of remembrance was written in his presence of those who respected the Lord and paid attention to him.
039	MAL	003	017	They shall be mine, says the Lord Almighty, my prized possession on the day when I take action. I will treat them kindly, as a father treats an obedient son.
039	MAL	003	018	Then you will once again be able to distinguish those who do right from those who do wrong, between those who serve him and those who don't.
039	MAL	004	001	Watch out! The day is coming—it burns like an oven—when the proud and the wicked will be burned like straw. When that day comes they will be completely burned up, root and branch, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	004	002	But for those who have reverence for me, the sun of God's salvation will rise with healing in its wings, and you will be set free, leaping like calves released from their stalls.
039	MAL	004	003	You will trample the wicked as ashes under your feet on the day when I take action, says the Lord Almighty.
039	MAL	004	004	Remember the law of Moses my servant that I commanded him and all Israel to follow—all the instructions and ceremonies I gave on Mount Sinai.
039	MAL	004	005	Look! I am going to send Elijah the prophet before the day of the Lord arrives, the great and terrifying day.
039	MAL	004	006	He will restore harmony between parents and children, and if that does not happen, I will come and strike the land with a curse.
