# BOOK	040	MAT	Matthew	Matthew
040	MAT	001	001	This book is the record of Jesus the Messiah, the son of David, the son of Abraham, beginning with the family line:
040	MAT	001	002	Abraham was the father of Isaac; and Isaac the father of Jacob; and Jacob the father of Judah and his brothers;
040	MAT	001	003	and Judah the father of Perez and Zerah (their mother was Tamar); and Perez the father of Hezron; and Hezron the father of Ram;
040	MAT	001	004	and Ram the father of Amminadab; and Amminadab the father of Nahshon; and Nahshon the father of Salmon;
040	MAT	001	005	and Salmon the father of Boaz (his mother was Rahab); and Boaz the father of Obed (his mother was Ruth); and Obed the father of Jesse;
040	MAT	001	006	and Jesse the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon (his mother had been Uriah's wife);
040	MAT	001	007	and Solomon the father of Rehoboam; and Rehoboam the father of Abijah; and Abijah the father of Asa;
040	MAT	001	008	and Asa the father of Jehoshaphat; and Jehoshaphat the father of Jehoram; and Jehoram the father of Uzziah;
040	MAT	001	009	and Uzziah the father of Jotham; and Jotham the father of Ahaz; and Ahaz the father of Hezekiah;
040	MAT	001	010	and Hezekiah the father of Manasseh; and Manasseh the father of Amon; and Amon the father of Josiah;
040	MAT	001	011	and Josiah the father of Jehoiachin and his brothers, at the time of the exile to Babylon.
040	MAT	001	012	After the exile to Babylon, Jehoiachin was the father of Shealtiel; and Shealtiel the father of Zerubbabel;
040	MAT	001	013	and Zerubbabel the father of Abiud; and Abiud the father of Eliakim; and Eliakim the father of Azor;
040	MAT	001	014	and Azor the father of Zadok; and Zadok the father of Akim; and Akim the father of Eliud;
040	MAT	001	015	and Eliud the father of Eleazar; and Eleazar the father of Matthan; and Matthan the father of Jacob;
040	MAT	001	016	and Jacob was the father of Joseph, who was the husband of Mary, to whom Jesus was born, the one who is called the Messiah.
040	MAT	001	017	So all the generations from Abraham to David add up to fourteen; from David to the Babylonian exile, fourteen; and from the Babylonian exile to the Messiah, fourteen.
040	MAT	001	018	This is how the birth of Jesus the Messiah happened. His mother, Mary, was engaged to Joseph, but before they slept together she became pregnant by the Holy Spirit.
040	MAT	001	019	Joseph, her fiancé, was a good man and didn't want to shame her publicly, so he decided to break the engagement discreetly.
040	MAT	001	020	While he was thinking about all of this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and told him, “Joseph, son of David, don't be afraid to marry Mary because she is pregnant by the Holy Spirit.
040	MAT	001	021	She will give birth to a son and you shall call him Jesus, for he will save people from their sins.”
040	MAT	001	022	(Now this all happened to fulfill what the Lord said through the prophet:
040	MAT	001	023	“A virgin will become pregnant, and will give birth to a son. They will call him Immanuel,” which means “God with us.”)
040	MAT	001	024	Joseph woke up and did what the angel of the Lord told him to do.
040	MAT	001	025	Joseph married Mary, but did not sleep with her until after she had given birth to a son, whom he named Jesus.
040	MAT	002	001	After Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea during the reign of King Herod, wise men came from the east to Jerusalem.
040	MAT	002	002	“Where is the King of the Jews who has been born?” they asked. “We saw his star in the east and we've come to worship him.”
040	MAT	002	003	When King Herod heard about it, he was very disturbed, and the whole of Jerusalem with him.
040	MAT	002	004	Herod summoned all the chief priests and religious teachers of the people, and asked them where the Messiah was supposed to be born.
040	MAT	002	005	“Bethlehem in Judea,” they told him, “for that's what the prophet wrote:
040	MAT	002	006	‘Bethlehem in the land of Judea, you are certainly not the least important of Judah's leading cities, for a leader will come from you who will be the shepherd for my people Israel.’”
040	MAT	002	007	Then Herod called the wise men and met with them in private and found out from them exactly when the star appeared.
040	MAT	002	008	He sent them to Bethlehem, telling them, “When you get there, search for the child. Once you find him let me know so that I can come and worship him too.”
040	MAT	002	009	After they had heard what the king had to say they went on their way, and the star which they had seen in the east led them until it stopped right above the place where the child was.
040	MAT	002	010	When they saw the star they couldn't contain their happiness!
040	MAT	002	011	They went into the house and saw the child with Mary his mother. They bowed and worshiped him. Then they opened their bags of treasure and presented him with gifts of gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
040	MAT	002	012	Warned by a dream not to return to Herod, they left for their own country by a different route.
040	MAT	002	013	After they'd left, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream, and told him, “Get up, and take the child and his mother, and flee to Egypt. Remain there until I tell you, because Herod is going to search for the child to kill him.”
040	MAT	002	014	So Joseph got up and took the boy and his mother, and left during the night for Egypt.
040	MAT	002	015	They stayed there until Herod's death. This fulfilled what the Lord said through the prophet, “I called my son out of Egypt.”
040	MAT	002	016	When Herod realized he'd been fooled by the wise men, he got very angry. He sent men to kill all the young boys in Bethlehem and the regions nearby who were two years old and under. This was based on the time frame he'd discovered from the wise men.
040	MAT	002	017	In this way Jeremiah's prophecy was fulfilled:
040	MAT	002	018	“The sound of terrible weeping and mourning was heard in Rama, Rachel crying for her children. They are dead, and she can't be comforted.”
040	MAT	002	019	After Herod died the angel of the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in Egypt, and told him,
040	MAT	002	020	“Get up! Take the child and his mother, and return to the land of Israel, because those who were trying to kill the child are dead.”
040	MAT	002	021	So Joseph got up and took the boy and his mother, and returned to the land of Israel.
040	MAT	002	022	But Joseph was afraid to go there after he learned that Archelaus had succeeded his father Herod as king of Judea. Warned in a dream, Joseph went to the Galilee area
040	MAT	002	023	and settled down in Nazareth. This fulfilled what the prophets had said, “He will be called a Nazarene.”
040	MAT	003	001	Some time later John the Baptist appeared on the scene, proclaiming in the Judean desert,
040	MAT	003	002	“Repent, for the kingdom of heaven has arrived!”
040	MAT	003	003	He was the one Isaiah spoke about when he said, “A voice is heard crying out in the desert, ‘Prepare the way of the Lord. Make the paths straight for him.’”
040	MAT	003	004	John had clothes made of camel hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.
040	MAT	003	005	People came to him from Jerusalem, all of Judea, and the entire Jordan region,
040	MAT	003	006	and were baptized in the Jordan River, publicly admitting their sins.
040	MAT	003	007	But when John saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming to be baptized, he said to them, “You vipers' brood! Who warned you to run away from the coming judgment?
040	MAT	003	008	Show by what you do that you have truly repented,
040	MAT	003	009	and don't presume to say proudly to yourselves, ‘Abraham is our father.’ I tell you that God could make children of Abraham from these stones.
040	MAT	003	010	In fact the ax is ready to chop down the trees. Every tree that doesn't produce good fruit will be chopped down and thrown into the fire.
040	MAT	003	011	Yes, I baptize you in water to show repentance, but after me is coming one who is greater than I am. I'm not worthy even to remove his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.
040	MAT	003	012	He has his winnowing tool ready in his hand. He will clean up the threshing floor and gather the wheat into the storehouse, but he will burn the chaff with fire that can't be put out.”
040	MAT	003	013	Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan River to be baptized by John.
040	MAT	003	014	But John tried to change his mind. He told Jesus, “I need to be baptized by you, and you come to me to baptize you?”
040	MAT	003	015	“Please do so, because it's good for us to do what God says is right,” Jesus told him. So John agreed to do it.
040	MAT	003	016	Immediately after he was baptized, Jesus came out of the water. The heavens were opened, and he saw God's Spirit like a dove descending, landing on him.
040	MAT	003	017	A voice from heaven said, “This is my son whom I love, who pleases me.”
040	MAT	004	001	Then Jesus was led by the Spirit into the desert to be tempted by the devil.
040	MAT	004	002	After fasting forty days and nights, he was hungry.
040	MAT	004	003	The tempter came and said to him, “If you really are the Son of God, order these stones to turn into bread.”
040	MAT	004	004	Jesus answered, “As Scripture says, ‘Human beings do not live by only eating bread, but by every word that comes from the mouth of God.’”
040	MAT	004	005	Then the devil took him to the holy city and placed him on the top of the Temple.
040	MAT	004	006	“If you really are the son of God, then throw yourself off,” he told Jesus. “As Scripture says, ‘He will order his angels to save you from harm. They will catch you so that you won't fall by tripping over a stone.’”
040	MAT	004	007	Jesus answered, “As Scripture also says, ‘You shall not tempt the Lord your God.’”
040	MAT	004	008	Then the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world in all their glory.
