040	MAT	005	001	When Jesus saw the crowds following him he went up a mountain. There he sat down together with his disciples.
040	MAT	005	002	He began teaching them, saying:
040	MAT	005	003	“Blessed are those who recognize they are spiritually poor, for the kingdom of heaven is theirs.
040	MAT	005	004	Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.
040	MAT	005	005	Blessed are those who are kind for they will own the whole world.
040	MAT	005	006	Blessed are those whose greatest desire is to do what is right, for they will be satisfied.
040	MAT	005	007	Blessed are those who are merciful, for they will be shown mercy.
040	MAT	005	008	Blessed are those who have pure minds, for they will see God.
040	MAT	005	009	Blessed are those who work to bring peace, for they will be called children of God.
040	MAT	005	010	Blessed are those persecuted for what is right, for the kingdom of heaven is theirs.
040	MAT	005	011	Blessed are you when people insult you and persecute you, and accuse you of all kinds of evil things because of me.
040	MAT	005	012	Be glad, be really glad, for you will receive a great reward in heaven—for they persecuted the prophets who came before you in just the same way.
040	MAT	005	013	You are the salt of the earth, but if the salt becomes tasteless, how can you make it salty again? It's good for nothing, so it's thrown out and trodden down.
040	MAT	005	014	You are the light of the world. A city built on a hill can't be hidden.
040	MAT	005	015	No one lights a lamp and then puts it under a bucket. No, it's placed on a lamp-stand and it provides light to everyone in the house.
040	MAT	005	016	In the same way you should let your light shine before everyone so they can see the good things you do and praise your heavenly Father.
040	MAT	005	017	Don't think I came to abolish the law or the writings of the prophets. I didn't come to abolish them, but to fulfill them.
040	MAT	005	018	I assure you, until heaven and earth come to an end, not a single letter, not a single dot of the law will come to an end before everything is fulfilled.
040	MAT	005	019	So whoever disregards the least important commandment, and teaches people to do so, will be called the least in the kingdom of heaven; but whoever practices and teaches the commandments will be called great in the kingdom of heaven.
