041	MAR	015	042	It was Friday, the day before the Sabbath. When evening came,
041	MAR	015	043	Joseph of Arimathea, a member of the governing council who was himself waiting for the kingdom of God, had the courage to go to Pilate and ask for Jesus' body.
041	MAR	015	044	Pilate was surprised that Jesus had died so soon, so he summoned the centurion and asked him if Jesus had already died.
041	MAR	015	045	Once he had confirmation from the centurion, Pilate gave permission for Joseph to take the body.
