042	LUK	001	001	As you know, many others have attempted to put down in writing the things that have been fulfilled that involve us.
042	LUK	001	002	They based their accounts on evidence from the earliest eyewitnesses and ministers of the Word,
042	LUK	001	003	and so I also decided that since I have followed these things very carefully from the beginning, it would be a good idea to write out an accurate account of all that happened.
042	LUK	001	004	I have done this Theophilus, Your Excellency, so you can be certain that what you were taught is completely reliable.
042	LUK	001	005	During the time when Herod was king of Judea, there was a priest called Zechariah, who came from the Abijah priestly division. He was married to Elizabeth, who was also descended from Aaron the priest.
042	LUK	001	006	They both did what was right before God, being careful to follow all the Lord's commandments and regulations.
042	LUK	001	007	They had no children because Elizabeth wasn't able to have any, and they were both growing old.
042	LUK	001	008	While Zechariah was serving as a priest before God, on behalf of his priestly division,
042	LUK	001	009	he was chosen by lot according to priestly custom to enter the Temple of the Lord and burn incense.
042	LUK	001	010	During the time of offering incense a large crowd of people were praying outside.
042	LUK	001	011	An angel of the Lord appeared to Zechariah, standing to the right of the altar of incense.
042	LUK	001	012	When Zechariah saw the angel, he was startled and became terrified.
042	LUK	001	013	But the angel told him, “Don't be afraid, Zechariah. Your prayer has been heard, and your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you shall call him John.
042	LUK	001	014	He will bring you joy and gladness, and many will celebrate his birth.
042	LUK	001	015	He will be great in the sight of the Lord. He will refuse to drink wine or other alcoholic drink. He will be filled with the Holy Spirit even before he's born.
042	LUK	001	016	He will turn many Israelites back to the Lord their God.
042	LUK	001	017	He will go ahead of the Lord in the spirit and power of Elijah, to turn the fathers back to thinking about their children, and to turn those who are rebellious back to a right understanding—to prepare a people ready for the Lord.”
042	LUK	001	018	“How can I be sure about this?” Zechariah asked the angel. “I'm an old man, and my wife is getting old too.”
042	LUK	001	019	“I am Gabriel,” the angel replied. “I stand in God's presence, and I was sent to speak to you and give you this good news.
042	LUK	001	020	But since you didn't believe what I told you, you'll become dumb, unable to speak, until the appointed time when my words come true.”
042	LUK	001	021	Outside the people were waiting for Zechariah, wondering why he was taking so long in the Temple.
042	LUK	001	022	When eventually he came out, he couldn't speak to them. They realized he'd seen a vision in the Temple, for though he could make gestures, he was completely unable to speak.
