# BOOK	044	ACT	Acts	Acts
044	ACT	001	001	Dear Theophilus, in my previous book I wrote about all that Jesus did and taught from the beginning
044	ACT	001	002	until the day he was taken up to heaven. This was after he'd given instructions through the Holy Spirit to his chosen apostles.
044	ACT	001	003	Over the course of forty days after the death he suffered, he showed himself to them, proving that he was alive with convincing evidence. He appeared to them, and told them about the kingdom of God.
044	ACT	001	004	While he was still with them he instructed them, “Do not leave Jerusalem. Wait to receive what the Father promised, just as you heard it from me.
044	ACT	001	005	It's true that John baptized in water, but in just a few days' time you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit.”
044	ACT	001	006	So when the disciples met with Jesus, they asked him, “Lord, is this the time when you will re-establish Israel's kingdom?”
044	ACT	001	007	“You don't need to know about the dates and times that are set by the Father's authority,” he told them.
044	ACT	001	008	“But you will be given power when the Holy Spirit comes upon you, and you will be my witnesses in Jerusalem, throughout Judea and Samaria, and to the farthest places on earth.”
044	ACT	001	009	After Jesus had told them this, he was taken up as they were watching and a cloud hid him from their sight.
044	ACT	001	010	While they were staring intently at the sky as he ascended, two men dressed in white were suddenly standing beside them.
044	ACT	001	011	“Men of Galilee, why are you standing here staring at the sky?” they asked. “This same Jesus who has been taken up from you to heaven shall come in the same way you saw him go into heaven.”
044	ACT	001	012	Then the disciples went back to Jerusalem from the Mount of Olives which is about a Sabbath day's walk from Jerusalem.
044	ACT	001	013	When they arrived, they went upstairs to the upper room where they were staying: Peter, John, James and Andrew; Philip and Thomas; Bartholomew and Matthew; James the son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas the son of James.
044	ACT	001	014	They all joined together in prayer, together with the women and Mary, Jesus' mother, and his brothers.
044	ACT	001	015	At this time Peter stood up and addressed a crowd of around one hundred and twenty believers who had gathered together.
044	ACT	001	016	“My brothers and sisters,” he said, “The Scriptures, spoken by the Holy Spirit through David, had to be fulfilled regarding Judas, who guided those who arrested Jesus.
044	ACT	001	017	He was counted as one of us, and shared in this ministry.”
044	ACT	001	018	(Judas had bought a field with his ill-gotten gains. There he fell down headfirst, and his body burst apart, spilling out all his intestines.
044	ACT	001	019	Everybody who lived in Jerusalem heard about this so that the field was called in their language “Akeldama,” which means, “Field of blood.”)
044	ACT	001	020	As it's written in the book of Psalms, “Let his home be abandoned, and no one live there,” and “Let someone else take over his position.”
044	ACT	001	021	“So now we have to choose someone who has been with us the whole time that Jesus was with us,
044	ACT	001	022	from the time John was baptizing up until the day Jesus was taken up to heaven from us. One of these must be chosen to join together with us as we witness, giving evidence of Jesus' resurrection.”
044	ACT	001	023	Two names were put forward: Joseph Justus, also known as Barsabbas, and Matthias.
044	ACT	001	024	They prayed together and said, “Lord, you know everyone's thoughts. Please show us which of these two you have chosen
044	ACT	001	025	to replace Judas as an apostle in this ministry that he gave up to go to where he belongs.”
044	ACT	001	026	They cast lots, and Matthias was chosen. He was counted as an apostle with the other eleven.
044	ACT	002	001	When the day of Pentecost came, they were all meeting together in one place.
044	ACT	002	002	Suddenly a noise came from heaven like a roaring wind that filled the whole house where they were staying.
044	ACT	002	003	They saw what looked like separate tongue-shaped flames that settled on each of them.
044	ACT	002	004	All of them were filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in different languages as the Spirit gave them the ability to do so.
044	ACT	002	005	At that time there were devout Jews from every nation on earth living in Jerusalem.
044	ACT	002	006	When they heard this noise, a large crowd of them gathered. They were puzzled because everyone heard their own language being spoken.
044	ACT	002	007	They were totally amazed, saying, “Look, these people who are speaking—aren't they all Galileans?
044	ACT	002	008	So how is it that we can all hear them speaking in our own mother tongue?
044	ACT	002	009	Parthians, Medes and Elamites; people from Mesopotamia, Judaea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,
044	ACT	002	010	Phrygia and Pamphylia; from Egypt and the area of Libya around Cyrene; visitors from Rome, both Jews and converts,
044	ACT	002	011	Cretans and Arabians—we hear them speaking in our own languages about all the great things God has done.”
044	ACT	002	012	They were all amazed and confused. “What does this mean?” they asked each other.
