044	ACT	003	001	Peter and John were on their way up to the Temple at the time of the afternoon prayer, around 3 p.m.
044	ACT	003	002	A man who had been lame from birth was being carried there. Every day he was placed beside the Temple gate called “Beautiful” so he could beg from the people going into the Temple.
044	ACT	003	003	He saw Peter and John as they were about to enter the Temple and asked them for some money.
044	ACT	003	004	Peter looked right at him. John did, too. “Look at us!” Peter said.
044	ACT	003	005	The lame man gave them his full attention, expecting to get something from them.
044	ACT	003	006	“I don't have any silver or gold,” Peter told him, “but I'll give you what I have. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, walk!”
044	ACT	003	007	Peter took him by the right hand and helped him up. Right away his feet and ankles became strong.
044	ACT	003	008	He jumped to his feet, and then began to walk. He went with them into the Temple, walking and jumping and praising God.
044	ACT	003	009	Everyone there saw him walking around and praising God.
044	ACT	003	010	They recognized him as the beggar who used to sit by the Temple's Beautiful Gate, and they were surprised and amazed at what had happened to him.
044	ACT	003	011	He held on tightly to Peter and John while everyone ran to them by Solomon's Porch in complete astonishment at what had happened.
044	ACT	003	012	When Peter saw this opportunity he told them, “People of Israel, why are you surprised at what's happened to this man? Why are you staring at us as if it was by our own power or faith that we made him walk?
044	ACT	003	013	The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob—the God of our forefathers—has glorified his servant Jesus. He was the one you betrayed and rejected in the presence of Pilate, even after Pilate had decided to release him.
044	ACT	003	014	You rejected the one who is holy and good, and demanded a murderer be released to you.
044	ACT	003	015	You killed the author of life, the one God raised from the dead—and we are witnesses to this.
044	ACT	003	016	By trusting in Jesus' name this man was healed by him. You see this man here; you know him. Through trusting in Jesus this man has received complete healing right in front of all of you.
044	ACT	003	017	Now I know, brothers and sisters, that you did this in ignorance, like your rulers.
044	ACT	003	018	But God fulfilled what he had prophesied through all the prophets: that his Messiah would suffer.
044	ACT	003	019	Now repent, and change your ways, that your sins can be wiped away, so the Lord can send opportunities for you to heal and recover,
044	ACT	003	020	and send Jesus, the Messiah appointed for you.
