044	ACT	003	023	Anybody who doesn't listen to him will be totally removed from the people.’
044	ACT	003	024	All the prophets who have spoken, from Samuel on, prophesied about these days.
044	ACT	003	025	You are the sons of the prophets, and of the agreement which God made with your fathers when he said to Abraham, ‘From your descendants all the families of the earth will be blessed.’
044	ACT	003	026	God prepared his Servant and sent him to you first, to bless you by turning every one of you from your evil ways.”
044	ACT	004	001	While they were talking to the people, the priests, the captain of the Temple guard, and the Sadducees came up to them.
044	ACT	004	002	They were angry that they were teaching the people, telling them that through Jesus there is resurrection from the dead.
044	ACT	004	003	They arrested them and placed them under guard until the following day since it was already evening.
044	ACT	004	004	But many who had heard the message believed it, and the total number of believers grew to about five thousand.
044	ACT	004	005	The next day, the rulers, elders, and religious leaders met together in Jerusalem.
044	ACT	004	006	They included the high priest Annas, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and others of the high priest's family.
044	ACT	004	007	They brought Peter and John before them and asked, “By what power or by whose authority have you done this?”
