045	ROM	014	021	It's better not to eat meat or drink wine or anything else that would cause your fellow-believer to stumble.
045	ROM	014	022	What you personally believe is between you and God. Happy are those who don't condemn themselves for doing what they think is right!
045	ROM	014	023	But if you have doubts whether it's right or wrong to eat something, then you shouldn't, because you're not convinced it's right. Whatever isn't based on conviction is sin.
045	ROM	015	001	Those of us who are spiritually strong ought to support those who are spiritually weak. We shouldn't just please ourselves.
045	ROM	015	002	We should all encourage others to do what's morally right, building them up.
045	ROM	015	003	Christ didn't live to please himself, but as Scripture says of him, “The insults of those who abused you have fallen on me.”
045	ROM	015	004	These Scriptures were written down in the past to help us understand, and to encourage us so that we could wait patiently in hope.
045	ROM	015	005	May the God who gives patience and encouragement help you to be in full agreement among yourselves as you follow Christ Jesus,
045	ROM	015	006	so that you can with one mind and with one voice together glorify God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ!
045	ROM	015	007	So accept one another, just as Christ accepted you, and give God the glory.
045	ROM	015	008	I maintain that Christ came as a servant to the Jews to show God tells the truth, keeping the promises he made to their forefathers.
045	ROM	015	009	He also came that foreigners could praise God for his mercy, as Scripture says, “Therefore I will praise you among the foreigners; I will sing praises to your name.”
045	ROM	015	010	And also: “Foreigners, celebrate with his people!”
045	ROM	015	011	And again: “All you foreigners, praise the Lord, let all peoples praise him.”
045	ROM	015	012	And again, Isaiah says, “Jesse's descendant will come to rule the nations, and foreigners will put their hope in him.”
045	ROM	015	013	May the God of hope completely fill you with all joy and peace as you trust in him, so that you will overflow with hope through the power of the Holy Spirit!
045	ROM	015	014	I'm convinced that you, my brothers and sisters, are full of goodness, and that you are filled with every kind of knowledge, so you are well able to teach one another.
045	ROM	015	015	I've been blunt in the way I have written to you about some of these things, but this is just to remind you. For God gave me grace
045	ROM	015	016	to be a minister of Christ Jesus to the foreigners, like a priest sharing God's good news, so that they could become an acceptable offering, made holy by the Holy Spirit.
045	ROM	015	017	So even though I have something to boast about because of my service for God,
045	ROM	015	018	(I wouldn't dare talk about any of this except as Christ has done it through me), I have led foreigners to obedience through my teaching and demonstration,
045	ROM	015	019	through the power of signs and miracles done with the Holy Spirit's power. From Jerusalem all the way over to Illyricum, everywhere I've shared fully the good news of Christ.
045	ROM	015	020	In fact I was keen to spread the good news in places that hadn't heard the name of Christ, so that I wouldn't be building on what others have done.
045	ROM	015	021	As Scripture says, “Those who haven't been told the good news will discover him, and those who haven't heard will understand.”
045	ROM	015	022	That's why I was prevented so many times from coming to see you.
045	ROM	015	023	But now, as there's nowhere left here to work, and since I've looked forward to visiting you for many years,
045	ROM	015	024	when I go to Spain I hope to see you when I pass through. Maybe you can give me some help for my journey once we've enjoyed some time together.
045	ROM	015	025	At the moment I'm on my way to Jerusalem to help the believers there,
045	ROM	015	026	because the believers in Macedonia and Achaia thought it was a good idea to send a contribution to the poor among the believers in Jerusalem.
045	ROM	015	027	They were happy to do this because they're in their debt. Now that foreigners are sharing their spiritual benefits, they owe it to the Jewish believers to help them in material things.
045	ROM	015	028	So once I've done this, and have safely delivered this contribution to them, I'll visit you on my way to Spain.
045	ROM	015	029	I know that when I come, Christ will give us his full blessing.
045	ROM	015	030	I want to encourage you, my brothers and sisters through our Lord Jesus Christ and through the love of the Spirit, to join together in praying hard for me.
045	ROM	015	031	Pray that I may be kept safe from the unbelievers in Judea. Pray that my work in Jerusalem will be welcomed by the believers there.
045	ROM	015	032	Pray that I will come to you with gladness, as God wills, so we can enjoy one another's company.
045	ROM	015	033	May the God of peace be with you all. Amen.
045	ROM	016	001	I recommend to you our sister Phoebe, who is a deaconess at the Cenchreae church.
045	ROM	016	002	Please welcome her in the Lord, as believers should, and help her in whatever way she needs, because she has been a great help to many people, myself included.
045	ROM	016	003	Pass on my greetings to Prisca and Aquila, my co-workers in Christ Jesus,
045	ROM	016	004	who risked their lives for me. It's not just me who is very thankful for them, but all the churches of the foreigners too.
045	ROM	016	005	Please also give my greetings to the church that meets in their home. Pass on my best wishes to my good friend Epaenetus, the first person to follow Christ in the province of Asia.
045	ROM	016	006	Give my greetings to Mary, who worked hard for you,
045	ROM	016	007	and also Andronicus and Junia, from my own country and fellow-prisoners. They are well-known among the apostles, and became followers of Christ before me.
045	ROM	016	008	Give my best to Ampliatus, my good friend in the Lord;
045	ROM	016	009	to Urbanus, our co-worker in Christ; and to my dear friend Stachys.
045	ROM	016	010	My greetings to Apelles, a trustworthy man in Christ. Greetings to Aristobulus's family,
045	ROM	016	011	to my countryman Herodion, and to those from Narcissus' family who belong to the Lord.
045	ROM	016	012	My best wishes to Tryphaena and Tryphosa, hard workers for the Lord, and to my friend Persis, who has done so much in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	013	Give my greetings to Rufus, an exceptional worker, and his mother—who I count as my mother too.
045	ROM	016	014	Greetings to Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the fellow-believers who are with them.
045	ROM	016	015	Best wishes to Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, Olympas, and to all the believers with them.
045	ROM	016	016	Greet one another affectionately. All the churches of Christ send their greetings to you.
045	ROM	016	017	Now I'm pleading with you my fellow-believers: watch out for those who cause arguments and confuse people about the teachings you learned. Stay away from them!
045	ROM	016	018	These people are not serving Christ our Lord but their own appetites, and by their smooth-talking and pleasant words they deceive the minds of unsuspecting people.
045	ROM	016	019	Everyone knows how faithful you are. This makes me really happy. However, I want you to be wise about what's good, and innocent of anything bad.
045	ROM	016	020	The God of peace will soon break the power of Satan and make him subject to you. May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
045	ROM	016	021	Timothy my co-worker sends his greetings, as do Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my fellow-countrymen.
045	ROM	016	022	Tertius—who wrote down this letter—also sends you greetings in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	023	My host Gaius, and the whole church here, send you greetings. Erastus the city treasurer, sends his best wishes, as does our fellow-believer Quartus.
045	ROM	016	025	Now to him who can make you strong Through the good news I share and the message of Jesus Christ, According to the mystery of truth that has been revealed, The mystery of truth, hidden for eternity,
045	ROM	016	026	now made visible; Through the prophets' writings, and Following the command of the eternal God, The mystery of truth is made known to everyone everywhere so they can trust and obey him;
045	ROM	016	027	To the one and only wise God, Through Jesus Christ— To him be glory for ever. Amen.
#
# BOOK	046	1CO	1 Corinthians	1 Corinthians
046	1CO	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, called to be an apostle of Jesus Christ according to the will of God, and from Sosthenes, our brother.
046	1CO	001	002	It is sent to the church of God in Corinth, those who are being made right in Christ Jesus, called to live holy lives—and to everyone who worships the Lord Jesus Christ everywhere, the Lord both of them and of us.
046	1CO	001	003	May you have grace and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	004	I'm always thanking God for you because of the grace of God given to you in Christ Jesus.
046	1CO	001	005	Through him you have been made rich in everything, in all that you say and every aspect of what you know.
046	1CO	001	006	In fact the testimony of Christ was proved valid in your experience,
046	1CO	001	007	so that you're not missing any spiritual gift as you wait for the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	008	He will also keep you strong to the very end, so you will be kept right until the day of the Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	009	God is trustworthy who called you to share together in fellowship with his son Jesus Christ our Lord.
046	1CO	001	010	Brothers and sisters, I plead with you in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ that you all agree and that you're not divided. Instead develop a united attitude and purpose.
046	1CO	001	011	For I have been told things about you, my brothers and sisters, by some of Chloe's people—that you are quarreling among yourselves.
046	1CO	001	012	Let me explain what I mean. You're all making different claims: “I follow Paul,” or “I follow Apollos,” or “I follow Peter,” or “I follow Christ.”
046	1CO	001	013	Is Christ divided? Did Paul die on a cross for you? Was it in the name of Paul that you were baptized?
046	1CO	001	014	I'm grateful to God that I didn't baptize any of you, except Crispus and Gaius,
046	1CO	001	015	so nobody can claim they were baptized in my name.
046	1CO	001	016	(Oh, and I also baptized the Stephanas family—I can't think of anyone else.)
046	1CO	001	017	For Christ didn't send me out to baptize, but to spread the good news, and not with eloquent human wisdom, otherwise the cross of Christ would be made powerless.
046	1CO	001	018	For the message of the cross is nonsense to those who are lost, but it's the power of God to those of us who are saved.
046	1CO	001	019	As Scripture says, “I will destroy the wisdom of the wise, and I will wipe out the cleverness of the clever.”
046	1CO	001	020	So how about the wise, the writers, and the philosophers of this age? Hasn't God turned the wisdom of this world into foolishness?
046	1CO	001	021	Since God in his wisdom allowed the world in its wisdom not to know God, it was God's gracious plan that by the foolishness of the good news those who trusted in him would be saved.
046	1CO	001	022	The Jews ask for miraculous signs, and Greeks look for wisdom,
046	1CO	001	023	but our message is of Christ killed on a cross—offensive to the Jews, and foolishness to the foreigners.
046	1CO	001	024	However, for those who are called by God, both Jews and foreigners, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God.
046	1CO	001	025	For the foolishness of God is wiser than we are; and the weakness of God is stronger than we are.
046	1CO	001	026	Brothers and sisters, remember your calling—and that this did not include many who are wise, humanly speaking; not many who are powerful; not many who are important.
046	1CO	001	027	Instead God chose the things the world considers foolish to humiliate those who think they are wise. He chose the things the world considers weak to humiliate those who think they are strong.
046	1CO	001	028	He chose the things that are unimportant and despised by the world, even things that are not, to bring to nothing the things that are,
046	1CO	001	029	so that nobody should boast in God's presence.
046	1CO	001	030	It's because of him that you live in Christ Jesus, who God made to be wisdom for us. He sets us right, keeps us right, and frees us.
046	1CO	001	031	So as Scripture says, “Whoever wants to boast, let them boast in the Lord.”
046	1CO	002	001	Brothers and sisters, when I came to you I didn't try to impress you with wonderful words or great wisdom when I told you what God had to say to you.
046	1CO	002	002	I decided that while I was with you I didn't want to concentrate on anything except Jesus Christ, and that he was crucified.
046	1CO	002	003	I came to you in weakness, fearful and trembling.
046	1CO	002	004	I didn't speak to you with persuasive words of wisdom to convince you. I just explained it all to you through the evidence and power of the Spirit.
046	1CO	002	005	That way your trust in God wouldn't rely on human wisdom but on the power of God.
046	1CO	002	006	However, we do use words of wisdom when we speak to those who are spiritually mature, but this isn't wisdom that comes from this world, or from the rulers of this world who soon fade from the scene.
046	1CO	002	007	On the contrary we explain God's wisdom in terms of a revealed mystery that was previously hidden which God planned for our glory before the creation of the worlds.
046	1CO	002	008	None of the rulers of this world understood anything about this—for if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.
046	1CO	002	009	But as Scripture says, “No one has ever seen, and no one has ever heard, and no one has ever imagined what God has prepared for those who love him.”
046	1CO	002	010	But God has revealed this to us through the Spirit, because the Spirit delves into the depths of God.
046	1CO	002	011	Who knows anyone's thoughts except the actual person? In the same way no one knows God's thoughts except the Spirit of God.
046	1CO	002	012	For we have received the Spirit from God, not the spirit of this world, so that we could understand what God so generously gave us.
046	1CO	002	013	That's what we speak about—not using words taught by human wisdom, but what the Spirit teaches. We explain what is spiritual using spiritual terms.
046	1CO	002	014	Of course people who are not spiritual don't accept what comes from God's Spirit. It's just foolish nonsense to them, and they can't understand it, because what is spiritual has to be properly examined.
046	1CO	002	015	People who are spiritual investigate everything, but are not placed under investigation themselves.
046	1CO	002	016	For “who understands the Lord's mind, and would think to instruct him?” But we do have Christ's mind!
046	1CO	003	001	My brothers and sisters, I couldn't talk with you as spiritual believers, but as worldly people—like baby Christians.
046	1CO	003	002	I gave you milk—I couldn't give you solid food to eat, because you weren't ready for it.
046	1CO	003	003	Even now you're not ready for it, because you're still worldly. Since you're still jealous and argumentative, doesn't that show you're worldly, behaving just like ordinary people do?
046	1CO	003	004	When one of you says, “I follow Paul,” while another says, “I follow Apollos,” doesn't that show you're being so very human?
046	1CO	003	005	Who is Apollos, anyway? And who is Paul? We're just servants through whom you believed. Each of us does the work God gave us to do.
046	1CO	003	006	I did the planting, Apollos did the watering—but it was God who made you grow!
046	1CO	003	007	So the one who does the planting doesn't count for anything, any more than the one who does the watering. The only one who matters is God who is growing you!
046	1CO	003	008	The one planting and the one watering have the same goal, and both will be rewarded according to what they've done.
046	1CO	003	009	We are workers together with God—and you are God's field, his building.
046	1CO	003	010	Through the grace of God that he gave to me, I laid down the foundation like a skilled building supervisor. Now someone else is building on it. Whoever does the building needs to watch what they're doing.
046	1CO	003	011	For no one can lay any other foundation than what's already laid—that is Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	003	012	Those who build on that foundation may use gold, silver, precious stone, wood, hay, or straw—
046	1CO	003	013	but whatever is used to build with will be exposed. For on the Day of Judgment, fire will reveal it and test it. Everyone's work will be shown for what it is.
046	1CO	003	014	Those whose building survives will be rewarded.
046	1CO	003	015	Those whose building is burned up will lose out. They will still be saved, but it will be like passing through fire!
046	1CO	003	016	Don't you know you are God's temple and that God's Spirit lives in you?
046	1CO	003	017	Anyone who destroys God's temple will be destroyed by God, for God's temple is holy, and you are the temple.
046	1CO	003	018	Don't deceive yourselves. If there's any one of you who thinks they're worldly wise, they should become fools so they can become truly wise!
046	1CO	003	019	This world's wisdom is plain foolishness to God. As Scripture says, “He uses the cleverness of the wise to catch them out,”
046	1CO	003	020	and “The Lord knows the arguments of the wise are pointless.”
046	1CO	003	021	So don't boast about people. For you have everything,
046	1CO	003	022	whether it's Paul or Apollos or Peter—or the world, or life, or death, or the present, or the future. You have everything—
046	1CO	003	023	and you are Christ's, and Christ is God's.
046	1CO	004	001	So think of us as Christ's servants given the responsibility for “the mysteries of God.”
046	1CO	004	002	More than this, those who have such responsibilities are required to be trustworthy.
046	1CO	004	003	Personally it hardly matters to me if you or anyone else judges me—in fact I don't even judge myself.
046	1CO	004	004	I don't know of anything I've done wrong, but that doesn't make me morally right. It's the Lord who judges me.
046	1CO	004	005	So don't judge anything before the right time—when the Lord comes. He will bring to light all the darkest secrets that are hidden, and he will reveal people's motives. God will give everyone whatever praise they deserve.
046	1CO	004	006	Now, brothers and sisters, I have applied this to Apollos and myself as an example for you. That way you will learn not to go beyond what has been written, and not in arrogance prefer one over the other.
046	1CO	004	007	Who made you so special? What do you have that you weren't given? Since you were given it, why do you proudly claim you weren't?
046	1CO	004	008	You think you have all you need. You think you're so wealthy. You think you're kings already, and don't need us. I wish you were really ruling as kings, so we could rule with you!
046	1CO	004	009	The way I see it, God has put us apostles on display as the last in the line, condemned to die. We have been made a public show before the entire universe, to angels and to human beings.
046	1CO	004	010	We're Christ's fools, but you are so wise in Christ! We're the weak ones, but you are so strong! You have the glory, but we are despised!
046	1CO	004	011	Right up till now we're hungry and thirsty. We have no clothes. We're badly beaten up, and we have no place to call home.
046	1CO	004	012	We struggle on doing manual work. When people curse us, we bless them. When they persecute us, we put up with it.
046	1CO	004	013	When they insult us, we respond with kindness. Even now we are treated like dirt, the worst trash in the whole world.
046	1CO	004	014	I'm not writing like this to make you feel ashamed, but to caution you as my children whom I love so much.
046	1CO	004	015	Even though you may have thousands of Christian instructors, you don't have many fathers—it was in Christ Jesus that I became your father when I shared the good news with you.
046	1CO	004	016	So I'm pleading with you to imitate me!
046	1CO	004	017	That's why I sent Timothy to you, my trustworthy son in the Lord whom I love so much. He will remind you about the way I follow Christ, just as I always teach in every church I visit.
046	1CO	004	018	Some among you have become arrogant, thinking I wouldn't bother coming to see you.
046	1CO	004	019	But I am coming to visit you soon, if that's what the Lord wants. Then I'll find out what these arrogant people are saying, and what kind of power they have.
046	1CO	004	020	For the kingdom of God is not about mere words, but about power.
046	1CO	004	021	So what do you want? Shall I come with a stick to beat you, or in love and a gentle spirit?
046	1CO	005	001	I hear reports that sexual immorality is happening among you, immorality that even the foreigners don't practice. A man is living with his father's wife!
046	1CO	005	002	You are so proud of yourselves! Shouldn't you have wept with sadness, and excluded the man who did this?
046	1CO	005	003	Even though I'm not physically present there, I am there in spirit and just as if I were there I've already made my judgment of the one who has done this.
046	1CO	005	004	When you meet together in the name of the Lord Jesus, I'll be there with you in spirit and with the power of our Lord Jesus.
046	1CO	005	005	Hand over this man to Satan so his sinful nature may be destroyed and he himself be saved on the day of the Lord.
046	1CO	005	006	You shouldn't be proud about this. Don't you know that it only takes a little yeast to make the whole batch of dough rise?
046	1CO	005	007	Get rid of this old yeast so that you can be a new batch of dough to make bread without yeast. Christ our Passover lamb has been sacrificed.
046	1CO	005	008	So let us celebrate this festival, not with old yeast or the yeast of evil and wickedness, but with the bread made without yeast, the bread of sincerity and truth.
046	1CO	005	009	In my previous letter I wrote that you should not associate with immoral people.
046	1CO	005	010	I wasn't referring to the immoral people of this world, those who are greedy and cheat others, or those who worship idols, otherwise you'd have to leave this world!
046	1CO	005	011	What I meant when I wrote was that you shouldn't associate with anyone who is called a Christian who is immoral or greedy or worships idols; or who is abusive or a drunkard or who cheats others. Don't even share a meal with anyone like that!
046	1CO	005	012	It's not my place to judge those outside the church. But shouldn't you judge those who are inside the church?
046	1CO	005	013	God judges those that are outside the church. “Expel the wicked from among you.”
046	1CO	006	001	How dare any of you file a lawsuit before pagan judges if you have a dispute with your neighbor! Instead you should bring this before other believers.
046	1CO	006	002	Don't you know that Christian believers will judge the world? If you're going to judge the world, are you not fit to judge in the most minor cases?
046	1CO	006	003	Don't you know we are going to judge angels? How much more those things that relate to this life!
046	1CO	006	004	So if you have to judge things that relate to this life, how can you go to judges that are not respected by the church?
046	1CO	006	005	I'm trying to shame you by saying this. What? You can't find one wise person among you who can settle a dispute that you have?
046	1CO	006	006	Instead one believer takes another believer to court, and places the issue before unbelievers!
046	1CO	006	007	The very fact you have lawsuits against each other already is a complete disaster. Wouldn't it be better to accept the injustice? Why not let yourselves be defrauded?
046	1CO	006	008	But you would rather cause injustice and defraud even your fellow-believers in church.
046	1CO	006	009	Don't you know those who are unjust will not inherit the kingdom of God? Don't be fooled! People who are immoral, worship idols, commit adultery, are sexual perverts, homosexuals,
046	1CO	006	010	thieves, greedy, drunkards, abusers, or cheats, will not inherit the kingdom of God.
046	1CO	006	011	Some of you were once like that, but you have been made clean and holy. You have been made right in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ, and in the Spirit of our God.
046	1CO	006	012	People say, “I'm free to do anything”—but not everything is appropriate! “I'm free to do anything”—but I will not let anything control me! People say,
046	1CO	006	013	“Food for the stomach, and the stomach for food”—but God will destroy both of them. Also, the body is not meant to be used for immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body.
046	1CO	006	014	By his power God raised the Lord from the dead, and he will raise us up the same way.
046	1CO	006	015	Don't you know your bodies are parts of Christ's body? Should I take the parts of Christ's body and join them to a prostitute? Absolutely not!
046	1CO	006	016	Don't you realize that anyone who has sex with a prostitute becomes “one body” with her? Remember that Scripture says, “The two will become one body.”
046	1CO	006	017	But whoever is joined to the Lord is one with him in spirit!
046	1CO	006	018	Stay away from sexual immorality! All other sins that people commit are outside of the body, but sexual immorality is a sin against your own body.
046	1CO	006	019	Don't you know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit that is within you, that you received from God?
046	1CO	006	020	You don't belong to yourself—a price was paid for you! So glorify God in your body!
046	1CO	007	001	Now about what you wrote to me: “It's good not to marry.”
046	1CO	007	002	However, because of the temptation to sexual immorality, it is better that each man have his own wife, and each woman her own husband.
046	1CO	007	003	The husband should meet his wife's sexual needs, and the wife her husband's.
046	1CO	007	004	The wife's body doesn't just belong to her, but her husband; and similarly the husband's body doesn't just belong to him but his wife.
046	1CO	007	005	So don't deprive each other, except by mutual consent for a while—for example because you want to spend time in prayer. Afterwards come together again so that Satan won't tempt you to sin because of your lack of self-control.
046	1CO	007	006	I'm telling you this not as a command, but as a concession.
046	1CO	007	007	However, I wish that everyone was like me, but each person has their own gift from God—one has this gift, one has another.
046	1CO	007	008	To those who are not yet married, or who are widowed, I would say it is better if they remain like me.
046	1CO	007	009	But if they lack self-control, then they should get married—for it is better to marry than burn with desire.
046	1CO	007	010	These are my instructions to those who are married—in fact not from me but the Lord: The wife should not leave her husband
046	1CO	007	011	(or if she does, she should not remarry, or she should return to her husband); and the husband should not leave his wife.
046	1CO	007	012	Now, to the rest of you (and this is me speaking, not the Lord), I would say, If a Christian man has a non-Christian wife and she is willing to stay with him, he should not leave her.
046	1CO	007	013	And if a Christian woman has a non-Christian husband, and he is willing to stay with her, she should not leave her husband.
046	1CO	007	014	For a husband who is not a Christian, the marriage relationship is made holy by the Christian wife, and for a wife who is not a Christian, the marriage relationship is made holy by the Christian husband. Otherwise it would mean your children were impure, but now they are holy.
046	1CO	007	015	However, if the non-Christian spouse leaves, let them leave. In such cases the Christian man or woman is not slavishly bound, for God has called us to live in peace.
046	1CO	007	016	Wives, who knows? You may save your husband! Husbands, who knows? You may save your wife!
046	1CO	007	017	Apart from such cases, each of you should remain in the situation that the Lord has placed you, and continue to live the life to which God has called you. That's my instruction to all the churches.
046	1CO	007	018	Were you circumcised when you were converted? Don't become uncircumcised. Were you uncircumcised when you were converted? Don't become circumcised.
046	1CO	007	019	Circumcision doesn't mean anything, and uncircumcision doesn't mean anything. Keeping the commandments of God is what really matters.
046	1CO	007	020	Everyone should remain in the position they were in when they were called.
046	1CO	007	021	If you were a slave when you were called, don't worry—though if you have an opportunity to become free, take it.
046	1CO	007	022	If you were a slave when the Lord called you, you are now free, working for the Lord. In the same way if you were called when you were free, you are now Christ's slave!
046	1CO	007	023	A price has been paid for you, so don't become a slave to anyone.
046	1CO	007	024	Brothers and sisters, remain in the position you were in when you were called, living with God.
046	1CO	007	025	Now about “people who are not married,” I don't have a specific instruction from the Lord, so let me give you my opinion as someone who by the Lord's mercy is considered trustworthy.
046	1CO	007	026	Because of the present difficult situation we are in I think it is best to just stay as you are.
046	1CO	007	027	Are you already married? Don't try to get divorced. Are you unmarried? Don't look to get married.
046	1CO	007	028	If you do get married, you haven't sinned. If an unmarried woman gets married, she hasn't sinned. But you will have many troubles in this current world and I would want to spare you these.
046	1CO	007	029	I'm telling you, brothers and sisters, that time is short, and from now on for those who are married it may seem as if they are not married,
046	1CO	007	030	and those who weep as if they did not weep, and those that celebrated as if they had not celebrated, and those that bought as if they did not own,
046	1CO	007	031	and those who are engaged with the world as if it is not fulfilling—for the present world order is passing away.
046	1CO	007	032	I would prefer you to be free from such worries. A man who is not married pays attention to what is important to the Lord, and how he can please the Lord.
046	1CO	007	033	But a man who is married pays attention to what is important in this world, and how he can please his wife.
046	1CO	007	034	As a result his loyalties are divided. Similarly an unmarried woman or girl pays attention to what is important to the Lord, so she may live a life dedicated both in body and spirit. But a married woman pays attention to what is important in this world, and how she can please her husband.
046	1CO	007	035	I'm telling you this for your benefit. I'm not trying to put a noose around your neck, but to show you the right thing to do so you can serve the Lord without being distracted.
046	1CO	007	036	But if a man thinks he's behaving improperly with the woman he's engaged to, and if he thinks he will give in to his strong sexual desire, and if he thinks he ought to get married, he is not sinning by getting married.
046	1CO	007	037	But if a man stays true to his principles, and there is no obligation to marry, and if he has the power to keep his feelings under control and stay engaged to her, he does well not to marry.
046	1CO	007	038	So the man who marries the woman he's engaged to does well, while the one who does not get married does better.
046	1CO	007	039	A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is free to marry anyone she wants in the Lord.
046	1CO	007	040	But in my opinion she would be happier if she didn't remarry—and I think I too have the Spirit of God when I say this.
046	1CO	008	001	Now about “food sacrificed to idols.” So “we all have knowledge” about this subject. Knowledge makes us proud, but love strengthens us.
046	1CO	008	002	If anyone thinks they know anything, they don't know as they really should know!
046	1CO	008	003	But whoever loves God is known by God.
046	1CO	008	004	So regarding eating food sacrificed to idols: we know that there are no such things as idols in the world, and that there is only one real God.
046	1CO	008	005	Even though there are some things called “gods,” whether in heaven or on earth—in fact there are many “gods” and “lords.”
046	1CO	008	006	But for us there is only one God, the Father, from whom everything was made, and he is the goal of our existence; and one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom everything was made, and he is the means of our existence.
046	1CO	008	007	But not everyone has this “knowledge.” Some who up to now have been so used to idols as a reality that when they eat food sacrificed to an idol, their conscience (which is weak) tells them they have defiled themselves.
046	1CO	008	008	But food doesn't gain us God's approval! If we don't eat this food, we're not bad, and if we do eat this food, we're not good.
046	1CO	008	009	Just take care not to use this freedom you have to eat food sacrificed to idols to become offensive to those with a weaker attitude.
046	1CO	008	010	If another believer sees you who have such “better knowledge” eating food in an idol temple, won't his weak conscience be convinced to eat food sacrificed to idols?
046	1CO	008	011	By your “better knowledge” the weaker believer is destroyed, a believer for whom Christ died.
046	1CO	008	012	In this way you sin against other believers, wounding their weaker consciences, and you sin against Christ.
046	1CO	008	013	So if eating food sacrificed to idols would cause my fellow believer to stumble, I will never eat such meat ever again, so that I don't offend any believer.
046	1CO	009	001	Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Haven't I seen Jesus our Lord? Aren't you the results of my work in the Lord?
046	1CO	009	002	Even if I'm not an apostle to others, at least I am one to you. The proof of my being an apostle of the Lord is you!
046	1CO	009	003	Here is my reply to those who question me about this:
046	1CO	009	004	Don't we have the right to be provided with food and drink?
046	1CO	009	005	Don't we have a right to be accompanied by a Christian wife, like the rest of the apostles, the Lord's brothers, and Peter?
046	1CO	009	006	Is it only Barnabas and myself who have to work to support ourselves?
046	1CO	009	007	Which soldier ever had to pay his own salary? Who plants a vineyard and doesn't get to eat its fruits? Who feeds a flock and doesn't consume its milk?
046	1CO	009	008	Am I just speaking from a human point of view? Doesn't the law say the same thing?
046	1CO	009	009	In the law of Moses it's written, “Don't muzzle the ox when it's threshing out the grain.” Was God just thinking about oxen?
046	1CO	009	010	Wasn't he directing this at us? Surely this was written for us—for anyone who plows should plow in hope and anyone who threshes should hope to share in the harvest.
046	1CO	009	011	If we sowed what is spiritual with you, does it really matter if we reap some material benefit?
046	1CO	009	012	If others exercise this right over you, don't we deserve it even more? Even so we did not exercise this right. On the contrary we would rather put up with anything than hold back the gospel of Christ.
046	1CO	009	013	Don't you know that those who work in temples receive their meals from temple offerings, and those who serve at the altar receive their portion of the sacrifice on the altar?
046	1CO	009	014	In just the same way the Lord ordered that those who announce the good news should live from supporters of the good news.
046	1CO	009	015	But I have not made use of any of these provisions, and I'm not writing about this to suggest it should be done in my case. I'd rather die than to have anyone take away my pride in not having received any benefit.
046	1CO	009	016	I have nothing to boast about in sharing the good news because it's something I feel compelled to do. In fact it's dreadful for me if I don't share the good news!
046	1CO	009	017	If I'm doing this work because of my own choice, then I have a reward. But if it wasn't my choice, and an obligation was placed on me,
046	1CO	009	018	then what reward do I have? It's the opportunity to share the good news without charging for it, not demanding my rights as a worker for the good news.
046	1CO	009	019	Even though I am free and serve no one, I have placed myself in service to everyone so that I might gain more.
046	1CO	009	020	To the Jews I behave like a Jew so that I might win Jews. To those who are under the law I behave as someone under the law (even though I am not obligated under the law), so that I might win those under the law.
046	1CO	009	021	To those who don't operate according to the law, I behave like them (though not disregarding God's law, but operating under the law of Christ), so that I might gain those who don't observe the law.
046	1CO	009	022	To those who are weak, I share in their weakness so that I may win the weak. I have ended up being “everyman” to everyone so that by using every possible means I might win some!
046	1CO	009	023	I do all this for the sake of the good news so that I too may share in its blessings!
046	1CO	009	024	Wouldn't you agree that there are many runners in a race, but only one gets the prize? So run your best, so you may win!
046	1CO	009	025	Every competitor who participates in the games maintains a strict training discipline. Of course they do so to win a crown that doesn't last. But our crowns will last forever!
046	1CO	009	026	That's why I run straight in the right direction. I fight accurately, not punching the air.
046	1CO	009	027	I also treat my body severely to bring it under my control, for I don't want somehow to be disqualified after sharing the good news with everybody else.
046	1CO	010	001	Now I want to explain this to you, brothers and sisters. Our forefathers lived under the cloud, and they all passed through the sea.
046	1CO	010	002	Symbolically then they were baptized “into Moses” in the cloud and in the sea.
046	1CO	010	003	They all ate the same spiritual food
046	1CO	010	004	and drank the same spiritual drink, for they “drank from a spiritual rock” that accompanied them. That rock was Christ.
046	1CO	010	005	However, God wasn't happy with most of them, and they perished in the desert.
046	1CO	010	006	Now these experiences are examples to us to show us we should not desire what is evil, as they did.
046	1CO	010	007	You must not worship idols, as some of them did, as it's recorded in Scripture: “The people feasted and drank, and indulged in pagan worship.”
046	1CO	010	008	We must not commit sexual sins, as some of them did, and as a result 23,000 died in one day.
046	1CO	010	009	Nor should we push God to the limit, as some of them did, and were killed by snakes.
046	1CO	010	010	Don't complain at God, as some did, and died at the hands of the destroying angel.
046	1CO	010	011	All the things that happened to them are examples to us and were written down to warn us, we who are living close to the end of time.
046	1CO	010	012	So if you think you're strong enough to stay standing—be careful you don't fall!
046	1CO	010	013	You won't experience any greater temptation than anyone else, and God is trustworthy. He won't allow you to be tempted more than you can bear, and when you are tempted, he will provide for you a way out so you can stay strong.
046	1CO	010	014	So my good friends, stay away from idol worship.
046	1CO	010	015	I'm talking to sensible people, so you decide whether I'm telling the truth.
046	1CO	010	016	When we give thanks for the cup we use in the Lord's Supper, don't we share in the blood of Christ? When we break the communion bread, don't we share in the body of Christ?
046	1CO	010	017	By eating from one loaf of bread, we show that even though we are many, we are one body.
046	1CO	010	018	Look at the people of Israel. Don't those who eat the sacrifices made on the altar share together?
046	1CO	010	019	What am I saying then? That anything sacrificed to idols means anything, or that an idol has any real existence? Of course not!
046	1CO	010	020	The pagans are sacrificing to demons, and not to God. I don't want you to have anything to do with demons!
046	1CO	010	021	You can't drink the Lord's cup as well as the cup of demons; you can't eat from the Lord's table as well as the table of demons.
046	1CO	010	022	Are we trying to make the Lord jealous? Are we stronger than he is?
046	1CO	010	023	Some say, “I'm free to do anything”—but not everything is appropriate! “I'm free to do anything”—but not everything is constructive!
046	1CO	010	024	You shouldn't look out for yourself, but for your neighbor.
046	1CO	010	025	Eat whatever is sold in the market without asking questions because of your conscience,
046	1CO	010	026	for “the earth and everything in it belong to God.”
046	1CO	010	027	If a non-Christian invites you to a meal, and you feel like going, eat whatever you are served, without asking questions because of your conscience.
046	1CO	010	028	But if someone tells you, “This food has been sacrificed to idols,” don't eat it for the sake of the one who mentioned it and for conscience' sake.
046	1CO	010	029	His conscience I mean, not yours. For why should my freedom be determined by someone else's conscience?
046	1CO	010	030	If I choose to eat with thankfulness, why should I be criticized for eating what I'm thankful to God for?
046	1CO	010	031	So whether you eat or drink or whatever you do, make sure to do everything to the glory of God.
046	1CO	010	032	Don't cause offense, whether it's to Jews or Greeks or the church of God—
046	1CO	010	033	just as I try to please everybody in all I do. I don't think of what benefits me, but what benefits others, so that they may be saved.
046	1CO	011	001	You should imitate me, just as I imitate Christ.
046	1CO	011	002	I'm grateful that you always remember me and that you are keeping to the teachings just as I passed them on to you.
046	1CO	011	003	I do want you to understand that Christ is the head of every man, the man is the head of the woman, and God is the head of Christ.
046	1CO	011	004	A man's head is dishonored if he prays or prophesies with his head covered.
046	1CO	011	005	A woman's head is dishonored if she prays or prophesies with her head uncovered—it's just as if she had her hair shaved off.
046	1CO	011	006	If a woman's head is not covered, then she should have her head shaved. If it's scandalous for a woman to be shorn or shaven, then she should have her head covered.
046	1CO	011	007	A man shouldn't cover his head, because he is the image and glory of God, while the woman is the glory of the man.
046	1CO	011	008	Man didn't come from woman, but woman came from man;
046	1CO	011	009	and man was not created for the woman, but the woman was created for the man.
046	1CO	011	010	That's why the woman should have this sign of authority on her head out of respect for the watching angels.
046	1CO	011	011	Even so, from the Lord's perspective, the woman is as essential as the man, and the man as essential as the woman.
046	1CO	011	012	As the woman came from the man, so the man comes from the woman—but more importantly everything comes from God.
046	1CO	011	013	Judge for yourselves: is it appropriate for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered?
046	1CO	011	014	Doesn't nature itself indicate that a man with long hair disgraces himself?
046	1CO	011	015	However, a woman with long hair brings herself glory, because her hair is given to her as a covering.
046	1CO	011	016	But if anyone wants to argue about this, we don't have any other custom than this, and neither do any other of God's churches.
046	1CO	011	017	Now in giving you the instructions that follow I can't commend you, because when you meet together you cause more harm than good!
046	1CO	011	018	First of all, I hear that when you have church meetings that you are split into different factions, and I believe there's some truth to this.
046	1CO	011	019	Of course such splits among you must happen so those who are genuine can prove themselves by their evidence!
046	1CO	011	020	When you meet together you're not really celebrating the Lord's Supper at all.
046	1CO	011	021	Some want to eat first before everyone else, leaving others hungry. Still others get drunk.
046	1CO	011	022	Don't you have your own houses to eat and drink in? Do you look down on God's church, and humiliate those who are poor? What should I tell you? That you're doing really well? I have nothing good to say about you for doing this!
046	1CO	011	023	For I received from the Lord what I passed on to you: the Lord Jesus on the night he was betrayed took some bread.
046	1CO	011	024	After giving thanks, he broke the bread into pieces and said, “This bread is my body, which is given for you. Remember me by doing this.”
046	1CO	011	025	In the same way he took the cup, after the meal, and said, “This cup is the new agreement sealed with my blood. Remember me when you drink it.
046	1CO	011	026	For every time you eat this bread and drink from this cup you announce the Lord's death, until he returns.”
046	1CO	011	027	So anyone who eats the bread or drinks from the Lord's cup in a dishonorable way will be guilty of doing wrong against the body and blood of the Lord.
046	1CO	011	028	Let each person examine themselves, and then let them eat the bread and drink from the cup.
046	1CO	011	029	Those who eat and drink bring judgment on themselves if they don't recognize their relationship with the body of the Lord.
046	1CO	011	030	That's the reason why many of you are weak and sick, and some even have died.
046	1CO	011	031	However, if we really examined ourselves, we would not be judged like this.
046	1CO	011	032	But when we are judged, we are being disciplined by the Lord so that we won't be condemned along with the world.
046	1CO	011	033	So my brothers and sisters, when you meet together to eat the Lord's Supper, wait for each other.
046	1CO	011	034	If anyone is hungry, then eat at home so that when you meet together you won't bring condemnation on yourselves. I'll give you more directions when I visit.
046	1CO	012	001	Now about “spiritual gifts.” My brothers and sisters, I want to explain this to you.
046	1CO	012	002	You know that when you were pagans, you were deceived, being led astray by worshiping idols who couldn't even speak.
046	1CO	012	003	Let me make it clear to you: no one who speaks in the Spirit of God says, “Curse Jesus!” and no one can say, “Jesus is Lord!” except by the Holy Spirit.
046	1CO	012	004	Now there are different kinds of spiritual gifts, but they come from the same Spirit.
046	1CO	012	005	There are different kinds of ministries, but they come from the same Lord.
046	1CO	012	006	There are different ways of working, but they come from the same God, who is at work in all of them.
046	1CO	012	007	The Spirit is given to each of us and is revealed for the good of all.
046	1CO	012	008	One person is given by the Spirit the ability to speak words of wisdom. Another is given a message of knowledge by the same Spirit.
046	1CO	012	009	Another receives the gift of strongly trusting in God by the same Spirit. Another receives gifts of healing from that one Spirit.
046	1CO	012	010	Another is given the ability to perform miracles. Another receives the gift of prophecy. Another is given the gift of spiritual discernment. Another receives the ability to speak different languages, while another is given the gift of interpreting languages.
046	1CO	012	011	But all of these gifts are the work of the one and the same Spirit, sharing with each person as he alone chooses.
046	1CO	012	012	Just like the human body is one unit but has many parts—all the parts of the body even though there are many of them, make up one body—so is Christ.
046	1CO	012	013	For it was through one Spirit that we were all baptized into one body. It doesn't matter whether we are Jews or Greeks, slave or free—we all were given the one Spirit to drink.
046	1CO	012	014	The body is not made of one part, but many parts.
046	1CO	012	015	If the foot were to say, “Because I'm not a hand, I'm not part of the body,” would that make it not part of the body?
046	1CO	012	016	If the ear were to say, “Because I'm not an eye, I'm not part of the body,” would that make it not part of the body?
046	1CO	012	017	If the whole body was an eye, how could you hear anything? If the whole body was an ear, how could you smell anything?
046	1CO	012	018	But God has arranged each part in the body, every last one of them, placing them just as he wanted.
046	1CO	012	019	If they were all the same part, what would happen to the body?
046	1CO	012	020	However, since there are many parts, they make up the body.
046	1CO	012	021	The eye can't tell the hand, “I don't need you,” or the head tell the feet, “I don't need you.”
046	1CO	012	022	Quite the opposite: some of those parts of the body that seem the most insignificant are the most essential.
046	1CO	012	023	In fact those parts of the body we do not consider to be decent to reveal we “honor” more by covering them up—what is indecent we treat with greater modesty!
046	1CO	012	024	What's presentable doesn't need such covering up. God has so arranged the body that more honor is given to the parts that are less presentable.
046	1CO	012	025	This is so there wouldn't be any conflict within the body—the different parts should care equally for each other.
046	1CO	012	026	So when one part is suffering, all the other parts of the body suffer with it, and when one part is treated well, then all the other parts of the body are happy too!
046	1CO	012	027	Now you are the body of Christ, and each one makes up a part of it.
046	1CO	012	028	In the church, God has arranged first for some to be apostles, secondly for some to be prophets, thirdly teachers. Then there are those who perform miracles, those with healing gifts, those who can help others, those good at administration, and those who can speak different languages.
046	1CO	012	029	Not everyone is an apostle, or a prophet, or a teacher, or able to perform miracles.
046	1CO	012	030	Not all have healing gifts, or the ability to speak languages, or to interpret languages.
046	1CO	012	031	But you should really want to have the most significant gifts. So now I will show you a far better way.
046	1CO	013	001	If I were to have eloquence in human languages—even the language of angels—but have no love, then I would only be an echoing gong or a clashing cymbal.
046	1CO	013	002	If I were to speak prophecies, to know every secret mystery and be completely knowledgeable, and if I were able to have so much faith I could move mountains, but have no love, then I am nothing.
046	1CO	013	003	If I were to donate everything I own to the poor, or if I were to sacrifice myself to be burned as a martyr, and have no love, then I gain nothing.
046	1CO	013	004	Love is patient and kind. Love is not jealous. Love is not boastful. Love is not proud.
046	1CO	013	005	Love does not act improperly, or insist on having its own way. Love is not argumentative and doesn't keep a record of wrongs.
046	1CO	013	006	Love takes no delight in evil but celebrates the truth.
046	1CO	013	007	Love never gives up, keeps on trusting, stays confident, and remains patient whatever happens.
046	1CO	013	008	Love never fails. Prophecies will come to an end. Tongues will become silent. Knowledge will become useless.
046	1CO	013	009	For our knowledge and our prophetic understanding are incomplete.
046	1CO	013	010	But when completeness comes, then what is incomplete disappears.
046	1CO	013	011	When I was a child, I spoke like a child, I thought like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I grew up I left behind such childlike ways.
046	1CO	013	012	At the moment we peer into a mirror's dim reflection, but then we shall see face to face. For now I only have partial knowledge, but then I shall know completely, just as I am completely known.
046	1CO	013	013	Trust, hope, and love last forever—but the most important is love.
046	1CO	014	001	Make love your most important objective! But also do your best to gain spiritual gifts, especially the ability to speak God's message.
046	1CO	014	002	Those who speak in a tongue are not talking to people, but to God, because nobody can understand them as they speak mysteries in the Spirit.
046	1CO	014	003	However, the words of those who speak for God build people up—they provide encouragement and comfort.
046	1CO	014	004	Those that speak in a tongue only build themselves up, but those who speak God's message build up the church. I would like it if you all spoke in tongues, but I'd prefer if you could speak God's message.
046	1CO	014	005	Those who speak for God are more important than those who speak in tongues, unless they interpret what's been said, so that the church can be built up.
046	1CO	014	006	Brothers and sisters, if I come to you speaking in tongues, what benefit would I be to you unless I bring you some revelation, or knowledge, or prophetic message, or teaching?
046	1CO	014	007	Even when it comes to something non-living such as musical instruments like a flute or a harp—if they don't produce clear notes, how will you know what tune is being played?
046	1CO	014	008	Similarly, if the trumpet doesn't give a clear sound, who will get ready for battle?
046	1CO	014	009	It's the same situation for you—unless you speak using words that are easy to understand, who will know what you're saying? What you say will be lost on the wind.
046	1CO	014	010	There are surely many languages in this world, and there is meaning in every one of them.
046	1CO	014	011	If I don't understand the language, those who speak make no sense to me, and I make no sense to them.
046	1CO	014	012	It's the same for you—if you are keen to have spiritual gifts, try to have many of those that will build up the church.
046	1CO	014	013	Anyone who speaks in a tongue should pray that they're able to translate what they say.
046	1CO	014	014	For if I pray out loud in a tongue, my spirit is praying, but it does nothing for my understanding!
046	1CO	014	015	So then, what should I do? I will pray “in the Spirit,” but I will pray with my mind too. I will sing “in the Spirit,” but I will sing with my mind too.
046	1CO	014	016	For if you only pray “in the Spirit,” how can ordinary people that don't have understanding say “Amen” after your prayer of thanks, since they haven't a clue what you said?
046	1CO	014	017	You might have said a great prayer of thanks, but the other hasn't been helped!
046	1CO	014	018	I thank God that I can speak in tongues more than all of you.
046	1CO	014	019	But in church I would rather speak five understandable words to teach others than ten thousand words in a tongue nobody understands.
046	1CO	014	020	Brothers and sisters, don't think like children. Be as innocent as babies in regard to evil, but be grown up in your understanding.
046	1CO	014	021	As Scripture records, “‘I will speak to my people through other languages and the lips of foreigners, but even then they won't listen to me,’ says the Lord.”
046	1CO	014	022	Speaking in tongues is a sign, not to believers, but those who don't believe. Speaking God's prophetic message is the opposite: it is not for those who don't believe, but for believers.
046	1CO	014	023	If the whole church is meeting together and you are all speaking in tongues, and some people come in who don't understand, or people who don't believe, won't they say that you are insane?
046	1CO	014	024	But if everyone is speaking God's message, and someone comes in who isn't a believer, or someone who doesn't understand, they will be convinced and called to account by everyone's words.
046	1CO	014	025	Their secret thoughts will be revealed, so they will fall to their knees and worship God, affirming that God is truly among you.
046	1CO	014	026	So then, brothers and sisters, what should you do? When you meet together, different people will sing, or teach, or share a special message, or speak in a tongue, or give an interpretation. But everything should be done to build up and encourage the church.
046	1CO	014	027	If anyone wants to speak in a tongue, make it just two, or three at the most, taking turns, and someone should interpret what is said.
046	1CO	014	028	If there's no one there to interpret, those who speak in tongues should keep quiet in church and only speak to themselves, and God.
046	1CO	014	029	Similarly, have two or three of those who give God's prophetic message speak, and let everyone else think about what was said.
046	1CO	014	030	However, if a special revelation comes to someone who is sitting down, then the first speaker should give way to them.
046	1CO	014	031	You can all speak for God, one at a time, so that everyone can learn and be encouraged.
046	1CO	014	032	It is for those who speak for God to control their prophetic inspiration,
046	1CO	014	033	for God is not a God of disorder but of peace and quiet. This is the way it should be in all the churches of God's people.
046	1CO	014	034	“Women should stay quiet in the churches—they shouldn't speak. They should respect their situation, as the laws states.
046	1CO	014	035	If they want to learn they can do so at home, asking their husbands. It is not proper for women to speak in church.”
046	1CO	014	036	What? Did the word of God begin with you? Are you the only ones it came to?
046	1CO	014	037	Anyone who thinks they are a prophet, or that they have some spiritual gift, should be aware that what I'm writing to you is a command of the Lord.
046	1CO	014	038	Those who ignore this will themselves be ignored.
046	1CO	014	039	So my brothers and sisters, make it your aim to speak for God. Don't prohibit speaking in tongues.
046	1CO	014	040	Just make sure everything done is done properly and in an orderly manner.
046	1CO	015	001	Now I want to remind you about the good news I announced to you. You accepted it, and you have stood firm for it.
046	1CO	015	002	It is through this good news that you are saved if you hold on to the message that I gave you. Otherwise you trusted for nothing!
046	1CO	015	003	I passed on to you what I myself had also received, a message of vital importance: that Christ died for our sins, according to Scripture;
046	1CO	015	004	he was buried and was raised from the dead on the third day, again in accordance with Scripture.
046	1CO	015	005	He appeared to Peter, then to the Twelve.
046	1CO	015	006	After that he appeared to more than five hundred brothers and sisters at the same time, most of whom are still alive today, though some have died.
046	1CO	015	007	He appeared to James, then all the apostles.
046	1CO	015	008	Last of all, he also appeared to me, someone born as it were at the wrong time.
046	1CO	015	009	For I'm the least important apostle of all, not even fit to be called an apostle since I persecuted God's church.
046	1CO	015	010	But by God's grace I am what I am, and his grace given to me wasn't wasted. On the contrary I've worked harder than all of them—though not me, but God's grace working through me.
046	1CO	015	011	So whether it's I or they, this is the message we shared with you that brought you to trust in God.
046	1CO	015	012	Now if the message declares that Christ has been raised from the dead, how is it that some of you say there's no resurrection of the dead?
046	1CO	015	013	If there's no resurrection of the dead then Christ hasn't been raised either.
046	1CO	015	014	And if Christ isn't raised, then our message we shared with you is pointless, and your trust in God is pointless too.
046	1CO	015	015	In addition, we would be shown to be false witnesses of God when we testified that God raised Christ from the dead. But God didn't raise Christ from the dead if it's true that there's no resurrection.
046	1CO	015	016	If the dead are not raised, then Christ hasn't been raised either,
046	1CO	015	017	and if Christ hasn't been raised, then your trust in God is useless, and you are still in your sins.
046	1CO	015	018	This also means that those who died in Christ are lost.
046	1CO	015	019	If our hope in Christ is only for this life, we're the most pitiful people of all!
046	1CO	015	020	But Christ has been raised from the dead, the firstfruits of the harvest from those who have died.
046	1CO	015	021	Just as death came through a man, the resurrection of the dead came through a man.
046	1CO	015	022	Just as in Adam all die, so in Christ all will be made alive.
046	1CO	015	023	But each in their own turn: Christ the firstfruits, then those who belong to Christ when he comes.
046	1CO	015	024	After this comes the end, when Christ hands over the kingdom to God the Father, having destroyed all rulers, authorities, and powers.
046	1CO	015	025	Christ has to rule until he has put all his enemies under his feet.
046	1CO	015	026	The last enemy that will be destroyed is death.
046	1CO	015	027	As Scripture says, “He put everything under his feet.” (Of course when it says “everything” is put under him it's obvious this doesn't refer to God who placed everything under Christ's authority.)
046	1CO	015	028	When everything has been placed under Christ's authority, then the Son will also place himself under God's authority, so that God who gave the Son authority over everything may be all in all.
046	1CO	015	029	Otherwise what will those people do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead are not raised at all, why then would people be baptized for them?
046	1CO	015	030	As for us, why do we place ourselves in danger hour after hour?
046	1CO	015	031	I die every day—let me say it bluntly, my brothers and sisters. This is just as sure as the pride I have for what Christ Jesus has done in you.
046	1CO	015	032	Humanly speaking, what would I gain by fighting with those people in Ephesus who were like wild animals, if the dead are not raised? If the dead are not raised, “let's eat and drink, for tomorrow we die”!
046	1CO	015	033	Don't be fooled: “Bad company ruins good character.”
046	1CO	015	034	Come to your senses as you should, and stop sinning! Some of you don't know God. I tell you this to shame you.
046	1CO	015	035	Of course somebody will ask, “How exactly are the dead raised? What kind of body will they have?”
046	1CO	015	036	What a foolish question! What you sow doesn't sprout into life unless it dies.
046	1CO	015	037	When you sow, you don't sow the plant it will grow into, just the bare seed, whether wheat or whatever you're planting.
046	1CO	015	038	God makes the plant grow into the form he has chosen, and different seeds produce different plants with different forms.
046	1CO	015	039	What living things are made from is not the same. Human beings have one kind of body tissue, while animals have another, birds another, and fish another.
046	1CO	015	040	There are heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. Heavenly bodies have one kind of beauty, earthly bodies another.
046	1CO	015	041	The sun shines in one way, and the moon another, while the stars are different again, with each one shining in a different way.
046	1CO	015	042	It's the same with the resurrection of the dead. The body is sown in decay; it is raised to last forever.
046	1CO	015	043	It is sown in shame; it is raised in glory. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power.
046	1CO	015	044	It is sown as a natural body; it is raised as a spiritual body. Just as there are natural bodies there are spiritual bodies.
046	1CO	015	045	As Scripture says, “The first man, Adam, became a living being”; but the last Adam a life-giving spirit.
046	1CO	015	046	The spiritual did not come first, but the natural—the spiritual came after that.
046	1CO	015	047	The first man is from the dust of the earth; the second man is from heaven.
046	1CO	015	048	Earthly people are like the man made from the earth; heavenly people are like the man from heaven.
046	1CO	015	049	Just as we bore the likeness of the earthly man so we shall bear the likeness of the man from heaven.
046	1CO	015	050	However, I tell you this, my brothers and sisters: our present bodies cannot inherit the kingdom of God. These decaying bodies cannot inherit what lasts forever.
046	1CO	015	051	Listen, I'm going to reveal a mystery! Not all of us will die—but we will all be changed,
046	1CO	015	052	in a moment, in the blink of an eye, at the sound of the last trumpet. The trumpet will sound, and the dead will be raised never to die again, and we will be changed.
046	1CO	015	053	For this perishable body must be clothed with a body that never perishes. This mortal life must be clothed with immortality.
046	1CO	015	054	When this perishable body has been clothed with a body that never perishes, and this mortal life has been clothed with immortality, then the Scripture will come true that says, “Death has been totally conquered and destroyed.
046	1CO	015	055	Death—where's your victory? Death—where's your sting?”
046	1CO	015	056	The sting that causes death is sin; and the power of sin is the law;
046	1CO	015	057	but praise God who gives us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	015	058	So my dear brothers and sisters: be strong, stand firm, doing everything you can for the Lord's work, since you know that nothing you do in the Lord is wasted.
046	1CO	016	001	Now about “collecting money for fellow-believers.” I'm giving you the same instructions for you to follow as I did to the churches in Galatia.
046	1CO	016	002	On the first day of the week everybody should set aside some money you've earned. I don't want there to be any collections to have to be made when I'm with you.
046	1CO	016	003	When I get there I will write recommendation letters for whoever you choose, and they will take your donation to Jerusalem.
046	1CO	016	004	If it works out for me to go too, they can come with me.
046	1CO	016	005	After I've been to Macedonia, I plan to come and visit you. I pass that way through Macedonia
046	1CO	016	006	and I may stay with you for a while, perhaps spend the winter, and then you can send me on my way to wherever I'm headed.
046	1CO	016	007	This time I don't want to come and see you for just a short time. I hope I can stay for a while with you, if that's what the Lord permits.
046	1CO	016	008	However, I will stay on at Ephesus until Pentecost,
046	1CO	016	009	because a tremendous door of opportunity has opened up for me there, though there are plenty who oppose me.
046	1CO	016	010	Now if Timothy arrives, make sure that he has nothing to fear by being with you, for he's working for the Lord just as I am.
046	1CO	016	011	Don't let anyone look down on him. Cheerfully send him on his way so he can come and see me—the brothers and sisters and I are waiting for him.
046	1CO	016	012	As for our brother Apollos: I urged him to go and see you together with the other believers, but he wasn't willing to go at the moment. He'll come and visit when he gets the chance.
046	1CO	016	013	Stay alert. Stand firm in your trust in God. Take courage. Be strong.
046	1CO	016	014	Whatever you do, do it in love.
046	1CO	016	015	You know that Stephanas and his family were among the first converts in Achaia, and they dedicated themselves to helping God's people. I'm pleading with you, my brothers and sisters,
046	1CO	016	016	to respect their leadership, and everyone who helps the work with such dedication.
046	1CO	016	017	I'm delighted that Stephanas, Fortunatas, and Achaicus have arrived here, for they did what you weren't able to.
046	1CO	016	018	They have been a great source of encouragement to me, and to you. People like that deserve your recognition.
046	1CO	016	019	The churches of Asia send their greetings. Aquila and Priscilla, along with the church that meets in their home, send their best wishes.
046	1CO	016	020	All the brothers and sisters here send their greetings. Greet one another affectionately.
046	1CO	016	021	I Paul write this greeting with my own hand.
046	1CO	016	022	Anyone who doesn't love the Lord should be excluded from the church. Come Lord!
046	1CO	016	023	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
046	1CO	016	024	My love to all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen.
