# BOOK	047	2CO	2 Corinthians	2 Corinthians
047	2CO	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ according to the will of God, and from Timothy, our brother. It is sent to the church of God in Corinth, together with all of God's people throughout Achaia.
047	2CO	001	002	May you have grace and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	001	003	Praise be to God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! He is the compassionate Father and the God of all comfort.
047	2CO	001	004	He comforts us in all our troubles, so that we can comfort those who are also in trouble with the comfort we ourselves receive from God.
047	2CO	001	005	The more we share in Christ's sufferings, the more we receive the abundant comfort of Christ.
047	2CO	001	006	If we are in distress, it is for your comfort and salvation. If we are being comforted, it is for your comfort, which results in you patiently bearing the same sufferings that we suffer.
047	2CO	001	007	We have great confidence in you, knowing that as you share in our sufferings you also share in our comfort.
047	2CO	001	008	Brothers and sisters, we won't keep you in the dark about the trouble we had in Asia. We were so overwhelmed that we were afraid we wouldn't have the strength to continue—so much so we doubted we would live through it.
047	2CO	001	009	In fact it was like a death sentence inside us. This was to stop us relying on ourselves and to trust in God who raises the dead.
047	2CO	001	010	He saved us from a terrible death, and he will do so again. We have total confidence in God that he will continue to save us.
047	2CO	001	011	You help us by praying for us. In this way many will thank God for us because of the blessing that God will give us in response to the prayers of many.
047	2CO	001	012	We take pride in the fact—and our conscience confirms it—that we have acted properly towards people, and especially to you. We have followed God's principles of holiness and sincerity, not according to worldly wisdom but through the grace of God.
047	2CO	001	013	For we are not writing anything complicated that you can't read and understand. I hope you'll understand in the end,
047	2CO	001	014	even if you only understand part of it now, so that when the Lord comes you will be proud of us, just as we are of you.
047	2CO	001	015	Because I was so sure of your confidence in me I planned to come and visit you first. That way you could have benefited twice,
047	2CO	001	016	as I would go on from you to Macedonia, and then return from Macedonia to you. Then I would have had you send me on my way to Judea.
047	2CO	001	017	Why did I change my original plan? Do you think I make my decisions lightly? Do you think that when I plan I'm like some worldly person who says Yes and No at the same time?
047	2CO	001	018	Just as God can be trusted, when we give you our word it's not both Yes and No.
047	2CO	001	019	The truth of the Son of God, Jesus Christ, was announced to you by us—me, Silvanus, and Timothy—and it wasn't both Yes and No. In Christ the answer is absolutely Yes!
047	2CO	001	020	However many promises God has made, in Christ the answer is always Yes. Through him we respond, saying Yes to the glory of God.
047	2CO	001	021	God has given both us and you the inner strength to stand firm in Christ. God has anointed us,
047	2CO	001	022	placed his stamp of approval on us, and given us the guarantee of the Spirit to convince us.
047	2CO	001	023	I call God as my witness that it was to avoid causing you pain that I chose not to come to Corinth.
047	2CO	001	024	This isn't because we want to dictate how you relate to God, but because we want to help you have a joyful experience—for it's by trusting God that you stand firm.
047	2CO	002	001	That's why I decided that I would avoid another sad visit with you.
047	2CO	002	002	For if I make you sad, who will be there to make me happy? It won't be those I've made sad!
047	2CO	002	003	That's why I wrote what I did, so that I wouldn't be sad over those who should make me happy. I was so sure that all of you would share in my happiness.
047	2CO	002	004	I was crying many tears when I wrote to you, in great anguish and with a heavy heart—not to make you sad, but so you would know how much love I have for you.
047	2CO	002	005	Not to put it too strongly, but the person caused more pain to all of you than to me.
047	2CO	002	006	This person suffered enough punishment from the majority of you,
047	2CO	002	007	so now you should forgive him and be kind to him. Otherwise he may sink into despair.
047	2CO	002	008	So I urge you to publicly affirm your love towards him.
047	2CO	002	009	That's why I wrote, so I could discoverer your true character and whether you're doing everything you were told to do.
047	2CO	002	010	Anyone you forgive, I forgive too. What I have forgiven, whatever it may be, I have forgiven before Christ for your benefit.
047	2CO	002	011	In this way Satan will not be able to take us in, because we know the tricks he thinks up.
047	2CO	002	012	Now when I arrived in Troas to spread the good news of Christ, the Lord opened a door of opportunity for me.
047	2CO	002	013	But my mind wasn't at peace because I couldn't find my brother Titus. So I said goodbye and went over to Macedonia.
047	2CO	002	014	But praise be to God, who always leads us in a triumphal procession in Christ, and reveals through us the sweet scent of his knowledge wherever we go!
047	2CO	002	015	We are like a fragrance of Christ to God, rising up from among those who are being saved as well as those who are dying.
047	2CO	002	016	To those who are dying it is the smell of decay, while to those who are being saved it is the scent of life! But who is up to such an assignment?
047	2CO	002	017	We are not like the majority who trade in the word of God for profit. Quite the opposite: we are sincere in sharing the word of God in Christ, knowing God is watching us.
047	2CO	003	001	Are we starting to speak well of ourselves again? Or do we need to have some letter of recommendation for you, or from you, as some people do?
047	2CO	003	002	You are our letter, written in our experience with you, that everybody reads and knows about.
047	2CO	003	003	You demonstrate that you are a letter from Christ, delivered by us; not written with ink but with the Spirit of the living God; not written on stone slabs but in our living experience as human beings.
047	2CO	003	004	We have total confidence before God through Christ.
047	2CO	003	005	Not that we would consider ourselves able to do this on our own—it's God who gives us this capacity!
047	2CO	003	006	He also gave us the ability to be ministers of a new agreement, based not on the letter of the law, but on the spirit. The letter of the law kills, but the spirit gives life.
047	2CO	003	007	However, the old way of relating to God, written in letters carved in stone, ended in death, even though it came with God's glory—so much so that the Israelites couldn't even bear to look at Moses' face because it shone so brightly, even though the glory was fading.
047	2CO	003	008	If that was so, shouldn't the new way of relating to God in the Spirit come with even greater glory?
047	2CO	003	009	If the old way that condemns us has glory, the new way that makes us right with God has so much more glory!
047	2CO	003	010	For the old that was once glorious has no glory at all in comparison with the incredible glory of the new.
047	2CO	003	011	If the old that is fading away had glory, the new that continues has so much more glory.
047	2CO	003	012	Since we have such a confident hope, we are truly bold!
047	2CO	003	013	We don't have to be like Moses, who had to put on a veil to cover his face so the Israelites wouldn't be dazzled by the glory, even though it was fading away.
047	2CO	003	014	In spite of that, they had a hard, stubborn attitude. For right up until today when the old agreement is read, the same “veil” remains. Only through Christ can it be removed.
047	2CO	003	015	Even today, whenever the books of Moses are read, a veil covers their minds.
047	2CO	003	016	But when they turn and accept the Lord, the veil is removed.
047	2CO	003	017	Now the Lord is the Spirit, and wherever the Spirit of the Lord is, there's freedom.
047	2CO	003	018	So all of us, with our faces unveiled, see and reflect the glory of the Lord as in a mirror. We are being transformed into the same mirror image, whose glory grows brighter and brighter. This is what the Lord the Spirit does.
047	2CO	004	001	So then, since God in his mercy has given us this new way of relating to him, we don't give up.
047	2CO	004	002	But we have given up secret, shameful acts. We don't behave in deceitful ways and we don't distort the word of God. We demonstrate who we are by revealing the truth before God so everybody can decide in their own minds.
047	2CO	004	003	Even if the good news we share is veiled, it is veiled to those who are dying.
047	2CO	004	004	The god of this world has blinded the minds of those who don't trust in God. They can't see the light of the good news of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God.
047	2CO	004	005	We are not promoting ourselves, but Christ Jesus as Lord. In fact we are your servants for Jesus' sake.
047	2CO	004	006	For God who said, “Let light shine out of the darkness,” shone in our minds to illuminate the knowledge of God's glory in the face of Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	004	007	But we have this treasure in clay jars, to show that this supreme power comes from God and not from ourselves.
047	2CO	004	008	We are attacked from every direction, but we are not crushed. We are at a loss as to what to do, but never in despair.
047	2CO	004	009	We are persecuted, but never abandoned by God. We are knocked down, but not dead yet!
047	2CO	004	010	In our bodies we always share in the death of Jesus, so that we can also demonstrate the life of Jesus in our bodies.
047	2CO	004	011	While we live we are always under the threat of death for Jesus' sake, so that the life of Jesus may be revealed in our mortal bodies.
047	2CO	004	012	As a result, we are facing death so that you may have life!
047	2CO	004	013	Since we have the same spirit of trust in God that Scripture refers to when it says, “I trusted in God, and so I spoke out,” we also trust in God and speak out for him.
047	2CO	004	014	We know that God who raised the Lord Jesus will also raise us with Jesus, and will bring us into his presence with you.
047	2CO	004	015	It's all for you! As God's grace reaches many more, thankfulness to God will be even greater, to his glory.
047	2CO	004	016	So we don't give up. Even though our physical bodies are falling apart, our inner selves are being renewed daily.
047	2CO	004	017	These trivial troubles we have only last for a little while, but they produce for us an ever-increasing degree of glory.
047	2CO	004	018	We don't concern ourselves with what can be seen, for we look forward to what can't be seen. What we see is temporary, but what we can't see is eternal.
047	2CO	005	001	We know that when this earthly “tent” we live in is taken down, we have a house prepared by God, not made by human hands. It is eternal and is in heaven.
047	2CO	005	002	We sigh with longing for this, wanting so badly to be clothed with this new heavenly home.
047	2CO	005	003	When we put on this clothing we won't be seen naked.
047	2CO	005	004	While we are in this “tent” we sigh, being weighed down by this life. It's not so much that we want to take off the clothing of this life but that we look forward to what we shall be clothed with, so that what is mortal may be overwhelmed by life.
047	2CO	005	005	It's God himself who prepared us for all this, and who provided the Spirit as a guarantee to us.
047	2CO	005	006	So we remain confident, knowing that while we are at home here in our physical bodies, we are away from the Lord.
