047	2CO	006	001	As workers together with God we also plead with you not to make your acceptance of God's grace worthless.
047	2CO	006	002	Just as God said, “At the right time I heard you, and on the day of salvation I rescued you.” Believe me: now is the right time! Now is the day of salvation!
047	2CO	006	003	We don't put anything in anyone's way that would trip them up, making sure the work we do won't be criticized.
047	2CO	006	004	Instead we try to demonstrate we are good servants of God in every way we can. With a great deal of patience we put up with all kinds of trouble, hardship, and distress.
047	2CO	006	005	We have been beaten up, thrown into prison, and attacked by mobs. We have been worked to the bone, suffering sleepless nights and hunger.
047	2CO	006	006	We demonstrate who we are by living blameless lives in the knowledge of God, with a great deal of patience, being kind and filled with the Holy Spirit, showing sincere love.
047	2CO	006	007	We speak truthfully, living in the power of God. Our weapons consist of what is true and right; we attack with our right hand and we defend with our left.
047	2CO	006	008	We continue whether we are honored or dishonored, whether we are cursed or praised. People call us frauds but we tell the truth.
047	2CO	006	009	We are disregarded, even though we are well-known; given up for dead, but we're still alive; lashed, but not killed.
047	2CO	006	010	Seen as miserable, we are always rejoicing; as poor, but we make many rich; as destitute, but we own everything!
047	2CO	006	011	I've been speaking bluntly, my Corinthian friends, loving you with a big heart!
047	2CO	006	012	We haven't kept our love from you, but you have kept your love from us.
047	2CO	006	013	Please respond in the same way, as if you were my children, and be big-hearted!
047	2CO	006	014	Don't join together with people who don't believe—for what connection does goodness have with wickedness? What do light and darkness have in common?
047	2CO	006	015	How could Christ and the devil ever agree? How could a believer and an unbeliever share together?
047	2CO	006	016	What compromise could the Temple of God make with idols? For we are a temple of the living God, just as God said: “I will live in them and walk among them. I will be their God, and they will be my people.”
047	2CO	006	017	“So leave them, and separate yourselves from them, says the Lord. Don't touch anything that is unclean, and I will accept you.”
