047	2CO	007	010	The kind of sorrow God wants us to have makes us change our minds and brings salvation. This kind of sorrow leaves no sense of regret, but worldly sorrow brings death.
047	2CO	007	011	See what happened to you when you had this very same experience of sorrow that God wants. Remember how enthusiastic you became, how keen you were to defend yourselves, how angry you were at what had happened, how seriously you took it, how you longed to do right, how concerned you were, how you wanted justice to be done. In all of this you showed that you were sincere in wanting to make things right.
047	2CO	007	012	So when I wrote to you, I wasn't writing about who did the wrong or who was wronged, but to show you how devoted you are to us in God's sight.
047	2CO	007	013	We are so encouraged by this. Added to our own encouragement, we were so pleased to see how happy Titus was, because you set his mind at rest.
047	2CO	007	014	I boasted to him about you, and you didn't let me down. Just as all I've told you is true, my boasting about you to Titus has proved to be true too!
047	2CO	007	015	Titus cares for you even more as he remembers how you did what he told you, how you welcomed him with great respect.
047	2CO	007	016	I am so happy that I can be completely confident of you.
047	2CO	008	001	Brothers and sisters, we want to let you know about the grace of God shown to the Macedonian churches.
047	2CO	008	002	Even though they have suffered terrible trouble, they are overflowing with happiness; and even though they are very poor, they are also overflowing in their generosity.
047	2CO	008	003	I can confirm that they gave what they could, in fact even more than that! By their own choice
047	2CO	008	004	they kept on pleading with us to have a part in this privilege of sharing in this ministry to God's people.
047	2CO	008	005	They didn't just do what we hoped they would do, but they gave themselves to the Lord, and then to us, as God wanted them to do.
047	2CO	008	006	So we have encouraged Titus—since it was he who started this work with you—to return and complete this gracious ministry of yours.
047	2CO	008	007	Since you have an abundance of everything—your trust in God, your eloquence, your spiritual knowledge, your complete dedication, and in your love for us—make sure that your abundance also extends to this gracious ministry of giving.
047	2CO	008	008	I'm not ordering you to do this, but to prove how sincere your love is in comparison with the dedication of others.
047	2CO	008	009	For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ. Even though he was rich, he became poor for you, so that through his poverty you could become rich.
047	2CO	008	010	This is my advice: it would be good if you finished what you started. Last year you were not only the first to give but the first to want to do so.
047	2CO	008	011	Now finish what you planned to do. Be as keen to finish as you were to plan, and give as you are able.
047	2CO	008	012	If the willingness is there, it's fine to give what you have, not what you don't have!
047	2CO	008	013	This is not to make things easier for others and harder for you, but simply to be fair.
047	2CO	008	014	At the moment you have more than enough and can meet their needs, and in turn when they have more than enough they can meet your needs. In that way everyone is treated fairly.
047	2CO	008	015	As Scripture says, “The one who had much didn't have any excess, and the one who didn't have much didn't have too little.”
047	2CO	008	016	Thanks be to God that he gave to Titus the same devotion for you that I have.
047	2CO	008	017	Though he agreed to do what we told him, he's coming to see you because he really wants to, and had already decided to do so.
047	2CO	008	018	We're also sending with him a brother who is praised by all the churches for his work in spreading the good news.
047	2CO	008	019	He was also appointed by the churches to go with us as we deliver this gracious offering we're carrying. We do this to honor the Lord and to show our eagerness to help others.
047	2CO	008	020	We want to guard against anyone criticizing us about how we use this gift.
047	2CO	008	021	We're concerned to do things the right way, not only in the eyes of the Lord, but also in the eyes of everyone.
047	2CO	008	022	We're also sending with them another brother who has proved to be reliable on many occasions, and who is eager to help. He is now even more eager to help because of the great confidence he has in you.
047	2CO	008	023	If anyone asks about Titus, he is my companion. He works with me on your behalf. The other brothers are representatives from the churches and an honor to Christ.
047	2CO	008	024	So please welcome them before all the churches and show them your love, proving how rightly proud we are of you.
047	2CO	009	001	I really don't need to write to you about this offering for God's people.
047	2CO	009	002	I know how keen you are to help—I was boasting about this to those in Macedonia that you in Achaia have been ready for over a year, and your enthusiasm has encouraged many of them to give.
047	2CO	009	003	But I'm sending these brothers so that my boasting about you regarding this won't be proved wrong, and that you're prepared, just as I said you would be.
047	2CO	009	004	This is just in case some Macedonians should come with me and find you unprepared. We, not to mention you, would be really embarrassed if this project failed!
047	2CO	009	005	That's why I decided I should ask these brothers to visit you in advance, and complete the arrangements to collect this offering, so that it would be ready as a gift, and not as something demanded.
047	2CO	009	006	I want to remind you of this: If you only sow a little, you'll only reap a little; if you sow plenty, you'll reap plenty.
047	2CO	009	007	Everybody should give as they've already decided—not reluctantly, or because they have to, for God loves those who give with a cheerful spirit.
047	2CO	009	008	God is able to graciously provide you with everything, so that you will always have all you need—with plenty to help others too.
047	2CO	009	009	As Scripture says, “He gives generously to the poor; his generosity is everlasting.”
047	2CO	009	010	God, who provides seed to the sower and gives bread for food, will provide and multiply your “seed” and increase your harvest of generosity.
047	2CO	009	011	You will be made rich in every way so that you can always be very generous, and your generosity will lead others to be grateful to God.
047	2CO	009	012	When you serve in this way, not only are the needs of God's people met, but also many will give grateful thanks to God.
047	2CO	009	013	By giving this offering you show your true nature, and those who receive it will thank God for your obedience, since it shows your commitment to the good news of Christ and your generosity in giving to them and everyone else.
047	2CO	009	014	They will pray for you with much fondness because of God's abundant grace working through you.
047	2CO	009	015	Thank God for his gift that is far greater than words can express!
047	2CO	010	001	This is me Paul, personally appealing to you through Christ's kindness and gentleness, the one who is “shy” when I have to face you but who is “bold” when I'm not there.
047	2CO	010	002	I'm pleading with you, so that the next time I'm with you I won't have to be as tough as I think I'll have to be, boldly dealing with those who think we behave in worldly ways.
047	2CO	010	003	Even though we live in this world, we don't fight as the world does.
047	2CO	010	004	Our weapons are not of this world but God's mighty power that destroys fortresses of human thinking, demolishing misleading theories.
047	2CO	010	005	Every high wall that stands tall and proud against the knowledge of God is knocked down. Every rebel idea is captured and brought into obedient agreement with Christ.
047	2CO	010	006	When you are completely obeying Christ then we're ready to punish any disobedience.
047	2CO	010	007	Look at what's staring you in the face! Anyone who considers that they belong to Christ should think again—just as they belong to Christ, so do we!
047	2CO	010	008	Even though I may seem to be boasting a little too much about our authority, I'm not embarrassed about it. The Lord gave this authority to us to build you up, not to knock you down.
047	2CO	010	009	I'm not trying to scare you by my letters.
047	2CO	010	010	People say, “His letters are tough and severe, but in person he's feeble, and he's a useless speaker.”
047	2CO	010	011	People like that should realize that what we say through letters when we're not there we will do when we are there!
047	2CO	010	012	We're not so arrogant to compare ourselves with those who think so much of themselves. Those who measure themselves by themselves, and compare themselves with themselves, are really foolish!
047	2CO	010	013	But we won't boast about ourselves in extravagant terms that can't be measured. We simply measure what we have done using God's system of measurement that he gave us—and that includes you.
047	2CO	010	014	We are not over-extending our authority in saying this, as if we didn't get as far as you, for we did get to you and share with you the good news of Christ.
047	2CO	010	015	We're not boasting in extravagant terms that can't be measured, claiming credit for what others have done. On the contrary, we hope that as your trust in God grows, our work among you will greatly increase.
047	2CO	010	016	Then we can share the good news in places way beyond you, without boasting about what's already been done where someone else has worked.
047	2CO	010	017	“If anyone wants to boast, boast about the Lord.”
047	2CO	010	018	It's not those who praise themselves that are respected, but those that the Lord praises.
047	2CO	011	001	I hope you can put up with a little more foolishness from me—well you already do put up with me!
047	2CO	011	002	I agonize over you with a divine kind of jealousy, for I promised you to a single husband—Christ—so that I could present you as a pure virgin to him.
047	2CO	011	003	I worry that in some way, just as the serpent deceived Eve with his devious cunning, that you might be led astray in your thinking from your sincere and pure commitment to Christ.
047	2CO	011	004	If anyone comes and tells you about a different Jesus to the one we shared with you, you easily go along with them, accepting a different spirit to the one you received, and a different kind of good news to the one you believed.
047	2CO	011	005	I don't believe I'm inferior to these “super-apostles.”
047	2CO	011	006	Even though I may not be skilled in giving speeches, I do know what I'm talking about. We have made this absolutely clear to you in every way.
047	2CO	011	007	Was it wrong of me to humble myself so you could be elevated, since I shared the good news with you at no charge?
047	2CO	011	008	I robbed as it were other churches, taking pay from them so I could work for you.
047	2CO	011	009	When I was there with you and needed something, I wasn't a burden to anyone because the believers who came from Macedonia took care of my needs. I was determined never to be a burden to you and I never shall.
047	2CO	011	010	This is as certain as the truth of Christ that is in me: nobody in all Achaia will stop me boasting about this!
047	2CO	011	011	And why? Because I don't love you? God knows that I do!
047	2CO	011	012	I'll continue to do what I've always done, so as to remove any opportunity for those who want to boast that their work is the same as ours.
047	2CO	011	013	These people are false apostles, dishonest workers, who pretend to be apostles of Christ.
047	2CO	011	014	Don't be surprised at this for even Satan himself pretends to be an angel of light.
047	2CO	011	015	So it's no wonder then if those who serve him pretend to be agents of good. But their final end will be in accordance with what they've done.
047	2CO	011	016	Let me say it again: Please don't think I'm being foolish. However, even if you do, accept me as someone who is foolish, and let me also boast a little.
047	2CO	011	017	What I'm saying is not as the Lord would say it—all this foolish boasting.
047	2CO	011	018	But since many others are boasting in the way the world does, let me boast too.
047	2CO	011	019	(You're happy to put up with fools, since you are so wise!)
047	2CO	011	020	You put up with people who make you slaves, who take what you have, who exploit you, who arrogantly put you down, who hit you in the face.
047	2CO	011	021	I'm so sorry that we were too weak to do anything like that! But whatever people dare to boast about, I dare to do too. (Here I'm talking like a fool again.)
047	2CO	011	022	Are they Hebrews? Me too. Are they Israelites? Me too. Are they descendants of Abraham? Me too.
047	2CO	011	023	Are they servants of Christ? (I know I'll sound like I'm crazy, talking like this.) But I have done so much more. I've worked harder, been imprisoned more often, whipped more times than I can count, faced death time and again.
047	2CO	011	024	Five times I received from the Jews the forty lashes less one.
047	2CO	011	025	Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. Once I spent twenty-four hours adrift on the ocean.
047	2CO	011	026	During my many journeys I have faced the dangers of crossing rivers, robber gangs, attacks from my own countrymen, as well as from foreigners. I have faced danger in cities, in the deserts, and on the sea. I have faced the danger of people who pretend to be Christians.
047	2CO	011	027	I have faced hard labor and struggles, many sleepless nights, hunger and thirst, often going without food, cold, without enough clothing to keep warm.
047	2CO	011	028	Besides all this, I face the daily concerns of dealing with all the churches.
047	2CO	011	029	Who is weak, and I don't feel weak too? Who is led into sin, and I don't burn up?
047	2CO	011	030	If I have to boast, I will boast about how weak I am.
047	2CO	011	031	The God and Father of the Lord Jesus—may he be praised forever—knows I am not lying.
047	2CO	011	032	While I was in Damascus, the governor under King Aretas had the city guarded in order to capture me.
047	2CO	011	033	But I was lowered in a basket from a window in the city wall, and so I escaped from him.
047	2CO	012	001	I suppose I have to boast, even though it doesn't really help. Let me go on to visions and revelations from the Lord.
047	2CO	012	002	I know a man in Christ who fourteen years ago was taken up to the third heaven (whether physically in the body, or out of it, I don't know, but God knows).
047	2CO	012	003	I know that this man (whether taken up physically in the body, or apart from it, I don't know, but God knows),
047	2CO	012	004	how he was taken up into Paradise, and heard things too wonderful to be spoken, in words so sacred that no human being is allowed to say.
047	2CO	012	005	Something like that I'll boast about, but I won't boast about myself, except for my weaknesses.
047	2CO	012	006	I wouldn't be foolish if I wanted to boast, because I'd be telling the truth. But I won't boast, so that nobody will think more of me than what they see me doing or hear me saying.
047	2CO	012	007	Also, because these revelations were so amazingly great, and so that I wouldn't become proud, I was given a “thorn in my flesh”—a messenger from Satan to hurt me so that I wouldn't become proud.
047	2CO	012	008	I pleaded with the Lord three times to get rid of this problem.
047	2CO	012	009	But he told me, “My grace is all you will need, for my power is effective in weakness.” That's why I happily boast about my weaknesses, so that Christ's power may reside in me.
047	2CO	012	010	So I appreciate weaknesses, insults, troubles, persecutions, and difficulties that I suffer for Christ's sake. For when I'm weak, then I'm strong!
047	2CO	012	011	I'm talking like a fool, but you made me do it! You should really have been speaking well of me, for in no way am I inferior to the super-apostles, even though I don't count for anything.
047	2CO	012	012	Yet the marks of an apostle were patiently demonstrated among you—signs, wonders, and powerful miracles.
047	2CO	012	013	In what way were you inferior to the other churches except I wasn't any burden to you? Please forgive me for doing you wrong!
047	2CO	012	014	Now I'm preparing to visit you for the third time, and I won't be a burden to you. I don't want what you have, I want you yourselves! After all, children shouldn't save up for their parents, but parents should for their children.
047	2CO	012	015	I will happily spend myself, and be spent, for you. If I love you so much more, will you love me even less?
047	2CO	012	016	Well, even if that's so, I wasn't a burden to you. Maybe I was being devious, and tricked you with my cunning ways!
047	2CO	012	017	But did I take advantage of you by anyone I've sent to you?
047	2CO	012	018	I urged Titus to go and see you, and I sent another brother with him. Did Titus take advantage of you? No, we both have the same spirit and use the same methods.
047	2CO	012	019	Maybe you're thinking that all along we've been just trying to defend ourselves. No, we speak for Christ before God. Everything we do, friends, is for your benefit.
047	2CO	012	020	I do worry when I visit that somehow I won't find you as I would want to, and that you won't find me as you would want to! I'm afraid that there will be arguments, jealousy, anger, rivalry, slander, gossip, arrogance, and disorder.
047	2CO	012	021	I'm afraid that when I visit, my God will humble me in your presence, and that I will be weeping over many of those who have sinned previously, and who still have not repented of impurity, sexual immorality, and indecent acts that they committed.
047	2CO	013	001	This is my third visit to you. “Any charge must be verified by two or three witnesses.”
047	2CO	013	002	I already warned those of you who were sinning when I visited the second time. Even though I'm not there, I'm warning them again—and all the rest of you—that when I visit I won't hesitate to act against them,
047	2CO	013	003	since you're demanding proof that Christ is speaking through me. He is not weak in the way he relates to you; rather he works powerfully among you.
047	2CO	013	004	Even though he was crucified in weakness, now he lives through the power of God. We too are weak in him, but you will see that we live with him through the power of God.
047	2CO	013	005	Examine yourselves to see if you are trusting God. Put yourselves to the test. Don't you yourselves realize that Jesus Christ is in you? Unless you have failed the test…
047	2CO	013	006	However, I hope that you realize that we have not failed the test.
047	2CO	013	007	We pray to God that you won't do anything bad—not so we can show we passed the test, but so you can do what is good, even if we appear to be failures.
047	2CO	013	008	We can't do anything against the truth, only for the truth.
047	2CO	013	009	We're happy when we are weak, and you are strong—we pray that you may continue to improve.
047	2CO	013	010	That is why I write about this while I'm not with you, so that when I am with you I won't have to treat you harshly by imposing my authority. The Lord gave me authority for building up, not for tearing down.
047	2CO	013	011	Finally, brothers and sisters, I say goodbye. Continue to improve spiritually. Encourage one another. Be in agreement. Live in peace, and the God of love and peace will be with you.
047	2CO	013	012	Greet each other with Christian affection.
047	2CO	013	013	All the believers here send their greetings.
047	2CO	013	014	May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God, and the communion of the Holy Spirit be with you all.
#
# BOOK	048	GAL	Galatians	Galatians
048	GAL	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, an apostle not appointed by any human organization or human authority. Quite the contrary: I was appointed by Jesus Christ and God the Father who raised Jesus from the dead.
048	GAL	001	002	All the brothers and sisters here with me join in sending this letter to the churches in Galatia.
048	GAL	001	003	May the grace and peace of God the Father and our Lord Jesus Christ be with you!
048	GAL	001	004	Jesus gave himself for our sins to set us free from this current world of evil, following the will of our God and Father.
048	GAL	001	005	To him be glory forever and ever! Amen.
048	GAL	001	006	I'm shocked at how quickly you're abandoning the God who by the grace of Christ called you. You are turning to a different kind of good news
048	GAL	001	007	that isn't good news at all! Some people there are confusing you, wanting to pervert the good news of Christ.
048	GAL	001	008	But if anyone, even we ourselves, or even an angel from heaven, should promote any other kind of good news than what we have already told you, let them be condemned!
048	GAL	001	009	I repeat what we've told you before: if anyone promotes any other kind of good news than what you've already accepted, let them be condemned!
048	GAL	001	010	Whose approval do you think I want—that of people, or of God? Do you think I'm trying to please people? If I wanted to please people I wouldn't be a servant of Christ!
048	GAL	001	011	Let me make it clear, my friends, regarding the good news I'm declaring—it did not come from any human being.
048	GAL	001	012	I didn't receive it from anyone, and nobody taught it to me—it was Jesus Christ who revealed it to me.
048	GAL	001	013	You heard how I behaved as a follower of the Jewish religion—how I fanatically persecuted God's church, savagely trying to destroy it.
048	GAL	001	014	I surpassed my contemporaries in the practice of the Jewish religion because I was so fervently devoted to the traditions of my ancestors.
048	GAL	001	015	But when God (who had set me apart from birth) called me through his grace, and was pleased
048	GAL	001	016	to reveal his Son to me so that I could announce the good news to the nations, I didn't discuss this with anyone.
048	GAL	001	017	I didn't go to Jerusalem to talk to those who preceded me as apostles; instead I left for Arabia, and then later returned to Damascus.
048	GAL	001	018	After three years I went to Jerusalem to visit Peter. I stayed with him for two weeks.
048	GAL	001	019	I didn't see any other apostles except James, the Lord's brother.
048	GAL	001	020	(Let me assure you before God that I'm not lying about what I'm writing to you!)
048	GAL	001	021	Then I went to Syria and Cilicia.
048	GAL	001	022	Even so, my face wasn't known to those in the churches of Judea.
048	GAL	001	023	They had only heard people say, “The man who used to persecute us is now spreading the faith he once tried to destroy!”
048	GAL	001	024	—and they praised God because of me.
048	GAL	002	001	Fourteen years later I returned to Jerusalem with Barnabas. I took Titus along with me.
048	GAL	002	002	I went because of what God had shown me. I met with the recognized church leaders there in private and explained to them the good news I was sharing with the foreigners. I didn't want the course I had followed, and what I was working so hard for, to come to nothing.
048	GAL	002	003	But as it turned out, nobody even insisted that Titus who was with me should be circumcised, though he was Greek.
048	GAL	002	004	(That issue only arose because some false Christians slipped in to spy on the freedom we have in Christ Jesus, trying to make us slaves.
048	GAL	002	005	We never gave in to them, not even for a moment. We wanted to make sure to keep the truth of the good news unchanged for you.)
048	GAL	002	006	But those considered to be important didn't add anything to what I said. (It doesn't concern me what kind of leaders they were, because God doesn't judge people the way we do.)
048	GAL	002	007	On the contrary, once they realized that I'd been given responsibility to share the good news with the foreigners just as Peter had been given the responsibility to share the good news with the Jews,
048	GAL	002	008	(for the same God who worked through Peter as apostle to the Jews also worked through me as apostle to the foreigners),
048	GAL	002	009	and once they recognized the grace that had been given to me, then James, Peter, and John, who bore the responsibility of church leadership, shook Barnabas and me by the hand as their fellow-workers.
048	GAL	002	010	We were to work for the foreigners, while they would work for the Jews. Their only instruction was to remember to look after the poor, something I was already very committed to.
048	GAL	002	011	However, when Peter came to Antioch I did have to confront him directly, because he was clearly wrong in what he did.
048	GAL	002	012	Before some of James' friends arrived, Peter used to eat with the foreigners. But when these people came he stopped doing this and stayed away from the foreigners. He was afraid of being criticized by those who insisted that men had to be circumcised.
048	GAL	002	013	As well as Peter, other Jewish Christians became hypocritical too, to the extent that even Barnabas was persuaded to follow their hypocrisy.
048	GAL	002	014	When I realized that they weren't taking a firm stand for the truth of the good news, I said to Peter in front of everyone, “If you're a Jew yet live like the foreigners and not like Jews, why are you forcing the foreigners to live like Jews?
048	GAL	002	015	We may be Jews by birth, and not ‘sinners’ like the foreigners,
048	GAL	002	016	but we know that nobody is made right by doing what the law demands—it is only through trusting in Jesus Christ. We have trusted in Christ Jesus so that we could be made right by placing our confidence in Christ, and not through doing what the law says—because nobody is made right by observing the requirements of the law.”
048	GAL	002	017	For if, as we look to be made right in Christ, we ourselves prove to be sinners, does that then mean that Christ is in the service of sin? Of course not!
048	GAL	002	018	For if I were to rebuild what I've destroyed, then I only demonstrate I'm a law-breaker.
048	GAL	002	019	For through the law I died to the law in order that I could live for God.
048	GAL	002	020	I've been crucified with Christ— so it's no longer I who lives, but it is Christ living in me. The life I now live in this body, I live by trusting in the Son of God, who loved me, and who gave himself for me.
048	GAL	002	021	How could I dismiss God's grace? For if we could be made right through keeping the law then Christ died a pointless death!
048	GAL	003	001	You Galatians, you've lost your heads! Who has put you under a spell? The death of Jesus Christ on a cross was clearly presented to you so you could see!
048	GAL	003	002	So tell me—did you receive the Spirit by keeping the law, or by placing your trust in what you heard?
048	GAL	003	003	You really have lost your heads! You began living in the Spirit. Do you really think you can now make yourselves perfect by your own human efforts?
048	GAL	003	004	Did you go through so much suffering for nothing? (It really wasn't for nothing was it?)
048	GAL	003	005	Let me ask you: does God give you the Spirit and do so many miracles among you because you keep the law, or is it because you trust in what you heard?
048	GAL	003	006	It's just like Abraham who “trusted God, and was considered to be right.”
048	GAL	003	007	So you should acknowledge that those who trust in God are the children of Abraham.
048	GAL	003	008	In Scripture it was foreseen that God would make right the foreigners who trusted in him. The good news is revealed to Abraham beforehand with the words, “Through you all the nations will be blessed.”
048	GAL	003	009	Consequently those who trust in God are blessed along with Abraham who trusted God.
048	GAL	003	010	All those who rely on keeping the law are under a curse, for as Scripture says, “Cursed is everyone who doesn't carefully obey everything that's written in the book of the law.”
048	GAL	003	011	Clearly nobody is made right with God by attempting to keep the law, for “Those who are made right will live by trusting God.”
048	GAL	003	012	Obedience to the law has nothing to do with trusting God. Scripture only says, “You will live if you observe everything the law requires.”
048	GAL	003	013	Christ has rescued us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us. As Scripture says, “Cursed is everyone who is hanged on a tree”—
048	GAL	003	014	so that through Christ Jesus the blessing of Abraham could come to the foreigners as well, and we could receive the promise of the Spirit by trusting God.
048	GAL	003	015	Brothers and sisters, here's an example from daily life. If a contract is drawn up and agreed, signed and sealed, nobody can ignore it or add to it.
048	GAL	003	016	Now the promises were given to Abraham, and to his son. It doesn't say, “sons” as if plural, but singular: “and to your son,” meaning Christ.
048	GAL	003	017	Let me explain. The law, coming four hundred and thirty years later, doesn't cancel the previous agreement that God made, breaking the promise.
048	GAL	003	018	If the inheritance is derived from obedience to the law, it no longer comes from the promise. But God graciously gave it to Abraham by means of the promise.
048	GAL	003	019	What was the point of the law, then? It was added to show what wrongdoing really is, until the son came to whom the promise had been made. The law was put in place by angels through the hand of a mediator.
048	GAL	003	020	But a mediator isn't needed when there's only one person involved. And God is one!
048	GAL	003	021	So does the law work against God's promises? Of course not! For if there was a law that could give life, then we could be made right by keeping it.
048	GAL	003	022	But Scripture tells us that we all are prisoners of sin. The only way we can receive God's promises is by trusting in Jesus Christ.
048	GAL	003	023	Before we trusted in Jesus we remained in the custody of the law until this way of trusting was revealed.
048	GAL	003	024	The law was our guardian until Christ came, so that we could be made right by trusting him.
048	GAL	003	025	But now this way of trusting Jesus has come, we no longer need such a guardian.
048	GAL	003	026	For you are all God's children through your trust in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	027	All of you who were baptized into Christ have clothed yourselves with Christ.
048	GAL	003	028	There's no longer Jew or Greek, slave or free, male or female—you are all one in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	029	If you are Christ's, then you are Abraham's children, and you are heirs of the promise!
048	GAL	004	001	Let me explain what I'm saying. An heir who is underage is no different from a slave, even though the heir may be the owner of everything.
048	GAL	004	002	An heir is subject to guardians and managers until the time set by the father.
048	GAL	004	003	It's just the same for us. When we were children, we were slaves subject to the basic rules of the law.
048	GAL	004	004	But at the appropriate time God sent his Son, born of a woman, born under the rule of law,
048	GAL	004	005	so that he could rescue those who were kept under the rule of law, so that we could receive the inheritance of adopted children.
048	GAL	004	006	To show you are his children, God sent the Spirit of his Son to convince us, causing us to call out, “Abba,” meaning “Father.”
048	GAL	004	007	Since you are now no longer a slave, but a child, and if you are his child, then God has made you his heir.
048	GAL	004	008	At the time when you didn't know God, you were enslaved by the supposed “gods” of this world.
048	GAL	004	009	But now you've come to know God—or better, to be known by God. So how can you go back to those useless and worthless rules? Do you want to be slaves to those rules all over again?
048	GAL	004	010	You're observing special days and months, seasons and years.
048	GAL	004	011	I'm concerned that all I did for you has been wasted!
048	GAL	004	012	I'm pleading with you, my friends: be like me, because I became like you. You've never treated me badly.
048	GAL	004	013	You remember that it was because I was sick that I shared with you the good news on my first visit.
048	GAL	004	014	Even though my illness was difficult for you, you didn't despise or reject me—in fact you treated me like an angel of God, like Christ Jesus himself.
048	GAL	004	015	So what's happened to all your gratefulness? I tell you, back then if you could have pulled out your eyes and given them to me, you would have!
048	GAL	004	016	So what has happened—have I become your enemy by telling you the truth?
048	GAL	004	017	These people are keen to gain your support, but not for any good reasons. On the contrary, they want to keep you away from us so that you will enthusiastically support them.
048	GAL	004	018	Of course it's good to want to do good. But this should be at all times, not just when I'm there with you!
048	GAL	004	019	My dear friends, I want to work with you until Christ's character is duplicated in you.
048	GAL	004	020	I really wish I could be with you right now so I could change my tone of voice… I'm so worried about you.
048	GAL	004	021	Answer me this, you people who want to live under the law: Don't you hear what the law is saying?
048	GAL	004	022	As Scripture says, Abraham had two sons, one from the servant girl, and one from the free woman.
048	GAL	004	023	However, the son from the servant girl was born following a human plan, while the son from the free woman was born as the result of the promise.
048	GAL	004	024	This provides an analogy: these two women represent two agreements. One agreement is from Mount Sinai—Hagar—and she gives birth to slave children.
048	GAL	004	025	Hagar symbolizes Mount Sinai in Arabia, and corresponds to the current Jerusalem, because she is in slavery with her children.
048	GAL	004	026	But the heavenly Jerusalem is free. She is our mother.
048	GAL	004	027	As Scripture says, “Rejoice you who are childless and who have never given birth! Shout aloud for joy, you who have never been in labor—for the abandoned woman has more children than the woman who has a husband!”
048	GAL	004	028	Now my friends, we are children of promise just like Isaac.
048	GAL	004	029	However, just as the one born according to a human plan persecuted the one born through the Spirit, so it is today.
048	GAL	004	030	But what does Scripture say? “Send away the servant girl and her son, for the son of the servant girl will not be an heir together with the son of the free woman.”
048	GAL	004	031	Therefore, my friends, we're not children of a servant girl, but of the free woman.
048	GAL	005	001	Christ set us free so we could have real freedom. So stand firm and don't get burdened down again by a yoke of slavery.
048	GAL	005	002	Let me, Paul, tell you bluntly: if you rely on the way of circumcision, Christ will be of absolutely no benefit to you.
048	GAL	005	003	Let me repeat: every man who is circumcised has to keep the whole of the law.
048	GAL	005	004	Those of you who think you can be made right by the law are cut off from Christ—you have abandoned grace.
048	GAL	005	005	For through the Spirit we trust and wait in hope to be made right.
048	GAL	005	006	For in Christ Jesus being circumcised or uncircumcised doesn't achieve anything; it's only trust working through love that matters.
048	GAL	005	007	You were doing so well! Who got in the way and prevented you from being convinced by the truth?
048	GAL	005	008	This “persuasion” certainly isn't from the one who calls you.
048	GAL	005	009	You only need a little bit of yeast to raise the whole batch of dough.
048	GAL	005	010	I'm confident in the Lord that you won't change the way you think, and that the one who is confusing you will face the consequences, whoever he is.
048	GAL	005	011	As for me, brothers and sisters, if I were still advocating circumcision—why am I still persecuted? If that was true, it would remove the issue of the cross that offends people so much.
048	GAL	005	012	If only those who are causing you trouble would go even further than circumcision and castrate themselves!
048	GAL	005	013	You, my brothers and sisters, were called to freedom! Just don't use your freedom as an excuse to indulge your sinful human nature—instead serve one another in love.
048	GAL	005	014	For the whole law is summed up in this one command, “You shall love your neighbor as yourself.”
048	GAL	005	015	But if you attack and tear into one another, watch out that you don't completely destroy yourselves!
048	GAL	005	016	My advice is to walk by the Spirit. Don't satisfy the desires of your sinful human nature.
048	GAL	005	017	For the desires of the sinful nature are opposed to the Spirit, and the desires of the Spirit are opposed to the sinful nature. They fight one another, so you don't do what you want to do.
048	GAL	005	018	But if the Spirit leads you, you're not under the law.
048	GAL	005	019	It's clear what the sinful human nature produces: sexual immorality, indecency, sensuality,
048	GAL	005	020	idolatry, sorcery, hatred, rivalry, jealousy, anger, selfish ambition, dissension, heresy,
048	GAL	005	021	envy, drunkenness, feasting, and similar things. As I warned you before so I warn you again: nobody who behaves like this will inherit the kingdom of God.
048	GAL	005	022	But the Spirit produces fruit such as love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, trust,
048	GAL	005	023	gentleness, self-control—and there's no law against these kinds of things!
048	GAL	005	024	Those who belong to Christ Jesus have nailed to the cross their sinful human nature, together with all their sinful passions and desires.
048	GAL	005	025	If we live in the Spirit we should also walk in the Spirit.
048	GAL	005	026	Let's not become boastful, or irritate and envy one another.
048	GAL	006	001	My friends, if someone is led astray by sin, you who are spiritual should bring them back with a gentle spirit. Watch out that you don't get tempted too.
048	GAL	006	002	Carry each other's burdens, for in this way you fulfill the law of Christ.
048	GAL	006	003	Those who think they're really something—when they're actually nothing—only fool themselves.
048	GAL	006	004	Carefully examine your actions. Then you can be satisfied with yourself, without comparing yourself to anyone else.
048	GAL	006	005	We have to take responsibility for ourselves.
048	GAL	006	006	Those that are taught the Word should treat their teachers well, sharing with them all good things.
048	GAL	006	007	Don't be fooled, God can't be treated with contempt: whatever you sow, that's what you reap.
048	GAL	006	008	If you sow according to your sinful human nature, from that nature you'll reap self-destruction. But if you sow according to the Spirit, from the Spirit you'll reap eternal life.
048	GAL	006	009	Let's never tire of doing good, for we'll reap a harvest at the proper time, if we don't give up.
048	GAL	006	010	So while we have time, let's do good to everyone—especially to those who belong to the family of faith.
048	GAL	006	011	Notice how big the letters are, now that I'm writing with my own hand!
048	GAL	006	012	Those people who only want to make a good impression are forcing you to be circumcised just so they won't be persecuted for the cross of Christ.
048	GAL	006	013	Even those who are circumcised don't keep the law, but they want to have you circumcised so that they can boast about you and claim you as their followers.
048	GAL	006	014	May I never boast except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ. Through this cross, the world has been crucified to me, and I've been crucified as far as the world is concerned.
048	GAL	006	015	Circumcision or uncircumcision doesn't matter—what matters is that we're created brand new!
048	GAL	006	016	Peace and mercy to all who follow this principle, and to the Israel of God!
048	GAL	006	017	Please, don't anyone trouble me anymore, because I carry on my body the scars of Jesus.
048	GAL	006	018	My brothers and sisters, may the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
#
# BOOK	049	EPH	Ephesians	Ephesians
049	EPH	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus according to God's will, to the Christians in Ephesus and those who trust in Christ Jesus.
049	EPH	001	002	Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	001	003	Praise God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with all that's spiritually good in the heavenly world,
049	EPH	001	004	just as he chose us to be in him before the beginning of this world, so that in love we could be holy and without fault before him.
049	EPH	001	005	He decided in advance to adopt us as his children, working through Jesus Christ to bring us to himself. He was happy to do this because this is what he wanted.
049	EPH	001	006	So we praise him for his glorious grace that he so kindly gave us in his beloved Son.
049	EPH	001	007	Through him we gain salvation through his blood, the forgiveness of our sins as a result of his priceless grace
049	EPH	001	008	that he so generously provided for us, together with all wisdom and understanding.
049	EPH	001	009	He revealed to us his previously-hidden will through which he was happy to pursue his plan
049	EPH	001	010	at the appropriate time to bring everyone together in Christ—those in heaven and those on the earth.
049	EPH	001	011	In him—we were chosen beforehand, according to the plan of the one who is working everything out according to his will,
049	EPH	001	012	for the purpose that we who were the first to hope in Christ could praise his glory.
049	EPH	001	013	In him—you too have heard the word of truth, the good news of your salvation. In him—because you trusted in him you were stamped with the seal of the Holy Spirit's promise,
049	EPH	001	014	which is a down-payment on our inheritance when God redeems what he's kept safe for himself—us, who will praise and give him glory!
049	EPH	001	015	That's the reason, because I've heard of your trust in the Lord Jesus and the love that you have for all Christians,
049	EPH	001	016	why I never stop thanking God for you and remember you in my prayers.
049	EPH	001	017	I pray that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you a spirit of wisdom to see and know him as he really is.
049	EPH	001	018	May your minds be enlightened so you can understand the hope he's called you to— the glorious riches he promises as an inheritance to his holy people.
049	EPH	001	019	May you also understand God's amazing power
049	EPH	001	020	that he demonstrated in raising Christ from the dead. God seated Christ at his right hand in heaven,
049	EPH	001	021	far above any other ruler, authority, power, or lord, or any leader with all their titles—not only in this world, but also in the coming world too.
049	EPH	001	022	God has made everything subject to the authority of Christ, and has given him the responsibility as head over everything for the church,
049	EPH	001	023	which is his body, filled full and made complete by Christ, who fills and brings everything to completion.
049	EPH	002	001	At one time you were dead in your sins and evil actions,
049	EPH	002	002	living your lives according to the ways of the world, under the control of the devil, whose spirit is at work in those who disobey God.
049	EPH	002	003	All of us were once like that, our behavior determined by the desires of our sinful human nature and our evil way of thinking. Like everyone else, in our nature we were children of anger.
049	EPH	002	004	But God in his generous mercy, because of the amazing love he had for us
049	EPH	002	005	even while we were dead in our sins, has made us alive together with Christ. Trusting in him has saved you!
049	EPH	002	006	He raised us up with Christ, and in Christ Jesus seated us with him in heaven,
049	EPH	002	007	so that in all eternity to come he could demonstrate the amazing extent of his grace in showing us kindness through Christ Jesus.
049	EPH	002	008	For you've been saved by grace through trusting in him—it's not through yourselves, it's the gift of God!
049	EPH	002	009	This has nothing to do with human effort, so don't be proud of yourselves.
049	EPH	002	010	We're the product of what God does, created in Christ Jesus to do good, which God already planned that we should do.
049	EPH	002	011	So you who are “foreigners” humanly-speaking, called “uncircumcised” by those who are “circumcised” (which is only a procedure carried out by human beings), you need to remember
049	EPH	002	012	that once you had no relationship to Christ. You were barred as foreigners from being citizens of Israel, strangers to the agreement God had promised. You had no hope and you lived in the world without God.
049	EPH	002	013	But now, in Christ Jesus, you who were once a long way off have been brought near by the blood of Christ.
049	EPH	002	014	Christ is our peace. Through his body he made the two into one, and broke down the separating wall of hostility that divided us,
049	EPH	002	015	freeing us from the law with its requirements and regulations. He did this so he could create in himself one new person out of the two and so make peace,
049	EPH	002	016	and completely reconcile both of them to God through the cross as if they were just one body, having destroyed our hostility towards each other.
049	EPH	002	017	He came and shared the good news of peace with those of you who were far away, and those who were nearby,
049	EPH	002	018	because through him we both gain access to the Father through the same Spirit.
049	EPH	002	019	That means you're no longer strangers and foreigners; you are fellow citizens of God's people and belong to God's family
049	EPH	002	020	that's being built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, with Christ Jesus as the cornerstone.
049	EPH	002	021	In him the whole building is joined together, growing to form a holy temple for the Lord.
049	EPH	002	022	You too are being built together in him as a place for God to live by the Spirit.
049	EPH	003	001	This is why, I, Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ for the sake of you foreigners,
049	EPH	003	002	(well, I'm assuming you've heard that God gave me the specific responsibility of sharing God's grace with you),
049	EPH	003	003	how, by what God showed me, made clear the mystery that was previously hidden. I wrote to you briefly before about this,
049	EPH	003	004	and when you read this you'll be able to understand my insight into the mystery of Christ.
049	EPH	003	005	In past generations this wasn't made clear to anyone, but now it's been revealed to God's holy apostles and prophets by the Spirit
049	EPH	003	006	that foreigners are joint heirs, part of the same body, and in Christ Jesus share together in the promise through the good news.
049	EPH	003	007	I became a minister of this good news through the gift of God's grace that I was given by his power that was at work in me.
049	EPH	003	008	This grace was given to me, the least important of all Christians, in order to share with the foreigners the incredible value of Christ,
049	EPH	003	009	and to help everyone see the purpose of the mystery which from the very beginning was hidden in God who made everything.
049	EPH	003	010	God's plan was that through the church the various aspects of his wisdom would be revealed to the rulers and authorities in heaven.
049	EPH	003	011	This was in accordance with God's eternal purpose that he carried out in Christ Jesus our Lord.
049	EPH	003	012	Because of him and our trust in him we can come to God in total freedom and confidence.
049	EPH	003	013	So I'm asking that you don't get discouraged that I'm suffering—it's for you and you should value that!
049	EPH	003	014	This is why I kneel before the Father
049	EPH	003	015	from whom every family in heaven and on earth receives its nature and character,
049	EPH	003	016	asking him that out of his wealth of glory he may strengthen you in your innermost being with power through his Spirit.
049	EPH	003	017	May Christ live in you as you trust in him, so that as you are planted deep in love,
049	EPH	003	018	you may have the power to comprehend with all God's people the breadth and length and height and depth of Christ's love.
049	EPH	003	019	May you know the love of Christ that surpasses knowledge, so that you're made full and complete by the fullness of God.
049	EPH	003	020	Now may he who—through his power working in us—can do infinitely more than we ever ask for or even think about,
049	EPH	003	021	may he be glorified in the church and in Christ Jesus through all generations for ever and ever. Amen.
049	EPH	004	001	So I—this prisoner in the Lord—am encouraging you to make sure you live according to the principles to which you were called.
049	EPH	004	002	Don't think proudly of yourselves; be gentle and patient, showing tolerance to each other in love.
049	EPH	004	003	Make every effort to remain one in the Spirit through the peace that binds you together.
049	EPH	004	004	For there's one body, and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope.
049	EPH	004	005	The Lord is one, our trust in him is one, and there's one baptism;
049	EPH	004	006	there's one God and Father of everyone. He is over all and through all and in all.
049	EPH	004	007	To each of us grace was given in proportion to Christ's generous gift.
049	EPH	004	008	As Scripture says, “When he ascended to the heights he took captives with him, and gave gifts to humanity.”
049	EPH	004	009	(Regarding this: it says he ascended, but that means he also had previously descended to our lowly world.
049	EPH	004	010	The one that descended is the same one who also ascended to the highest heaven in order that he could make the whole universe complete.)
049	EPH	004	011	The gifts he gave were so that some could be apostles, prophets, evangelists, pastors and teachers,
049	EPH	004	012	with the purpose of preparing God's people for the work of helping others, to help the body of Christ to grow.
049	EPH	004	013	We grow together until we all reach the state of being one in our trust in and knowledge of the Son of God, completely grown up, measuring up to full maturity in Christ.
049	EPH	004	014	We shouldn't be little children any more, tossed about and blown along by every passing breeze of doctrine, confused by human trickery, led into error by crafty people who deceitfully scheme.
049	EPH	004	015	Instead by speaking the truth in love we ought to grow up in everything into Christ, who is our head.
049	EPH	004	016	It's because of him that the whole body operates, every joint holding it together as each individual part does what it's supposed to, and the whole body grows, building itself up in love.
049	EPH	004	017	So let me say this to you—in fact I insist on it in the Lord—that you should no longer live like the foreigners do, in their empty-headed way.
049	EPH	004	018	In the darkness of their minds they don't understand, and they have been cut off from the life of God because they don't know anything and in their stubbornness they don't want to know.
049	EPH	004	019	Because they are past caring they abandon themselves to sensuality, and greedily do all kinds of disgusting things.
049	EPH	004	020	But that's not what you learned about Christ!
049	EPH	004	021	Didn't you hear about him? Weren't you taught concerning him? Didn't you learn the truth as it is in Jesus?
049	EPH	004	022	So get rid of your former lifestyle, that old nature that ruins you through deceptive desires!
049	EPH	004	023	Let yourselves be remade spiritually and mentally,
049	EPH	004	024	and put on your new nature that God created so you will be like him, right and holy in the truth.
049	EPH	004	025	So reject lies, and tell the truth to each other—for we belong to each other.
049	EPH	004	026	Don't sin by getting angry; don't let evening come and find you still mad—
049	EPH	004	027	and don't give the devil any opportunity.
049	EPH	004	028	Thieves, stop your stealing, and do honest, productive work with your hands, so you'll have something to give to those who need it.
049	EPH	004	029	Don't use bad language. Speak words that will encourage people as necessary, so that those who listen will be helped.
049	EPH	004	030	Don't disappoint the Holy Spirit of God that marked you as belonging to him until the day of redemption.
049	EPH	004	031	Get rid of every kind of bitterness, rage, anger, verbal abuse, and insults, along with all forms of evil.
049	EPH	004	032	Be kind and compassionate to each other, forgiving one another, just as God in Christ forgave you.
049	EPH	005	001	So then, imitate God since you're his much-loved children.
049	EPH	005	002	Live in love, just as Christ loved you. He gave himself for us, a gift and sacrificial offering to God like a sweet-smelling perfume.
049	EPH	005	003	Sexual immorality or any kind of indecency or greed should never be mentioned concerning you, as God's people should not be doing such things.
049	EPH	005	004	Obscene talk, stupid chatter, and coarse jokes are totally inappropriate—instead you should be thanking God.
049	EPH	005	005	You know it's absolutely sure that no one who is sexually immoral, or commits indecency, or who is greedy, or is an idol-worshiper will inherit anything in the kingdom of Christ and God.
049	EPH	005	006	Don't let anyone fool you with lying words, for it's because of such things that God's judgment comes upon the children of disobedience.
049	EPH	005	007	So don't partner with them in this.
049	EPH	005	008	At one time you were darkness, but now you are light in the Lord. You are to live as children of light
049	EPH	005	009	(and the fruit of light is everything that's good and right and true),
049	EPH	005	010	demonstrating what the Lord really appreciates.
049	EPH	005	011	Don't have anything to do with the pointless things that darkness produces—instead expose them.
049	EPH	005	012	It's shameful even to speak about the things such people do secretly,
049	EPH	005	013	but when anything is exposed by the light then it's revealed as it is. Light makes everything visible.
049	EPH	005	014	That's why it's said, “Wake up, those of you who are sleeping, rise up from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.”
049	EPH	005	015	So be careful how you live your life, not foolishly, but wisely,
049	EPH	005	016	making the best use of opportunities because the days are evil.
049	EPH	005	017	So don't be ignorant—find out what the Lord's will is.
049	EPH	005	018	Don't get drunk on wine which will wreck your life, but be filled with the Spirit.
049	EPH	005	019	Share together with one another, using psalms and hymns and sacred songs, singing and making music to the Lord to express what you feel.
049	EPH	005	020	Always thank God the Father for everything in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	005	021	Each of you should be willing to accept what others tell you to do out of reverence for Christ.
049	EPH	005	022	Wives, do what your own husbands tell you to do, as you would if the Lord told you.
049	EPH	005	023	The husband is head of the wife in the same way as Christ is head of the church—his body and its savior.
049	EPH	005	024	In the same way that the church does what Christ says, wives should do what their husbands tell them in all things.
049	EPH	005	025	Husbands, you should love your wives in the same way as Christ loved the church and gave himself for it.
049	EPH	005	026	He made it holy, he made it clean by washing in the water of the word,
049	EPH	005	027	so that he could make the church his own, with no flaw or blemish or any kind of fault, but holy and blameless.
049	EPH	005	028	Husbands should love their wives just like this, as they love their own bodies. A man who loves his wife loves himself—
049	EPH	005	029	for no one ever hated his own body, but feeds it and looks after it, just as Christ does for the church,
049	EPH	005	030	for we are parts of his body.
049	EPH	005	031	“This is why a man leaves his father and mother, and is joined to his wife, and the two are united in one.”
049	EPH	005	032	This is a deep hidden truth—but I'm talking about Christ and the church.
049	EPH	005	033	However, each husband should love his own wife as he does himself, and the wife should respect her husband.
049	EPH	006	001	Children, do what your parents tell you, for this is the right thing to do.
049	EPH	006	002	“Honor your father and mother.” This is the first commandment that has a promise attached:
049	EPH	006	003	“that things may go well for you and you may live a long life on the earth.”
049	EPH	006	004	Fathers, don't make your children mad, but look after them by disciplining them and instructing them about God.
049	EPH	006	005	Servants, obey those who are your human masters, with proper respect and awe, doing things from sincere motives as if you were serving Christ.
049	EPH	006	006	Don't just work well when you're being watched to gain approval, but work like servants of Christ, honestly doing God's will,
049	EPH	006	007	happily serving as if you were doing it for the Lord, and not for people.
049	EPH	006	008	You know that whoever does what's good will be rewarded by the Lord, whether that person is a servant or someone who is free.
049	EPH	006	009	Masters, you should treat your servants the same way. Don't threaten them, remember that the Lord in heaven is both their master and yours, and he treats people the same, without favoritism.
049	EPH	006	010	Lastly, stay strong in the Lord, and in his mighty power.
049	EPH	006	011	Put on all the armor of God so you can withstand all the devil's attacks!
049	EPH	006	012	We're not fighting against human forces, but against supernatural rulers and powers, the dark lords of this world, against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavens.
049	EPH	006	013	Take all the weapons God provides so that you may be able to stand your ground in the day of evil and after doing all you can, to find yourself still standing!
049	EPH	006	014	So stand up, wrap the belt of truth around your waist, tie on the breastplate of justice and the right,
049	EPH	006	015	and put on the shoes of readiness to share the good news of peace.
049	EPH	006	016	Above all, take up the shield of trusting God, by which you'll be able to put out all the devil's flaming arrows.
049	EPH	006	017	Wear the helmet of salvation, and carry the sword of the Spirit—the Spirit that's the word of God.
049	EPH	006	018	Always pray in the Spirit as you do all this. Stay awake and keep on praying for all God's people.
049	EPH	006	019	Pray for me too so that I'll be given the right words to say, and that I'll be able to explain confidently the hidden truths of the good news.
049	EPH	006	020	I'm an imprisoned ambassador for the sake of the good news, so please pray that I will speak fearlessly, as I should.
049	EPH	006	021	Tychicus, our good friend and faithful minister, will give you all my news and explain everything so you'll know how I'm doing.
049	EPH	006	022	That's why I'm sending him to you—to tell you what's happened to us and to encourage you.
049	EPH	006	023	Peace to all the Christians there, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ, with love and trust in him.
049	EPH	006	024	Grace to all those who eternally love our Lord Jesus.
