# BOOK	050	PHI	Philippians	Philippians
050	PHI	001	001	This letter comes from Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus, to all God's people in Christ Jesus living in Philippi, and to the church leaders and assistants.
050	PHI	001	002	Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	001	003	When I think of you I'm so thankful to my God,
050	PHI	001	004	and I'm always glad to remember all of you in my prayers,
050	PHI	001	005	because you've been partners with me in spreading the good news right from the beginning up till now.
050	PHI	001	006	I'm absolutely sure that God who began this good work in you will continue working and bring it to a successful conclusion when Jesus Christ returns.
050	PHI	001	007	It's appropriate for me to be thinking this way about all of you because you mean so much to me. Whether I'm in prison or out there making the good news clear, all of you share God's grace together with me.
050	PHI	001	008	God is my witness as to my great affection for every one of you in the caring love of Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	001	009	My prayer is that your love may grow more and more in knowledge and understanding,
050	PHI	001	010	so that you can work out what's really important. That way you can be genuine and blameless when Christ returns,
050	PHI	001	011	filled with the fruits of living right that come through Jesus Christ and give glory and praise to God.
050	PHI	001	012	I want you to know, my brothers and sisters, that all I've experienced has worked out to move the good news forward!
050	PHI	001	013	For everyone—including the whole praetorian guard—now knows that I'm in chains for Christ;
050	PHI	001	014	and because of my chains most of the Christians here have been encouraged to speak God's word boldly and fearlessly!
050	PHI	001	015	Yes, some speak out of jealousy and rivalry. However, there are those who speak from good motives.
050	PHI	001	016	They act out of love, because they know that I'm meant to be here to defend the good news.
050	PHI	001	017	Those others present Christ deceptively because of their selfish ambitions, trying to cause me problems in my imprisonment.
050	PHI	001	018	But so what? All I care about is that Christ is presented every which way, whether just pretending or whether from true convictions. That's what makes me happy—and I will go on being happy!
050	PHI	001	019	Why? Because I'm convinced that through your prayers for me, and through the help of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, this will turn out to be my salvation.
050	PHI	001	020	For it's my strongest hope and expectation not to do anything of which I would be ashamed. Instead it's my bold hope, as always, that even now Christ will be greatly honored through me, whether I live or die.
050	PHI	001	021	As far as I'm concerned, living is for Christ, and dying brings gain.
050	PHI	001	022	But if I'm to go on living here and this would be productive work, then I really don't know what's best to choose!
050	PHI	001	023	For I'm in a dilemma—I really want to leave and be with Christ, which would be far better,
050	PHI	001	024	and yet to remain physically here is more important as far as you're concerned.
050	PHI	001	025	Since I'm absolutely sure of this, I know that I'll stay here, remaining with you all to help you as your trust and delight in God grows,
050	PHI	001	026	so that when I see you again your praise to Christ Jesus may be even greater because of me.
050	PHI	001	027	Just be sure that the way you live your lives corresponds to the good news of Christ, so that whether I come and see you or not I can get to hear how you're doing—that you stand firm in full agreement with one another, spiritually united as you work together for the trusting faith of the good news.
050	PHI	001	028	Don't let your enemies scare you. By being brave you will demonstrate to them that they will be lost, but that God himself will save you.
050	PHI	001	029	For you have been given the privilege not only of trusting in Jesus, but suffering for him as well.
050	PHI	001	030	You're experiencing the same struggle you saw me having—a struggle I still have, as you now know.
050	PHI	002	001	So then, if you're encouraged by being in Christ, if you're comforted by his love, if you share together in the Spirit, if you have compassion and sympathy—
050	PHI	002	002	then make my joy complete by thinking the same way and loving the same way, spiritually united and having one purpose.
050	PHI	002	003	Don't do anything from a spirit of selfishness or pride, but humbly think of others better than you do of yourself.
050	PHI	002	004	None of you should be preoccupied about your own things—instead concern yourself with the interests of others too.
050	PHI	002	005	The attitude you should have is the same as that of Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	002	006	Though in his nature he was always God, he wasn't concerned to cling onto his equality with God.
050	PHI	002	007	Instead he emptied himself, taking the nature of a servant, becoming like a human being.
050	PHI	002	008	Coming in human form, humbling himself, he submitted himself to death—even death on a cross.
050	PHI	002	009	That's why God placed him in the position of greatest honor and power, and gave him the most prestigious name—
050	PHI	002	010	so that in the name of Jesus everyone should bow in respect, whether in heaven or on earth or under the earth,
050	PHI	002	011	and all will declare that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.
050	PHI	002	012	So, my good friends, continue to work towards the goal of salvation with complete reverence and respect for God, following what you were told—not just when I was with you, but even more so now I'm away from you.
050	PHI	002	013	For it's God who is working within you, creating the will and the ability to do what he wants you to do.
050	PHI	002	014	Do everything without complaining or arguing
050	PHI	002	015	so that you'll be sincere, innocent of any wrong. Be God's blameless children living in the middle of a dishonest and corrupt people. Shine among them as lights to the world,
050	PHI	002	016	holding out to them the word of life. That way I'll have something to be proud of when Christ returns, proving I didn't run around and work for nothing!
050	PHI	002	017	So even if I pour out my life as a sacrifice and offering so you may trust in God, I'm happy for it, and I'm glad together with all of you,
050	PHI	002	018	just as you have such joy and are glad with me.
050	PHI	002	019	I'm hoping, if that's what the Lord Jesus wants, to send Timothy to you soon. It will cheer me up once I know how you're doing.
050	PHI	002	020	I don't know anyone who genuinely cares about you as he does.
050	PHI	002	021	Other people only worry about their own interests, not those of Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	002	022	But you already know what he's like—just as a child working to help his father, so he's worked with me to spread the good news.
050	PHI	002	023	So I hope to send him as soon as I see how I'm doing,
050	PHI	002	024	and I trust in the Lord that shortly I'll be able to come too.
050	PHI	002	025	But I thought it was important to send Epaphroditus to you. He's a brother to me, a co-worker and fellow-soldier. He's the one you sent to look after me,
050	PHI	002	026	and he's been longing to see all of you, worried about you because you'd heard he was sick.
050	PHI	002	027	He certainly was sick—he nearly died—but God had mercy on him. Not just on him, but on me too, so that I wouldn't have tragedy upon tragedy.
050	PHI	002	028	That's why I'm so keen to send him, so that when you see him you'll be happy, and I won't have to be so anxious.
050	PHI	002	029	So welcome him with much happiness in the Lord. Honor people like him,
050	PHI	002	030	because in working for Christ he nearly died, putting his life on the line to make up for the help you weren't in a position to give me.
050	PHI	003	001	To sum up: my dear friends, delight in the Lord! It's not a burden for me to repeat these things to you—it's to keep you safe!
050	PHI	003	002	Watch out for those dogs! Watch out for those who do evil! Watch out for those mutilators!
050	PHI	003	003	For it's we who are truly circumcised, worshiping by the Spirit of God, placing our assurance in Christ Jesus. We have no confidence in human abilities—
050	PHI	003	004	for if there was a way to rely on human nature then I myself could have that confidence! If anyone thinks they have confidence in such human things, then I outdo them:
050	PHI	003	005	I was circumcised on the eighth day, I'm an Israelite of the tribe of Benjamin, a true Hebrew. Regarding legal observance I'm a Pharisee;
050	PHI	003	006	as for religious dedication I was a persecutor of the church; while in regard to doing right according to the law I was blameless!
050	PHI	003	007	But in whatever way such things gained me anything, I count them as a loss for Christ.
050	PHI	003	008	Truly, I count everything as loss in exchange for the incredible benefit I've gained through knowing Christ Jesus my Lord. I've thrown away all these things for him, and consider them trash, so that I might gain Christ.
050	PHI	003	009	I want to be found in him, not being right because of what I've done, or what the law requires, but made right through confidence in Christ, set right by God through trusting in him.
050	PHI	003	010	I want to really know him, and the power of his resurrection—to take part in his suffering and become like him in his death,
050	PHI	003	011	so that somehow I might be part of the resurrection from the dead!
050	PHI	003	012	Not that I've already got it all, or that I'm already perfect—but I run so that I might win what was won for me by Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	013	My friends, I don't consider that I've already won, but this is my one objective: disregarding what is behind me, I strain forward to what is in front of me.
050	PHI	003	014	I run towards the finish line to win the prize of God's invitation to heaven through Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	015	Those of us who are spiritually mature should think like this, and if you think anything different, then God will reveal this to you.
050	PHI	003	016	We just need to make sure that we follow what we already have understood.
050	PHI	003	017	My friends, copy my example as others do and take note of the way to behave since you have us as a model.
050	PHI	003	018	The way some people live makes them enemies of the cross of Christ—as I've often told you before and repeat again though it pains me so much I want to weep.
050	PHI	003	019	They will end up being completely lost, these people whose “god” is their physical desires and who are proud of what they should be ashamed of, thinking only about the things of this world.
050	PHI	003	020	But our homeland is heaven, and we're waiting for a Savior, the Lord Jesus Christ, to come from there too.
050	PHI	003	021	He will re-create our defective human bodies so that they will be made like his glorious body using the power by which he brings everything under his control.
050	PHI	004	001	So stand firm in the Lord, my dear friends who mean so much to me, who make me so happy! To me you are my crowning achievement! I truly love you and long to see you!
050	PHI	004	002	Euodia and Syntyche—I urge you to resolve your differences with each other and agree in the Lord.
050	PHI	004	003	In fact, my faithful fellow-worker, let me ask you to help these women, for they worked together with me to spread the good news—as well as Clement and my other co-workers, whose names are recorded in the book of life.
050	PHI	004	004	Always be happy in the Lord—I repeat, Be happy!
050	PHI	004	005	Everyone should know about your kindness. The Lord will soon be here.
050	PHI	004	006	Don't worry about anything, but take everything to God in prayer, explaining your requests to him and thanking him for all he does.
050	PHI	004	007	Then the peace that comes from God, which is better than we can ever imagine, will protect your thoughts and attitudes in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	008	Lastly, whatever is true, honorable, right, pure, beautiful, commendable, whatever is truly good and deserves to be praised, think about these kinds of things.
050	PHI	004	009	Put into practice what you learned and received from me, what you saw me doing and heard me say. Then the God of peace will be with you.
050	PHI	004	010	I'm so happy in the Lord that you've at last thought about me again—realizing that you were concerned about me before but you couldn't do anything about it.
050	PHI	004	011	I'm not talking about my own needs, because I've already learned to be satisfied in whatever situation I find myself.
050	PHI	004	012	I'm used to having nothing, and I've experienced having plenty too. In every possible situation I've learned the secret of dealing with having plenty and going hungry, of being rich and of living in poverty:
050	PHI	004	013	I can do anything through him who makes me strong!
050	PHI	004	014	Even so it was good of you to share with me during my troubles.
050	PHI	004	015	You Philippians remember that right at the beginning of sharing the good news, when I left Macedonia, that yours was the only church that helped me financially.
050	PHI	004	016	Even when I was in Thessalonica you helped me out not once but twice.
050	PHI	004	017	Not that I'm looking for a donation—I'm looking for your “account” to increase in “profit.”
050	PHI	004	018	For I have everything, more than I need! I'm thankful to receive from Epaphroditus the things you sent. They're like a sweet-smelling sacrifice that pleases God and that he approves of.
050	PHI	004	019	My God will fill you with everything you need in accordance with his glorious wealth in Christ Jesus!
050	PHI	004	020	Glory be to God the Father, forever and ever. Amen.
050	PHI	004	021	Greet every fellow-believer in Christ Jesus. The Christian brothers and sisters with me send their greetings.
050	PHI	004	022	All the believers send you greetings, especially those from Caesar's palace.
050	PHI	004	023	May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.
