# BOOK	051	COL	Colossians	Colossians
051	COL	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus according to the will of God, and from our brother Timothy.
051	COL	001	002	To the believers and trusting Christians at Colossae: May you have grace and peace from God our Father.
051	COL	001	003	We are always thankful to God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ for you, and pray for you.
051	COL	001	004	We've heard about your trust in Christ Jesus and your love for all the believers
051	COL	001	005	because of the hope prepared for you in heaven. You already heard about this in the good news, the message of truth
051	COL	001	006	that came to you just as it has gone throughout the whole world, spreading widely and bringing results. It's done the same for you too, ever since you heard it and realized the true nature of God's grace.
051	COL	001	007	Our dear friend and fellow-worker Epaphras, who is a trustworthy minister of Christ on our behalf, taught you about this.
051	COL	001	008	He's also made clear to us your love in the Spirit.
051	COL	001	009	Because of this we haven't stopped praying for you from the time we heard about you, asking God to give you understanding of what he wants you to do and to give you every kind of spiritual wisdom and understanding.
051	COL	001	010	That way you'll live lives that rightly represent the Lord and please him, producing all kinds of good results and gaining greater knowledge of God.
051	COL	001	011	May you be made powerfully strong by his wonderful strength, having great patience and endurance.
051	COL	001	012	May you happily praise the Father, who has made it possible for us to share in the inheritance of God's people who live in the light.
051	COL	001	013	He rescued us from the tyranny of darkness and brought us into the kingdom of the Son he loves,
051	COL	001	014	through whom we have been set free and our sins forgiven.
051	COL	001	015	The Son is the visible image of the invisible God. He was before all creation,
051	COL	001	016	for everything was created through him—in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, empires, rulers, leaders and authorities—everything was created through him and for him.
051	COL	001	017	He existed before everything, and he holds everything together.
051	COL	001	018	He is also the head of the body, the church. He is the beginning, having the highest position of those raised from the dead, so that he is supreme in everything.
051	COL	001	019	God was pleased to have his full nature live in him,
051	COL	001	020	and through him brought back everything in the universe to himself, since he made peace through the blood of his cross, through him reconciling all those on the earth and in heaven.
051	COL	001	021	You once were alienated from God, enemies in the way you thought and the way you acted,
051	COL	001	022	but now he has reconciled you through his dying human body, bringing you into his presence where you stand holy, pure, and faultless.
051	COL	001	023	But your trust in him must continue rock-solid and immovable. Don't be shaken from the hope of the good news that you heard, the good news that's been shared throughout the world—that's the work that I Paul have been doing.
051	COL	001	024	I'm happy to have trouble for your sake, for by means of what happens to me physically I'm part of Christ's sufferings that he continues to experience for the sake of his body, the church.
051	COL	001	025	I serve the church following the direction God gave me about you, to present fully the word of God to you.
051	COL	001	026	This is the mystery that was hidden down through the ages and for many generations, but it's now been revealed to God's people.
051	COL	001	027	God wanted to make known to them the glorious wealth of this mystery to the nations: Christ living in you is the glorious hope!
051	COL	001	028	We're telling everyone about him, instructing and teaching them in the best way we know how so that we can bring everyone before God fully mature in Christ.
051	COL	001	029	That's what I'm working for too, making every effort as I rely on his strength which is powerfully at work in me.
051	COL	002	001	I want you to know how hard I'm working for you, and for those at Laodicea—in fact for all those who haven't met me personally—
051	COL	002	002	so that you may be encouraged. May you be bound together in love, experiencing the great benefit of being completely sure in your understanding, for this is what the true knowledge of God brings. May you know the revealed mystery of God, which is Christ!
051	COL	002	003	In him you can discover all the rich wisdom and knowledge of God.
051	COL	002	004	I'm telling you this so that no one will fool you by spinning you a tale.
051	COL	002	005	Even though I'm not physically there with you, I'm with you in spirit. I'm so happy to see the way you stick together and how firm you are in your trust in Christ.
051	COL	002	006	Just as you accepted Christ Jesus as Lord, go on following him,
051	COL	002	007	grounded in him and built up by him. May your trust in him continue to grow strong, following what you were taught, full of gratitude to God.
051	COL	002	008	Watch out that nobody enslaves you through their philosophy and worthless delusions, following human traditions and concepts of this world, and not following Christ.
051	COL	002	009	For the fullness of God's divine nature lives in Christ in bodily form,
051	COL	002	010	and you have been made full in him. He is supreme over every ruler and authority.
051	COL	002	011	You were “circumcised” in him but not by human hands. You have been set free from sinful human nature by the “circumcision” Christ performed.
051	COL	002	012	You were buried with him in baptism, and you were raised with him through your trust in what God did by raising him from the dead.
051	COL	002	013	And even though you were dead because of your sins and being physically “uncircumcised,” he brought you to life together with him. He has forgiven us all our sins.
051	COL	002	014	He wiped out the record of our debts according to the Law that was written down against us; he took away this barrier by nailing it to the cross.
051	COL	002	015	He stripped away the power of spiritual rulers and authorities, and having publicly revealed what they were truly like, he led them captive behind him in victory.
051	COL	002	016	So don't let anyone criticize you for what you eat or what you drink, or regarding which religious festival, new moon ritual, or ceremonial sabbaths you choose to observe.
051	COL	002	017	These are just a shadow of what was to come, for the physical reality is Christ.
051	COL	002	018	Don't let anyone cheat you out of your prize by insisting you have to beat yourself, or worship angels. They think they are better than anyone else because of visions they say they've had, and become ridiculously conceited in their sinful minds.
051	COL	002	019	Such people are not connected to the head that directs the body, nourished and joined together through the body's sinews and muscles. As the body is united together it grows the way God wants it to grow.
051	COL	002	020	If you died with Christ to the religious demands that this world insists upon, why would you make yourself subject to such demands as if you were still part of this world?
051	COL	002	021	Things like: don't handle that, don't taste that, don't touch that!
051	COL	002	022	These commands refer to things that don't last since they're used up, and they're based on man-made requirements and teachings.
051	COL	002	023	Such rules may make some kind of sense to those who practice self-centered piety, who are so proud of being humble, and who “mortify the body;” but in reality they don't help at all in dealing with sinful desires.
051	COL	003	001	So if you've been brought back to life with Christ, look for what comes from above, where Christ is, sitting at God's right hand.
051	COL	003	002	Fix your mind on what's above, not what's here on earth.
051	COL	003	003	You died, and your life is kept safe with Christ in God.
051	COL	003	004	When Christ—your life—is revealed, then you will also share in his visible glory.
051	COL	003	005	So kill your worldly nature—sexual sin, immorality, lust, evil desires, greedily wanting to have more—this is the worship of idols.
051	COL	003	006	Because of such things, those who disobey experience God's judgment.
051	COL	003	007	At one time you lived like that when you behaved in such a way,
051	COL	003	008	but now you should get rid of such things as anger, rage, wickedness, abuse, and using obscenities.
051	COL	003	009	Don't lie to each other, since you've discarded your old self and what you used to do,
051	COL	003	010	and put on your new self that is always being made more like your Creator, understanding better who he really is.
051	COL	003	011	In this new situation there's no Greek or Jew, circumcised or uncircumcised, foreigner, barbarian, slave or free, for Christ is everything, and he lives in all of us.
051	COL	003	012	Since you are God's special people, holy and dearly loved, adopt a sympathetic nature that is kind, humble, gentle, and patient.
051	COL	003	013	Be patient with one another, forgive others among you if you have grievances against one another. Just as the Lord forgave you, you should do the same.
051	COL	003	014	Above all, love one another, which is the perfect bond that will hold you together.
051	COL	003	015	May the peace of Christ direct your thinking, because you were called to this by God who makes you one, and thank God for it!
051	COL	003	016	Let Christ's message fully live in you. In every wise way teach and instruct one another through psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing praises to God in gratitude and sincerity.
051	COL	003	017	Whatever you do, whether in word or action, do everything in the name of the Lord Jesus, praising God the Father through him.
051	COL	003	018	You married women, respect your husbands appropriately in the Lord.
051	COL	003	019	You married men, love your wives and don't treat them badly.
051	COL	003	020	You children, always do what your parents tell you because this is what pleases the Lord.
051	COL	003	021	You fathers, don't make your children mad, so they won't feel like giving up.
051	COL	003	022	Those of you who are servants, do everything your human masters tell you, not with just an eye to please them, but honestly and sincerely, respecting the Lord.
051	COL	003	023	Do whatever you do really well, as if you're doing it for God, and not for people,
051	COL	003	024	because you know that the Lord will give you your reward—an inheritance! You're serving Christ the Lord!
051	COL	003	025	Whoever does what's wrong will be paid back for the wrong they've done, and God has no favorites.
051	COL	004	001	You masters, treat your servants in a way that is right and fair, recognizing that you too have a Master in heaven.
051	COL	004	002	Remember to keep on praying, with an alert and thankful mind!
051	COL	004	003	Pray for us too that God may open a door of opportunity to spread the message, to tell about the revealed mystery of Christ—which is the reason I'm here in prison.
051	COL	004	004	Pray that I may make it as clear as I should when I speak.
051	COL	004	005	Behave wisely with outsiders, making the best use of every opportunity.
051	COL	004	006	Always be gracious when you speak. Make sure it's in good taste, and think about how best to answer everyone.
051	COL	004	007	Tychicus will tell you all about what's happening to me. He's a dear brother, a trustworthy minister and co-worker in the Lord.
051	COL	004	008	I'm sending him to you for this very reason—so that you'll know how things are with me and this will cheer you up.
051	COL	004	009	Onesimus is going with him too, a trusted and dear brother, who's one of you. They'll explain to you everything that's going on here.
051	COL	004	010	Aristarchus who's with me here in prison sends his best wishes; likewise Mark, Barnabas' cousin (you've already had instructions to welcome him if he visits you),
051	COL	004	011	and Jesus—also called Justus—who are the only Jewish Christians among those working with me here for the kingdom of God, men who have been a great help to me.
051	COL	004	012	Epaphras who is one of you and a servant of Christ Jesus, sends his greetings. He's always passionate in his prayers on your behalf, praying that you'll stand firm as grown-up Christians, totally convinced about everything as God would want.
051	COL	004	013	For the record I can tell you that he's done a lot for you, and for those in Laodicea and Hierapolis as well.
051	COL	004	014	Luke, our dear doctor, and Demas also send their best.
051	COL	004	015	Greet the believers that are in Laodicea—Nympha too, and the church that meets in her house.
051	COL	004	016	And when this letter has been read to you, make sure it's read to the church in Laodicea too, and that you also read the letter sent to Laodicea.
051	COL	004	017	Tell Archippus, “See that you follow through in doing the ministry God gave you.”
051	COL	004	018	I, Paul, write my closing greetings with my own hand. Remember I'm in prison. Grace be with you.
#
# BOOK	052	1TH	1 Thessalonians	1 Thessalonians
052	1TH	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy to the church of the Thessalonians who belong to God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. May you have grace and peace!
052	1TH	001	002	We are always thanking God for all of you, never forgetting you in our prayers.
052	1TH	001	003	We remember you before our God and Father—how you put your trust in him into practice, how you work hard in love, and how you patiently wait in the hope of our Lord Jesus Christ.
052	1TH	001	004	Brothers and sisters, we already know that you are loved by God and are very special to him.
052	1TH	001	005	The good news we brought to you wasn't just words, but had power too, for the Holy Spirit completely convinced you. In the same way you know what kind of men we are since we demonstrated to you that we were working for your benefit.
052	1TH	001	006	You were imitating us and the Lord when you received the message, for despite your troubles you experienced the joy the Holy Spirit gives.
052	1TH	001	007	So you have become an example to all the believers in Macedonia and Greece!
052	1TH	001	008	You have broadcast the Lord's message, not only in Macedonia and Greece, but everywhere people have heard of your trust in God—so there's no need for us to tell anybody about it!
052	1TH	001	009	In fact they talk about what a marvelous welcome you gave us, how you abandoned idols and turned to God, how you serve the true and living God,
052	1TH	001	010	as you look forward to the coming of his Son from heaven—Jesus, the one God raised from the dead, who will save us from the judgment to come.
052	1TH	002	001	Brothers and sisters, you yourselves know what our visit meant to you, and that it wasn't wasted!
052	1TH	002	002	You'll recall that after having had much trouble and bad treatment at Philippi, with the help of God we still dared to share God's good news with you, despite the opposition we faced.
052	1TH	002	003	For what we speak about isn't deceptive, or worthless, or fraudulent.
052	1TH	002	004	On the contrary, we have God's approval for what we say—he's entrusted us with sharing the good news. We don't set out to please people, but God. He's the one who judges our motives.
052	1TH	002	005	As you know, we've never used flattering words. Nor were we covering up some greedy, selfish attitude—as God is our witness!
052	1TH	002	006	We weren't trying to win anybody's praise—not from you, nor anyone else. We could have become a “burden” to you as messengers of Christ,
052	1TH	002	007	but instead we acted kindly among you, like a mother caring for her own children.
052	1TH	002	008	We loved you so much that we were delighted to share with you not just God's good news, but also our very own selves, because you had become so dear to us.
052	1TH	002	009	Don't you remember, brothers and sisters, all our hard work—working day and night so we wouldn't be a burden to any of you as we shared God's good news with you?
052	1TH	002	010	You yourselves can testify as to how we acted, and God can too—how we treated you believers with a holy attitude, fairly and blamelessly.
052	1TH	002	011	You know how we cared for every one of you like a father caring for his own children. We encouraged you, comforted you, and shared with you our experience
052	1TH	002	012	so that you could live as God would want you to live—the God who calls you to his own kingdom and glory.
052	1TH	002	013	Another thing: we're always thanking God that when you heard and accepted the word of God, you didn't treat it as some human words, but what it truly is, the word of God. This is what is at work in those of you who trust in him.
052	1TH	002	014	The experience you brothers and sisters have had imitates that of God's churches that belong to Christ Jesus in Judaea. Just like your fellow Jewish Christians you suffered as they did at the hands of the Jewish leaders
052	1TH	002	015	who killed the Lord Jesus and the prophets, and chased us out. They don't please God and they are hostile to everyone,
052	1TH	002	016	trying to prevent us from speaking to the other nations to prevent them from being saved. They're always sinning to the maximum extent, but for them full judgment has arrived!
052	1TH	002	017	Brothers and sisters, since we felt as if we'd experienced a family separation because we hadn't seen you for a while (separated physically though not in spirit), we tried even harder to come and see you again face to face because that's what we wanted to do.
052	1TH	002	018	We really wanted to come and visit you, and I, Paul, tried again and again—but Satan stopped us.
052	1TH	002	019	For what gives us hope, what makes us happy, what we are really proud of as we stand before our Lord Jesus Christ when he comes back—is having you there too!
052	1TH	002	020	You are our pride and joy!
052	1TH	003	001	So when we couldn't bear it any longer, we decided it would be best for us to stay behind in Athens,
052	1TH	003	002	and send Timothy on to you. He is our brother and God's co-worker in spreading the good news of Christ. We sent him to strengthen and encourage you in your trust in God
052	1TH	003	003	so that none of you would be upset by your troubles—for you know we should expect such things.
052	1TH	003	004	Even while we were with you we kept on warning you that we would suffer persecution soon— and as you well know that is exactly what has happened.
052	1TH	003	005	This is why, when I couldn't stand it anymore, I sent to find out whether you were still trusting in God. I was concerned that the devil had successfully tempted you and that all our work had been for nothing!
052	1TH	003	006	Now Timothy has just returned from visiting you and he has brought us good news of your trust in God and the love you have. He's told us that you still have fond memories of us, longing to see us just as we long to see you.
052	1TH	003	007	This news really encouraged us while we were suffering troubles ourselves, brothers and sisters, knowing that you continue to hold on to your trust in God.
052	1TH	003	008	For us life is worth living now because you're standing firm in the Lord!
052	1TH	003	009	As we go into the presence of our God, how can we ever thank God enough for you because of all the joy you bring to us?
052	1TH	003	010	Night and day we pray for you as earnestly as possible, hoping to see you again face to face, and to help you continue developing your trust in God.
052	1TH	003	011	May God our Father and our Lord Jesus make it possible for us to come to see you soon.
052	1TH	003	012	May the Lord increase your love so it overflows to one another, and to everyone, just as we love you.
052	1TH	003	013	In this way may the Lord strengthen you so you may stand with minds that are holy and blameless before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all his holy ones.
052	1TH	004	001	A few more things: Brothers and sisters, we plead with you and urge you in the Lord Jesus to behave in ways that please God, just as we instructed you. Of course you're already doing this, just do it more and more!
052	1TH	004	002	You remember the instructions we gave you on behalf of the Lord Jesus.
052	1TH	004	003	What God wants is for you to live holy lives. So stay away from sexual immorality
052	1TH	004	004	in order that each of you may control yourselves in a way that is holy and respectful,
052	1TH	004	005	not indulging passionate lust like the heathen who have no knowledge of God.
052	1TH	004	006	Don't cheat or take advantage of another Christian in these matters, for the Lord is the one who executes justice in all such things, as we've already clearly explained to you, and warned you about.
052	1TH	004	007	For God did not call us to live impure lives, but holy lives.
052	1TH	004	008	So anyone who rejects this position isn't just rejecting what a human being is saying; they are rejecting God, who gives his Holy Spirit to you.
052	1TH	004	009	We certainly don't need to write and tell you to love fellow-believers, because God teaches you to love one another—
052	1TH	004	010	and in fact you are demonstrating this love to all the believers throughout Macedonia. Even so we want to encourage you, brothers and sisters, to love more and more.
052	1TH	004	011	Try to live a quiet life, minding your own business, doing your own work, as we've already explained to you,
052	1TH	004	012	so that your way of life may be respected by non-Christians and you won't have to rely on anyone to provide what you need.
052	1TH	004	013	We don't want you to be confused about what happens when people die, brothers and sisters, so that you won't grieve like others who don't have any hope.
052	1TH	004	014	Since we're convinced that Jesus died and rose again, we're also sure that God will bring with Jesus those who have died trusting in him.
052	1TH	004	015	What we're telling you comes from the Lord: Those of us who are alive and still here when the Lord comes certainly won't precede those who have died.
052	1TH	004	016	For the Lord himself will come down from heaven with a commanding shout, with the cry of the archangel, and with the sound of God's trumpet, and those who have died in Christ will rise first.
052	1TH	004	017	Then those of us who are alive and still here will be carried up together with them into the clouds, and we shall meet the Lord in the air. Then we will be with the Lord forever!
052	1TH	004	018	So encourage one another with these words.
052	1TH	005	001	Brothers and sisters, we don't need to write anything to you about prophetic times and dates.
052	1TH	005	002	You yourselves know very well that the day of the Lord will come like a thief in the night.
052	1TH	005	003	When people talk about peace and security suddenly they will be completely ruined. It will be just like the sudden onset of childbirth, and they certainly won't escape.
052	1TH	005	004	But you, brothers and sisters, are not in the dark about this so that you won't be caught by surprise when the Day of Judgment arrives suddenly like a thief.
052	1TH	005	005	For you are all children of light and children of the day. We don't belong to the night or to darkness.
052	1TH	005	006	So then we shouldn't be sleeping like everybody else—we should stay awake and keep ourselves clear-headed.
052	1TH	005	007	For it's during the night that people sleep; and it's at night that they get drunk.
052	1TH	005	008	But since we belong to the day we should keep our heads clear. We strap on the breastplate of trust and love. We put on the hope of salvation as a helmet.
052	1TH	005	009	For God hasn't placed us in a position to be punished, but has reserved us for salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ.
052	1TH	005	010	He's the one who died for us so that whether we're alive or dead we shall live together with him.
052	1TH	005	011	So encourage and strengthen one another, just as you are doing.
052	1TH	005	012	Brothers and sisters, we're asking you to respect those who work with you, who lead you in the Lord and teach you.
052	1TH	005	013	You should value them highly in love for the work they do. Live in peace with each other.
052	1TH	005	014	We urge you, brothers and sisters, to warn those who are lazy, encourage those who are anxious, help those who are weak, and be patient with everyone.
052	1TH	005	015	Make sure none of you pays back evil for evil, but always try to do good to one another, and to everyone.
052	1TH	005	016	Always be full of joy,
052	1TH	005	017	never stop praying,
052	1TH	005	018	be thankful in every situation—because this is what God in Christ Jesus wants you to do.
052	1TH	005	019	Don't hold the Spirit back,
052	1TH	005	020	don't look down on prophecy,
052	1TH	005	021	make sure to check everything. Hold on to whatever is good;
052	1TH	005	022	keep away from every kind of evil.
052	1TH	005	023	May the God of peace himself make you completely holy, and may your whole being—body, mind and spirit—be kept blameless for when our Lord Jesus Christ returns.
052	1TH	005	024	The one who calls you is trustworthy, and he will do this.
052	1TH	005	025	Brothers and sisters, pray for us.
052	1TH	005	026	Greet all the believers there affectionately.
052	1TH	005	027	I'm requiring you by the Lord that this letter be read to all the believers.
052	1TH	005	028	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
#
# BOOK	053	2TH	2 Thessalonians	2 Thessalonians
053	2TH	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy to the church of the Thessalonians who belong to God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	002	May you have grace and peace from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	003	We keep on thanking God for you, brothers and sisters—we just have to! This is the right thing to do because your trust in God is growing in leaps and bounds, and the love you all have for each other increases more and more.
053	2TH	001	004	We speak so proudly of you among the churches of God because of your patient courage and trust in God during all the persecution and trouble you're going through.
053	2TH	001	005	For this is evidence that God is right in the decisions he makes, and that you deserve the kingdom of God for which you are suffering.
053	2TH	001	006	Since God does what's right he will deal appropriately with those who cause you trouble.
053	2TH	001	007	He will free you from your suffering—and us too—when the Lord Jesus appears from heaven in blazing fire with his powerful angels,
053	2TH	001	008	bringing judgment on those who reject God and refuse to accept the good news of our Lord Jesus.
053	2TH	001	009	They will rightly experience the consequence of eternal loss, separated from the presence of the Lord and his glorious power,
053	2TH	001	010	on the day when he comes to receive glory from his people, admired by all those who trust in him. This includes you because you were convinced about what we told you.
053	2TH	001	011	That's why we continue to pray for you, that our God may make you worthy of what he's called us to do. May God powerfully fulfill every desire you have to do good and every action that comes from trusting him
053	2TH	001	012	so that the name of our Lord Jesus may be honored by what you do—and in turn you are honored by him through the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	001	Talking about the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and how we're brought together to him, brothers and sisters—
053	2TH	002	002	please don't become upset or concerned by any spiritual revelation, or message, or letter supposedly from us that makes you think that the day of the Lord has already come.
053	2TH	002	003	Don't let anyone deceive you in any way, because the Rebellion must come first, and the lawless man be revealed, the one whose end is destruction.
053	2TH	002	004	He is the enemy of God, and proudly sets himself up over everything that is called God and is worshiped. He even installs himself in God's Temple, claiming to be God.
053	2TH	002	005	Don't you remember that I told you all this while I was still with you?
053	2TH	002	006	Now you know what's keeping him in check, because he will be revealed for what he is at the appropriate time.
053	2TH	002	007	For the secret ways of lawlessness are already at work; however he who now restrains it will continue to do so until he is out of the way.
053	2TH	002	008	Then the lawless one will be revealed, the one whom the Lord Jesus will wipe out, blowing him away, destroying him by the brilliance of his coming.
053	2TH	002	009	He (the lawless one) comes to do Satan's work, having all kinds of powers, using miracles, and performing amazing but deceptive displays.
053	2TH	002	010	Using every type of evil trick he deludes those who are on their way to destruction, because they refused to love the truth and so be saved.
053	2TH	002	011	Because of this God sends them a convincing delusion so that they put their trust in the lie.
053	2TH	002	012	As a result everyone who did not trust in the truth will be condemned, for they preferred what is evil.
053	2TH	002	013	But we just have to keep on thanking God for you, brothers and sisters loved by the Lord, because God from the beginning chose you to be saved through the Spirit who makes you right as you trust in the truth.
053	2TH	002	014	This is what he called you to through the good news we shared with you, so that you could participate in the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	015	So, brothers and sisters, stand firm, and hold on to what you've been taught, whether by what you were told, or through a letter from us.
053	2TH	002	016	Now may our Lord Jesus Christ himself and God the Father (who through his grace gave us eternal confidence and a trustworthy hope),
053	2TH	002	017	encourage you and strengthen you so you can say and do everything that is good.
053	2TH	003	001	Lastly, brothers and sisters, please pray for us, so that the Lord's message may spread and be truly appreciated, just as it is by you—
053	2TH	003	002	and that we may be kept safe from immoral and evil men, because not everyone trusts in God.
053	2TH	003	003	But the Lord is trustworthy and will strengthen you, and protect you from the evil one.
053	2TH	003	004	We have great confidence in the Lord that you are doing and will continue to do what we told you.
053	2TH	003	005	May the Lord lead you into a deeper understanding of God's love for you and the endurance of Christ.
053	2TH	003	006	Now we want to tell you, brothers and sisters, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, not to associate with any believer who can't be bothered to work for their living—those who don't follow the teachings they learned from us.
053	2TH	003	007	You certainly know that you should follow our example, because while we were with you we weren't lazy,
053	2TH	003	008	—we didn't eat anyone's food without paying for it. Instead we worked hard day and night so we wouldn't be a burden to any of you.
053	2TH	003	009	Not that we don't have the right to do so—but we wanted to be an example to you, so that you could copy what we did.
053	2TH	003	010	Even while we were with you we gave strict instructions that anybody who didn't want to work shouldn't eat.
053	2TH	003	011	But now we hear that there are some lazy busybodies among you who don't work at all.
053	2TH	003	012	We're ordering such people, urging them in the Lord Jesus, to settle down and work to pay for their own food.
053	2TH	003	013	Brothers and sisters, don't give up doing good.
053	2TH	003	014	Take note of anyone who doesn't do what we're telling you in this letter, and make sure you don't associate with them, so that they may become embarrassed.
053	2TH	003	015	Don't consider them enemies, but warn them as a brother or sister.
053	2TH	003	016	May the Lord of peace himself grant you peace in every situation in every way. May the Lord be with all of you.
053	2TH	003	017	Notice the greeting to you from me, Paul, in my own handwriting. This is my signature on every letter I write.
053	2TH	003	018	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.
#
# BOOK	054	1TI	1 Timothy	1 Timothy
054	1TI	001	001	This letter comes from Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus appointed by the authority of God our Savior and Christ Jesus, who is our hope.
054	1TI	001	002	I'm sending it to you Timothy. You are my true son because of your trust in God. May you have grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.
054	1TI	001	003	When I was on my way to Macedonia I asked you to stay behind in Ephesus, so that you could speak with those who teach false ideas and insist that they stop.
054	1TI	001	004	They shouldn't concern themselves with legends and never-ending obsessions about ancestry. Such ideas only lead to pointless debates, instead of understanding God as we trust in him.
054	1TI	001	005	The reason why I insist on this is so we may have love that comes from a pure heart, from a clear conscience and sincere trust in God.
054	1TI	001	006	Some have deviated from these things, and have ended up talking nonsense.
054	1TI	001	007	They have ambitions to be teachers of the law, but they have no idea what they're talking about or what they're so boldly announcing!
054	1TI	001	008	Now we recognize that the law is good if people use it properly.
054	1TI	001	009	We also know that law isn't laid down for those who do what is good and right, but for those who are rebellious and ignore the law. It applies to people who have no use for God, who are sinful, who treat nothing as holy and are completely irreligious. It's for those who kill fathers and mothers, for murderers,
054	1TI	001	010	for those who are sexually immoral, homosexuals, kidnappers, liars, false witnesses—and anything else that's opposed to good teachings
054	1TI	001	011	as determined by the wonderful good news of our blessed God which he entrusted to me.
054	1TI	001	012	I'm just so grateful to Christ Jesus our Lord for the strength he's given me, and that he considered me trustworthy, appointing me to work for him.
054	1TI	001	013	Even though I used to insult God, and persecuted and abused God's people, God showed me mercy because of my ignorance and unbelief.
054	1TI	001	014	Our Lord in his grace filled me to overflowing with trust and love that comes from Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	001	015	You can trust this saying that everyone should accept: “Christ Jesus came to this world to save sinners,” and I'm the worst of them.
054	1TI	001	016	For this reason I was shown mercy—since I'm the worst sinner, Jesus Christ could demonstrate his infinite patience as an example to those who choose to trust in him and gain eternal life.
054	1TI	001	017	Honor and glory forever and ever to the eternal King, the immortal, invisible, and only God! Amen.
054	1TI	001	018	These are the instructions I want to give to you, Timothy, my son, following the prophecies that brought you this far, so you can fight the good fight!
054	1TI	001	019	Keep on trusting God and make sure you have a clear conscience. Some have refused to do this and have shipwrecked their trust in God.
054	1TI	001	020	Hymenaeus and Alexander are such people, and I have “handed them over to Satan” to teach them not to misrepresent God.
054	1TI	002	001	First of all, I want to encourage you to pray for everybody: make requests of God, ask on their behalf, and give thanks.
054	1TI	002	002	Pray like this for kings and all types of leaders so that we may live quiet and peaceful lives, always thinking about God and taking life seriously.
054	1TI	002	003	This is what is good, and what pleases God our Savior.
054	1TI	002	004	He wants everyone to be saved, and come to understand what truth really is.
054	1TI	002	005	For there is one God, and one mediator of God and mankind—the man Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	002	006	He gave himself so we could all be won back, demonstrating the evidence at the right time.
054	1TI	002	007	I was appointed to share this message and be its messenger, a teacher to the foreigners about trusting God and the truth (I'm not lying, I'm telling the truth!)
054	1TI	002	008	What I really want is for men everywhere to pray sincerely to God. No anger or arguments!
054	1TI	002	009	In the same way, women should dress sensibly, modestly, and appropriately. They should be attractive not in their hairstyle or by wearing gold or pearls or expensive clothes,
054	1TI	002	010	but by the good things they do—as is appropriate for women who claim to follow God.
054	1TI	002	011	Women should learn quietly, respecting their place.
054	1TI	002	012	I don't allow women to be instructors, or to dominate men; let them remain quiet.
054	1TI	002	013	For Adam was made first, and then Eve.
054	1TI	002	014	Adam wasn't deceived, but Eve was completely deceived, and she fell into sin.
054	1TI	002	015	However, women will be saved through becoming mothers, as long as they continue to trust and love, and to live holy, sensible lives.
054	1TI	003	001	This is a trustworthy statement: “If someone aspires to be an elder, this is a good work to want to do.”
054	1TI	003	002	An elder must be above reproach, married to one wife, self-controlled, well-balanced, sensible, hospitable, and able to teach.
054	1TI	003	003	He should be someone who doesn't get drunk or become violent, but is gentle, and is not argumentative or greedy for money.
054	1TI	003	004	He must handle his own family well. His children must respect what he tells them to do.
054	1TI	003	005	(For if a man doesn't know how to manage his own family, how can he manage God's church?)
054	1TI	003	006	He should not be a new believer, in case he gets so full of himself that he falls under the same condemnation as the devil.
054	1TI	003	007	People outside the church should also speak well of him so that he won't disgrace himself and fall into the devil's trap.
054	1TI	003	008	Similarly deacons should be respected, and not be hypocritical. They should not be addicted to drink, and should not be trying to dishonestly enrich themselves.
054	1TI	003	009	They must stick to the revealed truth about God, trusting in him with a pure conscience.
054	1TI	003	010	They should be tried out first, and if they can't be faulted then let them serve as deacons.
054	1TI	003	011	Their wives should be respected too. They should not slander people with gossip, and they should be self-controlled and trustworthy in all they do.
054	1TI	003	012	Deacons should be married to one wife, managing their children and their homes well.
054	1TI	003	013	Those who serve well as deacons gain a good reputation and much confidence in their trust in Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	003	014	Even though I hope to see you soon, I'm writing about all this to you so that
054	1TI	003	015	if I'm delayed you'll know how people should behave themselves in God's house. This is the church of the living God, the support pillar and foundation of the truth.
054	1TI	003	016	There's no question about it: the revealed truth about God is amazing! He was made known to us in human form, he was vindicated by the Spirit, seen by angels, declared to the nations, trusted in by the world, and taken up in glory!
054	1TI	004	001	However, the Spirit very clearly explains that in the last times some will abandon their trust in God, and will listen to deceptive spirits and beliefs that come from demons.
054	1TI	004	002	These hypocritical liars, whose consciences have been seared,
054	1TI	004	003	tell people to not marry and not to eat certain foods made by God that should be accepted with thanks by those who trust and know the truth.
054	1TI	004	004	Everything created by God is good, and nothing should be rejected but should be received with thanks,
054	1TI	004	005	since it is made sacred by the word of God and by prayer.
054	1TI	004	006	If you point out these things to the brothers and sisters you will be a good minister of Christ Jesus. You gain strength by trusting in the truth, and in the good teaching you've followed.
054	1TI	004	007	Reject what is irreligious, and old wives' tales. Make sure your exercise is spiritual—
054	1TI	004	008	for while physical exercise is useful to some extent, spiritual exercise is much more useful. For “it has promise for the present life, and for the life to come.”
054	1TI	004	009	You can trust this saying that should be accepted by everyone.
054	1TI	004	010	The reason we work and do the best we can is because our hope is in the living God. He is the Savior of all people, especially of those who trust in him.
054	1TI	004	011	This is what you should teach. Tell everyone to follow your instructions.
054	1TI	004	012	Don't let anyone look down on you because you are young. Be an example to those who trust in God—in the way you speak, the kind of life you live, in love, in trust, and in purity.
054	1TI	004	013	Until I get there, make sure you read the Scriptures to the church, and encourage them by your speaking and teaching.
054	1TI	004	014	Don't neglect the gracious gift you have that was given to you by prophetic inspiration when the church elders laid their hands on you.
054	1TI	004	015	Think carefully about these things, and dedicate yourself completely to them so that everyone can see the progress you're making.
054	1TI	004	016	Mind what you're doing and what you're teaching. Keep going with all of this, because as you do so you'll save both yourself and those who listen to you.
054	1TI	005	001	Don't rebuke a man who is older than you. Instead, encourage him as if he were your father. Treat younger men as brothers,
054	1TI	005	002	older women as mothers, younger women as sisters, with the highest standards of decency.
054	1TI	005	003	Help widows who don't have a family.
054	1TI	005	004	For the Christian responsibility of a widow's children or grandchildren is to do their duty for their own family, and repay their parents by helping them out. This is what pleases God.
054	1TI	005	005	Now a real widow, having no family, alone and without support, puts her hope in God and prays for help night and day.
054	1TI	005	006	But a widow who concentrates on pleasing herself is already dead, even though she's still physically alive.
054	1TI	005	007	Give people these instructions so that they will be above criticism.
054	1TI	005	008	But those who don't look after their relatives, especially their own family, have denied their beliefs, and are worse than those who don't believe.
054	1TI	005	009	Only widows over sixty who have been faithful to their husbands should be put on the list.
054	1TI	005	010	The widow should have a reputation for doing good. Did she bring up children properly? Has she been hospitable? Has she washed the feet of church members? Has she helped those who were in trouble? Has she really tried to do good in every way?
054	1TI	005	011	Don't take on widows who are younger, because when their physical desires make them want to remarry they abandon their dedication to Christ.
054	1TI	005	012	In this they are guilty of breaking their previous commitment.
054	1TI	005	013	They also get used to a lazy life, just visiting each other in their homes. Not only lazy, but they gossip and meddle, talking about things they shouldn't.
054	1TI	005	014	So my best advice is that younger widows marry and have children and take care of the home. That way there's no opportunity for criticism from the Enemy.
054	1TI	005	015	However, some have already gone the way of Satan.
054	1TI	005	016	Any Christian woman who has widows in the family should help them, so that the church is not burdened with the responsibility, and can help those widows who are truly in need.
054	1TI	005	017	Elders who direct the church well should be seen as doubly valuable, particularly those who work in speaking the Word and in teaching.
054	1TI	005	018	As Scripture says, “Don't muzzle the ox when it's threshing out the grain.” Also, “The worker deserves to be paid.”
054	1TI	005	019	Don't entertain any accusation against an elder unless two or three witnesses support it.
054	1TI	005	020	Censure those who sin in front of everyone as a warning to others as well.
054	1TI	005	021	Before God and Christ Jesus, and the holy angels, I instruct you to follow these instructions without bias. Don't do anything from an attitude of favoritism.
054	1TI	005	022	Don't be in a hurry to lay hands on anyone; and don't get involved in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure.
054	1TI	005	023	Don't just drink water, but use a little bit of wine because of your bad stomach—you're sick so often!
054	1TI	005	024	The sins of some people are really obvious, and they are clearly guilty, but the sins of others are not seen until later.
054	1TI	005	025	Similarly some good works are obvious, and even those that are hidden won't be for long.
054	1TI	006	001	All who are bound under slavery should consider their masters worthy of respect, so that God's name and Christian beliefs won't be defamed.
054	1TI	006	002	Slaves who have Christian masters should not disrespect them because they are brothers. Instead they should serve them even better, because those who are benefiting from their service are fellow-believers they should love. Teach these instructions, and encourage people to follow them.
054	1TI	006	003	Those who teach different beliefs, and don't listen to good counsel, particularly the words of our Lord Jesus Christ and the true teachings of God,
054	1TI	006	004	are arrogant and don't understand anything. They're obsessed with speculation and philosophical debates which only lead to jealousy, arguments, malicious gossip and evil suspicions—
054	1TI	006	005	the constant arguing of people whose minds are totally corrupt and who have lost the truth, thinking that they can profit financially from religion…
054	1TI	006	006	But knowing and following God is so incredibly satisfying!
054	1TI	006	007	For we didn't bring anything into the world, and we can't take anything out with us either.
054	1TI	006	008	But if we have food and clothes then that's enough for us.
054	1TI	006	009	Those who are determined to become rich fall into the trap of temptation, following many foolish and damaging impulses.
054	1TI	006	010	For the desire to be rich leads to many kinds of evil results. Some of those who longed for this have turned away from the truth, and have hurt themselves, experiencing a lot of pain.
054	1TI	006	011	But you as a man of God should run away from such things. You should seek to do what is right, practice true religion, and trust in God. Aim to love, to be patient, and gentle.
054	1TI	006	012	Fight the good fight as you trust in God. Hold on tightly to the eternal life to which you were called. This is what you promised to do in front of many witnesses.
054	1TI	006	013	My charge to you before God the Life-giver, and before Christ Jesus who testified to the good news before Pontius Pilate,
054	1TI	006	014	is to follow faithfully what you've been told so you will be above criticism until our Lord Jesus Christ appears.
054	1TI	006	015	At the right time Jesus will be revealed—he who is the blessed and only Sovereign, the King of kings, and Lord of lords.
054	1TI	006	016	He is the only one who is immortal, and lives in unapproachable light. No one has seen him or can see him—honor and eternal power is his! Amen.
054	1TI	006	017	Warn those who are rich in the present world not to become proud. Tell them not to place their trust in wealth that is so insecure but in God who so freely gives us everything for our enjoyment.
054	1TI	006	018	Tell them to do good, and to become rich in doing good things, ready to share what they have, and to be generous.
054	1TI	006	019	In this way they store up treasure that will provide a solid basis for the future, so that they can take hold of true life.
054	1TI	006	020	Timothy, take care of what's been given to you. Don't pay any attention to pointless chatter and arguments based on so-called “knowledge.”
054	1TI	006	021	Some who promote these ideas have wandered away from their trust in God. May grace be with you.
