# BOOK	057	PHM	Philemon	Philemon
057	PHM	001	001	This letter is sent from Paul, prisoner of Jesus Christ, and from our brother Timothy, to Philemon, our good friend and co-worker;
057	PHM	001	002	to our sister Apphia, to Archippus who fights alongside us, and to your house church.
057	PHM	001	003	May you have grace and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
057	PHM	001	004	I always thank my God for you, remembering you in my prayers,
057	PHM	001	005	because I hear of your trust in the Lord Jesus and your love for all believers.
057	PHM	001	006	I pray that you will put the generous nature of your trust in God into action as you recognize all the good things we share in Christ.
057	PHM	001	007	Your love, my dear brother, has brought me much happiness and encouragement. You have really inspired those of us who believe!
057	PHM	001	008	That's why even though I'm brave enough in Christ to order you to do your duty,
057	PHM	001	009	I would rather ask you this favor out of love. Old Paul, now also a prisoner of Christ Jesus,
057	PHM	001	010	is appealing to you on behalf of Onesimus who became my adopted son during my imprisonment.
057	PHM	001	011	In the past he was of no use to you, but now he's useful to both you and me!
057	PHM	001	012	I send him to you with my fondest wishes.
057	PHM	001	013	I'd have preferred to keep him here with me so that he could have helped me as you would have done while I am in chains for telling the good news.
057	PHM	001	014	But I decided not to do anything without your permission. I didn't want you to be forced to do good, but to do so willingly.
057	PHM	001	015	Maybe you lost him for a while so that you could have him back forever!
057	PHM	001	016	He's not a servant anymore, because he's more than a servant. He's a specially-loved brother, particularly to me, and even more to you, both as a man and as a fellow-believer in the Lord.
057	PHM	001	017	So if you consider me as a colleague working together with you for the Lord, welcome him as if you were welcoming me.
057	PHM	001	018	If he has done you any wrong, or owes you anything, charge it to my account.
057	PHM	001	019	I Paul am signing this with my own hand: I will repay you. Of course I won't mention what you owe me, including your very self!
057	PHM	001	020	Yes, brother, I'm expecting this favor from you in the Lord; please make me happy in Christ.
057	PHM	001	021	I'm writing about this to you because I'm convinced you'll do as I ask—in fact I know you'll do even more than I've asked!
057	PHM	001	022	In the meantime please have a room ready for me, for I hope to be able to return to see you soon in answer to your prayers.
057	PHM	001	023	Epaphras who is here in prison with me sends his greetings,
057	PHM	001	024	as do my co-workers Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke.
057	PHM	001	025	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.
