058	HEB	001	007	Regarding the angels, he says, “He makes his angels winds, and his servants flames of fire,”
058	HEB	001	008	but about the Son he says, “Your throne, God, lasts forever and ever, and justice is the ruling scepter of your kingdom.
058	HEB	001	009	You love what is right, and hate what is lawless. That is why God, your God, has placed you above everyone else by anointing you with the oil of joy.”
058	HEB	001	010	“You, Lord, laid the foundations of the earth in the beginning. The heavens are the product of your hands.
058	HEB	001	011	They will come to an end, but you will continue. They will wear out like clothes do,
058	HEB	001	012	and you will roll them up like a cloak. Like clothes, they will be changed, but you never change, and your life never ends.”
058	HEB	001	013	But he never said to any angel, “Sit at my right hand until I place your enemies in subjection under your feet.”
058	HEB	001	014	What are the angels? They are beings that serve, sent out to help those who will receive salvation.
058	HEB	002	001	So we should pay even closer attention to what we've learned so we don't drift away from it.
058	HEB	002	002	If the message the angels brought was trustworthy, and every sin and disobedient act brings its own consequence,
058	HEB	002	003	how will we escape if we don't pay attention to this great salvation that the Lord first announced, and then we had confirmed to us by those who heard him.
058	HEB	002	004	God also testified through signs and miracles, by acts that show his power, and by the gifts of the Holy Spirit, given as he chose.
058	HEB	002	005	It's not angels who will be in charge of the world to come that we're talking about.
058	HEB	002	006	But as it's been said, “What are human beings that you should worry about them? What is a son of man that you should care about him?
058	HEB	002	007	You set him a little lower than the angels; you crowned him with glory and honor, and placed him over all your creation.
058	HEB	002	008	You gave him authority over everything.” Nothing was left out when God gave him authority over everything. However, we see that not everything is subject to his authority yet.
058	HEB	002	009	But we see Jesus, for a little while placed a little lower than the angels, through the suffering of death crowned with glory and honor. Through God's grace Jesus experienced death for everyone.
058	HEB	002	010	It was appropriate that God, who creates and maintains everything, should bring many of his children to glory, and to completely prepare through suffering the one who leads them to salvation.
058	HEB	002	011	For both the one who makes people holy and those who are made holy belong to the same family. That's why he doesn't hesitate to call them “brothers,”
058	HEB	002	012	saying “I will announce your name to my brothers; I will praise you among your people when they meet together.”
058	HEB	002	013	Also: “I will place my trust in him,” and “Here I am, together with the children God has given to me.”
058	HEB	002	014	Because the children share flesh and blood in common, he shared in this in the same way so that through death he could destroy the one that had the power of death—the devil—
058	HEB	002	015	and free everyone who through fear of death were enslaved all their lives.
058	HEB	002	016	Of course it's not angels he's concerned about; he's concerned to help the children of Abraham.
