058	HEB	011	028	Trusting in God he observed the Passover and the sprinkling of blood, so that the destroying angel would not touch the Israelites.
058	HEB	011	029	Trusting in God the Israelites crossed the Red Sea as if it were dry land. When the Egyptians attempted to do the same they were drowned.
058	HEB	011	030	Trusting in God, the Israelites marched around the walls of Jericho for seven days, and the walls fell down.
058	HEB	011	031	Trusting in God, Rahab the prostitute didn't die with those who rejected God, because she had welcomed the Israelite spies in peace.
058	HEB	011	032	What other examples should I give? I don't have time to talk about Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah; about David, Samuel, and the prophets.
058	HEB	011	033	Because of their trust in God they conquered kingdoms, did what was good and right, received God's promises, shut the mouths of lions,
058	HEB	011	034	put out blazing fires, escaped being killed by the sword, were weak but made strong, did mighty deeds in war, and routed enemy armies.
058	HEB	011	035	Women were given their dead family members back through resurrection. Others were tortured, refusing to compromise and be pardoned, because they wanted to be part of a better resurrection.
058	HEB	011	036	Yet others suffered insults and whippings; they were put in chains and imprisoned.
058	HEB	011	037	Some were stoned, cut in pieces, tempted, killed by the sword. Some dressed in sheepskins and goatskins: destitute, oppressed, and mistreated.
058	HEB	011	038	The world was not worthy to have such people who wandered in the deserts and mountains, living in caves and holes in the ground.
058	HEB	011	039	All of these people, even though they had God's approval, didn't receive what God had promised.
058	HEB	011	040	God has given us something even better, so that they can't be complete without us.
058	HEB	012	001	For that reason, since we are surrounded by such a great crowd of people who gave evidence of their trust in God, let's get rid of everything that holds us back, the seductive sins that trip us up, and let's keep on running the race placed before us.
058	HEB	012	002	We should keep on looking to Jesus, the one who begins and completes our trust in God. Because of the joy ahead of him Jesus endured the cross, disregarding its shame, and sat down at the right hand of God's throne.
058	HEB	012	003	Think about Jesus who endured such hostility from sinful people so you don't grow tired and become discouraged.
058	HEB	012	004	Your resistance so far hasn't cost you blood as you fight against sin.
058	HEB	012	005	Have you forgotten God's appeal to you when he reasons with you as his children? He says, “My child, don't treat the Lord's discipline lightly, and don't give up when he corrects you either.
058	HEB	012	006	The Lord disciplines everyone he loves, and he punishes everyone he welcomes as his child.”
058	HEB	012	007	Be patient as you experience God's discipline because he is treating you as his children. What child doesn't experience a father's discipline?
058	HEB	012	008	If you are not disciplined (which everyone has experienced), then you are illegitimate and not true children.
058	HEB	012	009	For if we respected our earthly fathers who disciplined us, shouldn't we even more be subject to the discipline of our spiritual Father which leads to life?
058	HEB	012	010	They disciplined us for a short while as they thought appropriate, but God does so for our benefit in order that we can share his holy character.
058	HEB	012	011	When it happens, all discipline seems painful and not something to be happy about. But later on it produces peace in those who have been trained in this way so that they do what is good and right.
058	HEB	012	012	So strengthen your feeble hands, and your weak knees!
058	HEB	012	013	Make straight paths to walk on, so that those who are crippled won't lose their way, but will be healed.
058	HEB	012	014	Do your best to live in peace with everybody, and look for holiness—if you don't have this you won't see the Lord.
058	HEB	012	015	Make sure that none of you lack God's grace, in case some cause of bitterness arises to give trouble and end up corrupting many of you.
058	HEB	012	016	Make sure there's nobody who is sexually immoral, or irreligious, like Esau was. He sold his birthright for a single meal.
058	HEB	012	017	You remember that even when he wanted to receive the blessing later on he was refused. Even though he really tried, and cried hard, Esau couldn't change what he had done.
058	HEB	012	018	You haven't arrived at a physical mountain that can be touched, that burned with fire, to a stormy place of black darkness,
058	HEB	012	019	where the sound of a trumpet and a voice speaking was heard—and those who heard the voice begged never to hear it speak to them again.
058	HEB	012	020	For they couldn't take what they were told to do, such as, “Even if a farm animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned to death.”
058	HEB	012	021	The sight was so terrifying that Moses himself said, “I'm so scared I'm shaking!”
058	HEB	012	022	But you have arrived at Mount Zion, the city of the living God, heavenly Jerusalem, with its thousands and thousands of angels.
058	HEB	012	023	You have come to the church of the firstborn whose names are written down in heaven, to God, the judge of everyone, and to those good people whose lives are complete.
058	HEB	012	024	You have come to Jesus, who shares with us the new agreed relationship, to the sprinkled blood that means more than that of Abel.
058	HEB	012	025	Make sure you don't reject the one who is speaking! If they didn't escape when they rejected God on earth, it is even more certain that we won't escape if we turn away from God who warns us from heaven!
058	HEB	012	026	Back then God's voice shook the earth, but his promise is now: “One more time I'm going to shake not only the earth, but heaven too.”
058	HEB	012	027	This expression, “one more time,” indicates that all creation that is shaken is removed so that everything that is not shaken may remain.
058	HEB	012	028	Since we're receiving a kingdom that cannot be shaken, let us have a gracious attitude, so we can serve God in a way that pleases him, with reverence and respect.
058	HEB	012	029	For “our God is a fire that consumes.”
058	HEB	013	001	May love for each other as brothers and sisters always continue!
058	HEB	013	002	Don't forget to show love for strangers too, because by doing so some have welcomed angels without knowing it.
058	HEB	013	003	Remember those who are locked up in prison as if you were imprisoned with them. Remember those who are mistreated as if you were physically suffering with them.
058	HEB	013	004	Everyone should honor marriage. Husbands and wives should be faithful to each other. God will judge adulterers.
058	HEB	013	005	Don't love money; be content with what you have. God himself has said, “I'll never let you down; I'll never give up on you.”
058	HEB	013	006	That's why we can confidently say, “The Lord is the one who helps me, so I won't be afraid. What can anyone do to me?”
058	HEB	013	007	Remember your leaders who explained God's word to you. Look again at the results of their lives, and imitate their trust in God.
058	HEB	013	008	Jesus Christ is the same yesterday, today, and forever.
058	HEB	013	009	Don't get distracted by different kinds of strange teachings. It's good for the mind to be convinced by grace, not by laws concerning what we eat. Those who followed such laws didn't gain anything.
058	HEB	013	010	We have an altar that those priests of the Tabernacle have no right to eat from.
058	HEB	013	011	The carcasses of the animals, whose blood is carried by the high priest into the most holy place as an offering for sin, are burned outside the camp.
058	HEB	013	012	In the same way Jesus also died outside the city gate so that he could make God's people holy through his own blood.
058	HEB	013	013	So let us go out to him, outside the camp, experiencing and sharing in his shame.
058	HEB	013	014	For we don't have a permanent city to live in here; we're looking for the home that is still to come.
058	HEB	013	015	So let us through Jesus always offer a sacrifice of praise to God—this means speaking well of God, declaring his character.
058	HEB	013	016	And don't forget to do what is good, and to share with others what you have, for God is pleased when you make such sacrifices.
058	HEB	013	017	Follow your leaders, and do what they tell you, for they are watching out for you and are accountable. Act in such a way that they can do this happily—and not with sadness, for that wouldn't help you!
058	HEB	013	018	Please pray for us. We're convinced we have acted in good conscience, always wanting to do what's good and right in every situation.
058	HEB	013	019	I really want you to pray hard so that I can come back to see you soon.
058	HEB	013	020	Now may the God of peace who raised our Lord Jesus, the great shepherd of the sheep, from the dead, with the blood of an eternal agreement—
058	HEB	013	021	may he provide you with all that is good so you can do his will. May he work in us, doing everything that pleases him, through Jesus Christ—glory to him forever and ever. Amen.
058	HEB	013	022	I want to encourage you, brothers and sisters, to pay attention to what I've written to you in this short letter.
058	HEB	013	023	You should know that Timothy has been set free. If he gets here soon, I will come with him to see you.
058	HEB	013	024	Give my greetings to all your leaders, and to all the believers there. The believers here in Italy send their greetings.
058	HEB	013	025	May God's grace be with all of you. Amen.
