# BOOK	060	1PE	1 Peter	1 Peter
060	1PE	001	001	This letter comes from Peter, apostle of Jesus Christ, and is sent to God's chosen people: exiles scattered throughout the provinces of Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia.
060	1PE	001	002	You were chosen by God the Father in his wisdom, made holy by the Spirit, so that you might obey Jesus Christ and be sprinkled with his blood. May you have grace and peace more and more!
060	1PE	001	003	Praise God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! Through his great mercy we have been born again and given a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.
060	1PE	001	004	This inheritance is eternal, it never spoils or fades, and it is kept safe in heaven for you.
060	1PE	001	005	Through your trust in him, God will protect you by his power until salvation arrives—the salvation that is ready to be revealed at the last day.
060	1PE	001	006	So be glad about this, even though you may be sad for a short while as you endure various trials.
060	1PE	001	007	These prove that your trust in God is genuine, just as fire is used to prove if gold is genuine—even though that too can be destroyed—and your faith is more valuable than gold! In this way your trust in God will be recognized and you will receive praise, glory, and honor when Jesus Christ appears.
060	1PE	001	008	You love him even though you have never seen him. Though you cannot see him now, you trust in him and you're filled with wonderful, indescribable happiness.
060	1PE	001	009	Your reward for trusting in him is that you will be saved!
060	1PE	001	010	It was this salvation that the prophets searched for and investigated when they spoke of the grace that was prepared for you.
060	1PE	001	011	They tried to find out when and how this would take place, for the Spirit of Christ inside them spoke clearly about Christ's sufferings and glory to come.
060	1PE	001	012	It was explained to them that they were not doing this for themselves, but for you—since what they spoke about you've now learned from those who shared the good news with you by the Holy Spirit that heaven sent. Even the angels are eager to find out about all this!
060	1PE	001	013	Make sure your minds are in gear. Be clear-headed. Fix your hope exclusively on the grace you'll be given when Jesus is revealed.
060	1PE	001	014	Live like children who do what they're told. Don't allow yourselves to be shaped by your former sinful desires when you didn't know any better.
060	1PE	001	015	Now you need to be holy in everything you do, just as the one who called you is holy.
060	1PE	001	016	As Scripture says, “You are to be holy, for I am holy.”
060	1PE	001	017	Since you call him Father, and recognize he judges everyone impartially based on what they do, take your time here on earth seriously, respecting him.
060	1PE	001	018	You already know that you were not set free from your pointless way of living that you inherited from your forefathers by things that don't have lasting value, like silver or gold.
060	1PE	001	019	You were set free by the costly blood of Christ, who was like a lamb with no flaw or defect.
060	1PE	001	020	He was chosen before the world was created, but he was revealed in these last days for your benefit.
060	1PE	001	021	Through him you trust in God who raised him from the dead, and glorified him, so that you could have confidence and hope in God.
060	1PE	001	022	Now that you've dedicated yourselves by following the truth, love each other sincerely like a true family.
060	1PE	001	023	You've been born again, not the product of a mortal “seed,” but immortal, through the living, eternal word of God.
060	1PE	001	024	For: “All people are like grass, and all their glory like wildflowers. The grass withers and the flowers fall.
060	1PE	001	025	But the word of the Lord remains forever.” This word is the good news that was explained to you.
060	1PE	002	001	So give up all the evil things that you do: all your dishonesty, hypocrisy, and jealousy, all the ways you speak badly about others.
060	1PE	002	002	You should become like newborn babies who only want pure spiritual milk, so you can grow in salvation
060	1PE	002	003	now you've tasted how good the Lord really is.
060	1PE	002	004	As you come to him—the living stone that people rejected as useless, but is chosen by God and precious to him—
060	1PE	002	005	you also become like living stones, being built into a spiritual house. You are a holy priesthood that offers spiritual sacrifices that God welcomes through Jesus Christ.
060	1PE	002	006	As Scripture says, “See! I'm setting in Zion its main cornerstone, specially-chosen and valuable. Whoever trusts in him will not be disappointed.”
060	1PE	002	007	He is very valuable to you who do trust. But for those who don't, “The stone the builders rejected that became the main cornerstone”
060	1PE	002	008	is “The stone that trips you up and the rock that makes you fall.” People stumble over this message because they refuse to accept it—which for them is entirely predictable.
060	1PE	002	009	In complete contrast, you are a specially-chosen family, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people belonging to God. Consequently you can reveal the wonderful things he's done, calling you out of darkness into his marvelous light.
060	1PE	002	010	In the past you were nobodies, but now you are God's people. In the past you hadn't received mercy, but now you have received mercy.
060	1PE	002	011	My friends, I'm pleading with you as foreigners and strangers in this world not to give in to physical desires that are in conflict with what is spiritual.
060	1PE	002	012	Be sure to act appropriately when you're with non-Christians, so even if they accuse you of doing wrong, they will see the good things you do and glorify God when he comes.
060	1PE	002	013	Obey human authority for the Lord's sake, whether it is the king as the highest authority,
060	1PE	002	014	or governors that God appoints to punish those who do evil and to commend those who do good.
060	1PE	002	015	By doing what is good and right God wants you to silence the ignorant accusations of foolish people.
060	1PE	002	016	Yes, you are free people! So don't use your freedom as a cover-up for evil, but live as God's servants.
060	1PE	002	017	Respect everyone. Show your love to the community of believers. Have reverence for God. Respect the king.
060	1PE	002	018	If you are a servant then submit to your master—not just those who are good and kind, but those who are harsh masters as well.
060	1PE	002	019	For this is what grace is: to endure life's pain and unfair suffering, keeping your focus on God.
060	1PE	002	020	However, there's no credit when you're punished for doing something wrong. But if you suffer for doing what is good and right, and you put up with it, then God's grace is with you.
060	1PE	002	021	In fact this is what you were called to do, because Christ suffered for you and gave you an example, so you should follow in his footsteps.
060	1PE	002	022	He never sinned, he never lied;
060	1PE	002	023	and when he was badly treated, he didn't retaliate. When he suffered, he didn't threaten to take revenge. He simply placed himself in the hands of the one who always judges rightly.
060	1PE	002	024	He took the consequences of our sins on himself in his body on the cross, so that we could die to sin and live rightly. “By his wounds you are healed.”
060	1PE	002	025	At one time you were like sheep who had lost their way, but now you've returned to the Shepherd—the one who watches over you.
060	1PE	003	001	Wives, accept your husbands' authority in the same way, so that if some husbands refuse to accept the Word, they may still be won over without words by the way you behave,
060	1PE	003	002	recognizing your pure and reverent behavior.
060	1PE	003	003	Don't focus on outward attractiveness—hairstyles, gold jewelry, or fashionable clothes—
060	1PE	003	004	instead let it come from within, the lasting attractiveness of a gentle and peaceful spirit on the inside. That's what God values.
060	1PE	003	005	This is how holy women of the past who put their confidence in God made themselves beautiful, yielding to their husbands,
060	1PE	003	006	like Sarah who obeyed Abraham, and called him “lord.” You are her daughters if you do what's good and right and are not intimidated.
060	1PE	003	007	Husbands, in just the same way, be considerate to your wives as you live together with them. Though she may not be as strong as you are, you should honor her since she will inherit equally with you God's gift of life. Make sure to do this so nothing will get in the way of your prayers.
060	1PE	003	008	Finally, you should all have the same attitude. Be sympathetic and love each other. Be compassionate, and humble.
060	1PE	003	009	Don't pay back evil for evil, or retaliate when you're abused, instead you should give a blessing—because that's what you were called to do, so you could gain a blessing yourself.
060	1PE	003	010	Remember: “Those who want to love life, and to see good days, must refrain from speaking evil, and not tell lies.
060	1PE	003	011	Turn away from evil and do good; search for peace—run after it!
060	1PE	003	012	For God sees those who do right, and he hears their prayers, but he opposes those who do evil.”
060	1PE	003	013	Who will harm you if you're keen to do good?
060	1PE	003	014	For even if you suffer for doing what's right, you're still better off. Don't be scared over what people threaten, don't worry about it;
060	1PE	003	015	just keep your mind focused on Christ as Lord. Always be ready to explain to anyone who asks you the reason for the hope that you have. Do this in a gentle and respectful way.
060	1PE	003	016	Make sure your conscience is clear, so that if anyone makes accusations against you, they will be embarrassed for speaking badly about the good way you live your life in Christ.
060	1PE	003	017	It's certainly better to suffer for doing good (if that's what God wants), than to suffer for doing wrong!
060	1PE	003	018	Jesus died because of sins, once and for all, the one who is completely true and good and right died for those who are bad, so that he could bring you to God. He was put to death in the body, but he came to life in the spirit.
060	1PE	003	019	He went to speak to those “imprisoned”
060	1PE	003	020	that refused to believe, when God patiently waited in the time of Noah while the ark was being built. Only a few—in fact eight people—were saved “through water.”
060	1PE	003	021	This water symbolizes baptism that now saves you, not by washing off dirt from your body, but as a positive response to God that comes from a clear conscience. It is the resurrection of Jesus Christ that makes your salvation possible.
060	1PE	003	022	Having ascended to heaven, he stands at God's right hand, with angels, authorities, and powers placed under his control.
060	1PE	004	001	Since Christ suffered physically, you must prepare yourselves with the same attitude he had—for those who suffer physically have turned away from sin.
060	1PE	004	002	You will not live the rest of your lives following human desires, but doing what God wants.
060	1PE	004	003	In the past you've spent enough time following the ways of the world: immorality, sexual indulgence, drunken orgies, partying, binge drinking, and revolting idol-worship.
060	1PE	004	004	People think it's strange that you don't join them anymore in this wild and excessive lifestyle, so they curse at you. But they will have to explain what they've done to the one who is ready to judge the living and the dead.
060	1PE	004	005	That's why the good news was shared with those who've already died—
060	1PE	004	006	so that although they were rightly judged as far as being sinful human beings is concerned, they could live in the spirit as far as God is concerned.
060	1PE	004	007	Everything is coming to an end! So think clearly and stay alert when you pray.
060	1PE	004	008	Most of all, you should love one another very deeply, for love covers many of the wrong things people do.
060	1PE	004	009	Show hospitality to one another, and don't complain.
060	1PE	004	010	Whatever gift you've been given, share it with others among you, as people who wisely demonstrate God's grace in all its different forms.
060	1PE	004	011	Anyone who speaks should do so as though God is speaking through them. Anyone who wants to help others should do so through the strength that God gives, so that in everything God may be glorified through Jesus Christ. May glory and power be his forever and ever. Amen.
060	1PE	004	012	My friends, don't be alarmed at the “ordeals of fire” you're having, as if these were unexpected.
060	1PE	004	013	Be happy to the extent that you share in Christ's suffering, because when he appears in his glory, you will be incredibly happy!
060	1PE	004	014	If you are cursed in Christ's name, you're blessed, for God's glorious Spirit rests on you.
060	1PE	004	015	If you suffer, it should not be as a murderer, or a thief, or a criminal, or as a gossip—
060	1PE	004	016	but if it's as a Christian, then you don't need to be ashamed. Instead praise God that you're called by that name!
060	1PE	004	017	For the time of judgment has come—and it begins with the house of God. If it begins with us, what will be the end of those who reject God's good news?
060	1PE	004	018	“If it's hard for those who live right to be saved, what will happen to sinners, those who oppose God?”
060	1PE	004	019	So then those who suffer according to the will of God, the trustworthy Creator, should make sure they are doing good.
060	1PE	005	001	I want to encourage the elders among you. I'm also an elder, a witness to Christ's sufferings, and I will share in the glory that is to come.
060	1PE	005	002	Look after God's flock you have been given to care for, watching over it not because you're forced to, but gladly, as God wants you to. Do this willingly, not looking to make a profit from it.
060	1PE	005	003	Don't be arrogant, lording it over those who have been put in your care, but be an example to the flock.
060	1PE	005	004	When the chief Shepherd appears, you will receive a glorious crown that will never fade.
060	1PE	005	005	Young people, do what the elders tell you. Indeed all of you should serve one another in humility, because “God is against the proud, but favors the humble.”
060	1PE	005	006	Humble yourself before God's powerful hand so that he will lift you up at the appropriate time.
060	1PE	005	007	Surrender all your worries to him, because he cares for you.
060	1PE	005	008	Be responsible, and stay alert. The devil, your enemy, is prowling around like a roaring lion looking for someone to devour.
060	1PE	005	009	Stand firm against him, trusting in God. Remember that your fellow-believers around the world are going through similar troubles.
060	1PE	005	010	After you have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace who called you into his eternal glory in Christ, will himself restore you, support you, strengthen you, and give you a solid foundation.
060	1PE	005	011	To him be power forever and ever! Amen.
060	1PE	005	012	With the help of Silvanus, whom I consider a trustworthy brother, I send this letter to you. In these few words I've written I want to encourage you and testify that this is the true grace of God. Stand firm in God's grace!
060	1PE	005	013	The believers here in “Babylon,” chosen together with you, send their greetings to you, as does Mark, my son.
060	1PE	005	014	Greet each other with a kiss of love. Peace to all of you who are in Christ.
